const e={U0001:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus","U0001 is the umbrella code for trouble on the high-speed CAN, the fast two-wire network joining engine, transmission, brake and steering modules. GM/Saab logs it once a module's transmit error counter climbs past 255: that module disconnects itself, stops sending and works with substitute values.",["Bus pair chafed, pinched or crushed in the harness","Corroded, loose or bent pins at a module or splice connector","One module or its transceiver disturbing the whole bus","History entry after a voltage dip or tester connected with ignition on"],["Several warning lamps and messages at the same time","Scan tool reaches some modules only or none at all","Shifting, steering assist or brake functions in fallback mode","Many lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,3,["U0002","U0003","U0009","U0010","U0073"],""],U0002:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus Performance","U0002 stands for impaired rather than lost traffic on the high-speed CAN, and makers fill the slot in different ways. GM/Saab sets it when a supervised periodic message, which also tells the receiver that its sender is alive, has not shown up within the 250 ms supervision time; the receiver then carries on with a default value.",["Intermittent contact at connectors or splices of the bus pair","Module software reacting to short voltage dips (reflash available)","Weak battery or poor ground causing brief module resets","Electrical interference from retrofitted devices on the bus"],["Warning lamps that appear and disappear again","Single functions briefly unavailable","Code stored as history without a current fault"],3,3,["U0001","U0011","U0073","U0100"],""],U0003:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Open","U0003 reports a break in the (+) wire of the high-speed CAN, which GM and FCA also call CAN-High. At rest this line idles near 2.5 V and is lifted about one volt for each dominant bit. Once it is cut, modules on the far side of the break lose the differential pair and drop out, while nodes on the intact section may keep talking.",["CAN-High conductor broken at a flex point or after a repair","CAN-High terminal pushed back or corroded in a connector","Diagnostic interface connected with ignition on (history code only)"],["Modules beyond the break no longer reachable","Several warnings and fallback modes at once","Fault appears or disappears when the harness is moved"],3,2,["U0001","U0004","U0005","U0006"],""],U0004:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Low","U0004 means the (+) wire of the high-speed CAN, CAN-High, is dragged below its valid range, usually by a short to ground. This is one of the faults the physical layer cannot absorb: a sending node is unable to produce a dominant bit, every frame attempt fails, the error counters rise and the controllers end up bus-off, as onsemi's bench measurements show.",["CAN-High insulation damaged and touching body ground","Harness clamped by a screw, bracket or seat rail","Defective transceiver in one module pulling CAN-High down"],["Network-wide communication loss, scan tool cannot connect","Engine, gearbox, ABS and steering warnings together","Vehicle may not start or run in limp mode"],3,2,["U0001","U0003","U0005","U0007"],""],U0005:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) High","U0005 flags CAN-High, the (+) wire of the high-speed bus, sitting above its permitted range, generally because it touches battery voltage or a 5 V feed. Unlike a ground short this does not have to halt traffic: onsemi and NXP both found that frames still pass, but the voltage picture is distorted, noise immunity worsens and, on networks with a large capacitive load, bit timing can be violated.",["CAN-High chafed through against a battery or ignition feed","Moisture bridging CAN-High to a supply pin in a connector","Incorrectly connected accessory or retrofit module"],["Sporadic warnings, often with no lasting malfunction","Individual messages or modules dropping out under load or in damp weather"],3,0,["U0001","U0003","U0004","U0008"],""],U0006:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Open","U0006 points to an interrupted CAN-Low conductor, i.e. the (-) line on the high-speed network. That line rests near 2.5 V and sinks by about a volt whenever a dominant bit is sent. Nodes isolated by the break no longer receive a usable differential signal from the rest of the network, while the modules still joined on both wires can go on exchanging data.",["CAN-Low conductor fractured at a hinge or flex point","Corroded splice or connector in the CAN-Low path","CAN-Low terminal backed out after work on the harness"],["Part of the modules unreachable, others still respond","Warnings from the affected systems, sometimes only when moving doors or harness"],3,2,["U0001","U0003","U0007","U0008"],""],U0007:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Low","U0007 reports that the (-) line CAN-Low on the fast bus is held below its valid band, normally by a short to ground. The physical layer copes with this particular case: onsemi recorded ongoing transmission with a distorted level pattern and raised transceiver current, and NXP counts it among the hidden failures.",["CAN-Low insulation worn through against body metal","Water in a connector bridging CAN-Low to a ground pin","Module transceiver internally shorted on its CAN-Low pin"],["Usually no noticeable malfunction, code found during a scan","Occasional short-lived warnings, worse with moisture"],3,0,["U0001","U0004","U0006","U0008"],""],U0008:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) High","U0008 means CAN-Low, the (-) wire of the high-speed CAN, is forced too high, typically through contact with the 12 V system or another supply rail. This fault blocks the bus: CAN-Low can no longer be driven down, no dominant state develops, and both onsemi and NXP found that transmission becomes impossible.",["CAN-Low chafed against a battery or ignition supply wire","Retrofit wiring tapped into the bus pair by mistake","Bent pin or moisture linking CAN-Low to a supply contact"],["Total communication loss on the high-speed network","Many warning lamps, possible no-start","Scan tool cannot reach powertrain modules"],3,2,["U0001","U0005","U0006","U0007"],""],U0009:["High Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Shorted to Bus (+)","U0009 describes CAN-Low and CAN-High of the high-speed bus being shorted to each other. The voltage difference between them then stays at zero, which every receiver interprets as recessive, so a dominant bit can never form; onsemi's tests show transmission stopping entirely and controllers running into bus-off.",["Bus pair crushed so that both conductors touch","Water or corrosion bridging CAN-High and CAN-Low in a splice or connector","Failed transceiver shorting both bus pins inside a module"],["No communication on the high-speed network at all","Numerous warnings, fallback modes, possibly no start","Scan tool reaches only modules on other networks"],3,2,["U0001","U0002","U0004","U0008","U0018"],""],U0010:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus","U0010 is the general fault code for the medium-speed CAN, a slower two-wire network that several makers run next to the fast powertrain bus. Saab/GM documents it as mid-speed GMLAN with (+) and (-) wires and a terminating resistor across them, Ford as MS-CAN; on the F-Super Duty an unplugged connector C408 interrupts it and takes climate control, front control panel and headlamp logic down with it.",["Connector in the medium-speed network unplugged or not seated","Harness chafed or wet at doors, tailgate or body mounts","Residual code after module replacement or programming"],["Climate control, lighting or infotainment functions inoperative","Several body modules unreachable with the scan tool","On heavy trucks MIL and engine derate possible"],3,0,["U0001","U0011","U0012","U0018","U0019"],""],U0011:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus Performance","U0011 says the medium-speed CAN is running but not dependably: expected periodic messages come late or not at all, error frames accumulate, or a node briefly goes bus-off and rejoins. No manufacturer publicly documents U0011 in its J2012 sense with thresholds. The nearest model is GM's high-speed counterpart U0002, where a supervised message missing for more than 250 ms sets the code.",["Loose or corroded connector on the medium-speed pair","Low battery voltage or poor ground causing module resets","Module software miscounting or missing messages (update needed)"],["Comfort functions such as windows, locks or climate controls work intermittently","Code stored as history in body modules"],2,0,["U0002","U0010","U0012","U0015"],""],U0012:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Open","U0012 reports an interruption of CAN-High, the (+) wire of the medium-speed CAN. Saab's mid-speed GMLAN uses the same two-wire layout as the fast bus, with a terminating resistor between (+) and (-), so a break isolates the modules downstream and alters the resistance seen between the lines.",["Body or upfitter connector in the medium-speed (+) path left open","CAN-High conductor broken in a door or tailgate harness","Corroded or loose CAN-High terminal"],["Comfort and body modules behind the break inoperative","Climate, lighting or switch panel functions missing"],2,0,["U0003","U0010","U0013","U0015"],""],U0013:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Low","U0013 indicates that CAN-High on the medium-speed bus, the (+) wire, is pulled toward ground. Where this network uses the same differential layout as high-speed CAN, as Saab's terminated mid-speed GMLAN suggests, a grounded CAN-High rules out any dominant bit; onsemi and NXP list this short among those that end all communication.",["Medium-speed CAN-High insulation damaged against body ground","Wires broken open in a door boot or tailgate grommet","Comfort module transceiver pulling CAN-High down"],["All comfort and infotainment modules fail together","Engine and transmission keep working normally"],2,0,["U0004","U0010","U0012","U0014"],""],U0014:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) High","U0014 means CAN-High of the medium-speed bus lies above its normal range, most often because the (+) wire touches battery voltage. On a differential CAN of the high-speed type this is a fault the network rides through: onsemi and NXP found frames still being delivered, but with shifted levels, reduced noise margin and higher current draw in the transceivers.",["Medium-speed CAN-High rubbing against a supply wire","Moisture in a door or roof connector linking CAN-High to plus","Aftermarket device wired to the comfort bus incorrectly"],["Occasional unresponsive switches or flickering displays","Stored code without obvious malfunction"],2,0,["U0005","U0010","U0012","U0013"],""],U0015:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Open","U0015 stands for a break in CAN-Low, the (-) conductor of the medium-speed CAN. Modules separated by the break stop exchanging data with the rest of the network, whereas units still connected on both wires keep working; which functions disappear therefore depends on where the line is cut.",["CAN-Low conductor fractured in a moving harness section","Connector not reconnected after body or upfit work","Corroded CAN-Low splice"],["Only some comfort functions lost, depending on break location","Fault varies when doors or seats are moved"],2,0,["U0006","U0010","U0012","U0016"],""],U0016:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Low","U0016 reports CAN-Low of the medium-speed bus, the (-) wire, sitting below its valid range, typically through a short to ground. Transferred from the high-speed physical layer, which Saab's two-wire terminated mid-speed GMLAN resembles, this is a fault the bus tolerates: onsemi measured continuing transmission with deformed levels, and NXP files it as a hidden failure visible only to transceivers with diagnosis.",["Medium-speed CAN-Low chafed against a ground point or sheet edge","Water ingress in a footwell or door connector","Comfort module transceiver internally shorted on CAN-Low"],["Usually no lasting malfunction, code found during a scan","Sporadic glitches in comfort functions"],2,0,["U0007","U0010","U0015","U0017"],""],U0017:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) High","U0017 means CAN-Low on the medium-speed CAN, the (-) wire, is held too high, as a rule by contact with battery or another supply voltage. On a differential bus of the high-speed type this short is fatal for traffic: the line cannot be pulled down, no dominant bit appears, and onsemi and NXP both class it among the shorts that make transmission impossible.",["Medium-speed CAN-Low chafed against a supply wire","Moisture or bent pin linking CAN-Low to a supply contact","Accessory wiring connected to the comfort bus by mistake"],["All comfort and infotainment modules out at once","Climate, locking or radio not responding"],2,0,["U0008","U0010","U0015","U0016"],""],U0018:["Medium Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Shorted to Bus (+)","U0018 describes the two medium-speed CAN lines, CAN-Low and CAN-High, shorted together. With no voltage difference left, receivers see only recessive bits, nobody can win arbitration, and the controllers on the segment eventually go bus-off; onsemi's measurements on the comparable high-speed layer show transmission stopping completely.",["Medium-speed bus pair crushed so both wires touch","Water in a connector bridging (+) and (-)","Failed transceiver shorting both bus pins in a comfort module"],["Entire comfort network fails, powertrain unaffected","Body modules unreachable with the scan tool"],2,0,["U0009","U0010","U0012","U0015"],""],U0019:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus","U0019 is the general fault slot for the low-speed CAN, the slow body network serving doors, lighting, locks and comfort electronics. Two physical forms exist: the two-wire fault-tolerant CAN of ISO 11898-3, which NXP's TJA1055 runs at up to 125 kBd and keeps alive on one wire after a single break or short, and the one-conductor low-speed GMLAN that GM runs at 33.33 kbit/s. FCA names U0019 CAN B Bus;",["Damaged low-speed bus wiring or corroded, loose connector pins","Poor supply or ground at a module on the body bus","Module software logging the code without a real fault (FCA ProMaster BCM)","Faulty module or transceiver disturbing the low-speed bus"],["Comfort functions such as locks, lighting or windows fail or act erratically","Anti-theft alarm triggers without obvious reason","Lost-communication codes for several body modules","MIL on in some vehicles (FCA ProMaster 2015)"],3,0,["U0001","U0010","U0020","U0021","U0024","U0027"],""],U0020:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus Performance","U0020 reports a low-speed CAN that still runs but delivers its traffic unreliably. GM documents it for the 2011 Saab 9-5, whose low-speed GMLAN is a single wire: a module sets U0020 when a monitored cyclic message, which doubles as proof that the sender is available, fails to arrive, and then substitutes a default value.",["Code stored while modules wake up or after the supply was interrupted","Software anomaly in one module (GM video processing module 2019)","Gateway module stops communicating or has loose terminals","Intermittent contact in the low-speed bus wiring"],["Often no noticeable symptom, code found during a scan","Sporadic dropouts of comfort or display functions","Several modules store communication codes at the same time"],2,0,["U0002","U0019","U0029","U0100"],""],U0021:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Open","U0021 marks a break in the (+) wire of a two-wire low-speed CAN, called CAN-High in the fault-tolerant layout of ISO 11898-3. There the wire rests close to 0 V and is pulled toward 5 V for a dominant bit, the reverse of the high-speed pattern.",["CAN-High wire broken at a flex point such as a door transition","Pushed-back or spread terminal in a connector","Corrosion in a connector or splice"],["Usually no noticeable effect, the bus keeps running","Occasional comfort function glitches, especially with interference","Code stored only in modules on one side of the break"],2,0,["U0003","U0019","U0022","U0023","U0024"],""],U0022:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) Low","U0022 indicates a ground short on CAN-High, the positive conductor of a dual-wire low-speed CAN. In the fault-tolerant design of ISO 11898-3, where CAN-High idles at about 0 V and only rises for dominant bits, a ground short simply takes that rise away.",["CAN-High insulation chafed through against body ground","Wire pierced by a trim screw or trapped under a seat rail","Internal transceiver fault pulling CAN-High low"],["Frequently no symptom besides the stored code","Rare sporadic comfort function faults"],2,0,["U0004","U0019","U0021","U0023","U0025"],""],U0023:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (+) High","U0023 means CAN-High, the (+) conductor of a dual-line low-speed CAN, sits too high, typically shorted to battery voltage or a 5 V supply. Under ISO 11898-3 this pins the line at a level the receivers read as permanently dominant.",["CAN-High chafed against a battery feed or ignition wire","Water in a connector bridging CAN-High to a supply pin","Retrofitted accessory tapped into the wrong wire"],["Comfort functions mostly still work, occasional glitches","Increased sensitivity to interference, e.g. with radio transmitters nearby","Code stored in several body modules"],2,0,["U0005","U0019","U0021","U0022","U0026"],""],U0024:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Open","U0024 reports an interruption of the (-) line, CAN-Low, of a two-wire low-speed CAN. Under the ISO 11898-3 fault-tolerant scheme this wire idles near 5 V and is pulled toward ground for dominant bits. NXP's TJA1055 counts a broken CAN-Low as failure 2, keeps drivers and termination as they are and goes on receiving differentially;",["CAN-Low wire broken in a door or tailgate harness","CAN-Low terminal backed out of its connector","Corroded CAN-Low contact after water entry"],["Typically no symptom, code found during a scan","Comfort functions behind the break react sluggishly or sporadically"],2,0,["U0006","U0019","U0021","U0025","U0026"],""],U0025:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Low","U0025 flags CAN-Low pulled toward ground on a low-speed CAN with two conductors. In the fault-tolerant physical layer of ISO 11898-3 CAN-Low idles near 5 V, so a ground short forces it into its dominant state for good. NXP's TJA1055 (failure 4) first sees a permanently dominant receive signal;",["CAN-Low insulation damaged and touching body ground","Harness trapped by a panel, bracket or seat mechanism","Module transceiver internally shorting CAN-Low to ground"],["Comfort functions work but drop out now and then","Body modules store the code repeatedly"],2,0,["U0007","U0019","U0022","U0024","U0026"],""],U0026:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) High","U0026 means CAN-Low, the (-) line of a two-wire low-speed CAN, is held too high. Since this wire already sits near 5 V at rest in an ISO 11898-3 network, the outcome depends on where the short goes. Against the 5 V supply (failure 6a in NXP's TJA1055) the transceiver stays in differential mode with normal drivers and termination.",["CAN-Low chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Moisture in a connector linking CAN-Low to a supply pin","Faulty transceiver driving CAN-Low to its supply"],["Often no noticeable effect","Occasional comfort function dropouts when the bus runs on one wire"],2,0,["U0008","U0019","U0023","U0024","U0025"],""],U0027:["Low Speed CAN Communication Bus (-) Shorted to Bus (+)","U0027 describes the two wires of a low-speed CAN, (+) and (-), touching each other. On a high-speed bus such a short ends all traffic, but the fault-tolerant layer of ISO 11898-3 is built to ride it out.",["Harness crushed so that both bus wires make contact","Water in a splice or connector bridging the two wires","Damaged transceiver bridging its two bus pins"],["Comfort network keeps running, sometimes with dropouts","Higher sensitivity to electrical interference","Code stored in several body modules at once"],2,0,["U0009","U0018","U0019","U0021","U0024"],""],U0028:["Vehicle Communication Bus A","U0028 is the general code for Vehicle Communication Bus A, a neutral label each maker assigns to a network of its choosing. GM uses it in the radio of many 2013-19 models as the health indicator of the MOST infotainment ring, which the radio masters: a current U0028 symptom 00 points to a MOST module with a power, ground or wake-up fault, found by bypassing modules with kit EL-51578 until the code turns to history.",["Power, ground or wake-up fault at a module on the bus (GM MOST ring)","Bus or supply wiring chafed or pinched (Audi Q5 PHEV, GM dash harness)","Connectors not fully seated or locked, spread pins","Wrong module configuration or software fault (Isuzu FMS, GM brake module 2026)"],["Infotainment functions dead: blank radio display, no audio, steering wheel controls inoperative (GM)","Battery or electrical system warning in the cluster (Audi mild hybrid)","Several warning lamps, vehicle may not be drivable (Audi Q5 PHEV)","Further communication codes stored alongside"],3,2,["U0001","U0029","U0030","U0036","U0037"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A"],U0029:["Vehicle Communication Bus A Performance","U0029 reports that Vehicle Communication Bus A works, but not reliably; which network that is depends on the maker. In Audi's 48 V mild hybrids (A6 up to Q8, 2019-23) the engine control unit logs U002900 for its sensor/hybrid CAN, labelled there as no communication, together with U002800;",["Connector not fully seated or locked, spread or bent pins","Harness chafed on underbody trim or pinched at a dash bracket","Faulty sensor on the bus disturbing communication (Audi brake servo pressure sensor)","Gateway module stops communicating until reset"],["Yellow or red battery warning, battery not charging (Audi mild hybrid)","Intermittent warning messages from several systems","Comfort or infotainment functions drop out briefly"],3,2,["U0002","U0020","U0028","U0036","U0038"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0030:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (+) Open","U0030 stands for an open circuit in the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus A. What that wire is depends on the network a maker assigns to Bus A; where it is a two-wire CAN, like the sensor/hybrid CAN Audi files under this name in its 48 V mild hybrids, the (+) line is CAN-High. A break splits the bus: nodes on opposite sides lose each other, while modules sharing an intact section may still exchange frames.",["(+) wire of Bus A broken in the harness","Terminal backed out or spread in a connector","Connector left unplugged after a repair"],["Functions served by modules beyond the break stop working","Lost-communication codes for some modules on Bus A"],3,0,["U0003","U0028","U0031","U0032","U0033"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (+) — נתק"],U0031:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (+) Low","U0031 indicates a ground short on the (+) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus A. Where Bus A is a high-speed-style two-wire CAN, such as the sensor/hybrid CAN Audi assigns to this slot in its 48 V mild hybrids, the (+) wire is CAN-High, which has to rise by about a volt to form a dominant bit.",["(+) wire chafed through against body ground","Harness trapped under a panel or bracket","Transceiver of one module shorting the (+) line internally"],["All functions served by Bus A fail at once","Many lost-communication codes in other modules","Warning lamps or fallback modes depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0004","U0028","U0030","U0032","U0034"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0032:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (+) High","U0032 reports excess voltage on the (+) line of Vehicle Communication Bus A, usually from contact with battery voltage. If Bus A is a two-wire CAN of the high-speed type, as Audi's sensor/hybrid CAN, the (+) wire is CAN-High. onsemi's bench tests show frames still getting through with CAN-High at 12 V, only with distorted levels;",["(+) wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector bridging the (+) wire to a supply pin","Aftermarket device connected to the bus wire"],["Sporadic warnings or brief function dropouts","Only one module reports the fault, vehicle otherwise normal"],3,0,["U0005","U0028","U0030","U0031","U0035"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0033:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (-) Open","U0033 reports an interruption of the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus A; on a dual-line CAN like the sensor/hybrid CAN Audi lists as Bus A, that is CAN-Low. As with U0030, the network falls apart into pieces that can no longer hear each other, and NXP stresses that a standard high-speed transceiver has no means of detecting an open wire on its own.",["(-) wire of Bus A broken in the harness","Pushed-back or corroded terminal in a connector","Connector not reconnected after a repair"],["Modules beyond the break stop responding","Lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,0,["U0006","U0028","U0030","U0034","U0035"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (-) — נתק"],U0034:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (-) Low","U0034 flags the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus A pulled toward ground. On a high-speed-type CAN, the layout Audi uses for the sensor/hybrid CAN behind this slot, that wire is CAN-Low, which normally drops by about a volt for dominant bits.",["(-) wire insulation damaged and touching ground","Harness pinched by a bracket or panel","Faulty transceiver pulling the (-) line to ground"],["Intermittent communication errors, vehicle mostly normal","Code reported by a single module"],3,0,["U0007","U0028","U0031","U0033","U0035"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0035:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (-) High","U0035 means the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus A is held too high, typically shorted to battery voltage. On a two-wire high-speed-type CAN, such as Audi's sensor/hybrid CAN filed under Bus A, this is CAN-Low. onsemi's tests place CAN-Low at 12 V among the shorts that make transmission impossible: frames can no longer be sent and the controllers repeat them without success.",["(-) wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector linking the (-) wire to a supply pin","Damaged transceiver driving the (-) line high"],["All functions on Bus A fail together","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Warning lamps or fallback modes depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0008","U0028","U0032","U0033","U0034"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ A (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0036:["Vehicle Communication Bus A (-) Shorted to Bus A (+)","U0036 describes a short between the (+) and (-) wires of Vehicle Communication Bus A. On a CAN-type bus the differential voltage then stays at zero, receivers see only recessive bits and, as onsemi's measurements on high-speed CAN show, no frame can be sent any more; NXP adds that transceiver diagnosis cannot detect this short.",["Harness chafed so that both bus wires touch (Audi Q5 PHEV: underbody trim)","Water in a splice or connector bridging the two wires","Damaged transceiver shorting its bus pins"],["Several warning lamps on at once","Vehicle may refuse to drive (Audi Q5 PHEV)","Drive-motor and power-electronics codes stored alongside"],3,2,["U0009","U0027","U0028","U0029","U0110"],""],U0037:["Vehicle Communication Bus B","U0037 is the umbrella code for Vehicle Communication Bus B, the second neutral network slot after Bus A; each maker decides which network sits behind it, and published uses differ widely. Volkswagen's 2014 Touareg data book sets it when a CAN frame sent on Bus B goes unacknowledged.",["Loose or corroded ground or supply of a module on Bus B (FCA: ground G907A)","Module software misreporting or mishandling the bus (Volvo BCM2, Ford VDM, GM brake module 2026)","Damaged bus wiring or a poorly seated connector","A module on Bus B that has stopped answering"],["Warning lamps of the systems on Bus B, e.g. ABS lamp (Jeep) or check-engine lamp (Volvo)","Stop/start or chassis functions unavailable","Lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,2,["U0028","U0038","U0039","U0045","U0046","U0121"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B"],U0038:["Vehicle Communication Bus B Performance","U0038 flags Vehicle Communication Bus B as present but unreliable: frames arrive late, incompletely or for a while not at all, rather than the bus being dead outright. Volkswagen's 2014 Touareg data book describes the trigger as a global time-out in which no messages come in any longer.",["Internal fault in a module on Bus B (Honda Civic: transmission control module)","Loose or corroded terminals interrupting traffic now and then","Software mismatch between modules on the bus"],["Selector stuck in Park, engine does not crank (Honda Civic CVT)","Several warning lamps on at once","Functions drop out intermittently"],3,2,["U0029","U0037","U0047","U0101"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0039:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (+) Open","U0039 reports a break in the (+) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus B, which on a CAN-type network is CAN-High. Deutz assigns this code to the third CAN channel of its EMR L1 engine controller and lists it for main and secondary ECU simply as an open circuit on CAN 3, without naming the wire. On a classic high-speed CAN the interruption stays invisible to the transceiver;",["(+) wire of Bus B broken, often at a flex point","Terminal backed out or spread in a connector","Connector left open after repair work"],["Functions of modules beyond the break unavailable","Lost-communication codes for individual modules"],3,0,["U0030","U0037","U0040","U0041","U0042","U0048"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (+) — נתק"],U0040:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (+) Low","U0040 indicates the (+) line of Vehicle Communication Bus B pulled down to ground potential. On a high-speed-type CAN that is CAN-High, and onsemi's bench tests list it among the shorts that stop all transmission: each failed start of frame raises the transmit error counter by eight, the controller turns error passive after a handful of attempts and goes bus-off once the count passes 255.",["(+) wire chafed through against body ground","Harness crushed by a seat rail, bracket or panel","Transceiver of one module pulling the (+) line to ground"],["All functions on Bus B fail at once (high-speed type)","Many lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Fallback modes or warning lamps depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0031","U0037","U0039","U0041","U0043","U0049"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0041:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (+) High","U0041 means the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus B sits at too high a voltage, typically because it touches a battery or 5 V supply. For a high-speed-type CAN this is CAN-High, and NXP classes a short of CAN-High to battery or to VCC as a hidden failure: frames keep flowing, so only a transceiver with bus diagnosis, such as the TJA1043, reports it.",["(+) wire chafed against a battery or 5 V feed","Moisture in a connector bridging the (+) wire to a supply pin","Faulty transceiver driving the (+) line high"],["Often no noticeable symptom, code found during a scan","Sporadic warnings from one module"],3,0,["U0032","U0037","U0039","U0040","U0044","U0050"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0042:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (-) Open","U0042 points to an interrupted (-) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus B; on a CAN-type bus that is CAN-Low. The network then splits along the break, and on a standard high-speed CAN neither side's transceiver can tell what happened, since NXP states that line interruptions escape even transceiver diagnosis. Detection rests on time-outs for messages from nodes on the far side.",["(-) wire of Bus B broken in the harness","Corroded or pushed-back terminal in a connector","Connector not reconnected after a repair"],["Modules beyond the break no longer respond","Lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,0,["U0033","U0037","U0039","U0043","U0044"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (-) — נתק"],U0043:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (-) Low","U0043 reports the (-) line of Vehicle Communication Bus B shorted toward ground. Where Bus B is built like a high-speed CAN, that line is CAN-Low, and the fault is sneaky: onsemi measured frames still getting through, with distorted levels and the node drawing about 72 mA instead of 65 mA, because the CANH driver now pushes current through the termination into ground. NXP lists the case among hidden failures.",["(-) wire insulation damaged and touching ground","Harness trapped under a panel or bracket","Faulty transceiver pulling the (-) line to ground"],["Vehicle mostly normal, code stored by a single module","Occasional communication errors"],3,0,["U0034","U0037","U0040","U0042","U0044"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0044:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (-) High","U0044 means the (-) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus B is held at an excessive voltage, mostly through contact with battery plus. Where Bus B is a high-speed-type CAN, the conductor is CAN-Low, and onsemi found that with CAN-Low at 12 V no frame gets out any more;",["(-) wire chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector linking the (-) wire to a supply pin","Damaged transceiver driving the (-) line high"],["All functions on Bus B fail together (high-speed type)","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Fallback modes or warning lamps depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0035","U0037","U0041","U0042","U0043"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ B (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0045:["Vehicle Communication Bus B (-) Shorted to Bus B (+)","U0045 describes the two wires of Vehicle Communication Bus B touching each other. Deutz uses this code in the EMR L1 engine controller for a short circuit on its third CAN channel, without further detail. On a high-speed-type CAN, bridged wires leave no differential voltage, every bit reads recessive and, per onsemi, nothing can be transmitted while the CANH driver works into its current limit;",["Harness crushed so that both bus wires touch","Water in a splice or connector bridging the two wires","Damaged module input shorting its bus pins"],["Every function on Bus B unavailable (high-speed type)","Several warning lamps on at once","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks"],3,2,["U0036","U0037","U0040","U0044","U0054"],""],U0046:["Vehicle Communication Bus C","U0046 covers Vehicle Communication Bus C in general, the third manufacturer-assigned network slot after Bus A and Bus B. Public uses are rare. Stellantis lists U0046-00 among the faults addressed by powertrain control module flash 18-071-26 for the 2025 Ram 1500 with the 3.0-litre Hurricane twin-turbo six;",["Control module software that misjudges the bus (Ram 1500: PCM flash)","Damaged bus wiring or poorly seated connector on Bus C","Supply or ground fault at a module on Bus C"],["Check-engine lamp possible together with other stored codes (Ram 1500)","Functions of modules on Bus C unavailable","Lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,2,["U0028","U0037","U0047","U0048","U0055"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C"],U0047:["Vehicle Communication Bus C Performance","U0047 says that Vehicle Communication Bus C is up but its traffic is not dependable, for instance through sporadic error frames, messages arriving too late or brief dropouts. CAN controllers keep score with error counters: as onsemi explains with reference to ISO 11898-1, every failed transmission adds eight to the transmit counter, beyond about 128 the node turns error passive and past 255 it takes itself off the…",["Loose or corroded terminals on Bus C","A module on Bus C resetting because of weak supply or ground","Interference coupled into the bus wiring"],["Functions drop out briefly and return","Sporadic warning messages from several systems"],3,0,["U0002","U0029","U0038","U0046"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0048:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (+) Open","U0048 stands for an open (+) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus C, CAN-High where Bus C is a CAN. Deutz places the code on CAN 4 of its EMR L1 engine controller, listed for main and secondary ECU as an open circuit on that channel, just as U0039 covers CAN 3. Electrically, an interrupted CAN-High wire splits a high-speed CAN into islands that keep working internally;",["(+) wire of Bus C broken at a flex point or splice","Loose crimp or backed-out terminal","Connector not fully seated"],["Modules on the far side of the break unreachable","Lost-communication codes in several modules"],3,0,["U0030","U0039","U0046","U0049","U0050","U0051"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (+) — נתק"],U0049:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (+) Low","U0049 reports the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus C shorted to ground. If Bus C is a high-speed-type CAN, the affected conductor is CAN-High; for a dominant bit it should climb to roughly 3.6 V, which a grounded line cannot do, and onsemi's tests show the node unable to send anything while its CANH output works into a current limit of up to about 120 mA.",["(+) wire of Bus C chafed through to ground","Harness pinched during assembly or repair","Shorted transceiver in a module on Bus C"],["All functions on Bus C fail together (high-speed type)","Missing-message codes in modules on other networks"],3,2,["U0040","U0046","U0048","U0050","U0052"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0050:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (+) High","U0050 flags excess voltage on the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus C. On a high-speed-style CAN bus, the conductor is CAN-High sitting at battery or 5 V level, a condition onsemi found survivable: frames still pass, the dominant bits merely look different and the transceiver draws about as little as when idle, since its high-side driver delivers no current.",["(+) wire of Bus C touching a battery or 5 V feed","Moisture in a connector linking the bus wire to supply","Aftermarket device tapped into the bus wire"],["Usually no symptom, code found during a scan","Occasional single warning from a module on Bus C"],3,0,["U0041","U0046","U0048","U0049","U0053"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0051:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (-) Open","U0051 stands for a severed (-) conductor on Vehicle Communication Bus C, CAN-Low where Bus C is a CAN. Deutz, which places Bus C on the fourth CAN channel of the EMR L1 engine control unit, does not use this code and books CAN 4 faults only as open circuit (U0048) or short circuit (U0054).",["(-) wire of Bus C broken at a flex point or splice","Terminal pushed back or spread in a Bus C connector","Corroded splice interrupting the (-) line"],["Modules beyond the break no longer respond","Code comes and goes while other modules keep working"],3,0,["U0042","U0046","U0048","U0052","U0054"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (-) — נתק"],U0052:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (-) Low","U0052 signals a ground short on the (-) line of Vehicle Communication Bus C; where Bus C follows the high-speed CAN layout, the affected line is CAN-Low, and NXP's application note for the TJA1041 lists this short among the hidden bus failures: nodes keep communicating, so a controller only learns of it from a transceiver with bus diagnosis.",["(-) wire of Bus C chafed against body metal","Harness trapped under a trim panel or seat rail","Transceiver in one module pulling CAN-Low to ground"],["Often no noticeable symptom, code found during a scan","Occasional brief warning from a module on Bus C"],3,0,["U0043","U0046","U0049","U0051","U0053"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0053:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (-) High","U0053 reports too much voltage on the (-) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus C, meaning CAN-Low if Bus C is built as a high-speed CAN, and NXP's TJA1041 application note states that a short of CAN-Low either to battery or to the 5 V transceiver supply makes communication impossible, while onsemi's measurements show the transmitting node stuck in endless failed attempts. All Bus C members go quiet together.",["(-) wire of Bus C touching a battery or 5 V feed","Moisture in a connector bridging the (-) wire to a supply pin","Damaged transceiver holding CAN-Low high"],["All functions on Bus C drop out at once (high-speed type)","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Warning lamps or fallback modes depending on the affected modules"],3,2,["U0044","U0046","U0050","U0051","U0052"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ C (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0054:["Vehicle Communication Bus C (-) Shorted to Bus C (+)","U0054 describes a short between the two wires of Vehicle Communication Bus C. Deutz uses it in main and secondary EMR L1 engine controllers as a short circuit on CAN 4, the same channel whose open circuit is U0048. On a high-speed CAN the bridged pair carries no differential voltage, so no dominant bit can form;",["Harness crushed so that both Bus C wires touch","Water in a splice or connector bridging the pair","Damaged module input shorting its two bus pins"],["All modules on Bus C unreachable (high-speed type)","Engine controller reports CAN fault, connected machine functions fail (Deutz)"],3,2,["U0036","U0045","U0046","U0048","U0063"],""],U0055:["Vehicle Communication Bus D","U0055 covers Vehicle Communication Bus D as a whole, the fourth network slot a manufacturer can assign freely. Volvo documents it for the 2016-17 XC90 T8 plug-in hybrid: the engine control module stores U005500 with fault type intermittent, the driver information display shows the turtle symbol and the car lacks power.",["Control module software misjudging Bus D (Volvo XC90 T8: ECM update)","Supply or ground fault at a module on Bus D","Damaged wiring or loose connector on Bus D"],["Turtle symbol and reduced engine power (Volvo XC90 T8)","Functions of modules on Bus D unavailable","Lost-communication codes stored alongside"],3,2,["U0028","U0037","U0046","U0056","U0064"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D"],U0056:["Vehicle Communication Bus D Performance","U0056 says Vehicle Communication Bus D works, but its traffic is disturbed. Bentley documents it for the Continental GT (2018-20), GTC (2019-20) and Flying Spur (2020): U005600 with symptom numbers 12689537, 12689541 or 12689542 lands in the chassis control unit (address 0074) or in roll control systems 1 and 2 (00D4, 00D5). Bus D is a private CAN there, and its errors pull in a series of suspension codes;",["Chassis control software level prone to Bus D errors (Bentley)","Loose or dirty connector at a module on Bus D","Damaged harness between the modules on Bus D","A module on Bus D restarting because of weak supply"],["Red or yellow suspension warning lamp (Bentley)","Dynamic ride fault message, several suspension codes stored","Functions drop out briefly and return"],3,2,["U0029","U0038","U0047","U0055","U0065"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0057:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (+) Open","U0057 indicates an interrupted (+) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus D. Where Bus D is a two-wire CAN, such as the private chassis CAN Bentley files under that name, it is CAN-High. Apart from splitting the bus, a break changes the line itself: Texas Instruments describes high-speed CAN as a 120-ohm twisted pair terminated at both far ends, and warns against placing a terminator inside a node because the line loses…",["(+) wire of Bus D broken where the harness flexes","Connector left unplugged or not latched after a repair","Backed-out or spread terminal"],["Modules beyond the break unreachable","Sporadic errors among the remaining modules"],3,0,["U0039","U0048","U0055","U0058","U0060"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (+) — נתק"],U0058:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (+) Low","U0058 reports the (+) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus D shorted to ground. If Bus D is a high-speed-style CAN, that conductor is CAN-High, and NXP's TJA1041 application note puts this short on the list of failures that stop communication completely.",["(+) wire of Bus D chafed through to ground","Harness pinched by a bracket or fastener","Shorted transceiver in a module on Bus D"],["All functions on Bus D fail together","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Warning lamps or fallback modes depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0040","U0049","U0055","U0057","U0059"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0059:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (+) High","U0059 means the (+) line of Vehicle Communication Bus D sits at too high a voltage, typically from contact with a battery or 5 V feed. On a high-speed CAN layout the line concerned is CAN-High, and the fault belongs to the shorts NXP calls hidden: communication goes on, and only a transceiver with bus diagnosis can report it.",["(+) wire of Bus D touching a battery or 5 V feed","Moisture in a connector bridging the bus wire to supply","Aftermarket device tapped into the bus wire"],["Usually no symptom, code found during a scan","Occasional single warning from a module on Bus D"],3,0,["U0041","U0050","U0055","U0057","U0058"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0060:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (-) Open","U0060 stands for a break in the (-) line of Vehicle Communication Bus D, CAN-Low on a two-wire CAN such as Bentley's private chassis network. Nodes cut off by the break still see CAN-High move, but a high-speed receiver judges only the voltage difference between both wires, so frames from the other side become unreadable to them.",["(-) wire of Bus D broken in the harness","Connector not fully latched after work on the vehicle","Corroded terminal opening the (-) line"],["Functions of modules beyond the break fail","Lost-communication codes for individual modules on Bus D"],3,0,["U0042","U0051","U0055","U0057","U0061"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (-) — נתק"],U0061:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (-) Low","U0061 reports the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus D held at ground potential; a Bus D designed as high-speed CAN has CAN-Low in that role, which normally swings only between about 2.5 V and 1.5 V. Texas Instruments gives the tolerated common-mode range of ISO 11898 receivers as anything between -2 V and +7 V, so a grounded CAN-Low still lies inside the window and the receivers keep decoding;",["(-) wire of Bus D chafed against a ground point or body edge","Water in a connector linking CAN-Low to a ground pin","Faulty transceiver pulling the (-) line down"],["Often no symptom, code stored in a single module","Occasional interference-related message errors"],3,0,["U0043","U0052","U0055","U0060","U0062"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0062:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (-) High","U0062 means the (-) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus D is forced high, usually by contact with battery plus. Built as high-speed CAN, Bus D carries this fault on CAN-Low, which can then no longer be pulled down any more; onsemi and NXP both list this short among those under which no frame gets through, so every Bus D member eventually ends up bus-off and other networks log its absence.",["(-) wire of Bus D chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector linking the (-) wire to a supply pin","Termination or transceiver damaged by a lasting short to supply"],["All functions on Bus D fail together","Lost-communication codes in modules on other networks","Warning lamps or fallback modes depending on the modules involved"],3,2,["U0044","U0053","U0055","U0061","U0063"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ D (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0063:["Vehicle Communication Bus D (-) Shorted to Bus D (+)","U0063 covers a short circuit between both conductors of Vehicle Communication Bus D. On a CAN-type Bus D the receivers then measure no voltage difference, read every bit as recessive and cannot see any frame start; onsemi lists this short with those that block transmission completely.",["Harness crushed so that both Bus D wires touch","Water in a splice or connector bridging the pair","Damaged transceiver shorting its two bus pins"],["All modules on Bus D unreachable at once","Several warning lamps or fallback modes"],3,2,["U0036","U0045","U0054","U0055","U0072"],""],U0064:["Vehicle Communication Bus E","U0064 is the umbrella fault for Vehicle Communication Bus E, the fifth freely assignable network slot. Jaguar Land Rover documents it for the 2022-25 Range Rover (L460) and 2023-25 Range Rover Sport (L461): modules store U0064-88 (bus off) and U0064-87 (missing message), often together with U0080 codes for Bus F, when connector CM32B3/4 between the main body and instrument panel harnesses is not fully latched.",["Harness connector between body and instrument panel not fully latched (JLR CM32B3/4)","Bent or spread pins in that connector","Supply or ground fault at a module on Bus E"],["Electrical faults that come and go with cabin movement or temperature (JLR)","Modules on Bus E not responding, bus-off or missing-message entries","Codes for further networks stored alongside"],3,2,["U0037","U0046","U0055","U0065","U0080"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E"],U0065:["Vehicle Communication Bus E Performance","U0065 reports that Vehicle Communication Bus E is present but its communication is unreliable. In Audi and Volkswagen gateways this slot stands for the infotainment CAN. Audi lists U006500, labelled there as no communication on the infotainment CAN, in gateway J533 of the 2015-18 A3, paired with U111000 in the instrument cluster: the infotainment unit will not switch on, cannot be operated or goes blank now and…",["Contact carrier not seated in the infotainment unit's quad-lock connector (Audi A3)","Brief dropout of the infotainment unit during a software update (VW Golf)","Loose or corroded terminals on Bus E"],["Infotainment cannot be switched on or operated, screen sporadically blank (Audi A3)","Instrument cluster reports restricted functions","Stored only as a passive entry after a software update"],2,0,["U0029","U0047","U0056","U0064","U0184"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0066:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (+) Open","U0066 indicates a break in the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus E. Where Bus E is a two-wire CAN, like the infotainment CAN Audi and Volkswagen monitor under that slot, the (+) wire is CAN-High. The physical layer decides how visible the fault is.",["(+) wire of Bus E broken in the harness","Contact carrier or terminal not seated in a multi-pin connector","Connector left unplugged after a repair"],["Modules beyond the break, often infotainment units, unreachable","Lost-communication codes for individual modules"],3,0,["U0039","U0057","U0064","U0067","U0069"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (+) — נתק"],U0067:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (+) Low","U0067 tells of the (+) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus E being grounded. For a Bus E built as a high-speed CAN that is CAN-High, which a dominant bit needs to raise by about a volt; grounded, it cannot.",["(+) wire of Bus E chafed through to body ground","Harness trapped behind the dashboard or a trim panel","Shorted transceiver in a module on Bus E"],["All functions on Bus E fail together (high-speed type)","Missing-message codes in modules on other networks"],3,2,["U0040","U0058","U0064","U0066","U0068"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0068:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (+) High","U0068 flags the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus E at an excessive voltage, from battery or a 5 V rail. If Bus E is a high-speed CAN, the line in question is CAN-High, and traffic continues: onsemi saw frames pass with altered dominant levels, NXP files the case under hidden failures. Detecting it therefore depends on the module.",["(+) wire of Bus E chafed against a battery or 5 V feed","Moisture in a connector bridging the bus wire to supply","Aftermarket device connected to the bus wire"],["Usually no symptom, code found by chance","Code stored in only one module on Bus E"],3,0,["U0041","U0059","U0064","U0066","U0067"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0069:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (-) Open","U0069 concerns a severed (-) line on Vehicle Communication Bus E, CAN-Low where Bus E is a CAN such as the infotainment CAN Volkswagen Group gateways supervise. Beyond splitting the network, the break matters for signal quality: Texas Instruments points out that stubs on a high-speed CAN are unterminated and should stay short, around 0.3 m, because reflections in them must die out ahead of the sampling point.",["(-) wire of Bus E broken in the harness","Connector not fully latched, contacts lifting","Terminal backed out of its housing"],["Modules beyond the break unreachable","Sporadic message errors among the remaining modules"],3,0,["U0033","U0060","U0064","U0066","U0070"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (-) — נתק"],U0070:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (-) Low","U0070 points to a (-) line of Vehicle Communication Bus E with a path to ground, CAN-Low wherever Bus E is a high-speed CAN. Traffic survives the short, which onsemi and NXP both confirm, so drivers rarely notice anything; onsemi traced a higher node current, because the upper driver stage now pushes current through the 60-ohm termination into ground.",["(-) wire of Bus E chafed against body ground","Harness pinched during installation of trim or accessories","Faulty transceiver pulling CAN-Low to ground"],["Usually no symptom, code found during a scan","Occasional interference with audio or display functions on Bus E"],3,0,["U0034","U0061","U0064","U0069","U0071"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0071:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (-) High","With U0071 the (-) conductor of Vehicle Communication Bus E sits too high, mostly by a short to battery voltage. Where Bus E is a high-speed CAN this is CAN-Low, and the bus dies: the line can no longer be pulled down, onsemi's node failed every start of frame, and NXP's TJA1041 note lists CAN-Low at battery or at 5 V as faults that prevent any communication.",["(-) wire of Bus E chafed against a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector linking the (-) wire to a supply pin","Damaged transceiver driving the (-) line high"],["All functions on Bus E fail together (high-speed type)","Gateway or other modules report lost communication"],3,2,["U0035","U0062","U0064","U0068","U0070"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ E (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0072:["Vehicle Communication Bus E (-) Shorted to Bus E (+)","U0072 describes the (-) and (+) wires of Vehicle Communication Bus E touching each other. On a high-speed CAN this ends communication: with the pair bridged there is no differential voltage, onsemi found transmission impossible, and NXP's TJA1041 note lists the short with the faults its bus diagnosis cannot detect. A fault-tolerant low-speed CAN degrades more gently.",["Harness crushed so that both Bus E wires touch","Water in a splice or connector bridging the pair","Damaged module input shorting its bus pins"],["All modules on Bus E unreachable (high-speed type)","Several warning messages, gateway reports lost communication"],3,2,["U0036","U0045","U0054","U0063","U0064"],""],U0073:["Control Module Communication Bus A Off","U0073 is logged by a module whose own CAN controller has withdrawn from Bus A. Each failed transmission adds eight to its transmit error counter; above 255 the chip goes bus off and may rejoin only after 128 runs of 11 recessive bits (onsemi).",["Bus A wires chafed through or shorted to ground in the harness","Loose or corroded ground point of a module on Bus A","Backed-out or loose terminals, e.g. in the transmission connector","Open or shorted terminating resistor"],["MIL and several cluster warnings at the same time","Transmission stuck in one gear or shifting harshly","Gauges fluctuate or drop out briefly","Lost-communication codes such as U0100 or U0101 in other modules"],3,3,["U0001","U0028","U0074","U0100","U0101"],""],U0074:["Control Module Communication Bus B Off","U0074 tells that a module dropped into bus off on Bus B, which the makers that use it assign to an extra powertrain network. GM's 2019 ECM tables call it the Powertrain Expansion CAN, and the LT5 injection module rates its Bus B check Type B, two trips. On 2014-18 trucks and SUVs, PIP5427 ties U0074 to a lost link between ECM and fuel pump module that drives fuel pressure far above target and sets P2635;",["Damaged or poorly routed powertrain harness on Bus B","Engine module software fault, fixed by reprogramming","Loose connector, bent pin or badly seated fuse on a Bus B module"],["Service Engine Soon lamp or MIL on","Fuel pressure well above the requested value (GM trucks)","Shifter binds or shift concerns","No crank or start-stop inoperative"],3,3,["U0037","U0073","U0075","U0101","P2635"],""],U0075:["Control Module Communication Bus C Off","Which traffic runs on Bus C differs from brand to brand, so U0075 means little until the storing module is known. On the 2015 Cadillac Escalade with Driver Assist, the active safety module records it alongside radar and camera codes; GM found that a worn diagnostic interface or cable on DLC pins 3 and 11, where the object detection network ends, can create these entries falsely.",["Bus C wires chafed on a seat frame or body edge","Engine module software setting the code falsely","Defective diagnostic interface or cable creating false entries"],["Service messages for steering, stability control or airbag","Driver assistance, radar or front camera unavailable","MIL on with no driveability complaint (FCA)"],3,1,["U0046","U0074","U0076","U0131","U0151"],""],U0076:["Control Module Communication Bus D Off","GM is the main public user of U0076. In the 2019 tables for the Corvette LT5 engine, Bus D is the Powertrain Sensor CAN, a private link between the ECM and engine-side devices. The ECM sets the code when that bus has been off for one second after the controller has run for three seconds, Type B with MIL after two trips, and holds back its lost-message check toward the fuel level module meanwhile.",["ECM harness rubbing through on its bracket","Poor contact at a connector of the engine-side sensor bus","Faulty CAN transceiver inside the ECM"],["Service Engine Soon lamp or MIL on","Fuel gauge erratic or wrong","Message counter codes stored alongside"],2,1,["U0055","U0075","U0077","U0073"],""],U0077:["Control Module Communication Bus E Off","At GM, Bus E is usually a chassis-side network. In the 2018 tables for the LYX engine variant, the ECM watches it the same way as Bus A, more than five bus-off events within 0.81 s, but rates the result Type X without MIL; the transmission's default-to-park checks stay disabled while U0077 is set.",["Corroded underbody connector in the Bus E harness","High resistance in the communication enable (wake-up) circuit","One-off software event in a module, cleared without repair"],["Service ABS, StabiliTrak or power steering messages","Suspension or all-wheel-drive warnings","Heavy steering when the steering module drops off"],3,2,["U0064","U0074","U0076","U0078","U0121"],""],U0078:["Control Module Communication Bus F Off","At GM the bus behind U0078 is often the single-wire low-speed GMLAN that ties body modules together. Equinox and Terrain models from 2010 to 2015 set it with lost-communication codes for body module, cluster and liftgate when water corrodes connector X901 above the liftgate glass.",["Water intrusion and corrosion in a body harness connector","Low-speed bus wire pinched behind trim or headliner","Poor ground of the body control module"],["Interior lamps or liftgate inoperative","Radio, climate panel or cluster go blank","Intermittent no-crank"],2,0,["U0073","U0077","U0080","U0140","U0155"],""],U0079:["Control Module Communication Bus G Off","No manufacturer documents U0079 publicly, so what Bus G is depends entirely on the vehicle. The code belongs to the bus-off family: the controller of the reporting module has collected enough transmit errors to stop sending in order to protect the other nodes.",["Short between the Bus G wires or to ground","Faulty transceiver in the reporting module","Supply or ground dropouts at the reporting module"],["Functions of the reporting module unavailable","Lost-communication codes in other modules"],3,0,["U0078","U007A","U0089","U0100"],""],U007A:["Control Module Communication Bus H Off","Bus H appears in no public manufacturer document for U007A; the code merely says that one module's CAN controller has switched to bus off on the network its maker labels H. A sensible check order follows from the physics. A high-speed CAN carries a 120 ohm resistor at each end, so with the battery disconnected the two wires should show roughly 60 ohms between them;",["Bus H wires shorted together","Terminating resistor open or a terminating module disconnected","Transceiver damaged, e.g. by overvoltage"],["Functions on Bus H fail or work only intermittently","Warning messages from several systems"],3,0,["U0079","U007B","U0092","U0093"],""],U007B:["Control Module Communication Bus I Off","U007B is tied to no published manufacturer use; a Bus I only exists on vehicles split into many separate networks. The cause need not sit in the wiring at all. Onsemi describes a node whose transmit pin cannot produce a dominant level: every start-of-frame attempt fails and raises the error counter by eight, after 17 attempts it is error passive and shortly afterwards bus off, although the remaining bus may keep…",["Transceiver in the reporting module unable to drive the bus","Weak supply or ground at the reporting module","Short or open in the Bus I wiring"],["Only the reporting module's functions drop out","Code returns soon after clearing"],3,0,["U007A","U007C","U009B","U009C"],""],U007C:["Control Module Communication Bus J Off","For U007C no manufacturer publishes a use; a Bus J only exists where the electrical architecture splits the vehicle into ten or more CAN segments. Bus off is self-healing by design: once the controller has seen 128 sequences of 11 recessive bits it may rejoin, as onsemi explains, and the error counters start again from zero.",["Loose pin or connector on Bus J opening briefly","Voltage dip during engine cranking","Harness chafe causing brief shorts on Bus J"],["Stored history code without a current complaint","Brief, self-clearing dropouts of single functions"],3,0,["U007B","U007D","U009D","U009E"],""],U007D:["Control Module Communication Bus K Off","U007D is one of the few late-alphabet bus-off codes with a public trace, all from GM's 2017 full-size trucks and SUVs (Silverado, Sierra, Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon, Escalade). There a serial data gateway module connects many CAN segments, and PIT5586 lists U007D next to U0073, U0078 and a long row of lost-communication codes.",["Bent, backed-out or loose terminals at the gateway connectors","Gateway microcontroller locks up and stops communicating","Damaged wiring on Bus K"],["Instrument cluster gauges dead or fluctuating","No crank, no start or stall after starting","Radio, climate controls or steering wheel buttons inoperative","Numerous lost-communication codes in many modules"],2,2,["U0073","U0078","U007C","U007E","U0100"],""],U007E:["Control Module Communication Bus L Off","There is no public manufacturer documentation for U007E; the letter L is reserved for vehicles with a dozen or more networks. The code marks the last step of the CAN error ladder. A node stays error active while its counters are below 128 and signals faults with dominant flags; between 128 and 255 it becomes error passive and may flag errors only recessively;",["Persistent short or bad contact on Bus L","Fault inside the reporting module's CAN interface"],["Single comfort or assistance function missing","Partner modules report lost communication"],3,0,["U007D","U007F","U0100"],""],U007F:["Control Module Communication Bus M Off","U007F closes the range of bus-off codes that SAE runs from U0073 for Bus A to Bus M; the next code, U0080, already belongs to the general Bus F faults. No manufacturer publishes a use, and which physical network carries the letter M has to be read from the maker's service data. CARB only demands that missing digital communication be detected and stored separately, not how buses are named.",["Shorted line on Bus M","A node unable to drive the bus, e.g. defective transceiver","Poor supply, ground or connector contact at the storing module"],["Functions of the storing module unavailable","Several warning messages or none, depending on the module"],3,0,["U007E","U0080","U0073"],""],U0080:["Vehicle Communication Bus F","U0080 is the general fault of Vehicle Communication Bus F, and makers give that letter very different networks. In the 2019 Audi A6 and A7 3.0 TFSI the transmission module stores U008000 (Bus F) when its harness chafes on the crossmember or the FlexRay feed rubs on a module bracket, together with parking lock codes P17F4-P17F6 and U010100 in the engine module.",["Bus F wiring chafed on a crossmember or bracket","Inline connector of Bus F not fully latched","Module on Bus F starts communicating too late after wake-up (stored code only)","Supply or ground fault of a Bus F module"],["Transmission or other warning messages in the cluster","Stored code without any noticeable fault","Telematics or app services report errors"],3,2,["U0064","U0078","U0081","U0089","U0101"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F"],U0081:["Vehicle Communication Bus F Performance","U0081 marks Vehicle Communication Bus F as working but unreliable: frames arrive damaged, late or not at all from time to time, while the network as a whole stays up. No manufacturer documents U0081 publicly. Jaguar Land Rover shows how close the boundary is by recording invalid serial data on Bus F as failure type 81 of U0080 instead.",["Loose or corroded contact in a Bus F connector","Twisted pair of Bus F damaged or untwisted near a repair","Electrical interference from an aftermarket device","Module software that handles bus timing incorrectly"],["Functions on Bus F drop out briefly and return","Several modules store communication codes at the same time"],3,0,["U0065","U0078","U0080","U008A"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0082:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (+) Open","U0082 reports an interrupted (+) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus F. Where Bus F is FlexRay, as Audi's A6/A7 bulletin suggests, this is bus plus (BP); in a CAN it would be CAN-High. FlexRay signals by the voltage difference between BP and BM, and NXP's TJA1081B only accepts activity once that difference exceeds a threshold of about 150 to 300 mV.",["(+) wire of Bus F broken at a flex point or after chafing","Terminal of the (+) wire pushed back in a connector","Inline connector of Bus F not fully latched"],["Modules on the far side of the break no longer respond","Warnings that come and go with vehicle movement"],3,2,["U0066","U0080","U0083","U0085"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (+) — נתק"],U0083:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (+) Low","U0083 means the (+) line of Vehicle Communication Bus F is held too low, normally by a short to ground. On FlexRay, which Audi links to Bus F, the line is bus plus (BP). NXP builds its TJA1081B to survive such a short and lists short-circuit detection on the bus lines among its diagnostic features;",["(+) wire of Bus F chafed through to body metal","Harness pinched by a trim panel or bracket","Faulty transceiver pulling the (+) line to ground"],["Several functions on Bus F fail at once","Many lost-communication codes in other modules"],3,2,["U0067","U0080","U0082","U0084"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0084:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (+) High","U0084 is set when the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus F carries too much voltage, typically after contact with battery power. For a FlexRay Bus F, as in Audi's A6/A7, the wire is bus plus (BP); NXP rates the bus pins of its TJA1081B to withstand shorts to 14, 24 and 48 V and caps the output current at about 72 mA, so the hardware usually survives while signal levels are wrong.",["(+) wire of Bus F touching a battery or ignition feed","Water in a connector bridging the bus to a supply pin","Faulty aftermarket wiring tapped into the bus"],["Often no symptom, code found during a scan","Sporadic dropouts of functions on Bus F"],3,0,["U0068","U0080","U0083","U0087"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0085:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (-) Open","U0085 points to a severed (-) conductor on Vehicle Communication Bus F, that is bus minus (BM) where Bus F is FlexRay, as in the Audi A6/A7, or CAN-Low in a CAN. How hard the break hits depends on the topology. FlexRay may run two independent channels, and Wikipedia notes that traffic can carry on with reduced bandwidth when one of them fails, so a break on one channel may cost little more than redundancy.",["(-) wire of Bus F broken after chafing or repeated flexing","Spread or corroded terminal of the (-) wire","Poor earlier repair splice in the bus pair"],["Individual modules on Bus F stop responding","Code present with little or no effect when a second channel takes over"],3,2,["U0069","U0080","U0082","U0086"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (-) — נתק"],U0086:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (-) Low","U0086 says the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus F sits too low, usually shorted to ground. On a FlexRay Bus F, as in the Audi A6/A7, that wire is bus minus (BM). At rest both FlexRay lines float near half the transceiver supply, and NXP specifies a near-zero difference between them in idle.",["(-) wire of Bus F chafed against body metal","Harness trapped under a seat rail or trim","Transceiver of one module pulling the (-) line to ground"],["Modules on Bus F fail to wake or drop out","On CAN layouts often no noticeable symptom"],3,2,["U0070","U0080","U0085","U0087"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0087:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (-) High","U0087 stands for a (-) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus F pulled too high, most often through contact with battery voltage. If Bus F is the FlexRay of an Audi A6/A7, the wire is bus minus (BM); held above BP, it creates a constant negative difference that receivers treat as DATA_0, so the channel looks permanently busy and no node can place a frame.",["(-) wire of Bus F shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Moisture in a connector linking the (-) pin to a supply","Internally shorted transceiver in one module"],["All functions on Bus F fail together","Warning lamps and messages from several systems"],3,2,["U0071","U0080","U0084","U0086"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ F (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0088:["Vehicle Communication Bus F (-) Shorted to Bus F (+)","With U0088 the two conductors of Vehicle Communication Bus F are bridged to each other. Signalling on both FlexRay and CAN rests on the difference between the wires, so with them joined there is none: a FlexRay receiver such as NXP's TJA1081B sees a difference below its activity threshold and treats the line as idle, while every sending node reads back something other than what it transmits and sets its bus error…",["Bus F pair crushed so both wires touch","Water or corrosion bridging both wires in a splice or connector","Transceiver with an internal short between its bus pins"],["Complete loss of the functions served by Bus F","Lost-communication codes for several modules"],3,2,["U0072","U0080","U0082","U0085"],""],U0089:["Vehicle Communication Bus G","U0089 covers Vehicle Communication Bus G as a whole, the seventh of the network letters that SAE leaves for manufacturers to assign. No manufacturer documents U0089 publicly, and neither a service bulletin nor an OBD table names a network for the letter G, so the bus behind it can only be identified from the service information for the specific car.",["Damaged wiring or connector on Bus G","Supply or ground fault of a module on Bus G","Internal fault of a module disturbing the bus"],["Functions handled by Bus G modules fail or act erratically","Several modules hold communication codes"],3,2,["U0079","U0080","U008A","U0092","U0100"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G"],U008A:["Vehicle Communication Bus G Performance","U008A means Vehicle Communication Bus G still carries traffic, but not cleanly. No manufacturer documents U008A publicly. If Bus G is a CAN, every node counts its own transmit and receive errors; Wikipedia describes that a node turns error passive once a counter exceeds 127 and leaves the bus only after the transmit count passes 255, which is the bus-off case coded as U0079.",["Loose or corroded contact in a Bus G connector","Aftermarket device tapped into Bus G with a long branch","Termination of Bus G missing or out of tolerance"],["Short dropouts of functions on Bus G","Messages that appear briefly and vanish"],3,0,["U0079","U0081","U0089","U0093"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U008B:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (+) Open","On Vehicle Communication Bus G, U008B flags an open (+) conductor, which on a CAN means CAN-High. No manufacturer documents U008B publicly. A useful clue comes from the termination: Texas Instruments describes a high-speed CAN line ending in a 120-ohm resistor at each end, which a meter across CAN-High and CAN-Low sees as about 60 ohms.",["(+) wire of Bus G broken at a hinge, seat or door passage","Terminal of the (+) wire pushed out of its connector cavity","Corroded splice in the (+) wire"],["Some modules on Bus G not reachable with a scan tool","Intermittent faults that change with temperature or movement"],3,0,["U0089","U008C","U008E","U0094"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (+) — נתק"],U008C:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (+) Low","U008C indicates a (+) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus G pulled too low, usually grounded. No manufacturer documents U008C publicly. On a high-speed CAN the (+) wire is CAN-High, which Texas Instruments describes as rising from about 2.5 V to 3.5 V for every dominant bit while CAN-Low drops to 1.5 V, giving the 2 V difference receivers decode. A grounded CAN-High cannot rise, so no node can assert a dominant bit;",["(+) wire of Bus G chafed against body metal","Harness pinched by a screw, panel or seat","Defective transceiver holding CAN-High to ground"],["All modules on Bus G drop out together","Many warnings and lost-communication codes at once"],3,2,["U0079","U0089","U008B","U008D","U0095"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (+) — ערך נמוך"],U008D:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (+) High","U008D is stored when the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus G carries excessive voltage, from a short to battery or another supply. No manufacturer documents U008D publicly. On a high-speed CAN this concerns CAN-High, and traffic often continues: NXP lists the fault among those that stay hidden unless a transceiver with bus diagnosis catches it, and onsemi saw frames still pass.",["(+) wire of Bus G touching a battery or 24 V feed","Water in a connector linking the bus to a supply pin","Terminating resistor damaged by an earlier short"],["Often no symptom, code found during a scan","Sporadic dropouts on Bus G after a wiring fault"],3,0,["U0089","U008C","U0090","U0096"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (+) — ערך גבוה"],U008E:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (-) Open","With U008E the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus G is open, CAN-Low where Bus G is a CAN. U008E is not documented publicly by any maker. Seen with an oscilloscope, CAN-Low beyond the break no longer drops from about 2.5 V to the 1.5 V that Texas Instruments gives for a dominant bit, so receivers there get only the CAN-High half of the signal and less margin against noise.",["(-) wire of Bus G broken at a flex point","Bus G connector not fully latched or a terminal backed out","Corroded splice interrupting the (-) wire"],["Modules beyond the break respond only sometimes","Code comes and goes with temperature or road shocks"],3,0,["U0089","U008B","U008F","U0097"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (-) — נתק"],U008F:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (-) Low","U008F is the low-voltage fault on the (-) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus G, which on a CAN means CAN-Low touching ground. No public manufacturer document uses U008F. On a high-speed CAN this is one of the faults that let messages through: onsemi measured working transmission with distorted levels, and the node drew about 72 instead of 65 mA because a terminating resistor now drains to ground.",["(-) wire chafed through to the body or a bracket","Moisture in a connector bridging the (-) pin to a ground pin","Damaged transceiver in one module pulling the line down"],["Often no noticeable effect, code found during a scan","Sporadic dropouts on Bus G"],3,0,["U0089","U008E","U0090","U0091","U0098"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0090:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (-) High","U0090 is logged when Bus G's (-) wire is pulled up, typically by a short to a supply feed; in CAN terms this is the CAN-Low line. U0090 is not described in any public manufacturer source. Unlike a grounded CAN-Low, this fault normally stops the bus: onsemi found transmission impossible with CAN-Low at 12 V, and NXP rates it as a short under which communication fails.",["(-) wire shorted to a permanent battery feed","(-) wire touching a switched ignition feed in the harness","Retrofitted equipment spliced into the bus wires"],["All modules on Bus G stop responding at once","Warning lamps and lost-communication codes in several systems","Fault may come and go with the ignition switch position"],3,2,["U0079","U008D","U008F","U0091","U0099"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ G (-) — ערך גבוה"],U0091:["Vehicle Communication Bus G (-) Shorted to Bus G (+)","U0091 closes the Bus G block: the (-) and (+) wires of Vehicle Communication Bus G are joined, on a CAN CAN-Low to CAN-High. No manufacturer has published a use of U0091. With both wires bridged no voltage difference can form, so a high-speed CAN carries no frames at all. Transceiver self-diagnosis is of little help here;",["Bus wires crushed together, e.g. under a seat rail or panel","Corroded or wet splice bridging both wires","Internal short in one module's transceiver"],["Complete loss of the functions served by Bus G","Scan tool cannot reach any module on Bus G"],3,2,["U0079","U0088","U008F","U0090","U009A"],""],U0092:["Vehicle Communication Bus H","U0092 stands for Vehicle Communication Bus H as a whole, the eighth network letter in SAE's list. Which network a carmaker files under H is not stated in any public bulletin or OBD table, and no manufacturer documents U0092 itself; the service data of the specific model has to tell. The code reflects CARB's rule that a digital input which stops communicating must be detected and get its own fault code.",["Wiring or connector fault on Bus H","Weak battery or voltage drop so modules fall off the bus","Blown main fuse or bad feed supplying several Bus H modules"],["Several functions handled by Bus H modules fail together","Problems worse at cranking or with a low battery"],3,2,["U0089","U007A","U0093","U009B"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H"],U0093:["Vehicle Communication Bus H Performance","U0093 says Vehicle Communication Bus H works, but with too many errors or too much delay. U0093 appears in no public manufacturer document. Unlike the wire codes U0094 to U009A, nothing is open or shorted; the signals are merely unreliable. A frequent background is a ground offset between modules.",["Loose or corroded ground point of a Bus H module","Loose terminal causing short interruptions","Interference coupled in from nearby loads or retrofitted devices"],["Functions on Bus H drop out briefly and recover","Modules restart or freeze sporadically"],3,0,["U008A","U0092","U007A","U009C"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0094:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (+) Open","U0094 reports that the (+) wire of Bus H is interrupted, CAN-High where Bus H is a CAN. No manufacturer documents U0094 publicly. How much the break matters depends on the kind of CAN. A fault-tolerant low-speed CAN up to 125 kBd, built with transceivers such as NXP's TJA1055, keeps receiving differentially with a broken CANH wire, and the chip's error output toggles only if the gap separates the sending node from…",["Broken (+) wire, e.g. at a hinge or flexing harness section","Terminal pushed out of a connector","Corroded splice with high resistance"],["Single modules on Bus H not reachable","Fault appears intermittently or with movement"],3,0,["U008B","U0092","U0095","U0097"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (+) — נתק"],U0095:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (+) Low","U0095 indicates that the (+) wire of Vehicle Communication Bus H is held too low, usually through a ground short (CAN-High on a CAN). No public manufacturer document uses U0095. The effect depends heavily on the bus type. On a high-speed CAN, onsemi found that no frame can be sent with CAN-High grounded;",["(+) wire chafed against the body","Harness pinched during a repair or installation","Faulty transceiver holding the (+) line low"],["On high-speed CAN: all Bus H modules fail together","On fault-tolerant CAN: little or no noticeable effect"],3,2,["U007A","U008C","U0094","U0096","U0098"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (+) — ערך נמוך"],U0096:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (+) High","U0096 is set once excessive voltage appears on the Bus H (+) wire, as from a short to battery or to the module supply; on a CAN this is CAN-High. U0096 is not documented by any manufacturer in public. On a high-speed CAN such a short often leaves traffic running; NXP lists CAN-High to battery and to the 5 V supply among hidden failures. A fault-tolerant low-speed CAN reacts in steps.",["(+) wire touching a supply wire","Water in a connector bridging the (+) pin to a supply pin","Faulty transceiver driving the (+) line high"],["Often no symptom, code found during a scan","Sporadic dropouts on Bus H"],3,0,["U008D","U0095","U0099"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (+) — ערך גבוה"],U0097:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (-) Open","U0097 points to an open (-) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus H, CAN-Low if Bus H is a CAN. The code is absent from public manufacturer documents. Effects vary: NXP's fault-tolerant TJA1055 keeps receiving differentially with a broken CANL, while on a high-speed CAN the nodes beyond the break lose part of their signal. Sleep behaviour matters too;",["Broken (-) wire in the harness","Spread or bent terminal losing contact","Poor earlier repair or splice in the (-) wire"],["Modules beyond the break respond only sometimes","Code with little effect on fault-tolerant layouts"],3,0,["U008E","U0094","U0098","U009A"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (-) — נתק"],U0098:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (-) Low","U0098 is stored once the Bus H (-) wire, CAN-Low on a CAN, sits too low, normally from a short to ground. No manufacturer has made a use of U0098 public. With fault-tolerant low-speed CAN the short unfolds in stages: the receive pin of NXP's TJA1055 initially stays dominant without pause; once a time-out has passed, the chip disables its CANL driver and goes on receiving single-wire over CANH.",["(-) wire chafed to ground","Harness pinched by a fastener or panel","Faulty transceiver pulling the (-) line to ground"],["Usually no noticeable symptom","Occasional errors on Bus H in electrically noisy conditions"],3,0,["U008F","U0095","U0097","U0099"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (-) — ערך נמוך"],U0099:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (-) High","U0099 describes a (-) wire on Vehicle Communication Bus H held at too high a voltage, most often through contact with battery power; on a CAN that wire is CAN-Low. Nothing public from a manufacturer covers U0099.",["(-) wire shorted to a battery feed","Corrosion or water in a connector between (-) and a supply pin","Faulty transceiver driving the (-) line high"],["On high-speed CAN: Bus H goes silent","On fault-tolerant CAN: degraded but working communication"],3,2,["U007A","U0090","U0096","U0098"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ H (-) — ערך גבוה"],U009A:["Vehicle Communication Bus H (-) Shorted to Bus H (+)","U009A means the two wires of Vehicle Communication Bus H touch each other, on a CAN CAN-Low against CAN-High. No manufacturer documentation of U009A is public. On a high-speed CAN this ends all traffic; onsemi's bench node could not send and drew about 47 mA against roughly 65 mA on a healthy bus.",["Bus wires crushed together","Wet or corroded splice joining both wires","Internal short in a module's transceiver"],["On high-speed CAN: complete loss of Bus H functions","Lost-communication codes for several modules"],3,2,["U007A","U0091","U0094","U0097"],""],U009B:["Vehicle Communication Bus I","U009B addresses Vehicle Communication Bus I overall, the ninth network letter. Which network sits behind I is left to the manufacturer and not named in any public bulletin; U009B itself is not documented publicly by any maker. CARB requires that a lost digital input be detected with a separate code, which is the role of this group.",["Open or shorted wire on Bus I","One module holding the bus dominant","Missing supply or ground at a Bus I module"],["Functions of Bus I modules fail or act erratically","Lost-communication codes in several modules"],3,2,["U007B","U0092","U009C","U009D"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ I"],U009C:["Vehicle Communication Bus I Performance","U009C reports that Vehicle Communication Bus I carries traffic, but not at the quality the module expects. U009C has not been documented in public by any manufacturer. The causes lie in signal integrity rather than a hard fault.",["Loose contact causing bit errors","Repair with untwisted or overly long wire","Missing or wrong termination"],["Brief dropouts of functions on Bus I","Delayed reactions of displays or controls"],3,0,["U007B","U0093","U009B","U009E"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ I — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U009D:["Vehicle Communication Bus J","U009D covers Vehicle Communication Bus J in general, the tenth letter, and like I it has only this code and a performance code in the list, so open or shorted lines also end up here. No public bulletin names the network behind J, and no manufacturer documents U009D publicly. CARB's requirement for a separate code when a digital input stops communicating is the regulatory basis.",["Open or shorted wire on Bus J","Module not waking or waking late","Supply or ground fault at a Bus J module"],["Functions of Bus J modules missing after start","Lost-communication codes, sometimes only after parking"],3,2,["U007C","U0092","U009B","U009E"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ J"],U009E:["Vehicle Communication Bus J Performance","U009E flags unreliable traffic on Vehicle Communication Bus J without a total loss. No manufacturer publishes a use of U009E. Interference is a likely source. Texas Instruments names fluorescent lamps, switching power supplies and motor drives as typical emitters of common-mode noise that couples onto bus lines, and explains that a receiver without good rejection may take it for data.",["Interference from nearby loads or retrofitted electronics","Bus wires untwisted at a repair","Loose contact in a Bus J connector"],["Short dropouts on Bus J, often with certain loads switched on","Warnings that appear briefly and clear"],3,0,["U007C","U0093","U009C","U009D"],"ערוץ התקשורת של הרכב‏ J — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U0100:["Lost Communication With ECM/PCM A","U0100 is stored by a module that has stopped hearing the engine or powertrain controller, ECM/PCM A; a second engine controller has its own code, U0115. Usually the transmission controller logs it, often alongside other listeners. GM's 2019 ten-speed TCM rates it Type A (MIL on the first trip) and holds it back while its own bus-off code U0073 is active;",["ECM/PCM without power or ground (fuse, main relay, ground point)","Damaged CAN lines or loose, corroded terminals between ECM and TCM","Weak battery or voltage dip during cranking (history code)","ECM internally faulty or software not running"],["MIL on, often several U codes in other modules","Transmission stuck in a substitute gear or harsh shifts","Gauges for engine speed or temperature drop out","Engine may stall or not crank"],2,3,["U0073","U0115","U0101","U0301","U0401"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)‏ A"],U0101:["Lost Communication With TCM","U0101 means the transmission controller has dropped off the bus as seen by another node, mostly the engine controller. GM's 2019 truck ECMs watch eight TCM frames, most of them at 500 ms intervals, and set the code as Type A after battery and run voltage have exceeded 11 V for 3 s, provided U0073 is not active;",["TCM without power or ground (fuse, relay, connector)","Spread or corroded terminals at the transmission harness connector","Chafed or open CAN lines to the TCM","TCM internally faulty, overheated or not programmed"],["MIL on, transmission warning in the cluster","Gear indicator blank or flashing","Transmission locked in one gear","Scan tool cannot reach the TCM"],2,3,["U0073","U0100","U0302","U0402"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מחשב תיבה (TCM)"],U0102:["Lost Communication With Transfer Case Control Module","U0102 is logged when the transfer case control module, which shifts between two- and four-wheel drive and between high and low range, stops sending. GM's 2025 engine controllers expect frame $035 and fail it when gaps exceed 425 ms within a 5 s window; the code is Type C, emissions-neutral and without MIL. The earlier two-mode hybrid trucks (2012 table) used Type B with 500 ms detection between 10 and 18 V.",["Transfer case module without power or ground","Water or corrosion in the module connector (often mounted low on the frame)","Damaged CAN lines to the transfer case module","Transfer case module internally faulty"],["4WD or AWD warning, range selection ignored","Transfer case stays in its last mode","Usually no MIL"],2,0,["U0073","U0303","U0403","U0114"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת תיבת העברה"],U0103:["Lost Communication With Gear Shift Control Module A","U0103 points to gear shift control module A, the electronic selector (lever, rotary knob or buttons) in shift-by-wire cars. GM's 2025 engine controllers talk to it over a LIN line and set the code as Type B once its response is absent for at least 500 ms.",["Selector module software fault (update available from the maker)","Loose ground or blown fuse feeding the selector","Open or shorted LIN/CAN line to the selector","Selector module internally faulty"],["Service Shifter or Shift System Fault message","Selector stuck in Park or gear changes refused","MIL or wrench lamp on","Intermittent no-crank"],2,3,["U0101","U0304","U0404"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ A"],U0104:["Lost Communication With Cruise Control Module","U0104 names the cruise control module, today usually the radar unit of adaptive cruise control that sends speed and distance requests to the engine. GM's 2019 truck ECMs check its frames $2CB and $2CD, treat gaps beyond 500 ms that persist for 3 s as a failure and classify the result as Type C, emissions-neutral and without MIL; detection pauses while the bus-off code of the carrying bus (U0073, U0074) is active.",["Radar/cruise module without power or with a wet, loose connector (front bumper area)","Front-end damage or bumper repair affecting module or wiring","Damaged CAN lines to the module","Cruise/radar module internally faulty"],["Cruise or adaptive cruise unavailable, warning message","Forward collision alert may switch off as well","No MIL"],2,0,["U0073","U0074","U0305","U0405"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שיוט"],U0105:["Lost Communication With Fuel Injector Control Module","U0105 concerns a separate fuel injector control module that drives the injectors on command of the engine controller. GM's 2005 Duramax 6.6 L (LLY) received a status message from this injector driver via CAN (J1939) whose toggle bit must flip every 20 ms; if it stalls for three updates, 30 failures in 50 checks give a Type B code.",["Injector module supply low or missing (fuse, relay, battery voltage)","Loose or corroded connector or damaged CAN lines to the module","Injector module internally faulty (heat, power stage)"],["MIL on","Misfire, rough running or reduced power","Engine stalls or will not start"],3,3,["U0100","U0306","U0406"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מזרק דלק"],U0106:["Lost Communication With Glow Plug Control Module 1","U0106 reports that glow plug control module 1 of a diesel engine no longer communicates. In Ford's 2023 diesel summary (6.7 L and 3.0 L) the GPCM is declared lost after 5 s of silence. GM's 2015 Cruze diesel table fails it when no GPCM message arrives for 0.25 s over a 10 s test (Type B);",["Water or corrosion in the glow plug module connector or harness","Module supply fuse, relay or ground faulty","Damaged CAN lines to the glow plug module","Glow plug module internally faulty (overtemperature, driver)"],["MIL on","Long cranking or no start when cold","White smoke after cold start","Wait-to-start lamp behaves oddly"],2,1,["P0381","P064C","U0307","U0407"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 1"],U0107:["Lost Communication With Throttle Actuator A Control Module","U0107 targets a stand-alone throttle actuator control (TAC) module, as used before throttle control moved into the engine controller. In GM's 2004 and 2005 truck tables (4.3–6.0 L and 8.1 L) the PCM and TAC module traded data over a dedicated serial link; the PCM declared a gap after 18.75 ms and the TAC module after 25 ms.",["Open, shorted or chafed serial data lines between PCM and TAC module","TAC module supply or ground faulty","Corroded connector at the TAC module","TAC module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Reduced engine power, throttle barely opens","Idle unstable or engine stalls"],2,3,["U0100","U0308","U0408"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ A"],U0108:["Lost Communication With Alternative Fuel Control Module","U0108 covers a separate controller for an alternative fuel such as LPG or CNG, added to an engine that otherwise runs a gasoline control strategy. Roush CleanTech's fourth-generation propane systems for Ford E- and F-Series trucks (2016–2018) are a documented user: the PCM expects CAN traffic from the system's Smart Relay Module and stores U0108 when those messages keep missing.",["Alternative fuel module without power or ground (fuse, relay)","Damaged CAN wiring between conversion module and PCM","Water or corrosion in the module connectors","Alternative fuel module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Rough idle or poor running on the alternative fuel","System may stay on or revert to gasoline"],2,1,["U0309","U0409","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלק חלופי"],U0109:["Lost Communication With Fuel Pump Control Module A","U0109 means the engine controller no longer hears fuel pump control module A, the electronics that drive the in-tank pump at variable speed. GM's 2019 Corvette LT5 table watches frames $1EB and $4D9 and sets the code after 10 s as Type B over two trips.",["Loose fuse, relay or feed terminal supplying the pump module","Fuel pump module internally faulty (common on some trucks, replaced by bulletin)","Corroded connector or damaged wiring near the tank or frame","Engine controller software setting the code falsely"],["MIL on","Long cranking, stalling or no start","Hesitation under load from low fuel pressure"],2,3,["U016C","U0310","U0410","P0627","P025A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת משאבת דלק‏ A"],U010A:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Recirculation Control Module A","U010A is set when a stand-alone control module for exhaust gas recirculation A stops communicating. J2012 reserves this slot for engines whose EGR valve or EGR system is run by its own electronics on the bus rather than as a plain output of the engine controller; module B (U010B) would be a second such unit. No manufacturer documents U010A publicly, and the NHTSA bulletin index holds no entry for it.",["EGR module A without power or ground","Heat-damaged wiring or connector near the exhaust side","Open or shorted bus lines to module A","EGR module A internally faulty"],["MIL on","EGR deactivated, higher NOx","Possible reduced power mode"],2,3,["U010B","U040B","U010C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת סחרור גזי פליטה‏ A"],U010B:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Recirculation Control Module B","U010B names the second exhaust gas recirculation control module, B. Its existence implies an engine with two separately controlled EGR units, for example a high- and a low-pressure loop on a diesel or one unit per cylinder bank; which one is B is the maker's choice. The code itself only says that a node expecting periodic messages from module B no longer receives them.",["EGR module B without power or ground","Open or chafed bus branch to module B","Loose or heat-damaged connector at module B","EGR module B internally faulty"],["MIL on","Second EGR path inactive, possible NOx increase","Module B not reachable with a scan tool"],2,3,["U010A","U040C","U010D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת סחרור גזי פליטה‏ B"],U010C:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Control Module A","U010C reports that turbocharger/supercharger control module A, in practice the electronic actuator that positions variable-geometry vanes or a wastegate, has gone silent. GM's 2017 small-diesel table (2.8 L Duramax and Cruze diesel) watches its frames $099 and $499 on a dedicated sensor bus and logs U010C once 10 s pass without them, rated Type B with two trips, provided that bus is not off (U0076).",["Electronic turbo actuator faulty (heat, internal electronics)","Actuator supply, fuse or ground faulty","Heat-damaged connector or bus lines at the turbo"],["MIL on","Low power, reduced boost","Other boost codes such as P003A or P0234 stored"],3,3,["U010D","U040D","U0076","P003A","P0234"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מגדש‏ A"],U010D:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Control Module B","U010D is the counterpart of U010C for a second charger control module, B. It applies to engines with two independently actuated chargers, such as sequential or twin turbo layouts, or a turbo plus an electronically controlled supercharger. Every node that expects cyclic data from module B logs the code once that traffic stops.",["Charger module B without power or ground","Heat-damaged wiring or connector at the second charger","Charger actuator/module B internally faulty"],["MIL on","Reduced power, second charger not used","Module B not reachable with a scan tool"],3,3,["U010C","U040E","P0234"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מגדש‏ B"],U010E:["Lost Communication With Reductant Control Module","U010E concerns the reductant control module that runs dosing, pump and heaters of a diesel SCR system with urea solution (DEF/AdBlue). GM's 2017 small-diesel table expects frame $092 and several $4Cx/$4Ex frames on bus B and, after 10 s of silence, records a Type A fault with MIL on the first trip, unless bus B is off (U0074).",["Reductant module without power or ground (fuse, relay)","Corroded or wet connector at the tank-mounted module","Damaged bus lines along the frame to the module","Engine controller software setting the code falsely"],["MIL and DEF/AdBlue warning","Countdown to speed limit or restart block","Further SCR codes such as P20EE"],2,3,["U0074","U030F","U040F","U02A2","P20EE"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U010F:["Lost Communication With Air Conditioning Control Module","U010F is logged when the air conditioning control module stops reporting. J2012 keeps it apart from the HVAC control module (U0164): the A/C unit governs the refrigerant side, such as compressor clutch or electric compressor drive and pressures, while the HVAC module handles blower, flaps and temperature choice. Saab's 2011 code lists for the 9-5 and 9-4x carry U010F 00 next to U0164 00, which documents GM/Saab use.",["A/C module without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Damaged bus lines to the A/C module","Condensate or water at module or connector","A/C module internally faulty"],["Air conditioning does not cool","Windows fog up, demisting weak","No MIL"],2,0,["U0164","U040A"],""],U0110:["Lost Communication With Drive Motor Control Module A","U0110 means drive motor control module A, the power electronics running the electric traction motor of a hybrid or EV, has stopped talking. Audi's TSB 2065538/1 (Q5 and A7 PHEV, 2019–2021) finds U011000 in the transmission controller after a brief 12 V dip trips the low-voltage monitor; a full bus sleep of about 20 minutes plus clearing codes cures it.",["12 V battery weak or voltage dip, inverter electronics drop off the bus","Water or corrosion in high- or low-voltage connectors of the drive system","Damaged CAN lines to the inverter","Drive motor control module internally faulty"],["Vehicle does not enter READY or will not start","Red drive-system or electrical warning","Electric drive unavailable, limp mode"],4,3,["U0100","U0115","U0311","U0411","U0293"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ A"],U0111:["Lost Communication With Battery Energy Control Module A","U0111 indicates that battery energy control module A, which measures cell voltages, temperatures and current of the high-voltage or 48 V battery, has dropped off the network. GM's 2018 Volt hybrid controller expects it on bus A and sets the code as Type B over two trips once messages have been absent for 5 s above 10.2 V; while it is pending, GM suspends pack voltage and current plausibility checks.",["Battery module software or calibration fault (update released)","Module fails to wake up in extreme cold or after a 12 V dip","Damaged CAN lines or connector at the battery pack","Battery energy control module internally faulty"],["MIL or service-hybrid/charging warning","No READY, electric drive or charging unavailable","Start-stop inoperative (mild hybrid)","12 V battery drained"],4,3,["U0112","U0312","U0412","U0293"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ A"],U0112:["Lost Communication With Battery Energy Control Module B","U0112 is logged when a second battery energy control module, B, stops talking on the bus while a partner still waits for its data. Mitsubishi's 2018 Outlander PHEV is a documented case: the main battery management unit (BMU) supervises a sub-BMU inside the traction pack and stores U0112 once that unit's frames have been missing for 0.3 s, after the BMU has seen 8–16 V for more than 2 s;",["Open, shorted or chafed CAN lines between main and sub battery module inside the pack","Corroded or loose connector at the traction battery","Battery module B internally faulty or without supply","Receiving main battery module faulty"],["MIL or hybrid system warning","Reduced electric range or electric drive unavailable","Vehicle does not reach READY"],4,3,["U0111","U0313","U0413","U0293"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ B"],U0113:["Lost Communication With Emissions Critical Control Information","Unlike its neighbours, U0113 does not name one unit but a class of data: messages a controller depends on for emission control, for instance torque, speed or aftertreatment status supplied by another node. CARB's OBD II rule wants silence from a digital input recognised as a fault of its own with a dedicated code, and U0113 is the generic slot for that situation.",["Fault in the CAN wiring or connectors carrying the emission-related frames","Sending module without power, ground or wake-up","Software or configuration mismatch after module replacement or update","Receiving controller internally faulty"],["MIL on","Engine on substitute values, possibly reduced power","Further U codes in other modules"],4,3,["U0441","U0100","U0073","U0401"],""],U0114:["Lost Communication With Four-Wheel Drive Clutch Control Module","U0114 says the controller of a four-wheel-drive clutch has gone quiet. Such a unit sets how much torque reaches the secondary axle by clamping a multi-plate coupling, as in Haldex-type on-demand drivelines whose later generations carry their own integrated electronics. It needs wheel speeds, engine torque and brake status from the bus and is usually missed by the engine, transmission or ABS controller.",["Clutch module without power or ground (fuse, connector near the rear axle)","Water or corrosion in the module connector exposed under the car","Chafed or open CAN lines to the rear of the vehicle","Clutch control module internally faulty"],["AWD/4WD warning in the cluster","Drive only on the primary axle, wheelspin on slippery roads","Possibly stability control warning"],2,2,["U0414","U0314","U0102","U011D"],""],U0115:["Lost Communication With ECM/PCM B","U0115 is set when a second engine or powertrain controller, ECM/PCM B, vanishes from the bus; U0100 belongs to unit A. What B stands for depends on the maker: GM's Saab 9-5 and 9-4X lists call it ECM 2, Mercedes-Benz assigns U011500 to its drivetrain control unit. In the 2021 S 580, the 48 V integrated starter alternator logged U0115 with U0168 because of its own software;",["Software fault in the reporting or the B controller (updates released)","Water ingress or corroded terminals on the bus or relay connectors","Controller B not powered or not woken up in time","ECM/PCM B internally faulty"],["MIL or engine/drive system warning","No start or no READY on hybrids","Often no driveability complaint when the code is software-related"],4,3,["U0100","U0101","U0401","U0073"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)‏ B"],U0116:["Lost Communication With Coolant Temperature Control Module","U0116 means a module no longer hears the coolant temperature control module, a separate controller for engines with electronically managed cooling. Depending on the design it may command electric pumps, map-controlled valves or fans and pass coolant status on to the engine controller. No manufacturer documents this code publicly;",["Cooling module without power or ground (fuse, relay, ground point in the engine bay)","Heat-damaged or corroded connector near the engine","Damaged CAN or LIN wiring to the module","Coolant temperature control module internally faulty"],["Engine temperature or cooling system warning","Cooling fan or electric pump running continuously","Reduced engine power as protection"],2,3,["U0456","P25AF","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת טמפרטורת נוזל קירור"],U0117:["Lost Communication With PTO Control Module","U0117 points to a lost link with the power take-off (PTO) control module, which engages and governs an engine-driven output for auxiliary equipment such as a tipper body, aerial bucket or recovery winch. CARB defines such a PTO unit and lets the engine controller pause monitor counters while it runs, so dependable PTO status on the bus matters for OBD bookkeeping.",["Faulty upfitter wiring or connector between chassis and PTO controller","PTO module without power or ground","Vehicle configuration expects a PTO module that is missing or not programmed","PTO control module internally faulty"],["PTO cannot be engaged or disengages","Elevated idle or remote engine speed control unavailable","Warning message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0465","P064B","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת PTO"],U0118:["Lost Communication With Fuel Additive Control Module","U0118 concerns the fuel additive control module, which on some diesel cars meters a fuel-borne catalyst from a separate tank into the fuel. The additive lowers the temperature at which trapped soot burns in the particulate filter from above 600 °C to roughly 350–450 °C. If the engine controller no longer receives this module, it cannot be sure that dosing continues, and the regeneration strategy loses its footing.",["Additive module unplugged or its fuse removed, e.g. after filter work","Corroded connector at the additive tank or module under the vehicle","Damaged CAN wiring to the additive module","Fuel additive control module internally faulty or not coded"],["MIL and particulate filter warning","Regeneration fails, filter loads up","Reduced power in later stages"],2,3,["U0467","P2584","P2585","U0100"],""],U0119:["Lost Communication With Fuel Cell Control Module","U0119 is the slot for losing the fuel cell control module, the controller that runs the hydrogen stack of a fuel cell vehicle: air compressor, hydrogen supply, humidity, stack cooling and the electrical output handed to the drive. Older code tables still label U0116–U0120 as reserved, so some scan tools show no text for it. No manufacturer documents the code publicly;",["Fuel cell controller without 12 V supply or ground","Damaged CAN wiring or connector between stack controller and vehicle controller","Software fault or missing update in one of the controllers","Fuel cell control module internally faulty"],["Fuel cell or drive system warning","Power limited to the buffer battery","Vehicle does not reach READY"],4,2,["U0468","U0293","U0111"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת תא דלק"],U011A:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Sensor Module A","U011A appears when the engine controller loses exhaust gas sensor module A, the electronics that heat and evaluate a wide-band oxygen probe (or a similar exhaust sensor) and send the result as bus data instead of analogue signals. Chrysler's bulletin 25-002-14, which replaces 25-003-13 and 25-004-13, lists it for 2010–2012 Ram 2500/3500 pickups with the 6.7 L Cummins among oxygen-sensor faults;",["Heat-stressed wiring or poor terminal contact at the sensor module connector","Sensor module without power or ground","Exhaust gas sensor module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Further oxygen-sensor codes stored","Particulate filter regeneration restricted"],2,1,["U016D","U041B","U029D","P2626"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן גזי פליטה‏ A"],U011B:["Lost Communication With Rocker Arm Control Module A","U011B covers the first rocker arm control module. On overhead-cam engines that shut cylinders down or change valve lift, a solenoid routes engine oil to unhook a pin coupling two rocker arms; the cam-driven arm then moves on its own and the valve stays shut. Where a maker hands this switching to a dedicated controller, the engine controller sets U011B when that unit's messages stop.",["Rocker arm module without power or ground","Oil-soaked or heat-damaged connector on the cylinder head","Damaged CAN wiring between module and engine controller","Rocker arm control module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Cylinder deactivation or valve lift switching inactive","Higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["U011C","U041C","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נדנד שסתומים‏ A"],U011C:["Lost Communication With Rocker Arm Control Module B","U011C is the partner of U011B for rocker arm control module B, for example the controller of the second cylinder bank or of a second group of switchable rocker arms where the task is split across two units. The engine controller expects cyclic status from it, such as the confirmed lock state per cylinder, and records U011C once those frames fail to arrive.",["Module B without power or ground","Contaminated or loose connector at the second cylinder head","Open or shorted CAN lines to module B","Rocker arm control module B internally faulty"],["MIL on","Affected cylinders remain in full-lift mode","Uneven running or higher consumption"],2,1,["U011B","U041D","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נדנד שסתומים‏ B"],U011D:["Lost Communication With All Wheel Drive Control Module","U011D signals a lost all-wheel-drive control module. In contrast to a single coupling controller (U0114) or a transfer case module (U0102), this unit manages an entire on-demand AWD system, deciding when and how much torque goes to the secondary axle, which in some cars is driven by its own electric motor. It draws wheel speed, steering and torque data from the bus and reports its state to stability control.",["AWD module without power or ground","Water or corrosion at the module connector near the rear axle","Chafed or open CAN wiring to the module","All-wheel-drive control module internally faulty"],["AWD warning lamp or message","Drive on one axle only","Stability control may also show a warning"],2,2,["U0114","U0102","U0414"],""],U011E:["Lost Communication With Throttle Actuator B Control Module","U011E reports that the controller for throttle actuator B has gone silent. Most engines use a single electronic throttle whose motor the engine controller drives itself; a separately housed throttle controller is covered by U0107. SAE reserves B for a second actuator with its own bus-connected driver, but which production engines use one is not documented, and no manufacturer describes U011E publicly.",["Throttle B controller without power or ground","Damaged CAN wiring or connector to the controller","Throttle actuator B control module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Limp-home mode with reduced power","Poor throttle response or idle only"],2,3,["U0107","U0308","U0408"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B"],U011F:["Lost Communication With V2X Module","U011F concerns the V2X module, the radio unit through which a car exchanges messages with other vehicles, roadside infrastructure, pedestrians' devices or the network (vehicle-to-everything), either via short-range DSRC/ITS-G5 or via cellular C-V2X. It passes alerts such as an approaching hazard or signal-phase information on to the driver and to assistance systems.",["V2X module without power or ground","Damaged bus wiring or connector, e.g. after roof or antenna work","Software or configuration fault in the V2X or gateway module","V2X module internally faulty"],["Connected traffic and hazard warnings unavailable","Possible service message in the cluster"],2,0,["U042A","U0198"],""],U0120:["Lost Communication With Starter/Generator Control Module","U0120 means the starter/generator control module, which drives an electric machine that can both crank the engine and produce electrical power, has dropped off the bus. Mitsubishi documents it for the Outlander PHEV (2018 and 2022): the hybrid controller (PHEV-ECU) sets U0120 when, after its supply has been within 10–16 V for more than 5 s, no frames from the generator control unit (GCU) housed within the power…",["Fault on the CAN lines between hybrid controller and generator control unit","Starter/generator control unit faulty (replacement if it stores U0120 itself)","Low 12 V supply or poor ground at the power electronics","Receiving hybrid controller faulty"],["MIL and hybrid or charging warning","Start-stop or engine start by the electric machine unavailable","Battery not charged while driving"],4,3,["U0469","P0A1E","U0293","U0111"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מתנע/גנרטור"],U0121:["Lost Communication With Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Control Module A","U0121 is stored by any listener that stops receiving the ABS/ESC module, so it often shows up in engine, transmission, cluster and gateway at once. GM treats it as Type C without MIL (Chrysler bulletins list it with MIL): the 2019 LTG engine table watches frames $0C1/$0C5 (0.5 s) and the 2025 TCM table waits over 10 s; while it is active, the ECM skips wheel-speed plausibility checks.",["Water ingress or corroded terminals at the ABS/EBCM connector","Poor ground point or supply fuse of the ABS module","ABS/ESC software that fails to wake up or restarts (update released)","Chafed or pinched CAN wiring","ABS control module internally faulty"],["ABS, ESC and brake warning lamps on","Speedometer or gear display erratic, several U codes","Reduced brake assistance or vehicle stays in Park","Start-stop and driver assistance unavailable"],2,2,["U0415","U0315","U0073","U0122","U0129"],""],U0122:["Lost Communication With Vehicle Dynamics Control Module","U0122 tells you that a networked controller, often the engine or hybrid ECU, has stopped receiving the cyclic frames of the stability control unit (ESC/VSC/ASC, usually combined with the ABS hydraulic unit).",["Missing fuse, supply or ground at the stability/ABS unit","Damaged CAN wiring or faulty gateway between the bus segments","Receiving controller software reports the loss too eagerly (update exists, e.g. Subaru)","Stability control module internally faulty"],["ESC, traction control and ABS warning lamps on","Stability and traction control unavailable","MIL on in some vehicles (engine or hybrid ECU stores the code)"],2,3,["U0316","U0416","U0121","U0129","U0126"],""],U0123:["Lost Communication With Yaw Rate Sensor Module","U0123 is stored when the stability controller or another listener misses the messages of a networked yaw rate sensor, the unit that measures how fast the car rotates around its vertical axis. Without that signal ESC cannot compare the actual turn with the steering input. No manufacturer explains U0123 in an openly accessible document; Ford merely lists it among the OBD codes of the 2014 Boss 302S.",["Loose or corroded connector at the yaw rate sensor (often under the centre console or seat)","Fuse, supply or ground of the sensor module missing","Damaged chassis CAN wiring to the sensor","Yaw rate sensor module internally failed"],["ESC and traction control warning lamps on","Stability control switched off for the rest of the trip","Often stored together with U0124 when both signals come from one housing"],2,0,["U0513","U0124","U0125","C0063","U0122"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן קצב סבסוב"],U0124:["Lost Communication With Lateral Acceleration Sensor Module","With U0124 a controller reports that the frames from the lateral acceleration sensor module have stopped. This sensor tells the stability system how strongly the vehicle is being pushed sideways in a bend; together with yaw rate and steering angle it lets ESC detect skidding.",["Corroded or loose plug at the acceleration sensor module","Power or ground of the sensor module interrupted","Chafed bus wires on the way to the sensor","Sensor module internally faulty"],["ESC/traction warning lamp lit","Stability control deactivated","Frequently logged together with U0123"],2,0,["U0536","U0123","U0125","U0122"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן תאוצה צידית"],U0125:["Lost Communication With Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A","U0125 concerns the inertial measurement unit that bundles yaw rate plus lateral and longitudinal acceleration on one bus node. GM uses the code widely: the 2019 XT4 brake controller (EBCM) flags a missing IMU frame after 0.1 s, the 2025 object-detection module after 0.05 s and then disables adaptive cruise; both are Type C without MIL.",["Wire broken inside the insulation or rubbed through near a chassis connector (GM X411)","Loose or corroded plug at the inertial sensor","Brake controller software that drops the sensor (reflash released)","Multi-axis sensor internally faulty"],["Service ESC / StabiliTrak message, traction and ABS lamps","Adaptive cruise control or all-wheel drive unavailable","Electric parking brake warning on some models"],2,0,["U0123","U0124","U0122","U0074","U0126"],""],U0126:["Lost Communication With Steering Angle Sensor Module","U0126 means the steering wheel angle sensor, usually mounted on the steering column, is no longer heard on the bus. ESC needs this value to know the path the driver intends. Mitsubishi's 2019 Outlander PHEV sets U0126 in the PHEV-ECU when it loses its CAN link to the wheel-angle sensor and demands calibration after a sensor swap.",["Loose or damaged connector or clock-spring harness at the steering column","Power or ground of the steering angle sensor missing","Module software reporting the fault wrongly or after remote start (update)","Steering angle sensor faulty; recalibration needed after replacement"],["ESC and traction lamps on, stability control inactive","Check engine lamp on some models","Lane or park assist functions unavailable"],2,1,["U0328","U0428","U0131","U0122","U0125"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן זווית הגה"],U0127:["Lost Communication With Tire Pressure Monitor Module","U0127 is logged when the tyre pressure monitoring module, the receiver that collects the radio signals of the wheel sensors, stops answering on the vehicle network. In the VW group the gateway (address 0019) stores it: Audi bulletin 2065474 for A6/A7/RS 6/RS 7 2019–2022 finds the module J502 unreachable and blames moisture entering through its pressure equalisation element; the fix is a new module and bracket.",["Moisture inside the TPMS module through its vent element","Pins, power or ground at the TPMS module connector faulty","Damaged bus wiring to the module"],["TPMS warning lamp or message in the cluster","Tyre pressures not displayed","Scan tool cannot reach the TPMS module"],2,0,["U0330","U0430"],""],U0128:["Lost Communication With Park Brake Control Module","U0128 signals that the electric parking brake controller has dropped off the bus. GM rates it very differently by node: the 2017 engine table waits 10 s for the park brake message and treats a miss as Type A (MIL at once), while the 2019 chassis controller (ICCM) needs only 1 s but files it as Type C without MIL; from model year 2018 GM folds this ICCM check into U0121.",["Fuse, supply or ground of the park brake module missing","Chafed or corroded bus wiring, often affecting several modules at once","Weak battery causing the module to drop out (stored code)","Controller software issue fixed by reprogramming","Park brake control module internally faulty"],["Service Parking Brake message or brake warning lamp","Electric parking brake does not apply or release","MIL on in vehicles where the engine controller stores it"],2,1,["U0317","U0438","U0135","U0136","U0129"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת בלם חניה"],U0129:["Lost Communication With Brake System Control Module A","U0129 points to the brake system control module A, in GM vehicles the OBD node with diagnostic ID 7E5. GM's 2019 LTG engine table checks frames $0C1, $0C5, $0D1, $1C6 and others every 500 ms (one of them 10 s) and needs two trips to set the MIL; the 2018 hybrid controller and the 2025 ECM treat it as Type A, the 2017 table as Special Type C. Stellantis calls the partner Brake System Control Module 1.",["Fuse, supply or ground of the brake control module faulty","Low battery or jump start leaving stored network codes (ECM update released)","Damaged or corroded CAN wiring to the brake module","Brake system control module internally faulty"],["MIL or service engine lamp plus brake/ESC warnings","Gear selection or stop-start blocked on some vehicles","Several other U codes stored at the same time"],2,3,["U0318","U0418","U0121","U0128","U0122"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ A"],U012A:["Lost Communication With Chassis Control Module A","U012A reports that chassis control module A is silent. The unit behind the letter A varies between brands; GM uses the code in several engine and transmission tables. The 2016 ECM for the L20 engine waits for message $4DB and logs a missing frame as Type B, so the MIL comes after two trips;",["Power, ground or fuse of chassis module A missing","Bus wiring or connector to the module damaged","Voltage dip leaving a stored code","Chassis module A internally faulty"],["MIL on in vehicles where the engine controller logs it","Chassis functions controlled by module A unavailable","Hard start or stalling if the module drives the fuel pump"],2,3,["U042B","U012B","U0073"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שלדה‏ A"],U012B:["Lost Communication With Chassis Control Module B","U012B is the counterpart to U012A for a second chassis controller, labelled B. No manufacturer documents U012B in an openly available source, so its exact job (air suspension, damping, steering or another chassis task) depends on the vehicle.",["Fuse, power or ground of chassis module B interrupted","Damaged bus line or connector to module B","Chassis module B internally faulty or not programmed"],["Chassis warning message in the cluster","Functions handled by module B (e.g. suspension) unavailable","Scan tool cannot reach module B"],2,0,["U042C","U012A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שלדה‏ B"],U012C:["Lost Communication With Active Vibration Control Module","U012C covers the controller that drives active engine mounts or inertial shakers to cancel engine vibration, for example in cars that switch off cylinders. Such a unit needs engine speed and load from the network to generate a counter-phase force; a Honda patent (US 10360893) describes a separate AVC control unit with actuators and acceleration sensors that adapts its cancelling output to engine rotation.",["Power or ground of the vibration control unit missing","Bus wire or connector damaged near engine or subframe","Active vibration control module internally faulty"],["Noticeable engine vibration at idle or in cylinder deactivation mode","Humming or booming noise in the cabin","Fuel saving mode may stay disabled"],2,0,["U042D","P0A14"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת רעידה פעילה"],U012D:["Lost Communication With Generator A Control Module","U012D is stored when the powertrain controller loses contact with the regulator of generator A. In many Ford models this is the smart alternator, which the PCM commands over a LIN line that it often shares with the active grille shutters; for that reason U012D usually shows up together with U0284/U0285 and U042E.",["Water or corrosion in a connector of the shared LIN line (grille shutter, C202)","LIN wire chafed and shorted to ground near an engine mount bracket","Generator regulator internally faulty or without supply","Powertrain controller LIN driver faulty"],["Check Charging System message or battery lamp","MIL on in some models","Battery discharges, voltage unstable","Active grille shutter codes stored as well"],2,1,["U042E","U012F","U0284","U0285"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גנרטור‏ A"],U012E:["Lost Communication With Camshaft Position Control Module","U012E applies to engines whose camshaft phaser is driven by its own electronic unit rather than an oil control solenoid, as with electric intake valve timing. Mitsubishi bulletin TSB-23-11-003 for the 2022 Outlander lists U012E next to U0101, U0122, U0146, U0155 and U042F as communication codes of the engine controller and links it in the warranty chart to the electric intake valve timing control module circuit.",["Power or ground of the electric valve timing module interrupted","CAN wiring or connector at the engine damaged by heat or oil","Camshaft position control module internally faulty"],["MIL on","Reduced power and poorer response, especially at low engine speed","Rough idle or higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["U042F","P0010","P0011","P0013"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מצב גל זיזים"],U012F:["Lost Communication With Generator B Control Module","U012F is reserved for vehicles with a second generator, labelled B, whose regulator or control electronics talk to the powertrain or hybrid controller over a bus. That can be a second alternator on heavy-duty trucks or a further motor-generator in a hybrid drive. No manufacturer explains U012F in an open document;",["Wet or corroded connector in the bus line to generator B","Fuse, power or ground of the generator B electronics missing","Bus wire chafed against engine or bracket","Generator B regulator or control module faulty"],["Charging system warning","Battery voltage falls during driving","Hybrid system warning or reduced electric drive on hybrids"],2,0,["U012D","U0120"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גנרטור‏ B"],U0130:["Lost Communication With Steering Effort Control Module","U0130 is logged when a controller on the network stops hearing the steering effort control module, which varies how much assistance the driver gets at the wheel, usually depending on road speed.",["Fuse, supply or ground of the steering effort module missing","Damaged CAN wiring or loose connector at the steering module","Module configuration or software not matched after a repair (e.g. Ford after HV battery replacement)","Steering effort module internally faulty"],["Steering system warning lamp or message","Steering feels heavier or no longer adapts to speed","Further communication codes stored in several modules"],2,0,["U0319","U0131","U0126","U0420"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מאמץ היגוי"],U0131:["Lost Communication With Power Steering Control Module A","U0131 means a listener on the bus has missed the cyclic frames of power steering control module A, normally the electric steering unit on rack or column. GM documents several receivers: the ECM of 2019 models flags it after 10 s without message $1E5 as a Type C, emissions-neutral fault and then stops basing auto-stop decisions on steering angle;",["High-current fuse, supply or ground of the steering module open (e.g. Ford mega fuse F2)","Chafed or damaged harness on the bus or wake-up line (e.g. Jeep Cherokee, GM circuit 5986)","Steering module software, fixed by an update (Ford Super Duty 2020)","Power steering control module internally failed"],["Reduced or no steering assist, heavy steering","EPS or steering fault message in the cluster","Adaptive cruise control switched off (GM)","Check-engine lamp on some vehicles (e.g. Jeep)"],2,3,["U0420","U0320","U0126","U0130","U0134"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת הגה כוח‏ A"],U0132:["Lost Communication With Suspension Control Module A","U0132 is set when a module stops receiving suspension control module A, the controller for air springs, ride height or damping. GM names the K5 automatic level control module of 2021 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban and Yukon with air suspension: it goes silent, a leveling or headlamp service message comes up, and removing two fuses for a few minutes revives it (PIT5795).",["Suspension module locked up, recovers after a power cycle (GM PIT5795, Bentley)","Suspension module software, fixed by an update (FCA Ram, Audi J775)","Fuse, supply or CAN wiring of the suspension module faulty","Suspension control module internally failed"],["Air suspension or leveling warning in the cluster","Ride height control or headlamp leveling inoperative","MIL on some vehicles (e.g. Ram heavy duty)"],2,1,["U0421","U0321","U0139","U0133"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מתלים‏ A"],U0133:["Lost Communication With Active Roll Control Module","U0133 indicates that the active roll control module, which drives hydraulic or electromechanical anti-roll bars to reduce body lean in corners, no longer answers on the bus. No manufacturer publicly ties U0133 to that module: Saab's 2011 9-5 list uses the number for its air suspension control module instead, so older vehicles may interpret it differently.",["Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the roll control module faulty","Software of master and stabiliser units not compatible after a replacement (Bentley TPI 2055643)","Roll control module internally faulty"],["Chassis or suspension warning lamp","More body roll when cornering","Sport or dynamic driving modes unavailable"],3,0,["U0434","U0132","U0139"],""],U0134:["Lost Communication With Power Steering Control Module - Rear","U0134 is stored when a controller loses contact with the rear power steering control module, the actuator unit of a rear-wheel or four-wheel steering system. Such systems turn the rear wheels by a few degrees, opposite to the front ones at low speed for a smaller turning circle and in the same direction at higher speed for calmer lane changes. No manufacturer explains U0134 in a publicly available document.",["Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the rear steering module faulty","Corroded or wet connector at the rear axle actuator","Rear steering control module internally faulty"],["Steering system warning lamp or message","Larger turning circle, rear wheels no longer steer"],3,0,["U0435","U0131","U0126"],""],U0135:["Lost Communication With Differential Control Module - Front","U0135 reports that the front differential control module has dropped off the network. Such a module operates an electronically controlled clutch pack or locker in the front axle, either to move torque from one front wheel to the other or to lock both for traction off road. No manufacturer documents U0135 in public;",["Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the front differential module faulty","Water or corrosion in the connector near the front axle","Front differential control module internally faulty"],["4WD, locker or traction warning lamp","Front locker or torque vectoring not available"],3,0,["U0436","U0136","U0114","U0102"],""],U0136:["Lost Communication With Differential Control Module - Rear","U0136 is set when a listener misses the rear differential control module, which operates an electronic limited-slip or twin-clutch rear drive unit. GM's 2019 tables document it in the ECM of the Cadillac XT4 (LSY engine): if message $1CF from the rear drive module stays absent for 10 s while bus A is active and supply exceeds 11 V, the ECM stores U0136 as a Type B fault, so the MIL comes on after two trips.",["Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the rear drive module faulty","Corroded or damaged connector at the rear axle, exposed to spray water","Rear differential control module internally faulty"],["AWD or rear differential warning","Car drives with front-wheel drive only, less traction","MIL after two trips on GM vehicles"],3,1,["U0437","U0135","U0114"],""],U0137:["Lost Communication With Trailer Brake Control Module","U0137 means the trailer brake control module, which energises a towed trailer’s electric brakes in step with the tow vehicle's braking, is missing on the bus. Ford uses the code widely: on 2022 F-150 trucks without that module the ABS unit may store U0137 by mistake, and it can then be ignored (SSM 50418);",["Trailer or ABS module software, fixed by reprogramming (Ford SSM 53236, 50418)","Improperly seated connector, damaged harness or water intrusion at the module (FCA 9004253)","Module retrofitted or configured incorrectly (dealer-installed tow package)","Trailer brake control module internally faulty"],["Trailer brake fault message in the cluster","Trailer brakes not applied or gain control inoperative","Park assist disabled on some Ram trucks"],2,0,["U0438","U0121","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת בלם גרור"],U0138:["Lost Communication With All Terrain Control Module","U0138 is logged when another module no longer receives the all-terrain control module, the unit behind the selector that lets the driver pick a terrain or drive mode such as snow, sand or mud and then adapts traction control, throttle response and shift points. Ford lists U0138 in the OBD code tables of its 2014 vehicles and marks it as available in all three self-test modes, without an entry in the lamp column.",["Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the terrain module faulty","Loose or corroded connector at the module or the mode selector","All-terrain control module internally faulty"],["Terrain or drive mode cannot be selected","4WD or traction control warning lamp"],2,0,["U0439","U0102","U0114"],""],U0139:["Lost Communication With Suspension Control Module B","U0139 reports lost contact with suspension control module B, at GM the semi-active damping system (SADS). GM's 2025 tables let the ECM watch two SADS messages, $035 with a 10 s limit and $364 with 325 ms, and set U0139 as Type B with the MIL after two trips; the EBCM treats missing damper frames for 250 ms as Type C.",["Suspension module software locks up, recovers after a fuse reset (GM PIT6007)","High resistance or open in the module wake-up line (GM circuit 5986)","Fuse, supply, ground or CAN wiring of the damping module faulty","Suspension control module B internally faulty"],["Check-engine lamp, often without any other symptom (GM)","Service Suspension message, adaptive damping inactive","Harsher or softer ride than usual"],2,1,["U043A","U0132","U0133"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מתלים‏ B"],U013C:["Lost Communication With Accelerator Pedal Module","U013C applies to an accelerator pedal module that reports over a data bus instead of analog sensor lines. In a drive-by-wire system the pedal module carries the driver's torque request to the engine or drive controller, so that controller has to fall back to a safe state as soon as the pedal messages disappear. No manufacturer documents U013C publicly;",["Loose or corroded connector at the pedal module (footwell moisture)","Supply, ground or bus wiring of the pedal module faulty","Accelerator pedal module internally faulty"],["No response to the accelerator, engine stays at idle","Reduced power warning","MIL on depending on the manufacturer"],2,3,["U043D","P2122","P2127","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול דוושת גז"],U013D:["Lost Communication With Vacuum Sensor A","U013D stands for lost communication with vacuum sensor A, a networked sensor that reports the vacuum in the brake booster or a vacuum reservoir. Engines with little manifold vacuum, such as turbocharged direct-injection units, and hybrids use this value to switch on an electric vacuum pump or to throttle the engine so the brake assist stays sufficient. No manufacturer documents U013D in public;",["Loose or corroded connector at the vacuum sensor on the booster","Supply, ground or bus wiring of the sensor faulty","Vacuum sensor A internally faulty"],["Brake booster or brake assist warning","Electric vacuum pump runs constantly or start-stop disabled","MIL on depending on the manufacturer"],2,1,["U043E","U013E","P0556","P0557"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן ואקום‏ A"],U013E:["Lost Communication With Vacuum Sensor B","U013E concerns vacuum sensor B, the second networked vacuum sensor in vehicles that measure at more than one point, for example in the booster chamber and in a separate reservoir, or that read a redundant value. The receiving module, typically the engine or brake controller, sets the code when the frames of this sensor stop arriving.",["Loose or corroded connector at vacuum sensor B","Supply, ground or bus wiring shared with sensor A faulty","Vacuum sensor B internally faulty"],["Brake system or brake assist warning","Often stored together with U013D when both sensors share wiring"],2,1,["U043F","U013D","P0558"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן ואקום‏ B"],U013F:["Lost Communication With Pedestrian Alert Control Module","U013F reports that the pedestrian alert control module has gone silent. Electric and hybrid cars need it to produce a warning sound at low speed, because they are otherwise almost inaudible; FMVSS 141 in the US and UN R138 in Europe make such a sound mandatory.",["Water or corrosion at the module, a speaker or their connectors","Supply, ground or LIN/CAN wiring of the module faulty","Pedestrian alert control module internally faulty"],["No warning sound when driving slowly","Pedestrian alert fault message in the cluster"],2,0,["P0DED","P0DEE","P0DEF","U0140"],""],U0140:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module","U0140 is among the most frequent network codes: a listening controller misses the frames of the body control module, which handles lights, locks, wipers and often the power mode that wakes other units. The code sits in the listener, not in the BCM. GM watches it in many nodes;",["BCM fuse, power feed or ground missing or corroded","Chafed bus line or loose, wet connector between BCM and the listening modules","Weak battery, jump start or voltage dip leaves a stored history code","BCM or listener software or configuration out of date (Ford SSM 47040, FCA 18-013-22)","BCM internally faulty"],["Lights, central locking, wipers or interior lamps misbehave or fail","Radio, climate controls or gauges blank or erratic","Same code stored in several modules at once","MIL on in some vehicles (GM 2025 Type B, FCA PCM)"],2,1,["U0141","U0142","U0143","U0144","U0145","U0422"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב"],U0141:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module A","U0141 names the first of several body controllers. Unlike U0140, which stands for the single main BCM, the letter suits cars that spread body tasks over more units, and each maker decides which one is A. Mitsubishi uses U0141 for an ETACS timeout: its body controller ETACS-ECU stops sending, and keyless entry, liftgate, airbag, brake and steering units log the loss;",["Power, fuse or ground of body module A missing","Software of module A or of the listener needs updating (Audi J393, FCA PCM)","Bus wire or connector to module A damaged or loose","Body module A internally faulty"],["Keyless entry, liftgate or other body functions inoperative","Ignition cannot be switched on (Audi e-tron case)","MIL or several warning lamps on","Code stored in many modules at once"],2,1,["U0140","U0142","U0143","U0144","U0145"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב‏ A"],U0142:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module B","U0142 reports that a second body controller, labelled B, has stopped talking. No maker explains publicly which unit carries this letter; depending on the design it may be a rear body module, a power distribution box or a comfort unit next to the main BCM (U0140) and module A (U0141).",["Module B without power: fuse, transport short pin or relay missing","Flat battery or battery disconnect leaves a history code","Damaged bus wire or loose connector to module B","Body module B internally faulty"],["Body functions handled by module B do not work","Scan tool cannot reach module B","Often only a stored code without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0140","U0141","U0143","U0443"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב‏ B"],U0143:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module C","With U0143 a listener reports that body controller C has gone quiet. The letter only means a third body unit; its role is set by the maker. Ford is the one maker found using the code publicly: on the 2021 F-150 the trailer module stores U0143:87, the suffix marking a missing message, because of software parameters in that module.",["Software parameters in the listening module (Ford F-150 trailer module)","Power, fuse or ground of module C missing","Bus line or connector to module C damaged","Body module C internally faulty"],["Often none; code found only during a scan","Functions of module C (for example trailer-related outputs) unavailable","Scan tool cannot reach module C"],2,0,["U0140","U0141","U0142","U0444"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב‏ C"],U0144:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module D","U0144 is logged by one or more control units that no longer receive the cyclic messages of the body controller J2012 calls Body Control Module D. In GM's network logic every node broadcasts a state-of-health message with ignition on; if it stays away while the supply is between 9 and 16 V, the listeners store a code naming the silent unit, not themselves.",["Fuse, power or ground of the body module D missing","Chafed bus wire or loose, wet connector on the way to module D","Weak battery or voltage dip, so the module drops off the bus (history code)","Body module D internally faulty or not programmed"],["Body functions handled by module D (locks, lighting, seats) do not respond","Scan tool cannot reach module D","Same code stored in several other modules"],2,0,["U0140","U0141","U0142","U0143","U0145"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב‏ D"],U0145:["Lost Communication With Body Control Module E","U0145 means the network has lost contact with the body controller J2012 labels E. Receiving modules expect its periodic messages; GM's generic logic sets such a code when a supervised message carrying the sender's availability fails to arrive at 9-16 V.",["Loose, spread or pushed-out terminal in the bus harness (Stellantis case)","Open or short on the LIN/CAN line to module E","Power or ground of module E missing","Body module E or BCM internally faulty"],["Individual body functions such as lights or locks inoperative","Code appears together with U0140 in several modules","Fault comes and goes when the harness is moved"],2,0,["U0140","U0141","U0142","U0143","U0144"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מרכב‏ E"],U0146:["Lost Communication With Serial Data Gateway Module A","U0146 means the first gateway, the node that routes messages between bus segments, is silent; GM calls it serial data gateway module, Ford, Audi and GM's tables just Gateway A. GM's 2019 ECM expects message $3CF at least every 10 s with the battery above 11 V and treats a gap as Type B, so the MIL lights if it recurs on a second trip.",["Gateway software hangs and stops routing although powered (GM PIT5586G, Audi ICAS)","Bent, backed-out or loose terminals at the gateway connectors","Gateway fuse, power or ground missing","Gateway module hardware faulty"],["Instrument cluster gauges dead or fluctuating","No crank, no start or stalling","Many U-codes in several modules and multiple warning messages","MIL on (GM Type B)"],2,1,["U0147","U0148","U0149","U0150","U0447"],""],U0147:["Lost Communication With Serial Data Gateway Module B","U0147 points to a second gateway, B. Large vehicle networks often use more than one routing node, for example a central gateway plus a separate unit that connects the car to the outside world.",["Power, fuse or ground of gateway B missing","Bus wiring or connector to gateway B faulty","Telematics unit acting as gateway B faulty or in a fault state (FCA)","Gateway B software hangs after an update or voltage dip"],["Connected services, emergency call or remote app functions unavailable","Modules behind gateway B not reachable with a scan tool","Further codes such as radio communication or antenna faults"],2,0,["U0146","U0148","U0149","U0150","U0448"],""],U0148:["Lost Communication With Gateway C","U0148 reports that the third gateway, Gateway C, has gone silent. A gateway links separate bus segments (CAN, LIN, Ethernet) and forwards messages between them, so when it drops out, every module behind it disappears too. GM's procedure for U0100-U02FF explains the mechanism: listeners expect a periodic state-of-health message and log the missing sender once it fails to arrive at 9-16 V.",["Fuse, power or ground of gateway C missing","Damaged bus wiring or corroded connector at gateway C","Gateway C software fault or incomplete programming","Gateway C internally faulty"],["Several modules behind the gateway unreachable at once","Many U-codes stored across the vehicle","Multiple warning lamps or messages in the cluster"],3,2,["U0146","U0147","U0149","U0150"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שער תקשורת (Gateway)‏ C"],U0149:["Lost Communication With Gateway D","U0149 names Gateway D as the module whose messages no longer arrive. Vehicles with several gateways split the network into domains, and each gateway routes traffic between its own bus segments; losing D therefore cuts off the domain it serves.",["Gateway D without power or ground","Open or shorted bus wiring, wet or corroded connector at gateway D","Low battery voltage or battery disconnect (history code only)","Gateway D internally faulty"],["Group of modules in one domain does not answer","Many U-codes stored at the same time","Functions of the cut-off domain inoperative"],3,2,["U0146","U0147","U0148","U0150"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שער תקשורת (Gateway)‏ D"],U014A:["Lost Communication With Battery Energy Control Module C","U014A concerns a third battery energy control module, C. Hybrid and electric vehicles use such units to watch cell voltages, temperatures and state of charge and to protect the pack; distributed or modular designs give several sub-packs their own controller, which is where letters beyond A and B come in. No manufacturer documents U014A publicly.",["Low-voltage supply, fuse or ground of battery module C missing","Bus wiring or connector inside or at the battery pack damaged or corroded","Moisture or coolant in the pack affecting module C","Battery module C internally faulty or not programmed"],["Hybrid or EV system warning, reduced power","Charging refused or stopped","Vehicle may not enter ready mode"],4,3,["U0111","U0112","U014C","U044B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ C"],U014B:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charging Module","U014B covers the vehicle-side controller of a wireless charging system. Inductive charging transfers energy without a plug, through a coil in a ground pad and a receiving coil under the car; the SAE J2954 standard, finalised in 2020, defines power classes of 3.7, 7.7 and 11 kW and relies on resonant coupling with about 85 percent efficiency.",["Supply, fuse or ground of the inductive charging module missing","Wiring or connector to the underbody receiver damaged by water, salt or impact","Software of module and charge controller not matching","Inductive charging module internally faulty"],["Wireless charging does not start or stops","Charging warning message, cable charging still works","Module not reachable with a scan tool"],4,0,["U044C","U0111","U014A","U014C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול טעינה אינדוקטיבית סוללת מתח גבוה"],U014C:["Lost Communication With Battery Energy Control Module D","U014C is the fourth slot in the battery controller family and points at module D. Such a letter is only needed where a pack is split into many sub-packs with their own monitoring boards, or where a vehicle carries an extra battery, for example a second traction pack or a separate 48 V unit, each reporting to a master controller. The master or the hybrid controller logs U014C once D's frames stop.",["Supply or ground of battery module D missing","Internal pack communication line or connector to D faulty","Battery module D internally faulty","Master controller configured for a module D that does not match"],["Battery or hybrid system warning","Reduced drive power or no ready mode","Charging not possible"],4,3,["U0111","U0112","U014A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ D"],U014D:["Lost Communication With Mirror Control Module B","U014D concerns the second networked mirror unit. Modern mirrors carry motors for adjustment and folding, a heating element, auto-dimming glass, turn-signal repeaters or blind-spot lamps, and the electronics for them often sit on the bus as their own node. J2012 provides two such units, and the receiver, usually the body or door controller, stores U014D when unit B stops replying.",["Broken wire in the flexing harness between body and door","Fuse, power or ground of mirror module B missing","Vehicle configuration expects a mirror module that is not fitted (FCA case for module A)","Water ingress or impact damage in the mirror housing"],["Mirror adjustment, folding or heating inoperative on one side","Blind-spot or turn-signal lamp in the mirror dark","Often no other effect; code found during a scan"],2,0,["U0213","U044F","U0514"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מראה‏ B"],U014E:["Lost Communication With Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module B","U014E concerns a second inertial sensor module, B. Such a unit combines accelerometers and gyroscopes, measures turning rate and acceleration across and along the car, and sends the values over the bus. A second module typically appears where functions need redundant or separately mounted motion data, for instance brake-by-wire, driver assistance or rollover detection alongside the stability system.",["Connector or wiring of sensor module B corroded or broken","Power or ground of module B missing","Sensor module B internally faulty","Receiving controller software not matching module B"],["Stability control or traction warning on","Driver assistance such as adaptive cruise unavailable","Normal braking unaffected"],2,0,["U0125","U0123","U0124"],""],U0150:["Lost Communication With Gateway E","U0150 is the last code of the gateway block and points at Gateway E. Gateways are central nodes that connect bus systems of different speed and type and forward only the messages each side needs. When E stops sending, the modules that expect its traffic log U0150, the way GM's U0100-U02FF procedure describes for any silent sender: a supervised periodic message is missing although supply voltage is in range.",["Gateway E fuse blown or ground loose","Bus line to gateway E chafed or connector corroded","Gateway E software fault, update or reprogramming needed","Gateway E internally faulty"],["Modules routed through gateway E not reachable by the scan tool","Several functions fail together","Warning messages in the instrument cluster"],3,2,["U0146","U0147","U0148","U0149"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שער תקשורת (Gateway)‏ E"],U0151:["Lost Communication With Restraints Control Module","U0151 means the airbag control module, which reads crash sensors and fires airbags and belt pretensioners, no longer reaches a listener. Names vary: GM and Saab say sensing and diagnostic module, FCA occupant restraint controller, Honda SRS unit. GM's 2025 ECM allows most of its messages a gap of about 10 s and rates the loss Type C without MIL; the brake controller reacts after 100 or 250 ms, also Type C.",["Airbag module fuse, ground or connector faulty (often under the seat or centre console)","Airbag control module internally failed (Honda Accord 2008-10)","Airbag module software needs updating (Dodge Charger 2024)","Another node blocks the bus, for example a faulty head-up display (Mazda CX-3)"],["Airbag warning lamp stays on","Airbags may not deploy in a crash if the module has failed","Several warning lamps or MIL on (Dodge Charger 2024)","Scan tool cannot communicate with the airbag module"],4,1,["U0152","U0153","U0154","U0452"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מערכת הריסון"],U0152:["Lost Communication With Side Restraints Control Module - Left","U0152 is the left-hand partner of U0153: a separate controller for the side restraints on the left no longer sends. In most cars side impacts are detected by satellite sensors in sills, B- or C-pillars that feed the central airbag unit; Bosch, for example, mounts its peripheral acceleration sensors on the left and right of the body and links them over the PSI5 sensor interface.",["Connector under the left seat or in the pillar loose or corroded","Power or ground of the left side module missing","Water ingress at the sill or door damaging wiring or module","Left side restraints module internally faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side or curtain airbag possibly not ready","Code stored in the main airbag module"],4,0,["U0151","U0153","U0154","U0453"],""],U0153:["Lost Communication With Side Restraints Control Module Right","U0153 means the airbag system no longer hears from the separate control module for the right-side restraints. Some vehicles split the job: a central airbag unit plus side units that evaluate side impact sensors and fire side or curtain bags. When the right unit's periodic messages stop, the receiving modules store U0153, in the same way GM's U0100-U02FF logic treats any silent node.",["Loose or corroded connector at the right side module (B-pillar or under the seat)","Power or ground of the right side module missing","Bus wiring damaged after seat or trim work","Right side restraints module faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side or curtain airbag may not deploy","Scan tool cannot reach the right side module"],4,0,["U0151","U0152","U0154"],"אבדה התקשורת עם ימני מודול בקרת מערכת הריסון צד"],U0154:["Lost Communication With Restraints Occupant Classification System Module","U0154 is stored when the occupant classification module goes silent. This unit evaluates sensors in the front passenger seat, such as a weight mat or pressure bladder, and tells the airbag controller whether the seat is empty, holds a child seat or an adult, so that the passenger airbag can be suppressed or allowed.",["Connector under the passenger seat loose, damaged or pulled during seat work","Power or ground of the classification module missing","Classification module or seat sensor internally faulty","Network wake-up timing or software issue (Mercedes-AMG 2023)"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag on/off indicator wrong or flashing","Passenger airbag deactivated or in a default state"],4,0,["U0151","U0152","U0153","U0455"],""],U0155:["Lost Communication With Instrument Panel Cluster (IPC) Control Module","U0155 says a listener no longer receives the instrument cluster, which shows speed and warnings and on many cars also produces chimes and turn-signal ticks. The cause is not always the cluster: on 2017 GM full-size trucks and SUVs several modules logged U0155 when the serial data gateway hung, so dead gauges came from the gateway (PIT5586G). The code can also trigger the MIL.",["Cluster fuse, ground or connector behind the dash faulty","Gateway hangs and stops forwarding cluster messages (GM PIT5586G)","Software of another module causes false loss of communication (Honda 21-021, Ford SSM 49218)","Instrument cluster internally faulty"],["Gauges dead, frozen or sweeping","No chimes or turn-signal ticking","MIL on in some vehicles (Honda 2021-22, Ford Explorer 2020)","Several warning lamps and codes in many modules"],2,1,["U0423","U0156","U0140","U0146"],""],U0156:["Lost Communication With Information Center A","U0156 concerns information center A, the display and infotainment unit that shows messages, audio, navigation or vehicle settings. Two makers document the code. Mazda calls the partner the connectivity master unit, its infotainment head unit: on 2019-20 Mazda3 and CX-30 the vehicle and body controllers store U0156:00 with an in-vehicle network malfunction message (SA-029/20), and on 2024-25 CX-90 and CX-70 the…",["Supply fuse of the unit missing or not fully seated (Mazda SA-040/24)","Infotainment unit internally faulty, for example memory chip (Volvo TJ 25872)","Infotainment software hangs or needs an update","Bus wiring or connector behind the dash faulty"],["Center display black, no audio or navigation","Network malfunction or several warning messages in the cluster","Climate or vehicle settings that run through the screen unavailable"],2,0,["U0157","U0457","U0155","U0158"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מרכז מידע‏ A"],U0157:["Lost Communication With Information Center B","U0157 is set when the second information display, Information Center B, stops transmitting on the vehicle bus. J2012 provides two such driver information displays, A (U0156) and B, separate from the instrument cluster (U0155) and the head-up display (U0158); which screen counts as B is up to the manufacturer.",["Display unit B without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Bus line or connector behind the dashboard damaged","Display software hang or failed update","Information Center B internally faulty"],["Secondary display dark, frozen or showing no data","Messages normally shown on display B missing","Code stored in several modules"],2,0,["U0155","U0156","U0158"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מרכז מידע‏ B"],U0158:["Lost Communication With Head Up Display","U0158 means the head-up display, which projects speed, navigation arrows or warnings into the windscreen, has stopped answering the module that supervises it, usually the instrument cluster. GM lists it in the Saab 9-5 (2011) U-code table and covers it in bulletin 22-NA-113: on 2020-2022 Cadillac CT4/CT5 with RPO UV6 the cluster stores U0158 when LIN messages arrive at an awkward moment while the HUD enters standby,…",["HUD stuck in standby due to message timing, cured by cluster software (GM CT4/CT5)","Stored entry from transport/logistics mode on new vehicles (Stellantis)","HUD fuse, supply or ground interrupted","LIN/CAN line or connector under the dashboard faulty","Head-up display unit internally faulty"],["Head-up display blank or frozen","Brightness, height or page settings have no effect","Display returns after an ignition cycle"],2,0,["U0459","U0155","U0156","U0157"],""],U0159:["Lost Communication With Parking Assist Control Module A","U0159 reports that parking assist control module A, which evaluates the ultrasonic sensors and drives the distance warnings, has fallen silent. GM spells out the check for the brake module: the 2019 Cadillac XT4 EBCM (19OBDG03D) and the 2020 brake module tables (20OBDG03C) set it when the automatic-parking braking request is missing for more than 0.25 s, Type C, no MIL.",["Park assist module software fault, fixed by reprogramming (GM PIT5507E, 20-NA-099)","Modules on different software levels (Stellantis S2108000149)","Park assist module without power or ground","Harmless entry after remote start or wake-up (Ford, VW)","Bus line or connector in the bumper/rear area damaged"],["Park assist unavailable or Service Parking Assist message","Park assist switch cannot turn the system on or off","Code stored in brake module, cluster or BCM"],2,0,["U045A","U031D","U031E","U0129","U0121"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ A"],U015A:["Lost Communication With Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Control Module B","U015A concerns a second anti-lock brake controller, module B. Vehicles prepared for automated driving need braking that still works after a single fault, so suppliers pair two independent units, for example Bosch's iBooster with the ESP control unit.",["Brake module B without power or ground (own fuse in redundant layouts)","Bus line or connector to module B in the engine bay corroded or open","Brake modules on incompatible software after repair","ABS control module B internally faulty"],["Brake system or driver assistance warning in the cluster","Automated driving or adaptive cruise functions unavailable","Code stored in the primary brake controller"],4,2,["U0121","U045B","U031C","U0129","U015B"],""],U015B:["Lost Communication With Power Steering Control Module B","U015B is set when the second power steering controller, module B, stops sending. Redundant steering for automated driving splits the electronics into two paths so one can keep assisting if the other fails; Bosch describes such a fail-operational design with an electrical fallback giving roughly half the normal assist.",["Steering module B without power or ground (separate supply path)","Connector at the steering rack or column wet, loose or corroded","Steering modules not matched after replacement or update","Power steering control module B internally faulty"],["Steering system warning in the cluster","Lane centring or automated steering unavailable","Steering assist possibly reduced"],4,2,["U0131","U045C","U0320","U0126","U015A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת הגה כוח‏ B"],U015C:["Lost Communication With Automated Driving System Control Module A","U015C points to automated driving system control module A, the computer that fuses camera and radar data for adaptive cruise, lane centring and emergency braking. Stellantis documents it in detail. In 2024-25 Dodge Charger and Jeep Wagoneer S with Active Driving Assist (TSB 08-256-25 to 08-259-25), MIL plus U015C-00 and U045D-00 call for new software in the front long-range radar.",["Software in front radar or ADAS decision module outdated (Stellantis TSBs)","Ethernet cable routed too tight, connector pins loosened","ADS control module A without power or ground","ADS control module A internally faulty"],["Automatic Emergency Braking Unavailable message","Adaptive cruise and lane settings not stored between drives","MIL on (Stellantis)"],4,3,["U015D","U045D","U015E","U015F"],""],U015D:["Lost Communication With Automated Driving System Control Module B","U015D names automated driving system control module B. Where the driving assistance computer is split into two halves, each half and the navigation and motion module watch the other over Ethernet. Stellantis case S2508000095 for the 2026 Jeep Wagoneer lists U015D-00 in the CADM and in the GNMM, together with Ethernet link and time-sync faults. Replaced modules showed no defect;",["Ethernet harness too taut, pins pushed out or fretted (Stellantis S2508000095)","Harness clip in wrong position, connectors under strain","ADS control module B without power or ground","ADS control module B internally faulty"],["Blindspot Alert Unavailable message","Blind-spot lamps in the mirrors stay lit","Driver assistance features disabled intermittently"],4,2,["U015C","U045E","U015E","U015F"],""],U015E:["Lost Communication With Automated Driving System Interface Module A","U015E concerns interface module A, the link that passes commands from an automated driving computer to the base vehicle's brakes, steering and powertrain and reports their state back. Such interfaces belong to the act layer of the sense-think-act chain that Bosch uses to describe automated driving.",["Interface module A without power or ground","Bus or Ethernet connection to the interface damaged or strained","Interface and automation computer on mismatched software","Interface module A internally faulty"],["Automated driving mode cannot be activated","Takeover request or controlled stop during automated driving","Driver assistance warning in the cluster"],4,2,["U015F","U015C","U015D","U045F"],""],U015F:["Lost Communication With Automated Driving System Interface Module B","U015F is the companion code for automated driving system interface module B. A second interface lets a fail-operational design keep a path to the vehicle actuators when the first one drops out, which matters most above SAE level 2, where the system rather than the driver watches the road.",["Interface module B fuse, supply or ground faulty","Connector or line of the redundant bus path damaged","Module B not updated together with the other ADS modules","Interface module B internally faulty"],["Automated driving unavailable, redundancy fault message","Request to take over steering and braking","Code stored in the automation computer"],4,2,["U015E","U015C","U015D","U0460"],""],U0160:["Lost Communication With Audible Alert Control Module","U0160 is stored when the audible alert module, the unit that produces chimes for an open door, unfastened belt, key left in or lights on, drops off the bus. GM uses it: the Saab 9-5 (2011) U-code list calls the unit Chime Alarm Control Module, and by GM's generic procedure the code appears once the chime unit's cyclic status frame stays away while the supply is within 9 to 16 V.",["Chime module fuse blown or ground loose","Connector or bus line behind the dashboard damaged","Vehicle configured for a separate chime module that is not fitted","Audible alert module internally faulty"],["No chime for open door, belt or lights","Chime sounds continuously or at wrong times","Code stored in the BCM or cluster"],2,0,["U0461","U0155","U0140","U013F"],""],U0161:["Lost Communication With Compass Module","U0161 says the compass module no longer reports. In many vehicles the electronic compass sits in the interior mirror or the overhead console: a pair of perpendicular magnetic sensors measures the earth's field, and the module sends the heading to a display. A Gentex patent describes such a mirror compass and mentions output over the vehicle bus.",["Compass module or mirror without power or ground","Connector at the mirror or headliner loose, e.g. after windscreen replacement","Data line in the A-pillar or headliner damaged","Compass module or mirror electronics faulty"],["Compass heading missing or shown as dashes","Compass calibration not possible","Code stored in the cluster or overhead module"],2,0,["U0462","U0155","U0162","U0163"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מצפן"],U0162:["Lost Communication With Navigation Display Module","U0162 indicates that the navigation display, typically the screen unit of the head unit, no longer answers. Subaru documents it in two settings. TechTIPS 10/2015 describes a 2015 Legacy/Outback with Fujitsu Ten navigation that stored U0162 together with U0100, U0101 and U0122; the real cause was a wire not locked into the under-hood fuse box, which unseated the 30 A fuse feeding the IG2 relay.",["Supply interrupted, e.g. loose terminal at the fuse box (Subaru TechTIPS)","Software of the receiving module, e.g. rear radar control unit (Subaru 07-205-22)","Connector behind the head unit loose after radio work","Navigation display or head unit faulty"],["Navigation screen dark or not responding","Rear vehicle detection warning lamp on (Subaru)","Several communication codes stored at once"],2,0,["U0163","U0463","U016A","U0184"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול תצוגת ניווט"],U0163:["Lost Communication With Navigation Control Module","U0163 is logged when the navigation control module, the computer that works out position and route, stops communicating. In many cars this function is built into the head unit, in others it is a separate box behind the trim. Listeners such as the instrument cluster, a camera unit or the telematics module show turn arrows or a map on their own screens and therefore watch its messages;",["Navigation unit fuse, supply or ground faulty","Connector at the head unit or navigation box loose or corroded","Navigation software hang or failed map/software update","Navigation control module internally faulty"],["Navigation and route guidance unavailable","Turn arrows missing in the cluster or head-up display","Code stored in the cluster or other display modules"],2,0,["U0162","U0464","U016A","U0198"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ניווט"],U0164:["Lost Communication With HVAC Control Module","U0164 is stored by any module that stops hearing the HVAC control module, the unit that runs blower, flaps and temperature selection. GM documents two monitors in its 2025 tables (25OBDG03B): the body control module watches several HVAC frames and flags a gap longer than 12.5 s at 11-18 V, and the central gateway reacts after 6.5 s once a frame is overdue by 2.5 times its period;",["Loose or spread terminals at gateway or inline bus connectors","HVAC module without power or ground","Incomplete module configuration or hung module, cleared by battery reset (Ford)","HVAC control module faulty"],["Climate control panel dark or not responding","Blower, temperature or defrost stuck at last setting","Check engine light on some GM models after two trips","Code stored in several modules at once"],2,1,["U0165","U010F","U0424","U0324","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מיזוג אוויר"],U0165:["Lost Communication With HVAC Control Module - Rear","U0165 names a second climate unit, the rear HVAC control module, fitted in vans, minivans and large SUVs that heat and cool the back rows with their own blower and flaps. The code says this rear module has gone quiet on the network; the front unit is covered by U0164. No manufacturer documents U0165 publicly, and the GM/Saab and Ford code lists checked here skip it.",["Rear HVAC module without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Bus wiring to the rear unit chafed under trim or at sliding-door area","Vehicle coded for rear climate that is not fitted","Rear HVAC control module faulty"],["Rear climate controls without function","Rear blower stuck off or at one speed","Front climate keeps working normally"],2,0,["U0164","U0466","U0664","U010F"],""],U0166:["Lost Communication With Auxiliary Heater Control Module","U0166 reports that the auxiliary heater control module has stopped communicating. Such heaters, burning fuel or working electrically, warm the coolant or the cabin air before or during a drive and are common on diesels and cold-climate packages.",["Heater module fuse blown or ground corroded (often underbody mounting)","Corroded heater connector from road splash","Bus line to the heater damaged","Auxiliary heater control unit faulty"],["Auxiliary or parking heater does not start","Slow engine and cabin warm-up in cold weather","Code stored in the engine or climate controller"],2,0,["U0164","U0165","U0325"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גוף חימום עזר"],U0167:["Lost Communication With Vehicle Immobilizer Control Module","U0167 means the vehicle immobilizer control module, which checks the transponder in the key and then releases the engine controller, can no longer be heard on the bus. Since the key handshake cannot complete, the engine typically cranks without firing or does not crank at all. Ford's 2014 Boss 302S code list and the Saab 9-5 code list contain U0167.",["Immobilizer module or antenna ring without power or ground","Interrupted or faulty immobilizer software update (Triumph 2024)","Bus or connector at the steering column damaged","Immobilizer control module faulty"],["Engine cranks but does not start, or no crank","Immobilizer or key symbol flashes","Key not recognised"],3,0,["U0168","U0426","U0326","P0513","P0633"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אימובילייזר רכב"],U0168:["Lost Communication With Vehicle Security Control Module","U0168 points to the vehicle security control module, which handles anti-theft and key authorisation and in many layouts also hosts the immobilizer handshake. Chrysler shows the link: its 2011 field report names U0168 for the SKREEM/WCM, and bulletin 18-023-13 (Grand Voyager 2.8 L diesel 2012-2013) treats it as a sign of a failed ignition handshake that new PCM software fixes.",["Engine or security module software mishandles the key handshake (Chrysler, Jeep, Mercedes updates)","Security module without power or ground","Bus line or connector to the security module faulty","Security or keyless entry module faulty"],["No start or delayed start","Check engine light on (Jeep 4xe, Mercedes S 580)","Keyless entry, alarm or key detection not working"],3,1,["U0167","U0427","P0513","P0633"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אבטחת רכב"],U0169:["Lost Communication With Sunroof Control Module","U0169 is set when the sunroof control module drops off the vehicle network. This unit drives the motors for the glass panel and, where fitted, the sun blind, keeps track of their positions and provides the anti-pinch reversal. No manufacturer documents U0169 publicly; GM's U-code list and the bulletins in the NHTSA index do not contain it.",["Sunroof module fuse blown or ground loose","Water at module or connector from blocked roof drains","Headliner wiring or connector to the module damaged","Sunroof control module faulty"],["Sunroof does not open or close electrically","Comfort closing with the key no longer closes the roof","Roof positions or one-touch function lost"],2,0,["U046A","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גג שמש"],U016A:["Lost Communication With Global Positioning System Module","U016A covers the global positioning system module, the receiver that supplies position, speed and time to navigation, telematics and emergency-call functions. Ford uses the code: its 2014 Boss 302S code list includes it, and SSM 54351 explains that 2026 Transit vans built without a telematics control unit may log U016A in the module Ford calls SOBDMC, alongside U0146 in the ABS module.",["Module not fitted on this build, code without fault (Ford Transit 2026)","GPS or telematics unit without power or ground","Bus wiring or connector at the receiver faulty","GPS module faulty"],["Navigation shows wrong or no position","Telematics or emergency call reports location unavailable","Clock or compass no longer updated by satellite"],2,0,["U046B","U0163","U0146"],""],U016B:["Lost Communication With A/C Compressor Control Module","U016B appears when the control module of the electric A/C compressor, the inverter fed from the high-voltage battery in hybrids and EVs, stops talking to its partners. In GM's 2016 Volt table (16OBDG01) the engine controller watches frame $222 and fails after 10 s, Type B with MIL after two trips.",["Compressor unplugged while the bus was awake, stored code without real fault (GM 18-NA-096)","Compressor low-voltage harness chafed on axle shaft or bracket (GM PIC6609)","Compressor control module without 12 V supply or ground","Electric compressor inverter faulty"],["Air conditioning blows warm","Check engine or service high voltage message, charging possibly limited","Reduced battery cooling or charging power in heat"],4,1,["U046C","U032A","U010F","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן"],U016C:["Lost Communication With Fuel Pump Control Module B","U016C concerns fuel pump control module B, the second pump driver in vehicles with two pumps or two tanks; module A has U0109. Ford's 2020-2023 gasoline OBD summary watches pump B through its duty-cycle feedback line: a signal stuck at 0 % or 100 % sets U016C within 2-5 s at 11-16 V.",["Loose or corroded frame ground at the pump module (Ram G803A)","Fuse or relay for pump B or its driver open","Feedback or bus wiring between pump driver B and PCM damaged","Fuel pump control module B faulty"],["Check engine light on","Crank but no start, or stalling","Lack of power or rough running under load"],2,3,["U0109","U046D","U0310","P027A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת משאבת דלק‏ B"],U016D:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Sensor Module B","U016D refers to exhaust gas sensor module B, a second smart sensor unit in the exhaust that heats a probe, evaluates it and reports oxygen or NOx readings as bus data instead of an analog voltage. Module A has U011A. Which sensor counts as B depends on the maker, for instance the other bank or a probe further downstream behind an SCR catalyst.",["Sensor module connector or harness damaged by exhaust heat or corrosion","Sensor module without power or ground (fuse, relay)","Bus line to the module chafed under the vehicle","Sensor module B or integrated probe electronics faulty"],["Check engine light on","Readiness monitors for catalyst or exhaust sensors not complete","Diesel: SCR or emission warning, possibly reduced power"],2,1,["U011A","U046E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן גזי פליטה‏ B"],U0170:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor A","U0170 is the first slot in the J2012 block for remote restraint sensors: sensor A has gone silent for the airbag control unit or another listener. Chrysler follows that scheme. In the Jeep airbag tables it handed to NHTSA (Wrangler JK 2007-2010, Compass/Patriot MK, Liberty KK, Grand Cherokee WK and Commander XK 2008) U0170 is the up-front left satellite acceleration sensor, and B1B70 reports an internal fault of…",["Connector at the front satellite sensor unplugged or corroded, often after front-end repairs","Sensor A or its bracket damaged in a frontal knock","On GM vehicles (passenger presence module) chafed or pinched low-speed LAN wiring","Sensor input of the airbag control unit faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Early frontal crash detection on the left reduced (Chrysler)","On GM vehicles further U-codes in several modules at the same time"],4,0,["U0151","U0154","U0171","U0172","U0471"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ A"],U0171:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor B","U0171 says the airbag control unit receives nothing more from restraint sensor B. Chrysler documents it as the up-front right satellite acceleration sensor, the mirror image of U0170, in each Jeep airbag listing it supplied for investigation PE11-019, starting with the 2007 Wrangler; an internal defect of that unit is logged separately as B1B71. Front satellites of this kind sit inside the crumple zone.",["Connector of the right front sensor not reconnected after bumper or front-end work","Water or road salt in the sensor connector at the front","Front satellite sensor B damaged in a collision","Sensor line to the airbag unit open or shorted"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Frontal impact sensing on the right side relies on the central unit only","Code comes back immediately after clearing while the fault persists"],4,0,["U0151","U0170","U0172","U0472"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ B"],U0172:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor C","U0172 marks a lost link to restraint sensor C. Chrysler uses it for the first left side satellite acceleration sensor in the Jeep tables of NHTSA file PE11-019. The Wrangler JK has just this one sensor on each side, whereas Compass/Patriot, Liberty, Grand Cherokee and Commander add a second left unit reported as U0173.",["Water in the left footwell or sill area reaching the sensor connector","Connector disturbed during seat, carpet or trim removal","Left side satellite sensor failed after a side knock","Airbag control unit input or configuration faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side and curtain airbag deployment may be impaired","Fault can be intermittent with wet carpets or after rain"],4,0,["U0151","U0170","U0171","U0173","U0473"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ C"],U0173:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor D","U0173 tells that the airbag control unit no longer receives data from remote crash sensor D. Such satellite sensors sit in the crumple zone, doors or pillars and report acceleration in one or two axes so the control unit can judge direction and severity of an impact.",["Loose or corroded connector at satellite sensor D","Sensor line damaged, e.g. in the door or pillar area","Satellite sensor D failed (water ingress, impact)","Sensor input of the airbag control unit faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side impact detection on the affected side reduced","Code stays active until the sensor link is restored"],4,0,["U0151","U0170","U0171","U0172","U0174","U0175","U0176"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ D"],U0174:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor E","U0174 refers to restraint sensor E, the fifth remote crash sensor in J2012 lettering. No manufacturer documents U0174 publicly. Chrysler's Jeep tables in NHTSA file PE11-019 go from U0173 straight to U0175, so slot E is simply not used there.",["Connector at sensor E loose, wet or corroded","Airbag unit coded for a sensor E that is not fitted (e.g. after unit replacement)","Two-wire sensor line open or shorted","Crash sensor E internally failed"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Scan tool lists sensor E as not responding","Deployment paths depending on sensor E may be blocked"],4,0,["U0151","U0173","U0175","U0475"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ E"],U0175:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor F","U0175 is set when restraint sensor F stops reporting. Chrysler names it the right side satellite acceleration sensor 1 throughout the restraint code lists of the NHTSA probe PE11-019, from the 2007 Wrangler JK to the 2008 Grand Cherokee and Commander; its counterpart on the left is U0172, and B1B75 flags an internal defect of the sensor.",["Moisture in the right footwell or sill reaching the connector","Connector or line disturbed when the passenger seat was removed","Right side satellite sensor failed","Wrong sensor version or mounting orientation after replacement"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side and curtain airbag readiness reduced","Fault may appear only on bumpy roads (loose contact)"],4,0,["U0151","U0172","U0174","U0176"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ F"],U0176:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor G","U0176 points to restraint sensor G. In Chrysler's usage, as recorded in the NHTSA investigation PE11-019, it is the second right side satellite acceleration sensor. Of those Jeeps, only MK (Compass/Patriot), KK (Liberty), WK and XK (Grand Cherokee, Commander) carry it, together with its left twin U0173;",["Connector behind the rear side or pillar trim loose or damaged","Line to the rear right sensor pinched or chafed","Airbag unit configured for a second side sensor the vehicle does not have","Second right side sensor failed"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side impact detection for the rear right area reduced","Code stays active until sensor link or configuration is corrected"],4,0,["U0151","U0173","U0175","U0177","U0477"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ G"],U0177:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor H","U0177 is stored when crash sensor H, the eighth remote sensor of the restraint system in J2012 lettering, stops reporting to the airbag control unit. Remote acceleration or pressure sensors detect front, side or rear impacts early and feed the central unit that decides on deployment. No manufacturer documents U0177 publicly.",["Connector at sensor H loose, wet or corroded","Sensor wiring damaged by trim or body work","Crash sensor H failed","Airbag control unit input faulty or wrong configuration"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Impact detection in the zone of sensor H unavailable","Code returns immediately after clearing"],4,0,["U0151","U0170","U0176","U0178","U0179"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ H"],U0178:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor I","U0178 covers restraint sensor I, the ninth remote crash sensor; unlike many letter series, J2012 does use the letter I here. No manufacturer documents U0178 publicly. High sensor counts come mainly from combining sensor types: Bosch connects two or four door pressure sensors to the airbag unit in addition to the acceleration sensors on the body structure, so a four-door car can easily exceed eight satellites.",["Broken wire in the door hinge passage","Water inside the door at the sensor connector (failed vapour barrier)","Sensor I failed","Sensor interface of the airbag unit faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Fault may come and go with door movement","Impact detection in the zone of sensor I unavailable"],4,0,["U0151","U0177","U0179","U0479"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ I"],U0179:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor J","U0179 closes the J2012 block for remote restraint sensors and names sensor J, the tenth position (the letter I is used as well, see U0178). The airbag control unit checks that each connected satellite keeps sending; if sensor J falls silent, the unit stores U0179, switches on the airbag warning lamp and may disable the deployment paths that rely on it.",["Connector at sensor J loose or corroded","Open or shorted line between sensor J and the airbag unit","Crash sensor J failed, e.g. after a minor impact","Airbag control unit input faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Restraint deployment relying on sensor J may be disabled","Scan tool shows sensor J as not responding"],4,0,["U0151","U0170","U0177","U0178"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ J"],U017A:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor K","U017A is logged when restraint sensor K, the eleventh remote crash sensor, has stopped sending data to the restraints module. No manufacturer documents U017A publicly; the Chrysler Jeep lists in NHTSA file PE11-019 end at the sixth satellite. Why J2012 reserves so many slots becomes clear from supplier data: a current Bosch airbag control unit serves 12 PSI5 sensor interfaces, a premium version up to 18.",["Sensor K not reconnected after rear-end or boot floor repairs","Sensor line damaged along the rear body","Crash sensor K failed","Airbag unit configuration does not match the fitted sensors"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Restraint functions depending on sensor K may be disabled","Scan tool shows sensor K as absent"],4,0,["U0151","U0179","U017B","U047B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ K"],U017B:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor L","U017B means sensor L of the restraint system, the twelfth remote crash sensor in J2012 order, no longer answers. No manufacturer documents U017B publicly, so which component sits behind the letter depends on the car. One example of how sensor counts grow: airbag control units can also run pedestrian protection, fed by acceleration sensors or by a pressure tube in the front bumper.",["Sensor or its connector not refitted after bumper replacement","Sensor or wiring damaged by a minor front or side knock","Corroded connector in an exposed mounting position","Sensor L internally failed"],["Airbag or pedestrian protection warning on","Protective function assigned to sensor L disabled","Fault appears after body or bumper work"],4,0,["U0151","U017A","U017C","U047C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ L"],U017C:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor M","U017C is stored once restraint sensor M, the thirteenth remote crash sensor, falls silent. No manufacturer documents U017C publicly. For diagnosis it matters whether the code is current or only stored: according to the PSI5 working group, a brief drop in supply makes a sensor restart and send initialisation data first, so a loose contact can leave a history entry without a lasting fault.",["Intermittent contact at sensor M connector (history code)","Sensor not seated or sealed correctly after trim work","Sensor wiring chafed or open","Crash sensor M failed"],["Airbag warning lamp on or flickering","Code stored as history after the lamp went out again","Impact detection in the zone of sensor M unavailable while active"],4,0,["U0151","U017B","U017D","U047D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ M"],U017D:["Lost Communication With Restraints System Sensor N","U017D concerns restraint sensor N, the last of the fourteen sensor letters A to N; the two codes that follow belong to seat belt pretensioner modules. No manufacturer documents U017D publicly, and the Chrysler Jeep tables in NHTSA file PE11-019 never go past G. Bosch scales its premium airbag units to as many as 18 sensor inputs, so a fourteenth satellite is possible but rare.",["Connector at sensor N loose or corroded","Earlier wiring repair untwisted or with unsuitable connectors","Crash sensor N failed","Airbag unit expects a sensor N that is not installed"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Scan tool reports no response from sensor N","Restraint deployment relying on sensor N may be disabled"],4,0,["U0151","U017A","U017C","U047E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ N"],U017E:["Lost Communication With Seat Belt Pretensioner Module A","U017E reports that seat belt pretensioner module A no longer communicates. Such modules drive electric, reversible belt tensioners: Audi pre sense pulls the front belts tight by small motors when it senses emergency braking or skidding and releases them if no crash follows. On the 2015 A3, the airbag unit J234 runs the left and right tensioner modules J854/J855 over LIN; the pyrotechnic tensioners are separate.",["Connector at the belt retractor module in the pillar loose or damaged","New retractor with control module not coded or basic setting not done","Harness damaged or wrongly routed (Jeep JL, shifter area)","Software issue in the module or a listener such as the PCM (FCA 2021)"],["Warning message for pre-crash occupant protection","Belt no longer pre-tightened during emergency braking","Airbag lamp on; on some FCA models MIL as well"],4,0,["U0151","U017F","U047F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות‏ A"],U017F:["Lost Communication With Seat Belt Pretensioner Module B","U017F is the second pretensioner module code: module B has dropped off its link to the airbag unit. Audi documents it together with U017E00 in bulletin 2081251 for 2025-26 A5, A6, Q5 and Q6 e-tron models, where both codes accompany a proactive occupant protection warning and dealers are asked to file a case report.",["Retractor with control module replaced but not coded or basic-set","Supply or bus connector at module B loose","Pretensioner module B internally faulty","Bus line between airbag unit and module B damaged"],["Pre-crash protection fault message in the instrument cluster","Reversible belt tightening on one seat inoperative","Often stored together with U017E"],4,0,["U0151","U017E","U0480"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות‏ B"],U0180:["Lost Communication With Automatic Lighting Control Module","U0180 belongs to the automatic lighting control module, the unit that evaluates a light sensor and switches the headlamps on at dusk, in tunnels or with the wipers. Once it is silent, the auto-light feature can no longer be commanded.",["Light sensor or lighting module without power or ground","Moisture at connectors after rain or car wash (GM PIE0348)","Bus or LIN line to the windscreen sensor damaged","Automatic lighting module faulty"],["Automatic headlamps no longer switch on or off","Headlamps stay on as a default","GM Cadillac: no audio, chimes or turn-signal sound"],2,0,["U0481","U0181","U0182","U0183","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת תאורה אוטומטית"],U0181:["Lost Communication With Headlamp Leveling Control Module","U0181 says the module that controls automatic headlamp levelling has dropped off the bus. That module reads ride-height sensors on the axles and drives the actuator motors in the headlamps to keep the beam at the right angle under load.",["Levelling module without power or ground","Chafed harness or water in connectors or BCM area (GM Acadia/XT5)","Corroded connector at the module near the headlamp","Headlamp levelling module faulty or not coded"],["Headlamp beam height no longer adjusts","Headlamp or lighting warning in the cluster","Oncoming traffic dazzled or road poorly lit when loaded"],2,0,["U0180","U0182","U0183","U0140"],""],U0182:["Lost Communication With Lighting Control Module Front","U0182 is logged when the front lighting control module stops talking on the bus. This module drives front lamp functions such as swivelling or adaptive beam patterns. GM lists it as Lost Communication With Lighting Control Module - Front in the Saab 9-5 (2010-2011) U-code list.",["Front lighting module without power or ground","Corroded connector in the engine bay or headlamp area","Bus line to the module chafed or open","Front lighting module faulty"],["Adaptive or cornering light inoperative","Lighting warning lamp or message in the cluster","Front lamps fall back to a fixed default beam"],2,0,["U0180","U0181","U0183","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם קדמי מודול בקרת תאורה"],U0183:["Lost Communication With Lighting Control Module - Rear A","U0183 refers to rear lighting control module A, the unit that drives tail, brake, turn and in some designs reversing lamps at the back of the vehicle. A second rear unit, B, has U0252, the front module U0182. Such modules are found where LED rear lamps are switched and checked electronically, for example in a tailgate. No manufacturer documents U0183 publicly;",["Rear lighting module without power or ground","Wiring broken in the tailgate or boot lid hinge loom","Corroded connector at the rear lamp or module","Rear lighting control module A faulty"],["Tail, brake or turn lamps at the rear not working","Bulb or lighting warning in the cluster","Rear lamps in a fixed default mode"],2,0,["U0252","U0484","U0182","U0180"],""],U0184:["Lost Communication With Radio","U0184 is logged when the radio or infotainment head unit no longer answers on the bus; cluster, gateway, HVAC or amplifier store it, often several at once. GM bulletin 16-NA-115 (many 2014 GM models) reprograms the radio when it stays silent, shows a dark display or fails to wake up.",["Radio software hang or wake-up problem, fixed by reset or reprogramming (GM, Ford)","Spread or pushed-out terminals at radio or security gateway (Stellantis)","Vehicle still in transport mode (Ford)","Radio or head unit faulty"],["Radio dead, screen blank or no sound","Phone, reversing camera or voice control not available","U0184 stored in several modules"],2,0,["U0485","U0334","U0186","U0185","U0195"],"אבדה התקשורת עם רדיו"],U0185:["Lost Communication With Antenna Control Module","U0185 indicates that the antenna control module has stopped communicating. This unit, frequently an amplifier or tuner box near the rear screen, the roof fin or a bumper, conditions radio, TV, satellite or GPS signals and in some designs raises or lowers a motorised mast. U0185 has no public manufacturer documentation; neither the GM list nor the NHTSA bulletin index uses it.",["Antenna module without power or ground","Water ingress at roof fin or rear-screen amplifier","Bus wiring or connector to the antenna unit damaged","Antenna control module faulty"],["Poor or no radio reception","Satellite, TV or GPS reception lost","Power antenna does not move"],2,0,["U0486","U0184","U0258"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת אנטנה"],U0186:["Lost Communication With Audio Amplifier A","U0186 means the external audio amplifier A has dropped off the bus; the radio or cluster store it, and the speakers usually go quiet. GM PIC6153 (Volt 2016 with premium audio) warns against replacing the amplifier and asks to inspect its X1 connector, especially pin 4 (B+) and pin 8 (ground).",["Spread or backed-out terminals at amplifier or head unit connector (GM, Mazda)","Amplifier software stops bus communication, fixed by flash (Chrysler)","Amplifier fuse blown or ground loose","Audio amplifier A faulty"],["No sound or radio muted","Crackling or intermittent audio","Chimes or warning tones missing"],2,0,["U0487","U0262","U0184"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מגבר שמע‏ A"],U0187:["Lost Communication With Digital Disc Player/Changer Module A","U0187 opens the J2012 series for networked disc players and changers: module A is the main CD or DVD drive, while U0188 to U0190 cover B to D. In many older cars the changer sat apart from the head unit, in the glovebox, under a seat or in the trunk, and reported to it over a data line. U0187 has no public manufacturer documentation; GM lists no disc drives at all and the NHTSA bulletin index has no match.",["Disc unit A without power or ground","Data line or connector to the changer (glovebox, seat, trunk) damaged","Drive removed or head unit coded for a drive not fitted","Disc player/changer A faulty"],["CD or DVD source missing or not selectable","Disc cannot be loaded or ejected","Other audio sources work normally"],1,0,["U0188","U0189","U0190","U0488","U0184"],""],U0188:["Lost Communication With Digital Disc Player/Changer Module B","U0188 means the second networked disc player or changer, module B, no longer answers. Disc changers hold several CDs or DVDs and were often mounted apart from the radio, in the dash, a console or the boot, and linked to the infotainment bus. Receiving units set a lost-communication code once the expected periodic message of a node is missing, as GM's U0100-U02FF procedure explains for all such codes.",["Disc unit B without power or ground","Bus or connector to the changer (often in boot or console) damaged","Unit removed or vehicle coded for a device not fitted","Disc player/changer B faulty"],["Disc source B missing or not selectable","Discs not ejected or not played","Code stored in the radio or head unit"],1,0,["U0184","U0187","U0189","U0190"],""],U0189:["Lost Communication With Digital Disc Player/Changer Module C","U0189 covers the third disc player or changer on the bus, module C. Systems with more than one drive are found mostly in rear-seat entertainment or luxury setups, where a front unit and separate rear players feed different screens. The head unit or another listener stores U0189 once module C's cyclic messages stop arriving;",["Disc unit C fuse blown or ground loose","Connector or bus wiring to the rear player damaged","Vehicle coded for a third drive that is not fitted","Disc player/changer C faulty"],["Rear or third disc source unavailable","Rear screen shows no disc content","Code stored in the head unit"],1,0,["U0184","U0187","U0188","U0190"],""],U018A:["Lost Communication With Headlamp Leveling Control Module B","U018A covers headlamp leveling control module B. Cars with separate levelling electronics in each headlamp, or with a central controller plus lamp-side units, need a second address; U0181 is the first module. The electronics set the beam angle from ride-height sensor data so that load or pitch does not dazzle oncoming traffic, which LED and xenon lamps usually require.",["Levelling module B without power or ground","Corroded connector at the headlamp from moisture","Bus line to the headlamp damaged after a front-end repair","Headlamp levelling module B faulty or not coded"],["One headlamp no longer adjusts its beam height","Headlamp or lighting warning in the cluster","Uneven or very low beam pattern"],2,0,["U0181","U048B","U0180"],""],U0190:["Lost Communication With Digital Disc Player/Changer Module D","U0190 is the last code in the J2012 disc player block and names module D, a fourth networked drive or changer. When that unit goes silent, the modules expecting its periodic traffic store U0190; GM's procedure for U0100-U02FF adds that a code stored only in history after a flat battery or a module disconnected with the bus awake is not a reason to replace parts.",["Disc unit D without power or ground","History entry after flat battery or unit unplugged with bus awake","Connector or bus line to module D damaged","Disc player/changer D faulty"],["Disc source D missing","Magazine not loaded or ejected","Code stored in the head unit"],1,0,["U0184","U0187","U0188","U0189"],""],U0191:["Lost Communication With Television","U0191 means the television tuner has dropped off the vehicle network. J2012 simply calls it Television: a receiver for mostly digital terrestrial TV that hands the picture to the central display or to rear screens. GM fills the slot under that name in the Saab U-code lists of the 9-5 from 2010-2011 and the 9-4X from 2011; the NHTSA bulletin index has no matching entry.",["TV tuner without power or ground (fuse, connector)","History entry after flat battery or tuner unplugged with bus awake","Bus line or connector to the tuner damaged","TV tuner module faulty"],["TV source missing from the media menu","Black screen or no-signal message when TV is selected","Code stored in radio or display unit"],2,0,["U0184","U0196","U0492"],""],U0192:["Lost Communication With Personal Computer","U0192 is reserved for a personal computer that exchanges data with the vehicle network, for example a built-in carputer, a docked laptop in a police or service vehicle, or a PC-based infotainment unit. When that node stops sending, a listening module stores the code.",["Network coding expects a PC that is not fitted or was removed","Retrofit interface, dock or bus connector to the PC faulty","PC or its interface without supply, or shut down","Onboard PC faulty or software hung"],["PC functions or data no longer available in the vehicle","Code stored without any noticeable fault"],1,0,["U0191","U0198","U0493"],""],U0193:["Lost Communication With Digital Audio Control Module A","U0193 reports that digital audio control module A no longer sends its messages. Makers fill this slot differently. GM calls it Lost Communication With Digital Radio Receiver Control Module in the Saab 9-5 (2010-2011) U-code list, i.e. the separate receiver for digital or satellite radio, and its 2017-2021 GMC Acadia and Cadillac XT5 bulletin lists U0193 among codes caused by harness chafing or water in the BCM.",["Digital receiver module without power or ground","Chafed harness or water in connectors (GM Acadia/XT5)","Bus wire or connector to the receiver damaged","Digital audio module A faulty"],["Digital, satellite radio or traffic data unavailable","Radio shows no signal for the digital source","Code stored in radio and other modules"],2,0,["U0184","U0186","U0194","U0195"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ A"],U0194:["Lost Communication With Digital Audio Control Module B","U0194 marks the second digital audio control module, B, as silent on the bus. GM uses the code but does not name the module publicly: on the 2013-2014 Buick Enclave, Chevrolet Traverse and GMC Acadia the radio stores U0194 together with many other U-codes when the harness of the rear side object detection sensors rubs on the exhaust and disturbs the network.",["Network harness chafed elsewhere in the car disturbing the bus (GM Lambda)","Water in a bus connector (Ford C-MAX)","Audio module B without power or ground","Digital audio module B faulty"],["Radio shuts off or audio source drops out intermittently","Many U-codes stored at the same time","Cluster or other modules act up together with the radio"],2,0,["U0184","U0186","U0193","U0195"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ B"],U0195:["Lost Communication With Subscription Entertainment Receiver Module","U0195 concerns the subscription entertainment receiver module, the box that decodes a paid broadcast service such as SiriusXM satellite radio. Earlier code lists named it Satellite Radio Receiver Module, and makers have used it in that sense: Chrysler's code list for 2006-2010 Jeep models, filed with NHTSA in a defect investigation, reads U0195 as Lost Communication With SDARS, the satellite digital audio receiver.",["Receiver without power or ground","History entry after low battery voltage or jump start","Bus line or connector to the receiver damaged or corroded","Subscription receiver module faulty"],["Satellite radio band missing or showing no signal","Subscription service cannot be activated","Code stored in the radio or gateway"],2,0,["U0184","U0193","U0194","U0496"],""],U0196:["Lost Communication With Entertainment Control Module - Rear A","U0196 refers to rear entertainment control module A, the unit that gives rear passengers their own audio or video source, headphone zones and screen control. GM's Saab U-code lists assign it to the rear audio control module for the 9-5 (2010-2011) and the 9-4X (2011), meaning the rear audio panel with headphone sockets.",["Rear entertainment unit without power or ground","Bus wiring to the rear unit pinched or connector loose (seat, console, headliner)","History entry after low battery voltage","Rear entertainment control module faulty"],["Rear audio controls or headphone sockets dead","Rear screens dark or no source selectable","Code stored in radio or gateway"],2,0,["U0184","U0186","U0191","U0497"],""],U0197:["Lost Communication With Telephone Control Module","U0197 says the telephone control module, in most cars the Bluetooth hands-free unit, has gone quiet on the bus. FCA uses it widely under the name Hands Free Phone Module. Bulletin 08-112-14 covers 2013-2015 Town & Country, Grand Caravan, Compass, Patriot and Wrangler plus 2013-2014 Challenger, Avenger and 200 with Bluetooth not working; new HFM software loaded over USB cures it.",["Hands-free module software hangs at boot (FCA update)","Module without power or ground","Bus line or connector to the phone module faulty","Telephone control module faulty"],["Phone does not pair or calls are not possible hands-free","Display reports the hands-free module is still loading","MIL on in some FCA models"],2,1,["U0184","U0198","U0498"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת טלפון"],U0198:["Lost Communication With Telematic Control Module","U0198 marks the telematic control module as silent; that unit holds the cellular modem for remote apps, emergency and assistance calls. Ford's APIM stores it on 2012-2018 Focus Electric, Fusion Energi and C-MAX Energi when the TCU hangs: SSM 46534 and 47198 report a drained battery, dead MyFord Mobile features and no modem ESN, cured by pulling the TCU fuse for five minutes and reprogramming.",["Telematics unit hung or outdated software (Ford TCU reprogramming)","Water or corrosion in a body harness connector (GM X901)","Low-speed bus wire pinched or chafed in the roof or body","False history entry from a module self-test (Ford Super Duty)","Telematic control module faulty"],["Remote app, emergency or assistance call unavailable","Battery drained overnight (Ford plug-in models)","Network warning in the cluster, often with further U-codes"],2,0,["U0140","U0155","U0197","U0499"],""],U0199:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module A","U0199 reports that door control module A has dropped off the bus; most makers assign it to the driver's door. Chrysler bulletin 08-061-12 (300 and Charger 2005-2010) calls it the driver door module: the front windows and central locking stop working, a one-minute battery disconnect is tried first, and the module is replaced if contact does not return.",["Loose or backed-out pins in the door-to-body connector (VW)","Broken wires in the door hinge harness","Loose ground connection (Ford G201)","Driver door module faulty (Chrysler 300/Charger)"],["Power windows and locks on the door inoperative","Windows move on their own or several warning lamps light up","Mirror adjustment or switch lighting dead"],2,0,["U0200","U0201","U0202","U049A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ A"],U019A:["Lost Communication With Tachograph Module","U019A is stored when the tachograph stops sending on the vehicle bus. Tachographs log speed, distance and driving time in trucks and buses; in the EU every newly registered vehicle of that class has needed a digital unit since May 2006. Many engine and body controllers take road speed from the tachograph frame, so the fault reaches beyond the logbook.",["Tachograph without power, ground or ignition signal","CAN wiring or connector behind the tachograph damaged","Tachograph replaced or recalibrated without matching the bus configuration","Tachograph unit faulty"],["Tachograph warning or speed display missing","Cruise control or road speed limiter unavailable","Code stored in the engine controller"],3,0,["U0155","U049B"],""],U019B:["Lost Communication With Battery Charger Control Module A","U019B means battery charger control module A, the on-board charger of a plug-in vehicle, is no longer heard on the bus. Ford's 2014 OBD code list flags U019B as MIL-relevant, in line with CARB's rule that plug-in hybrids must detect charger faults that stop or slow charging.",["Damaged wires at harness couplings exposed to the environment (Audi A7 PHEV)","Gateway or controller software (Ford Lightning, Audi e-tron GT)","Charger without 12 V supply, ground or wake-up signal","On-board charger control electronics faulty"],["Vehicle does not charge or charge plug stays locked","Electrical system warning, drive system cannot be activated","Export power or backup power features unavailable"],3,1,["U01BB","U027A","U0293","U049C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ A"],U019C:["Lost Communication With Glow Plug Control Module 2","U019C points to a second glow plug control module, needed where a diesel has more preheating channels than one unit drives, for example one module per cylinder bank. No manufacturer documents U019C publicly; it is absent from GM's diesel tables and from the NHTSA bulletin index.",["Glow plug module 2 without supply, ground or ignition feed","Water or corrosion in the module connector near the engine","Bus line to module 2 chafed or connector loose","Glow plug control module 2 faulty"],["Hard starting when cold","White smoke and rough idle until warm","Preheat lamp behaves oddly, MIL on"],2,1,["U0106","U049D","P0670","P0683"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 2"],U019D:["Lost Communication With Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor","U019D concerns a temperature sensor at a direct ozone reduction (DOR) catalyst that reports over the network rather than a plain wire; the wired versions have P2567-P2571. A DOR catalyst is a coating on the radiator or A/C condenser that turns ozone in the passing air into oxygen, such as Engelhard's PremAir, first fitted by Volvo on the S80 and by Nissan on the Sentra CA.",["Sensor connector at the radiator corroded or damaged by road debris","Sensor left unplugged or radiator replaced after front-end repair","Bus or supply line to the sensor broken","DOR temperature sensor faulty"],["MIL on without noticeable driving fault","DOR monitor shown as not complete"],2,1,["P2567","P2568","P2572","U049E"],""],U019E:["Lost Communication With Transmission Range Control Module","U019E covers the transmission range control module, in shift-by-wire designs the electronics that engage park, reverse, neutral or drive on behalf of the driver's selector. Ford lists U019E in its 2014 OBD code list without the MIL marker it gives emissions-related codes. No further public manufacturer source was found; NHTSA's bulletin index is silent on it as well.",["Range control module without power, ground or wake-up","Bus connector at the transmission corroded or loose","Low battery voltage during cranking or parking","Transmission range control module faulty"],["Gear selection refused or vehicle stays in park","Shift system warning in the cluster","Transmission engages park on its own when stopping"],3,2,["U0101","U0103","U01BA","U049F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים"],U019F:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Pump Control Module","U019F means the electric engine coolant pump, which carries its own control electronics, has stopped answering. Mercedes documents it on two engines: on the M256 six-cylinder the engine controller stores U019F00 or U019F87 with a red coolant warning;",["Pump supply plug, 48 V connector or ground loose or dirty (Mercedes)","Water or corrosion in front-end connectors (Ford hybrids)","Similar-looking pumps swapped or wrong part ordered (Mazda PHEV)","Engine controller software outdated (Mercedes MED40)","Electric coolant pump electronics faulty"],["Red coolant temperature warning","MIL or check engine lamp on","Engine power reduced to protect against overheating"],2,3,["P26CA","P26CB","P26D0","U0284","U04A0"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע"],U01A0:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module A","U01A0 names battery interface control module A, the first slave board that reports cell voltages and temperatures of its pack section to the battery controller. GM's 2016-2019 plug-in hybrid tables explain how the code arises: the battery system module talks to eight such boards over a UART daisy chain;",["Chain wiring or connector between battery controller and module A interrupted","Module A without supply from its cell group or low-voltage feed","Battery interface control module A defective","Chain interface of the battery controller itself faulty"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive, red hybrid/EV warning","MIL on after the first failing trip (GM Type A)","Further module codes or U179C stored at the same time"],4,3,["U01A1","U04A1","U033A","U0111"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U01A1:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module B","U01A1 refers to battery interface control module B. In GM's eAssist mild hybrids it is the second and final board: bulletin PIT5513D lists two high-voltage battery interface control modules, K112A and K112B, for Silverado and Sierra trucks of 2016 to 2018 and the 2018 LaCrosse, and the GM tables 16OBDG07B and 19OBDG03B accordingly contain only U01A0 and U01A1.",["Chain connection between module A and module B interrupted or corroded","Battery interface control module B (GM K112B) defective","Common low-voltage feed of the powerpack interrupted (then usually A as well)"],["MIL only after two consecutive failing trips (GM Type B)","Start-stop and electric assist unavailable","Hybrid system warning message"],4,3,["U01A0","U01A2","U04A2","U033B","U0111"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U01A2:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module C","U01A2 is stored when battery interface control module C, the third board of the chain, stays silent. How a controller reaches that verdict is spelled out in GM's 2016 hybrid table: the battery system module first logs U179C for one or more missing boards, then orders all boards into a loopback mode that bypasses the daisy chain.",["Chain link between module B and module C broken (connector, ribbon, pin)","Module C fails the loopback test, board defective","Battery controller software that misreads the chain (update available)"],["Electrical system or hybrid warning in the instrument cluster","Reduced drive power or no electric driving","Code returns immediately after clearing"],4,3,["U01A1","U01A3","U04A3","U033C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C"],U01A3:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module D","U01A3 marks a lost link to battery interface control module D. Before this generic block existed, GM used proprietary numbers for the same fault: the GM U-code list published for the 2011 Saab 9-4X names U2603 to U2606 as the battery energy control module losing hybrid battery interface modules 1 to 4.",["Chain connection from module C to module D interrupted","Battery interface control module D defective","Scan tool or software generation reports the board under the older GM number"],["MIL and hybrid/EV warning (GM Type A)","Limited power, electric range shortened","Cell voltages of one pack section shown as unavailable"],4,3,["U01A2","U01A4","U02A0","U033D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D"],U01A4:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module E","U01A4 concerns battery interface control module E. Whether such a code points to one board or to a whole broken chain depends on the wiring scheme. In a plain daisy chain a break silences all boards behind it, and GM's logic names only the first.",["Chain link between module D and module E interrupted (open chain)","Module E itself defective (likely in ring designs when neighbours still report)","Return path of a ring layout damaged in addition to the main path"],["Battery warning and reduced output","Only module E reported missing although later boards are silent too (open chain)","MIL on the first trip (GM Type A)"],4,3,["U01A3","U01A5","U04A5","U033E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ E"],U01A5:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module F","U01A5 says the battery controller no longer receives data from interface module F. Once such a board drops out, the cells it covers are unsupervised: no voltage readings, no temperatures and no balancing for that section. GM therefore puts all of these codes into a fault bundle called BICM Loss of Comm in its 2018 hybrid table, which blocks battery diagnostics that would otherwise misfire on missing values.",["Chain connection between module E and module F interrupted","Battery interface control module F defective","Board F loses supply because its cell group or sense tap is open"],["Drive system cannot be activated, red warning lamp","Charging refused or stopped early","Other battery diagnostics suspended while the code is active"],4,3,["U01A4","U01A6","U04A6","U033F","P0AA5"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ F"],U01A6:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module G","U01A6 means battery interface control module G no longer reports to the battery controller. Because these boards sit inside the high-voltage pack, the chain runs between modules whose ground levels differ by hundreds of volts, so the link has to be galvanically isolated; Wikipedia's battery management article names optical couplers and radio as the hardware routes.",["Chain link between module F and module G interrupted","Moisture or coolant at the chain connectors of module G","Isolating coupler (transformer, optocoupler) on the link to G failed","Battery interface control module G defective"],["MIL and battery warning lamp","Insulation fault code stored alongside if moisture has entered","Reduced power or no ready mode"],4,3,["U01A5","U01A7","U04A7","U0340"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ G"],U01A7:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module H","U01A7 refers to battery interface control module H. On packs with exactly eight boards it is the tail of the chain: the GM plug-in hybrid tables for 2016 to 2019 stop at U01A7, and both Audi bulletins (A3 Sportback e-tron 2016, Q5 e 2022 and 2024) list precisely U01A000 to U01A700. Since the master always names the first board it cannot reach, H on its own excludes a break further up;",["Final chain link from module G to module H interrupted","Battery interface control module H defective","Termination or return line at the end of the chain faulty"],["MIL on the first trip (GM Type A)","Electrical system or hybrid warning, power reduced","All other module letters report normally"],4,3,["U01A6","U01A8","U04A8","U0341"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ H"],U01A8:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module I","U01A8 is the code for battery interface control module I and is only needed on packs with more than eight monitoring boards. GM's 2018 hybrid table contains it solely inside the fault bundle BICM Loss of Comm (U01A0-U01AC), adding that GM shares software across programs and only codes valid for the vehicle at hand apply; there is no monitor entry of its own, so neither threshold nor MIL type is published for I.",["Chain connection between module H and module I interrupted","Battery interface control module I defective","Battery controller configured for more boards than fitted"],["Battery or hybrid warning, power limited","Charging blocked"],4,3,["U01A7","U01A9","U04A9","U0342"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ I"],U01A9:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module J","U01A9 stands for battery interface control module J, the tenth board. Apart from wiring, a typical trigger after repairs is configuration: monitoring chips in a chain usually get their address when communication starts.",["Chain connection between module I and module J interrupted","Board J not addressed or registered after module replacement","Battery interface control module J defective"],["Code appears right after battery repair or module replacement","Vehicle not ready to drive or power limited"],4,3,["U01A8","U01AA","U04AA","U0343"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ J"],U01AA:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module K","U01AA covers battery interface control module K, the eleventh board, so only large packs can set it at all. Not every design uses wires for this link: GM's Ultium platform monitors its cells by radio, a system developed with Analog Devices, which according to Wikipedia needs about 90 % less wiring. With such a layout a lost module is a radio node the controller no longer hears;",["Wired link to K interrupted or, in wireless systems, radio link lost","Replacement board K not registered with the battery controller","Battery interface control module K defective"],["Battery warning, reduced range and power","DC fast charging limited or refused"],4,3,["U01A9","U01AB","U04AB","U0344"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ K"],U01AB:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module L","U01AB points at battery interface control module L, the twelfth position. The link to such a board has to bridge a large voltage offset, because the lowest and highest boards of a stack sit hundreds of volts apart.",["Twisted-pair chain line to module L chafed, pinched or unplugged","Isolating transformer or capacitor on the link to L failed","Battery interface control module L defective"],["Battery or hybrid warning","Power limited, charging may be blocked"],4,3,["U01AA","U01AC","U04AC","U0345"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ L"],U01AC:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module M","U01AC belongs to battery interface control module M and is the last one GM mentions: its 2018 hybrid table ends the fault bundle BICM Loss of Comm at U01AC, i.e. thirteen boards, whereas GM's model-specific tables from 2016 to 2019 only monitor A to H. For diagnosis the order of events matters more than the letter.",["Chain connection between module L and module M interrupted","Battery interface control module M defective","Controller calibration expects more boards than the pack contains"],["Summary code for missing boards stored together with U01AC","Battery warning and reduced output"],4,3,["U01AB","U01AD","U04AD","U0346"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ M"],U01AD:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module N","U01AD names battery interface control module N, the fourteenth board in a monitoring chain. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and even GM's broad fault bundle stops at M. The reason such codes exist at all lies in CARB's rule 1968.2, section (e)(15.2.3): hybrid OBD systems must supervise the electronic inputs of the energy storage system, such as cell voltage and temperature sensing, and store separate…",["Chain connection between module M and module N interrupted","Battery interface control module N defective"],["Battery warning, power and charging limited","Cell data of one pack section missing in the scan tool"],4,3,["U01AC","U01AE","U04AE","U0347"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ N"],U01AE:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module O","U01AE concerns battery interface control module O, which only exists in systems with at least fifteen monitoring nodes; no manufacturer documents the code publicly. Wikipedia distinguishes three ways to organise battery management: centralised (one controller wired to every cell), modular (several controllers, each covering a group of cells) and distributed (a board per cell with a single communication cable).",["Internal link to module O interrupted","Battery interface control module O defective","Board O without supply from its cell group"],["Warning lamp, power reduced","Charging postponed or refused"],4,3,["U01AD","U01AF","U04AF","U0348"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ O"],U01AF:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module P","U01AF closes the row and stands for battery interface control module P, the sixteenth monitoring board; no manufacturer documents it publicly. Some packs exceed that count: according to Wikipedia the Hummer EV battery consists of 24 Ultium modules, although that platform monitors wirelessly and GM does not publish how it maps modules to codes. The code is easily mixed up with its neighbours.",["Internal link to module P interrupted","Battery interface control module P defective"],["Battery warning while the battery controller itself still communicates","Power limited, charging blocked"],4,3,["U01AE","U04B0","U0349","U0111","U019B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ P"],U01B0:["Lost Communication With Battery Monitor Module","U01B0 says the 12 V battery monitor module, a small sensor on the negative battery post that reports voltage, current, temperature and state of charge, has stopped replying. GM polls it over LIN: its 2018 engine tables (18OBDG03A) flag the code once frame 18_C02 has been absent for 1.25 s, the 2025 body controller tables (25OBDG04A) after 12.6 s; both rate it Type B, two trips.",["Loose, corroded or damaged LIN connector or wire at the battery sensor","Weak or deeply discharged 12 V battery","Battery monitor sensor faulty (GM replaces it after the checks)","Parasitic drain preventing the sensor relearn"],["Stop/start system disabled, message in the driver display","MIL on","Battery state of charge shown wrongly or battery saver functions inactive"],2,1,["U04B1","U01BF","U0140"],""],U01B1:["Lost Communication With Particulate Matter Sensor B","U01B1 concerns a second particulate matter sensor in a diesel exhaust, used where a layout needs two of them. Such smart sensors carry their own control unit, which heats the element, measures soot build-up and sends the results to the engine controller over CAN. U01B1 is stored when that controller stops receiving frames from sensor B. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Heat-damaged or corroded harness or connector at sensor B near the exhaust","Sensor control unit without supply voltage or ground (fuse, relay)","Control unit of PM sensor B faulty"],["MIL on","Particulate filter monitor shows as not complete"],2,1,["U02A3","U04B2","U04A4","U05A4"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן חלקיקים‏ B"],U01B2:["Lost Communication With Planetary Gear Set Control Module","Hybrid transmissions such as the two-mode system developed by GM, Daimler, Chrysler and BMW use two or three planetary gear sets plus clutches to switch between power-split and fixed-ratio operation. A planetary gear set control module would run those shift elements and report their state to the hybrid or transmission controller.",["Damaged CAN wiring or connector at the transmission","Module without supply voltage or ground","Planetary gear set control module faulty"],["Hybrid system warning","Reduced power or limited fallback mode","MIL on"],3,3,["U04B3","U0101","U0293"],""],U01B3:["Lost Communication With Brake Blending Actuator","The brake blending actuator divides each braking request between regeneration by the drive motor and the friction brakes, keeping pedal feel steady while the share shifts. Bosch states that its electromechanical iBooster, together with the ESP hev unit, can blend up to 0.3 g of deceleration. U01B3 is stored when the unit coordinating the brakes, normally the hybrid or brake controller, no longer hears this actuator.",["CAN wiring or connector fault at the brake actuator","Actuator without supply voltage, often after low 12 V voltage","Brake blending actuator electronics faulty"],["Little or no regenerative braking","Changed brake pedal feel","Brake or hybrid system warning"],3,3,["U04B4","U01B4","U0129"],""],U01B4:["Lost Communication With Brake System Control Module B","Brake system control module B is the second brake controller in a two-unit layout, often the electric brake booster beside the stability control unit. GM's 2018 table for the CT6 plug-in hybrid (18OBDG01) has the engine controller flag U01B4 when frame $4FB from BSC2 has been missing for 10 s on the high-speed bus, Type B, two trips.",["Booster run-on interrupted at switch-off (Porsche, no part fault)","Damaged CAN wiring or connector at the brake module","Low 12 V supply during start or shutdown","Brake system control module B faulty"],["MIL on, sometimes with brake or stability warnings","Driver assistance functions unavailable","Changed brake pedal feel if the booster is affected"],2,3,["U0129","U04B5","U031C","U015A","U025E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ B"],U01B5:["Lost Communication With Catalyst Heater Control Module","Electric catalyst heating lets the converter start working within seconds of a cold start. Emitec's EMICAT disc runs on 12, 24 or 48 V and draws up to 300 A; in high-voltage hybrids Vitesco feeds it through a dedicated DC/DC converter, one form of the separate power electronics that make up a catalyst heater control module.",["Heat or corrosion damage at the heater module connectors near the exhaust","Module supply or high-current fuse open","Catalyst heater control electronics faulty"],["MIL on","Higher emissions and possibly rough running after a cold start"],3,1,["U04B6","U0100","U019D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גוף חימום ממיר קטליטי"],U01B6:["Lost Communication With Fuel Heater Control Module","A fuel heater warms diesel ahead of the filter so that paraffin wax, which separates out in the cold, cannot clog the element; ordinary diesel turns to gel at roughly −15 to −19 °C. Newer designs use a microcontroller: a patent describes a heater controller that sets power from outside air temperature in open loop or from fuel temperature in closed loop, and cuts out when battery voltage falls too low.",["Corroded or loose connector at the filter housing heater","Heater module supply fuse or relay failed","Fuel heater control electronics faulty"],["Hard starting or stalling in frost","Power loss from a clogged fuel filter in cold weather","Often no symptom in mild weather"],2,0,["U0100","U0106","U019C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גוף חימום דלק"],U01B7:["Lost Communication With Switch Input Module A","A switch input module collects a group of buttons, for instance in a door trim, steering wheel or centre console, and sends their states to other units as network messages instead of wiring every switch on its own. A patent by Eaton describes the idea: a central unit queries every switch by its address and accepts only answers whose address and state are valid.",["Loose connector or broken wire at the switch panel","Liquid spilled into the switch module","Switch input module A faulty"],["A group of buttons without function","Switch backlight or indicator lamps dark"],2,0,["U04BA","U01B8","U01B9","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול כניסת מתג‏ A"],U01B8:["Lost Communication With Switch Input Module B","Carmakers that fit more than one switch input module count them A, B, C. A modular layout patented by BCS Automotive Interface Solutions shows why there can be several: a main switch module, for example for the lighting, is extended by satellite modules of different kinds, and coding contacts in the connectors tell the main unit which type is plugged in.",["Connector of module B unplugged, loose or corroded","Missing supply voltage or ground at module B","Switch input module B faulty"],["Buttons served by module B without function","Other switch groups still working"],2,0,["U04BB","U01B7","U01B9"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול כניסת מתג‏ B"],U01B9:["Lost Communication With Switch Input Module C","Module C is the third switch input module. Such units often hang off a sub-bus: a Yazaki patent on door electronics shows a door unit that takes commands from CAN and forwards them over a LIN sub-bus to local nodes such as switches, window lift and mirror. When module C drops off, the receiver logs U01B9 and normally treats the affected switch states as released, a safe default.",["Wire broken in a moving harness section (door hinge, seat rail, steering column)","Fault in the unit that hosts the sub-bus of module C","Switch input module C faulty"],["Buttons served by module C ignored","Fault appears or disappears when moving a door, seat or the steering wheel"],2,0,["U04BC","U01B7","U01B8"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול כניסת מתג‏ C"],U01BA:["Lost Communication With Park Lock/Pawl Control Module","With park-by-wire, an electric actuator drives the parking pawl into a toothed wheel on the transmission output; no cable links it to the selector, so the park lock module alone decides when the pawl may drop in, normally only at standstill because at speed it would just ratchet over the teeth. U01BA is set when the transmission or vehicle controller loses contact with this module.",["Connector or wiring fault at the park lock actuator on the transmission","Low 12 V supply, e.g. weak battery","Park lock control module faulty"],["Vehicle will not shift out of Park or Park not confirmed","Warning to secure the vehicle with the parking brake"],3,2,["U04BD","U019E","U0103","U0101"],""],U01BB:["Lost Communication With Battery Charger Control Module B","Battery charger control module B is, by its name, a second on-board charger, as fitted on some electric cars to raise AC charging power. Polestar uses the code differently: Technical Journal 37630 (2026, vehicle type 359 from model year 2025) lists U01BB00 in the central computer GCCC when its only AC charger, the grid-to-HV converter GHCA, has failed.",["On-board charger unit failed (Polestar GHCA replaced)","Charger without 12 V supply, ground or wake-up signal","Bus wiring or connector at the charger damaged"],["AC charging impossible while DC fast charging works","Charging fault message or charge port LED error"],4,0,["U019B","U027A","U027B","U04BE","U0293"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ B"],U01BC:["Lost Communication With Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B","Engines with a water-cooled charge air cooler run a separate low-temperature coolant loop with an electric pump, usually a LIN slave of the engine controller. Rheinmetall's pumps of this kind are driven via PWM or LIN, and Bosch's PCE pump has a built-in diagnostic function reported to a higher-level unit. U01BC applies where a second pump, B, serves this loop. No manufacturer documents the code publicly.",["Water or corrosion in the pump connector at the front of the engine bay","Pump supply fuse or relay open","Electric coolant pump B electronics or motor faulty"],["MIL on","Reduced power or boost, especially in hot weather"],2,3,["U02A9","U05AA","U0100"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B"],U01BD:["Lost Communication With DC/DC Converter Control Module C","Electrified cars may carry several DC/DC converters, each turning one direct voltage into another: the main unit supplies the 12 V system from the traction battery, others feed 48 V consumers or single heavy loads. Vitesco, for instance, added a dedicated DC/DC converter in high-voltage hybrids purely to power the electrically heated catalyst.",["Low-voltage supply, wake-up line or connector of converter C faulty","Converter shut down by an open high-voltage interlock or contactor state","DC/DC converter C control electronics faulty"],["Electrical system or 12 V warning","Comfort loads switched off to save energy"],4,2,["U0298","U0299","U0599","U059A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ C"],U01BE:["Lost Communication With Drive Motor A Clutch Actuator","Some electrified drivetrains can uncouple a drive motor from its wheels so that an idle motor is not spun by the road. The Chevrolet Corvette E-Ray has such a disconnect: GM bulletin 24-NA-273 (January 2025, 2024–2025 models with LT2 engine) ties U01BE with a lit MIL to an internal microchip fault in the M162 drive motor disconnect clutch actuator, and the remedy is a new actuator.",["Internal electronic fault in the clutch actuator (GM M162 replaced)","Connector or wiring fault at the actuator on the drive unit","Actuator without supply voltage or ground"],["MIL on","Electric drive on one axle or all-wheel drive unavailable","Reduced acceleration"],4,3,["U04BF","U0110","U0411"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל מצמד מנוע הנעה‏ A"],U01BF:["Lost Communication With Battery Management Control Module","A battery management control module watches cell voltages, temperatures and current and decides how much power a pack may deliver or accept. The J2012 name does not tie it to the high-voltage battery.",["Bus wiring or connector between gateway and battery module damaged","Module supply interrupted or 12 V voltage too low","Battery management control module faulty"],["Battery or electrical system warning","Charging or drive power limited","MIL on (GM Type B)"],3,3,["U04C0","U0111","U01B0","U0412"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ניהול סוללה"],U0200:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module B","U0200 means door control module B has dropped off the bus; most makers use B for the front passenger door. For the 2005–2010 Chrysler 300 and Charger, bulletin 08-061-12 names it the passenger door module and replaces it when locks and windows stay dead.",["Passenger door module software (Audi Q5 J387 update)","Loose, bent or corroded pins in the door or A-pillar connector","Broken wires in the door hinge harness","Passenger door module faulty (Chrysler 300/Charger)"],["Passenger window or lock switch inoperative","Door does not lock or unlock centrally, sometimes intermittent","Child lock or door warning message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0199","U0201","U0501","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ B"],U0201:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module C","U0201 stands for door control module C, in the generic list the next door unit after driver (A) and front passenger (B), so on four-door cars usually a rear door. Audi, for example, gives each rear door its own controller (J388, J389, diagnostic addresses 00BB and 00BC), and its Q3 bulletin 2063376 deals with their child lock motors, but no Audi document names U0201. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Chafed or broken wires in the rear door hinge harness","Loose or corroded pins in the door connector","Rear door control module faulty"],["Rear window, lock or child lock inoperative","Door or child lock warning in the cluster"],2,0,["U0200","U0202","U0502","U0102"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ C"],U0202:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module D","U0202 means the body network no longer hears from door control module D, which most four-door layouts give to the right rear door. FCA STAR case S1908000143 (Rev. A, August 2020) records it on a minivan with Stow 'n Go seating: U0202 for the right rear door module came together with U0201 (left rear), U0230 (power liftgate) and the interior bus codes U0010/U0011, while the owner had a no-start, many lit warning…",["Body harness chafed at the B-pillar or under the seats (FCA minivan)","Broken wires in the rear door hinge harness","Corroded splice or door connector","Rear door module faulty"],["Right rear window or lock inoperative","Several warning lamps and further U-codes at the same time","Possible no-start or unrequested wiper stroke when the bus wiring is damaged"],2,0,["U0201","U0203","U0230","U0503","U0010"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ D"],U0203:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module E","U0203 reports a missing door control module E. For the 2011 Saab 9-5, GM fills this slot with the left rear door switch panel, so on these GM platforms E is the electronics behind the rear left window and lock switches rather than a fifth door.",["Instrument panel harness chafed at the steering column (GM Acadia/XT5)","Water at the body control module or in body connectors","Broken wires between rear door and body","Rear door switch panel module faulty"],["Left rear window or lock switches without function","Door locks cycle on their own while driving","Many other lost-communication codes stored at once"],2,0,["U0202","U0204","U0504","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ E"],U0204:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module F","U0204 is set when door control module F stops answering. On the 2011 Saab 9-4x, whose U-code list comes from GM, the letter F belongs to the right rear door switch panel, the mirror-image partner of U0203 on the left.",["Spread terminals in the diagnostic connector, false entries while testing (GM)","Broken wires in the right rear door hinge harness","Loose or corroded door connector pins","Rear door switch panel module faulty"],["Right rear window or lock switches inoperative","Codes appear together with an instrument self-test when the scan tool is plugged in"],2,0,["U0203","U0205","U0505","U0201"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ F"],U0205:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module G","U0205 covers door control module G. The generic list reserves eight door module slots, A to H, so G only comes into play on vehicles carrying more door electronics than four side doors; which unit gets the letter is the maker's choice. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Broken or chafed wires at the door transition","Missing fuse, power or ground feed of the door module","Door module faulty or hung after a voltage drop"],["Window, lock or mirror on the affected door inoperative","Door switch lighting dark"],2,0,["U0204","U020B","U0506","U0199"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ G"],U0206:["Lost Communication With Folding Top Control Module","U0206 indicates that the folding top control module, which drives the hydraulic or electric mechanism of a convertible roof and watches its end positions, has fallen silent on the bus. Lamborghini names U020600, stored in control unit 00C5, in its Revuelto baseline update bulletins L74X-A.11.25 (model year 2024) and L74X-A.05.25 (2025): if the entry shows up during the SVM code step, the technician adds it to the…",["Module software needs an update after programming (Lamborghini Revuelto)","Fuse, power or ground of the top module missing","Harness or connector in the top compartment damaged or wet","Folding top module faulty"],["Convertible top neither opens nor closes","Roof or top warning in the instrument cluster"],3,0,["U0207","U020A","U0507"],""],U0207:["Lost Communication With Moveable Roof Control Module A","U0207 concerns moveable roof control module A, the electronics of a power sunroof or glass roof. GM uses it: the 2011 Saab 9-5 list names the moveable roof control module, and GM preliminary information PIT5606J (GMC Acadia, Cadillac XT5 2017–2021) counts U0207 among the codes that appear after water gets in – mostly at the upper windshield corners hidden under the glass, rarely past the outer sunroof seal or a…",["Water leak at windshield corners, sunroof seal or blocked drain hose","Dash harness chafed at the steering column (GM Acadia/XT5)","Corroded connector at the roof module","Roof module faulty"],["Sunroof does not respond to the switch","Damp headliner or water marks near the A-pillar","Further U-codes in several modules"],2,0,["U020A","U0206","U0508"],""],U0208:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module A","U0208 says seat control module A has dropped out, mostly a driver's seat unit. The letter is used differently: FCA radio bulletin 08-108-14 (2015 Cherokee, Grand Cherokee, Ram) calls it the heated seat control module and removes a false U0208-00 on the Cherokee with new Uconnect radio software;",["Splice under the driver-side carpet corroded by salt water (Audi Q7/Q8)","Seat module or radio software (Ford SSM 55168, FCA 08-108-14)","Seat harness pinched or unplugged under the seat","Seat module faulty"],["Power or memory seat does not move","Seat heating or ventilation cannot be switched","Power running boards fail (Ford Expedition/Navigator)"],2,0,["U0209","U0210","U0211","U0509","U0244"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ A"],U0209:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module B","U0209 means seat control module B is no longer heard. On GM cars of 2010–2015 with heated front seats (LaCrosse, Regal, Verano, Camaro, Cruze, Equinox, Malibu, Sonic, Volt, Terrain) the HVAC module logs it when both seat heaters quit: preliminary information PIC5954 blames intermittent software in seat heating module K29, which is reset by pulling its fuse for five minutes, and PIC5954B adds a reprogramming;",["Seat heating module software hangs (GM K29, reset and reprogram)","Stored history entry from a software anomaly (GM 2020–2023 SUVs)","Fuse or supply of the seat module","Seat harness damaged under the seat"],["Both front seat heaters inoperative","Side bolster adjustment of the driver seat does not react"],1,0,["U0208","U0210","U050A","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ B"],U020A:["Lost Communication With Moveable Roof Control Module B","U020A stands for moveable roof control module B, a second roof unit beside module A (U0207); which drive it controls, for instance a separate sunshade or a further glass panel, depends on the maker. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Roof module software or missing initialisation","Wet or corroded connector in the headliner","Fuse or ground of roof module B","Roof module B faulty"],["Second roof panel or sunshade does not move","Roof stops halfway or needs repeated button presses"],2,0,["U0207","U0206","U050B"],""],U020B:["Lost Communication With Door Control Module H","U020B is the last of the eight door module slots and flags lost contact with door control module H. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and on ordinary four-door cars the letter stays empty. Where it is assigned, the receiving unit, usually body control module or gateway, misses the cyclic messages of that door unit;",["Poorly seated or corroded pins in the door-to-body connector","Wire break in the door transition","Door module H faulty"],["Window, lock or switches of one door inoperative","Door ajar or door system warning in the cluster"],2,0,["U0205","U0199","U050C","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת דלת‏ H"],U020C:["Lost Communication With Wireless Accessory Charging Module A","U020C means wireless accessory charging module A, the inductive Qi pad usually placed in the centre console, no longer talks on the network. No manufacturer documents this code publicly with module and threshold. The pad takes no part in driving, so its loss only switches off phone charging and the related display messages.",["Fuse or supply of the charging pad","Loose or damaged connector under the console","Module software hung or outdated","Charging module faulty"],["Phone does not charge on the wireless pad","No charging status shown on the centre display"],1,0,["U020D","U050D"],""],U020D:["Lost Communication With Wireless Accessory Charging Module B","U020D is the second wireless charging slot, B, meant for vehicles with two inductive pads, for example a further one for rear passengers. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The early GM system shows what sits behind such a unit: preliminary information PIC6049 (2015 Cadillac ATS, CTS, Escalade, Chevrolet Tahoe, Suburban, GMC Yukon with option K4C) placed the wireless charging module under technical…",["Fuse or supply of charging pad B","Connector or harness to the second pad","Charging module B faulty"],["Second wireless pad does not charge, first still works","Charging indicator for that pad missing"],1,0,["U020C","U050E"],""],U0210:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module C","U0210 flags lost contact with seat control module C. GM fills the slot in two ways: the 2011 Saab 9-5 list assigns it to the rear seat heating module, while bulletin 23-NA-206 and its predecessor PIT5762F (2020–2023 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon, Corvette, CT4, CT5) name the passenger front seat bladder control module, i.e. the air cells for lumbar support or massage.",["History entry from a software anomaly (GM 2020–2023, ignore if not current)","Seat harness unplugged or pinched","Fuse or supply of the seat module","Seat module C faulty"],["Rear seat heating inoperative","Passenger lumbar support or massage does not react","Code stored only in history without any complaint"],2,0,["U0209","U0211","U0511","U0246"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ C"],U0211:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module D","U0211 reports that seat control module D is absent from the bus. GM bulletin 21-NA-131, which replaces PIT5796A (2020–2021 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon and 2021 Corvette, CT4, CT5), names it the memory seat module: the driver assistance controller EOCM records U0211 and invalid data U0512 when software in the memory seat module misbehaves.",["Memory seat module software (GM 21-NA-131, reprogram)","Radio control module software (Honda Prologue 25-051)","Seat harness or connector under the driver seat"],["Seat memory and easy entry/exit inoperative","Backrest will not recline fully","Driver assistance message or Super Cruise unavailable"],2,0,["U0210","U0208","U0512","U0247"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ D"],U0212:["Lost Communication With Steering Column Control Module","U0212 means the steering column control module, which reads stalks and steering wheel buttons such as wipers, turn signals and cruise switches, is missing from the network. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary lets the engine computer set it once the SCCM's message has been absent for more than 5 s, while the 2014 Ford list carries it with no MIL flag.",["False code mapping with electric column lock (GM N06, diagnose U0236)","Switch or airbag connectors at the column loose or corroded","Harness chafed at the base of the steering column","Steering column control module faulty"],["Wipers, turn signals or steering wheel buttons inoperative","Cruise control unavailable","Code stored in several modules without any complaint"],2,0,["U0236","U0140","U0151","U0213"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת עמוד היגוי"],U0213:["Lost Communication With Mirror Control Module A","U0213 is set when mirror control module A stops reporting. In FCA vehicles A is the interior mirror: STAR case S2108000013 (2021 Jeep Grand Cherokee) found the BCM storing U0213-00 after a Restore Vehicle Configuration had wrongly marked the combined rear view mirror module CRVMM as fitted, for instance after enabling reverse camera grid lines per RRT 08-099-20;",["Mirror module enabled in configuration but not fitted (FCA)","Mirror connector at the windshield loose","Interior mirror module faulty"],["Code active without any noticeable fault","Auto-dimming or camera display in the mirror inoperative"],1,0,["U014D","U0514","U0212","U0140"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מראה‏ A"],U0214:["Lost Communication With Remote Function Actuation Module","U0214 stands for the remote function actuation module, the receiver for key fob, passive entry or phone as a key. Ford calls it RFA: SSM 51571 (Mustang Mach-E 2021–2023) and SSM 54773 (Nautilus 2021–2023) describe phone as a key failing and U0214 in several modules because the RFA hangs in programming mode following an over-the-air update; one minute without the RFA fuse in the BCM and a reprogramming bring it back.",["RFA module stuck in programming mode after an update (Ford)","LAN wire to the receiver pinched in the headliner (GM Acadia)","Fuse or supply of the receiver module","Receiver module faulty"],["Key fob, keyless entry or phone as a key inoperative","Intermittent no crank or radio and HVAC dropouts"],2,0,["U0515","U0140","U0155","U0213"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול הפעלת פונקציה מרוחקת"],U0215:["Lost Communication With Door Switch A","U0215 is logged when door switch unit A, a keypad with its own small controller, stops answering on the bus. NXP application note AN2205 shows how such a keypad usually works: it is a LIN slave that never speaks unprompted; the body controller asks it roughly every 100 ms and expects a four-byte reply holding key states and LIN error flags. If that reply goes missing, the master records the loss.",["LIN or supply wire broken where the harness flexes at the door hinge","Switch unit A without battery feed or ground","LIN line shorted to ground or battery (often silences several nodes at once)","Electronics in switch unit A failed"],["Window, mirror or lock keys on one panel do nothing","Panel backlighting stays dark","Code returns after clearing, sometimes only when the door is moved"],2,0,["U0216","U0217","U0218","U0219","U0220","U0221","U0516"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ A"],U0216:["Lost Communication With Door Switch B","U0216 reports that door switch unit B has dropped off the network. FCA uses the code on the 2014 Jeep Cherokee (KL) and its text names the driver door switch as the missing partner, so B is the driver's panel there.",["Outdated BCM software (FCA 2014 Cherokee, bulletin 08-013-15)","Vehicle configuration (Proxi) no longer consistent after battery disconnect","Damaged wiring or connector between driver door and body","Driver door switch unit failed"],["Cluster message Start/Stop Not Available","Code appears after the battery was disconnected","Keys on the driver's switch panel may not respond"],2,0,["U0215","U0217","U0218","U0219","U0220","U0221","U0517"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ B"],U0217:["Lost Communication With Door Switch C","U0217 is set when door switch unit C no longer answers its master. How much breaks then depends on the door architecture. In NXP's LIN door reference SG2034 the driver's control switch panel is itself the LIN master and commands the front and rear window lifters, door locks and mirror as slaves;",["Broken wire in the flexing harness between door and body","Corroded or loose connector at the switch panel","Switch panel electronics failed","Fault in the door or body module that polls the panel"],["Other windows can no longer be operated from the driver's panel","Keys on the affected panel inoperative","Mirror adjustment from the panel unavailable"],2,0,["U0215","U0216","U0218","U0219","U0220","U0221","U0518"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ C"],U0218:["Lost Communication With Door Switch D","U0218 means door switch unit D has gone silent. Rear-door panels are often bus nodes in their own right; on the 2011 Saab 9-5, GM even gives the left and right rear door switch panels separate codes. A detail worth knowing is the window lockout: the driver's panel sends a child-lock bit in its LIN reply, and according to NXP AN2205 the BCM or the individual window modules evaluate this bit and block the rear keys.",["Broken wire in the harness passage to the door","Moisture or corrosion at the switch panel connector","Switch panel D failed","Body or door module not polling the panel correctly"],["Window key in one door has no effect","Same window still moves from the driver's panel","Rear window lockout behaves unexpectedly"],2,0,["U0215","U0216","U0217","U0219","U0220","U0221","U0519","U0203"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ D"],U0219:["Lost Communication With Door Switch E","U0219 means the networked door switch unit E is no longer heard. In modern doors the switch packs for windows, mirrors and locks are often small bus nodes, typically LIN slaves under a door or body module, so each panel can report its own communication loss. The master that polls switch E stores U0219 once its replies stop; GM documents this setting rule for the whole U0100-U02FF range.",["Broken wire in the door hinge area (flexing harness)","Water ingress into the door switch pack","Switch unit E without power or ground","Door switch unit E faulty"],["Window, mirror or lock buttons in one door inoperative","Switch illumination off","Fault changes when the door is opened or closed"],2,0,["U0215","U0216","U0217","U0218","U0220"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ E"],U0220:["Lost Communication With Door Switch F","U0220 reports that door switch unit F has stopped communicating. Water is a well-documented enemy of such units. GM recall 14V404 (bulletin 14309) covered 2005–2007 TrailBlazer, Envoy, Rainier and Saab 9-7X: salty melt water reaching the driver-door module corroded its circuit board, so lock and window switches worked only now and then, windows could move by themselves and the board could overheat;",["Water or salt slush inside the switch unit, corroded circuit board","Corrosion at the door-to-body connector","Broken wire in the door harness","Switch unit failed without visible moisture"],["Window or lock keys work only intermittently","Window moves without a button press","Heat or burnt smell at the door switch panel"],2,0,["U0215","U0216","U0217","U0218","U0219","U0221","U0521"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ F"],U0221:["Lost Communication With Door Switch G","U0221 is stored when door switch unit G no longer replies. The weak spot is often the passage between door and body, where the harness bends at every opening. FCA STAR cases S1808000031 and S2108000106 (Jeep Compass 2018–2021) describe it: corrosion at the driver door-to-body connector and a badly seated rubber grommet led to intermittent windows, locks and mirrors, rear windows lowering on their own, door-ajar…",["Corroded door-to-body connector behind a poorly sealing grommet","Door connector not fully engaged","Wire chafed or broken inside the grommet","Switch unit G failed"],["Windows, locks and mirrors fail intermittently","Door-ajar warning while driving","Start/stop function stops working at times"],2,0,["U0215","U0216","U0217","U0218","U0219","U0220","U0522"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג דלת‏ G"],U0222:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor A","U0222 says door window motor A, a motor with its own electronics, is no longer heard. GM uses it on 2021–2025 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban and Yukon with air leveling (RPO F47): PIT5981B lists U0222 to U0225 as codes that can sit beside a low or leaning air suspension, a Service Leveling System message or short-term inflates that do nothing. The link is the door-ajar switch, wired directly to each window motor;",["Door wiring altered or damaged during an upfit (armored car, limousine)","Broken bus or supply wire in the door harness","Electronics of window motor A failed","Water or corrosion at the motor connector"],["Air suspension low, leaning or not leveling","Service Leveling System message in the driver information center","Door shown as closed in scan data although it is open","Window in the affected door does not move"],2,0,["U0223","U0224","U0225","U0226","U0227","U0228","U0523"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ A"],U0223:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor B","U0223 points to door window motor B dropping out of communication; GM lists it in PIT5981B together with A, C and D for its 2021–2025 full-size SUVs. Smart motors keep learned data: Atmel's AVR480 reference stores blocking points and anti-pinch parameters in EEPROM and acquires them while the window is first operated.",["Motor or door connector not fully reconnected after door trim work","Broken wire in the door harness","Electronics of window motor B failed","Blown fuse or missing ground for the motor"],["Window in the affected door does not move at all","Express-up unavailable","Fault appears right after door panel or glass work"],2,0,["U0222","U0224","U0225","U0226","U0227","U0228","U0524"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ B"],U0224:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor C","U0224 means door window motor C no longer reports in; GM's PIT5981B names it among the four window motor codes of its 2021–2025 full-size SUVs. Inside such a motor sits more than a driver stage: NXP's AN3147 reference counts Hall pulses to track glass position, detects pinching or stall and reports chip status such as overvoltage or overtemperature to the LIN master.",["Broken bus or supply wire in the door harness","Motor electronics damaged (overvoltage, overheating, Hall sensor board)","Fuse or ground for motor C missing"],["One-touch up and down unavailable","Window in the affected door does not move","Glass stops at random points or not at all"],2,0,["U0222","U0223","U0225","U0226","U0227","U0228","U0525"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ C"],U0225:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor D","U0225 marks door window motor D as missing from the bus. GM's PIT5981B names U0225 last in its list for 2021–2025 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban and Yukon and notes that the cases came mainly from vehicles altered by upfitters, so door wiring touched during a conversion deserves the first look.",["Door wiring changed during a vehicle conversion","LIN wire to motor D chafed, open or shorted","Electronics of window motor D failed"],["Window in the affected door inoperative","Air suspension not leveling on vehicles with door-ajar input via the motor","Further lost-communication codes from other door nodes"],2,0,["U0222","U0223","U0224","U0226","U0227","U0228","U0526"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ D"],U0226:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor E","U0226 is stored when door window motor E stops answering. No manufacturer documents U0226 publicly, and the door behind letter E is the maker's choice. Water, however, is a proven cause of failure for window motors with built-in electronics.",["Water inside the motor housing or its electronics","Corroded motor connector","Door membrane or water deflector not sealing","Broken wire in the door harness"],["Window stops working, often after rain or a car wash","Window moves jerkily before failing completely","Corrosion or moisture visible at the motor plug"],2,0,["U0222","U0223","U0224","U0225","U0227","U0228","U0527"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ E"],U0227:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor F","U0227 reports that door window motor F cannot be reached. Besides wiring faults, the LIN sleep and wake cycle is worth understanding here. In NXP's AN2960 window-lift example the motor node drops into low-power mode on a go-to-sleep request, or after four seconds without bus traffic, behaviour that LIN 2.0 makes mandatory for slaves, and it becomes active again on bus activity or through a wake pin.",["Weak or interrupted supply or ground at the motor","LIN transceiver in the motor electronics damaged","Broken wire in the door harness","Software fault in the LIN master (door or body module)"],["Window fails intermittently","Window and its one-touch function inoperative"],2,0,["U0222","U0223","U0224","U0225","U0226","U0228","U0528"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ F"],U0228:["Lost Communication With Door Window Motor G","U0228 concerns door window motor G, the last letter of this group. No manufacturer documents U0228 publicly. GM shows that a networked window motor does not automatically mean these generic codes: in the 2011 Saab 9-5 the body control module runs the front passenger and driver motors as devices 0 and 4 on LIN bus 3 and the two rear motors on LIN bus 4, and flags a lost motor with GM's own U1530, U1534, U1540 or…",["Broken bus or supply wire in the door harness","Corroded or loose motor connector","Electronics of window motor G failed"],["Window in the affected door does not move","Pinch protection and one-touch operation unavailable"],2,0,["U0222","U0223","U0224","U0225","U0226","U0227","U0529"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מנוע חלון דלת‏ G"],U0229:["Lost Communication With Heated Steering Wheel Module","U0229 means the heated steering wheel module no longer answers. GM PIT5883G (December 2022) explains one harmless case: many 2022–2023 GM models were built during a parts shortage with the heated wheel disabled (RPO 00G); there U0229, together with U152B or U1530, may be stored, should be ignored and lights no warning.",["Module without fuse feed or ground","Heated wheel disabled from the factory (GM RPO 00G), code to be ignored","Clockspring interrupted (when the module sits in the steering wheel)","Heated steering wheel module failed or not configured"],["Steering wheel heating does not switch on","Heater button indicator does not respond","Code stored without any noticeable fault (feature not fitted or disabled)"],2,0,["U052A","U0212"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול גלגל הגה מחומם"],U022E:["Lost Communication With Object Detection Maintenance Control Module A","U022E reports that object detection maintenance control module A has stopped talking on the vehicle network. The J2012 name points to a unit that keeps the detection sensors of the driver assistance system usable, for example by washing or heating camera, radar or lidar covers; patent US11077472B2 describes such a cleaning device for an object detection sensor.",["Module A without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Damaged or corroded bus wiring to module A","Washer fluid or water ingress at the module or its plug","Module A faulty or not programmed"],["Sensor cleaning or sensor blocked warning","Driver assistance features unavailable"],3,0,["U022F","U052F","U0530"],""],U022F:["Lost Communication With Object Detection Maintenance Control Module B","U022F is the B counterpart: a control unit expects messages from object detection maintenance control module B and receives none. Cars with many cameras and radars could split sensor upkeep, such as washer pumps, nozzle valves or cover heaters, across two units, and B would then serve the second group; which sensors that is stays the maker's choice, because no manufacturer documents U022F publicly.",["Fuse, ground or bus branch shared with module A interrupted","Corroded plug at module B","Module B faulty or software not matching"],["Sensor blocked or cleaning unavailable message","Camera or radar based assistance switched off"],3,0,["U022E","U0530","U052F"],""],U0230:["Lost Communication With Rear Gate Module","U0230 means the rear gate module, which runs a powered liftgate or tailgate with its drive, latch, cinch motor and pinch detection, has dropped off the bus. Toyota bulletin T-SB-0038-15 (Highlander and Highlander HV 2008-2013) names U0230 together with B2222 when the power back door reverses at the end of its travel or clunks at the striker, and gives a hinge and hatch inspection and repair.",["Water or corrosion in the harness connector at the liftgate","Wires broken in the flexing harness between body and gate","Bus wiring chafed along the body (seat or pillar area)","Rear gate module faulty"],["Power liftgate does not open or close electrically","Gate reverses or stops during power closing","Several lost communication codes stored at once"],2,0,["U0531","U0140","U0155"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול שער אחורי"],U0231:["Lost Communication With Rain Sensing Module","U0231 shows that the rain sensing module on the windscreen, an optical unit that registers droplets and often ambient brightness too, no longer answers. It usually sits on a LIN line below a body or wiper controller, which stores the code. FCA bulletin 08-050-22 Rev.",["Sensor plug not seated after windscreen or mirror work","Body control module software (FCA 08-050-22)","LIN wire damaged in the headliner or A-pillar","Rain sensing module faulty"],["Automatic wipers inoperative, manual stages still work","Automatic headlamps not switching"],1,0,["U0532","U0140"],""],U0232:["Lost Communication With Side Obstacle Detection Control Module A","U0232 means side obstacle detection control module A, one of the rear corner radars for blind spot and cross traffic warning, is missing from the network. Saab's 2011 list puts A on the left; Toyota bulletin T-SB-0063-19 (Tacoma 2016-2018) calls U0232 loss of the blind spot slave module. Volvo journal TJ 30858 (XC90, S90, 2016-2018) has the right unit log U023292 for its partner and prescribes new software.",["Mud, snow or ice packed between radar and bumper cover","Radar module software needing update","Open fuse or pinched wiring in the rear body or liftgate","Corroded radar connector"],["Blind spot system unavailable message","Mirror warning lamps do not light","Rear cross traffic alert inoperative"],2,0,["U0233","U0533","U024E"],""],U0233:["Lost Communication With Side Obstacle Detection Control Module B","U0233 is stored when side obstacle detection control module B no longer reports. In the Saab 2011 list B is the right hand unit, which matches Volvo TJ 30858 (XC90, S90, 2016-2018): there the left sensor logs U023392 for the right one, and a software update is the fix.",["Side radar software outdated","Dirt, snow or ice build-up behind the rear bumper","Corroded radar connector or harness","Side obstacle module B faulty"],["Blind spot or cross traffic alert unavailable","Sensor blocked message without any obstacle"],2,0,["U0232","U0534","U024F"],""],U0234:["Lost Communication With Convenience Recall Module","U0234 states that the convenience recall module has fallen silent on the network. Convenience recall means stored personal settings brought back on request or by key, typically seat, outside mirror, pedal and column positions and audio presets; patent US7525931B2 shows such a recall session started by a networked door module message.",["Module without power or ground (fuse, connector under seat or door)","Harness under the seat pinched by seat travel","Convenience recall module faulty"],["Memory buttons for seat and mirrors without function","Driver profile not recalled with the key"],2,0,["U0535","U0208"],""],U0235:["Lost Communication With Front Distance Range Sensor - Single Sensor or Center","U0235 means the forward long range radar, the single or centre sensor that measures the gap to traffic ahead for adaptive cruise and collision warning, has gone quiet. GM's 2025 OBD summary 25OBDG04B lets the object calculation module EOCM3 set it when any of six radar data bursts is absent for more than 0.25 s at 9-16 V, skipped in transport mode, after resets and during bus-off;",["Radar connector or wiring at the front end damaged (often after a collision)","Weak 12 V supply or BCM calibration (GM PIC6606)","Long range radar module faulty","Fault on the object or chassis bus shared with other modules"],["Adaptive cruise control unavailable","Collision alert or driver assist unavailable message"],3,0,["U023D","U023E","U0433"],""],U0236:["Lost Communication With Column Lock Module","U0236 reports that the column lock module, which electrically bolts and frees the steering shaft as theft protection, has stopped communicating. It has nothing to do with the steering angle sensor (U0126).",["Column lock module without power or ground (fuse, connector at column)","Harness at the steering column chafed or plug loose after column work","Electric column lock unit faulty","Low battery voltage during start request"],["Steering lock or service steering column warning","Engine does not crank or start","Steering wheel stays locked"],3,0,["U0537","U0212","U0126"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול נעילת עמוד"],U0237:["Lost Communication With Digital Audio Control Module C","U0237 means a third digital audio unit, module C, has gone silent. Ford uses the code in its newer infotainment layout: SSM 49737 (Mustang Mach-E 2021) and its follow-up SSM 51778 (2020-2022 Escape, Edge, Explorer, Expedition, F-150, Mach-E) list U0237 and U0238 when the speakers fall silent, chimes move to the instrument cluster and neither the ACM (audio control module) nor the digital signal processor (DSP)…",["Audio DSP software hung or outdated (Ford SSM 49737/51778)","Audio module without power (fuse, connector)","Digital audio module C faulty"],["No sound from the speakers","Warning chimes only from the instrument cluster"],2,0,["U0238","U0193","U0194","U0538"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ C"],U0238:["Lost Communication With Digital Audio Control Module D","U0238 is set when digital audio control module D stops sending. In Ford and Lincoln vehicles this is the digital signal processor for audio that drives the amplified speaker set, and the code is mostly logged by the ACM, the audio control module. SSM 52999 covers 2023-2024 Escape with Bang and Olufsen sound: intermittent silence with U0238 in ACM or APIM, cured by DSP reprogramming.",["DSP software fault (Ford SSM 52999)","DSP fuse open or with poor blade contact","Audio DSP module faulty"],["Intermittent or permanent loss of audio","Premium sound system without output"],2,0,["U0237","U0539","U0193","U0194"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ D"],U0239:["Lost Communication With Entrapment Control Module A","U0239 means entrapment control module A no longer sends messages. Such a unit watches a power closing panel, a window, sunroof, sliding door or gate, for a trapped object and reverses the motor. In the US, FMVSS 118 sets the reversal limits for windows and roof panels that close without constant switch input;",["Module A without power or ground","Bus wire broken in door hinge or roof harness","Water in the module or plug (door, roof drain)","Entrapment control module A faulty"],["One-touch or automatic closing does not work","Window or sunroof needs re-initialisation"],2,0,["U0240","U053A"],""],U023A:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Module A","U023A reports loss of image processing module A, usually the windscreen camera feeding lane keeping, auto high beam and collision warning. Ford calls it IPMA: Mustang 2024 (SSM 52077) logs U023A in the SCCM after a remote start with Pre-Collision Assist unavailable, and F-150 2021-2023 (TSB 24-2267) shows U023A:08 after SCCM programming, fixed by IPMA software.",["Camera module software or low power mode handling (Ford IPMA)","History code logged at power down without real fault (GM PIC5814)","Instrument cluster swapped from a car without lane departure alert (Toyota)","Camera plug or wiring at the windscreen damaged"],["Service front camera or pre-collision assist unavailable message","Lane keeping and auto high beam off","Code only stored as history"],3,0,["U023B","U023C","U053B","U0235"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ A"],U023B:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Module B","U023B points to image processing module B. GM uses it on its newer Super Cruise vehicles: PI PIC6607 (2026 Cadillac LYRIQ and VISTIQ) lists U023B SYM00 as a history entry next to U3000, U1624, U0140 and U053C and states that these do not explain a Super Cruise unavailable message, so the image processing module must not be replaced for them; the real fault is found with GM's Super Cruise diagnosis.",["History entry without effect (GM PIC6607)","Image processing module software outdated","Power, ground or bus wiring to module B interrupted"],["Super Cruise or camera based assistance unavailable","Surround view camera image blank"],3,0,["U023A","U023C","U053C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ B"],U023C:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Module C","U023C covers image processing module C, which GM uses for the video processing module (VPM) of its surround vision system. Bulletin 21-NA-209 (2021 Cadillac Escalade and Escalade ESV with RPO UXP) describes a black radio screen showing a triangle and a struck-through camera, with U023C and B1A62 current in the VPM K157;",["Video processing module software (GM 21-NA-209)","Fuse or supply to the video processing module","Camera or bus wiring to the module damaged"],["Black display with crossed-out camera symbol","Surround view cameras unavailable","Adaptive cruise control disabled"],3,0,["U023A","U023B","U053D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ C"],U023D:["Lost Communication With Front Distance Range Sensor - Left","U023D means the left front distance range sensor, a short range corner radar that watches the area ahead and to the left of the bumper, has stopped reporting. Corner radars widen the field of view of the central long range radar, which helps adaptive cruise pick up cutting-in traffic.",["Connector or harness at the left front corner damaged (collision, bumper work)","Road salt corrosion at the radar plug","Left front corner radar faulty"],["Adaptive cruise control unavailable","Front cross traffic or collision assist limited"],3,0,["U023E","U0235","U043B"],""],U023E:["Lost Communication With Front Distance Range Sensor - Right","U023E is the mirror image for the right front corner: the short range radar on the passenger side of the front bumper no longer delivers its object data. Together with the left unit (U023D) and the centre long range radar (U0235) it gives adaptive cruise and collision assistance a wider view of vehicles merging into the lane.",["Right front corner radar wiring damaged after collision or bumper removal","Supply or bus fault shared with the left corner radar","Right front corner radar faulty"],["Adaptive cruise control switched off","Driver assistance warning on the cluster"],3,0,["U023D","U0235","U043C"],""],U0240:["Lost Communication With Entrapment Control Module B","U0240 flags the second anti-trap unit, entrapment control module B, as missing on the network. Where a vehicle has more than one automatically closing panel, for example a sunroof plus a power sliding door, each may carry its own reversal electronics, and B denotes one of them as assigned by the maker; no manufacturer documents U0240 publicly.",["Module B without power or ground","Wiring broken in a moving harness (sliding door, roof frame)","Entrapment control module B faulty"],["Automatic close function of a panel disabled","Panel only moves while the switch is held"],2,0,["U0239","U053A"],""],U0241:["Lost Communication With Headlamp Control Module A","Headlamp control module A runs the electronic front lighting, for example beam levelling, cornering light or LED segments. Ford calls it HCM; it sits on the vehicle network and logs network faults of its own, as on the 2017 Lincoln MKZ after remote start (SSM 46508). U0241 is stored by a listener such as the body controller, cluster or gateway once the periodic frames of module A stop arriving within its timeout;",["Headlamp module without power or ground (fuse, connector at the lamp)","Damaged or corroded bus wiring in the front end, often after a collision or lamp replacement","Network disturbed by another module or accessory staying awake (Land Rover cooler box)","Headlamp module software fault or internal failure"],["Headlamp or adaptive lighting warning in the cluster","Cornering, levelling or matrix functions inactive, basic low beam only","Several U codes in other modules at the same time"],2,0,["U0242","U0542","U0181","U0182"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת פנס ראשי‏ A"],U0242:["Lost Communication With Headlamp Control Module B","Many cars fit one control module per headlamp, and the second one carries letter B. Jaguar labels the pair HCMA and HCMB on the 2020 XE (SSM74402), Bentley addresses them as light control left and right on the Continental GT (campaign 2056293/1), and a 2024 scan-tool release lists an HCMB for the Land Rover Discovery Sport. Which side B serves is not published. U0242 itself appears in no maker document;",["Module B without power or ground, e.g. blown fuse or loose lamp connector","Fault in a fuse, ground or bus branch shared with module A","Headlamp replaced without programming or with mismatched software","Module B internally faulty"],["Lighting warning in the cluster","Headlamp on one side without adaptive or LED functions","Daytime running or position light out on one side"],2,0,["U0241","U0543","U0542"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת פנס ראשי‏ B"],U0243:["Lost Communication With Parking Assist Control Module B","Parking assist module B is a second parking controller beside the main one, which J2012 covers with U0159. Stellantis uses the code by name: on 2021–2023 Jeep Grand Cherokee and 2022–2023 Wagoneer and Grand Wagoneer the cluster and the module listed as ETM store U0243-00 for lost contact with the central vision park assist module (CVPAM), which handles the surround view cameras, while body, steering and blind spot…",["Camera/park module hung by software, recovers after a power reset or update","Module B without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Bus wiring or connector to the module damaged or corroded","Module B internally faulty"],["Blue or blank screen in surround, front or rear camera view","Parking aid unavailable message","U0159 stored in several other modules at the same time"],2,0,["U0159","U0544"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ B"],U0244:["Lost Communication With Running Board Control Module A","Power running boards fold out when a door opens and stow when doors close or the vehicle starts moving; Ford's running board control module (RBM) runs the motors. Ford documents U0244 directly: on 2027 Expedition and Navigator the boards intermittently refuse to move and the cluster shows a running board fault message;",["Software fault in the module hosting the running board function (Ford 2027: driver seat module)","Low or fully discharged battery that left the module offline","Damaged or corroded wiring and connectors exposed under the body","Running board module internally faulty"],["Power running board fault message in the cluster","Boards stay extended or retracted","Seat heating, cooling or memory affected at the same time (Ford 2027)"],2,0,["U0251","U0545","U0208"],""],U0245:["Lost Communication With Entertainment Control Module - Front","The front entertainment module is the head unit with radio, navigation and the central display. Mitsubishi uses U0245 for this unit and spells out the logic: in its workshop manuals the combination meter sets the code when, with ignition on, 10–16 V and an intact supply fuse, it receives nothing from the audio visual navigation unit for 2,500 ms;",["Head unit rebooting or being updated, code left behind as history (erase afterwards)","Head unit without power or ground (fuse, connector behind the dash)","CAN wiring or connector between head unit and receiving module faulty","Head unit internally faulty"],["Radio and central display dark or frozen","Rear camera image or climate display on the screen missing","U0245 stored in several modules at once"],2,0,["U0546","U0249","U0196","U0184"],""],U0246:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module E","Seat control module E belongs to the letters beyond driver and passenger units. Ford fills it with the front seat climate control module (SCME), which runs heating and the backrest and cushion fans of the front seats; its 2024 module list in a scan-tool release names SCME that way.",["Loose, pinched or corroded connector under the front seat","Climate seat module without power or ground (fuse)","Module replaced or updated without correct configuration","Climate seat module internally faulty"],["Front seat heating and ventilation inoperative","Seat climate buttons or touchscreen entries without response"],2,0,["U0247","U0547","U0208","U0209"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ E"],U0247:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module F","In Ford's module naming, letter F stands for the rear seat climate control module (SCMF), the unit that heats and, where fitted, ventilates the second-row outboard seats; a 2024 scan-tool release lists it next to SCME for the front seats and SCMG/SCMH for the multi-contour seats.",["Harness or connector strained by folding or sliding the second-row seat","Rear climate seat module without power or ground","Module replaced without configuration","Module internally faulty, for example after liquid spilled on the seat"],["Rear seat heating or ventilation inoperative","Rear seat climate buttons without response"],2,0,["U0246","U0548","U0210","U0211"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ F"],U0248:["Lost Communication With Remote Accessory Module","No manufacturer explains publicly what the remote accessory module does or when U0248 is set. The name suggests a body-side unit that switches accessories outside the main controllers. Separate codes exist for Ford's SYNC interface unit (APIM, U0253) and for a remote start module (U0254).",["Module without power or ground (fuse, connector)","Retrofitted or removed accessory, module configured but not present","Bus wiring or connector to the module damaged","Module internally faulty"],["Accessory function controlled by the module inoperative","Code stored in other modules without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0549","U0253","U0254"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול אביזרים מרוחק"],U0249:["Lost Communication With Entertainment Control Module - Rear B","Rear B is the second rear entertainment unit; GM applies the code to a concrete part. Its 2011 Saab 9-5 code list names U0249 as lost communication with the rear radio audio control module, the rear seat audio controls with their own headphone outputs.",["Chafed or burnt network wiring elsewhere in the vehicle (GM: harness on muffler)","Rear unit without power or ground","Loose or corroded connector at the rear unit","Rear unit internally faulty"],["Rear audio controls or headphone outputs dead","Second rear screen without picture","Many U codes across modules, radio may switch off while driving"],2,0,["U0196","U054A","U0245","U0497"],""],U024A:["Lost Communication With Interior Lighting Control Module A","Interior lighting control module A switches and dims cabin lights such as dome, footwell and ambient strips. In newer cars these are often small LIN nodes under a master, usually the body controller. A Microchip demo board for LIN ambient light illustrates the traffic: the master sends colour and brightness per zone and polls a status frame back.",["Loose or corroded plug at a roof, door or footwell light unit","LIN line chafed or pinched in headliner, door or trim","Lighting module without power or ground","Lighting module internally faulty"],["Interior lights do not come on or stay on","Ambient lighting colour or brightness cannot be changed"],1,0,["U02BF","U054B","U05C0"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת תאורה פנימית‏ A"],U024B:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module G","Ford assigns seat control module G to the driver's multi-contour seat (SCMG), which runs massage and lumbar adjustment. Two Ford bulletins name U024B. TSB 19-2293, later 19-2390, covers multi-contour seats from the 2013 MKZ to 2019 F-150, Explorer, Expedition and Navigator: massage and lumbar respond only now and then from the switch or touchscreen, sometimes with B1471, U024B or U024C, because terminals fret in the…",["Fretting corrosion in the SCMG connector terminals under the seat","Module misconfigured after a software update (configuration app not run)","Seat harness strained by seat travel or poor routing","Multi-contour seat module internally faulty"],["Driver seat massage and lumbar inoperative or intermittent","Seat settings on the SYNC screen without response","B1471 stored alongside"],2,0,["U024C","U054C","U0208","U024D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ G"],U024C:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module H","Seat control module H is Ford's passenger multi-contour seat module (SCMH), the mirror of the driver unit G. It shares the fretting connector problem of TSB 19-2293: on the listed Ford and Lincoln vehicles passenger massage and lumbar act up, sometimes with U024C stored, and the repair replaces the SCMH connector and reroutes the harness.",["Fretting corrosion in the SCMH connector terminals","SCMH misconfigured after a software update","Passenger seat harness strained by seat movement","Passenger multi-contour module internally faulty"],["Passenger seat massage or lumbar inoperative or intermittent","Passenger seat functions unavailable on the SYNC screen"],2,0,["U024B","U054D","U0209"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ H"],U024D:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module J","Ford uses seat control module J (SCMJ), also called power fold seat module (PFSM), for the electrically folding third row. On 2025 Expedition and Navigator a software fault made the seats ignore the 3L, Both and 3R buttons; a relearn with the engine running and the liftgate open, holding Both for one minute and five seconds more after the seats stop, restores them until an update arrives (SSM 53681).",["Harness or connector damaged where it flexes with the folding seat","Fold seat module without power or ground (fuse)","Module software locked up, needs relearn or update","Fold seat module internally faulty"],["Third-row power fold buttons without effect","Seats stop half-way or stand misaligned"],2,0,["U054E","U024B","U024C","U0277","U0278"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ J"],U024E:["Lost Communication With Side Obstacle Detection Control Module C","Side obstacle detection modules are radar units that watch the blind spots and crossing traffic. Left and right units have their own codes, U0232 and U0233; letters C and D cover extra units. Ford names all four in SSM 51903 and its successors 53018 and 53569: SODL, SODR, SODCMC and SODCMD on 2021–2025 Ford and Lincoln models.",["Radar connector or harness in the bumper damaged, wet or corroded","Replacement or used module not configured for the vehicle","Radar module without power or ground","Radar module internally faulty"],["Blind spot system unavailable message","Blind spot and cross-traffic alerts missing"],2,0,["U024F","U054F","U0232","U0233"],""],U024F:["Lost Communication With Side Obstacle Detection Control Module D","Module D is the fourth side radar in Ford's scheme beside SODL, SODR and SODCMC. Ford's bulletins list SODCMD among units that log U2100 or U3002 after replacement on 2021–2025 models; SSM 53569 adds that a VIN mismatch can also follow swapping a tail lamp from another car, and that radar modules cannot move between vehicles without programming. Which corner D covers is not published. No maker document uses U024F.",["Rear radar harness chafed or heat-damaged near exhaust or bumper","Module or tail lamp from another vehicle fitted without programming","Radar module without power or ground","Radar module internally faulty"],["Side assist or blind spot warning message","One monitoring zone without alerts"],2,0,["U024E","U0550","U0232","U0233"],""],U0250:["Lost Communication With Impact Classification System Module","Within the airbag system, an impact classification module sorts a collision by type and force, so that airbags and belt pretensioners fire in the right combination and stage. U0250 is logged when its messages no longer reach the network, most plausibly by the restraint control module. No manufacturer publishes a description, timeout or fault type for this code.",["Loose or corroded connector or damaged harness to the module, often after body repair","Module without power or ground","Module damaged in a collision or not set up after replacement","Module internally faulty"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code also stored in the restraint control module"],4,0,["U0551","U0151"],""],U0251:["Lost Communication With Running Board Control Module B","Letter B denotes a second running board controller, which only exists where each side has its own unit. Ford's documented power running boards rely on a single running board control module (RBM): its 2015–2022 bulletins describe one RBM that logs U3003:16 and turns the feature from Auto to Off after a low or flat battery (SSM 50154) and one whose software flips the setting on F-Super Duty (SSM 52411).",["Water or salt corrosion at underbody connectors and wiring","Low or flat battery that left the module offline","Module without power or ground (fuse)","Module internally faulty"],["Running board on one side does not deploy or retract","Running board fault message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0244","U0552","U0545"],""],U0252:["Lost Communication With Lighting Control Module - Rear B","Module B for rear lighting is the second unit driving lamps at the back end, and in practice it is often the trailer electronics. GM's code list for the 2011 Saab 9-5 assigns U0252 to the trailer interface control module.",["Trailer or rear lighting module stuck off the bus, software needs reset or update (Ford TRM)","Loose or badly tightened body ground shared with the module (Ford G201)","Damaged or corroded harness and connectors at the rear or tow bar area","Stored history entry from a module self-test without a real fault"],["Trailer brake module fault or trailer warning in the cluster","Trailer lamps or rear lighting functions inoperative","Further U codes such as U0137 in body control module, cluster or steering module"],2,0,["U0553","U0137","U0182","U0140"],""],U0253:["Lost Communication With Accessory Protocol Interface Module","The accessory protocol interface module is Ford's SYNC computer (APIM), which connects touchscreen, phone and voice functions with the vehicle network. Other modules log U0253 when its frames stop arriving, and Ford bulletins show several listeners: the headlamp module of the 2017 Lincoln MKZ after a remote start, cured by new HCM software (SSM 46508);",["APIM or receiving-module software fault, fixed by reprogramming or over-the-air update","APIM without power or ground (fuse, connector behind the center display)","Network overload or a module locking up after remote start or battery work","Internal failure of the SYNC module"],["Center screen dark, frozen or rebooting","Drive mode or settings fall back to default, message Drive Mode Not Available","Code stored in ABS, headlamp or switch module without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0554","U031F","U0256","U0155"],""],U0254:["Lost Communication With Remote Start Module","A remote start module runs the engine from a key fob or app so the cabin can be heated or cooled before departure. GM's list for the 2011 Saab 9-5 treats it as a network node of its own under U0254.",["Software interface mismatch between gateway and accessory starter (Subaru), no real fault","Poor installation, loose connector or missing supply of an accessory or aftermarket starter","Starter removed or disconnected while the vehicle configuration still expects it","Internal failure of the remote start module"],["Remote start does not work or stops after a short time","Code found only during a full system scan, no other complaint"],2,0,["U0555","U0146","U0258","U0167"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול התנעה מרוחקת"],U0255:["Lost Communication With Front Display Interface Module","The front display interface module is the central screen in the dashboard. Ford calls it FDIM; in the U-code table of the 2011 Saab 9-5, a GM design, the same node is the info display module with U0255.",["Gateway module locked up or its connector terminals loose, many U codes at once (GM SDGM)","Display without power or ground (fuse, connector behind the screen)","Damaged bus wiring to the display after dashboard work","Internal failure of the display module"],["Central screen black or frozen","Audio, climate or vehicle settings cannot be shown or changed","With gateway faults also dead gauges, warning messages or no crank"],2,0,["U0556","U0257","U0256","U0146"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול ממשק תצוגה קדמית"],U0256:["Lost Communication With Front Controls Interface Module A","Module A of the front controls interface collects radio and climate key presses in the middle of the dash and passes them to the network. At Ford this is the FCIM; for the 2011 Saab 9-5 GM labels U0256 as the infotainment faceplate control module.",["Panel locked up by heavy network traffic, cleared by battery reset or new software","History entry left by a body controller self-test without a real fault (Ford :87)","Loose connector or missing supply at the panel after dashboard work","Internal failure of the control panel"],["Radio and climate keys on the center panel without function","Several warning lamps or messages at once, intermittent operation","Code only as history entry in the body controller, no complaint"],2,0,["U0557","U025D","U0257","U0255"],""],U0257:["Lost Communication With Front Controls/Display Interface Module","Some vehicles combine keys and screen in a single front controls/display interface module. Ford calls such a unit FCDIM, for example with the small audio display on the Escape (2013-2016) and the 2016 Transit Connect, Transit and Focus (SSM 47234), while the 2011 Saab 9-5 reserves U0257 for a unit merging info display and faceplate.",["Software fault in the combined display unit (Audi panoramic display)","Unit without power or ground, or connector not fully seated after dashboard work","Internal failure of the combined controls/display unit","Fault on the infotainment bus branch shared with other units"],["Screen does not respond to touch or stays dark","Radio preset or menu keys without function or erratic"],2,0,["U0558","U0255","U0256"],""],U0258:["Lost Communication With Radio Transceiver","Despite its name this unit has nothing to do with the audio tuner: Ford's radio transceiver module (RTM) handles the wireless link to keys and remote accessories. On the 2021-2022 Bronco Sport, Ford traced No Key Detected messages to blocked key frequencies or a flat key battery and advised laying the key in the forward console tray, the backup position close to the RTM (SSM 50341);",["Transceiver without power or ground, or loose connector","Open or shorted data line between transceiver and its master module","Transceiver software or configuration not matching after replacement","Internal failure of the radio transceiver"],["No Key Detected or key not recognized at start-up","Keyless entry, remote locking or keypad without function"],2,0,["U0559","U0254","U0167","U0140"],""],U0259:["Lost Communication With Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module A","A special purpose vehicle control module is extra electronics for converted vehicles such as police cars, ambulances or work trucks. GM sells one from 2024 as Universal Vehicle Module (option KGU) and calls it special purpose vehicle control module for Silverado and Sierra pickups and the Tahoe and Blazer EV police vehicles.",["Add-on controller without power or ground from the body builder's circuits","Damaged or wrongly spliced bus wiring from the conversion","Retrofit without the required vehicle configuration and module programming","Internal failure of the special purpose controller"],["Light bar, siren or other conversion functions inoperative or stuck","Upfitter switches or configurable inputs without effect"],2,0,["U055A","U025A","U025B","U025C"],""],U025A:["Lost Communication With Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module B","U025A concerns the second slot for special purpose controllers. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Why more than one slot exists becomes clear from an Audi patent: it describes a configurable control module for police cars, fire engines, taxis or vehicles for disabled occupants, linked through CAN, LIN or other interfaces, that turns a standard car into a commercial vehicle by adding function units.",["Second add-on unit unpowered, often via a switched or separately fused upfit circuit","Faulty splice or connector where the conversion joins the vehicle bus","Unit removed or replaced while the vehicle still expects it","Internal failure of controller B"],["Functions of the second conversion unit inoperative","Warning or message from the conversion control panel"],2,0,["U055B","U0259","U025B","U025C"],""],U025B:["Lost Communication With Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module C","With U025B a module on the bus reports that controller C (third slot of four) has gone quiet. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Ford's body builder bulletin for its 2023 Super Duty shows a pitfall that applies to all slots: the Upfitter Integration System module only cooperates with the programming tool when it, the SYNC module and the body control module carry matching software, and trucks built before…",["Software of vehicle modules and add-on unit not at matching levels","Controller C without power or ground from the upfit circuits","Fault on the sub-bus or link through which the unit is attached","Internal failure of controller C"],["Conversion functions of unit C inoperative","Programming or configuration tool cannot reach the unit"],2,0,["U055C","U0259","U025A","U025C"],""],U025C:["Lost Communication With Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module D","U025C is the last of the four lost-communication codes for special purpose controllers and covers unit D. No manufacturer documents it publicly, and none of the published systems names more than one such controller. GM's Universal Vehicle Module passes a subset of J1939 data to third-party devices;",["Vehicle configuration lists a fourth add-on unit that is not fitted or was removed","Unit D without power, ground or bus connection","Internal failure of controller D"],["Functions of the fourth conversion unit inoperative","Code stored without any noticeable complaint"],2,0,["U055D","U0259","U025A","U025B"],""],U025D:["Lost Communication With Front Controls Interface Module B","Front controls interface module B is a second switch panel at the front where the controls are split over two units. Ford uses this name (FCIMB): on 2023 Transit vans having SYNC 3 Lite and parking aid at the rear only, the parking aid disable switch sits in that panel, and vans built between 15 March and 2 June 2023 ignored it, since the park aid module carried a wrong configuration (SSM 51837).",["Second panel without power or ground, or connector loose after dashboard work","Head unit not on the bus where the maker maps U025D to it (Mercedes)","Wrong configuration of the panel or of the module that uses its switches","Internal failure of the second control panel"],["Switches on the second front panel without function","Functions that rely on head unit data unavailable (Mercedes)"],2,0,["U055E","U0256","U0257"],""],U025E:["Lost Communication With Electronic Brake Booster Control Module A","Instead of a vacuum servo, an electronic brake booster uses a pedal travel sensor and an electric motor for the assist, which also lets regenerative braking be blended in, as in Bosch's iBooster. Mitsubishi documents U025E-00 in the engine control module of the Outlander PHEV from 2023, where it means lost contact with the EBA, the electric driven intelligent brake unit.",["Damaged CAN wiring or connector between engine or brake controllers and the booster unit","Fault in the booster's power supply (high-current fuse, ground, 12 V battery)","Internal failure of the electric brake unit","Failure of the receiving engine control module"],["Check engine lamp after repeated detection (Mitsubishi)","Brake, ABS or stability warning lamps on","Harder brake pedal or reduced regenerative braking"],4,3,["U055F","U025F","U034B","U0121"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מגבר בלם אלקטרוני‏ A"],U025F:["Lost Communication With Electronic Brake Booster Control Module B","U025F concerns a second electronic brake booster control unit, B. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and none states which physical unit would carry the letter. Bosch describes where two units make sense: in automated vehicles its integrated power brake, which merges boosting and stability control in one unit, is backed by a separate redundant brake unit, and the iBooster together with ESP supplies the…",["Second brake unit without power or ground (separate fuse or supply path)","Damaged bus wiring or connector to the redundant unit","Internal failure of brake unit B"],["Brake system or driver-assist warning in the cluster","Automated or assisted driving functions unavailable"],4,2,["U0560","U025E","U034B","U0121"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מגבר בלם אלקטרוני‏ B"],U0260:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Switch Module A","Many power seat switches now contain electronics that scan the keys and report the result over a LIN or multiplex link rather than carrying motor current. A Lear patent describes a seat motor assembly with integrated electronics that talks to an external switch over a one- or two-wire multiplex link.",["Switch module software stuck in sleep mode, reset by unplugging and fixed by update","Loose or corroded connector or broken wire at the switch in the door or seat trim","LIN line to the seat module shorted or open","Internal failure of the switch module"],["Seat cannot be adjusted with its switch","Memory, lumbar or massage keys on that switch without function"],1,0,["U0561","U0261","U0271","U0272"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ A"],U0261:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Switch Module B","Seat control switch module B is a further switch unit with its own electronics, serving another seat or seat row; which position the letter stands for is not published. Lincoln bulletins show how closely switch and seat module interact: power seats in the second row of the 2025 Navigator did not slide when the switch was pressed, the rear seat modules SCMK/SCML held B167F:11, and the cure was to run their…",["Seat module configuration or software not matching the switch (Lincoln SCMK/SCML)","Loose connector or chafed wire under the seat or in the trim of the second switch","Wrong part level of the seat switch after production or replacement","Internal failure of switch module B"],["Passenger or rear seat does not move with its switch","Seat settings missing in the center display"],1,0,["U0562","U0260","U0271","U0272"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ B"],U0262:["Lost Communication With Audio Amplifier B","Large sound systems may use a second external amplifier, audio amplifier B. Such amplifiers take part in network traffic: a patent on modular add-on sound systems explains that the factory amplifier decodes gain commands that the head unit sends over the CAN bus, and that a replacement amplifier must therefore understand the maker's bus format, such as GMLAN.",["Amplifier connector not locked or pushed back, often in the rear harness","Amplifier B without power or ground (own fuse, switched supply)","Aftermarket audio installation that removed or bypassed the second amplifier","Internal failure of amplifier B"],["Some speakers silent while others still play","Static, crackling or sound dropping out"],2,0,["U0563","U0186","U0487","U0184"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מגבר שמע‏ B"],U0263:["Lost Communication With Speech Recognition Module","A speech recognition module turns spoken commands into actions for phone, audio or navigation. Some makers place it in a separate box: FCA built Uconnect Voice Command into its hands-free unit (HFM) of 2012-2017 Journey, Charger and 300. Old software could leave it stuck while loading, unresponsive and off the bus, or deaf to the voice key on the steering wheel, and a reflash cured it (08-055-17 REV. A).",["Voice module software hangs during start-up, fixed by reflash","Voice module without power or ground, or connector loose","Fault message created by cluster or head unit software although the module works","Internal failure of the speech recognition module"],["No reaction to the voice button on the steering wheel","Message that speech recognition cannot be started","Hands-free phone functions unavailable where combined in one module"],2,0,["U0564","U0197","U0253"],""],U0264:["Lost Communication With Camera Module - Rear","The rear camera module supplies the reversing picture; whichever unit expects its messages stores U0264 when they stop, depending on the brand the radio, the body controller, the cluster or a central vision module.",["Camera connector in tailgate or liftgate loose or not fully seated, often after body work","Pinched or chafed wire in the liftgate, camera fuse blown","New camera paired with outdated software in the display or vision module","Rear camera or camera control module internally faulty"],["Black or blank screen when reverse is selected","Camera system fault message, surround view button greyed out","Code stored in radio, cluster or body controller, sometimes with blind spot faults"],2,0,["U0565","U023A","U0232"],""],U0265:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor A","GM gives sensor A a clear identity: its bulletins describe U0265 as lost contact with the front view camera on the windshield (B174W), the camera for forward collision alert and steering assistance. On 2020 Cadillac CT4 and CT5 with forward collision alert that camera could reset itself;",["Windshield camera resets or drops off the bus because of its software","Camera hardware fault when the loss recurs often and is easy to repeat","Connector or supply at the camera mount disturbed, e.g. after windshield work","Fault on the shared bus that silences several sensors at once"],["Service Driver Assist or front camera message, lane and collision functions unavailable","Steering assist reduced message on some models","Emergency braking lamp briefly amber, then normal again"],3,0,["U0566","U026A","U0268","U0269","U0075"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ A"],U0266:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor B","Image processing sensor B has a documented owner at FCA, which reads U0266-00 as lost communication with the left camera of its 360-degree surround view. The central vision processing module (CVPM) takes each camera on its own colour-coded coaxial plug. On a 2022 Ram 1500 the driver mirror image stayed dark while every other camera worked, along with B23C6-92 and B23C6-1C;",["Coaxial camera lead in the driver door harness damaged or unplugged","Door or kick panel connector not secured after door repair","Camera plug loose at the central vision processing module","Left mirror camera internally faulty"],["Left side of the surround or top view black, other views normal","Fault appears intermittently, often after door work","Left camera performance code stored as well"],2,0,["U0567","U0264","U0267","U0265"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ B"],U0267:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor C","No vehicle maker documents U0267 in public service material, so the camera behind letter C remains unknown, and letters are assigned differently from brand to brand. What can break is clear from the hardware. Cameras usually send their data over a coaxial or twisted-pair serial link, and the receiving deserializer reports a lock status for each port;",["Camera link cable open or shorted, connector corroded","Link loses lock due to bit errors from a degraded cable or interference","Sensor C without supply, for example power over the coaxial line missing","Sensor C internally faulty"],["One camera view or camera-based assistant unavailable","Service message for the camera or driver assistance"],2,0,["U0568","U0266","U0268"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ C"],U0268:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor D","GM files U0268 among the codes of its object detection bus, a separate network that links the active safety module with the radars and the front camera on Cadillac Escalades of model years 2015–2020 equipped with driver assistance. Which sensor letter D denotes is not stated in the bulletins.",["Front fascia harness chafed at the right bumper bar, fuses blown","Connector of sensor D loose or damaged after front-end repairs","Short or open on the object detection bus","Sensor D internally faulty"],["Service messages for surround camera, park assist and adaptive cruise","Front parking, turn, daytime or cornering lamps dead, turn signal flashes fast","Several radar and camera U-codes stored at once"],2,0,["U0569","U0269","U026B","U026C","U0075"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ D"],U0269:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor E","U0269 is a further member of GM's object detection group, kept by the active safety module first on 2015 Escalades with the Y66 driver assist package and, after a 2017 update, on many 2013–2018 Buick, Cadillac and Chevrolet models; GM does not publish which sensor letter E names.",["Defective scan tool interface or cable on the object detection pins, false code","Object detection bus wiring damaged, for example in the front fascia","Sensor E without power or ground","Sensor E internally faulty"],["Scan tool cannot reach radars or front camera, several U-codes at once","Service Active Safety, Service Driver Assist or lane departure message","Code present only while a particular tester is connected"],2,0,["U056A","U0268","U026A","U0075"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ E"],U026A:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor F","At GM letter F belongs to the frontview camera module (K109, later B174W) on the windshield, which serves forward collision alert, IntelliBeam and the lane departure and lane keeping functions.",["Camera software sets false history codes or locks up, cured by reprogramming","Pushed-in or missing terminals in the camera connector","Supply or bus wiring to the windshield camera interrupted","Front camera module internally faulty"],["Intermittent Service Front Camera message","Lane departure warning, lane keep assist, collision alert or automatic high beam inoperative","Weak battery after standing for days, camera warm with ignition off"],2,0,["U056B","U0265","U023A","U0269"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ F"],U026B:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor G","Letter G, too, is visible only through GM: U026B appears in the active safety controller of Escalades from 2015 fitted with the Y66 assistance package, always grouped with U0265, U0268, U0269, U026A, U026C and U0075, and GM does not say which radar or camera G is. The grouping is itself the diagnostic hint.",["Common cause on the object detection bus or its supply when several codes appear","Plug or fuse of sensor G when the code appears alone","Faulty scan tool cable producing false codes","Sensor G internally faulty"],["Driver assistance or object detection service message","Code alone or together with U0075 and other sensor codes"],2,0,["U056C","U026C","U0268","U0075"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ G"],U026C:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor H","U026C rounds off the GM object detection group reported by the Escalade's active safety module; GM leaves open which sensor letter H stands for. The PIT5487 series, revised from 2016 up to version F in 2020 for model years 2015–2020, shows how the code turns up next to lighting faults.",["Chafed bumper harness supplying both lamps and sensors","Shared fuse blown by a short in the front wiring","Connector of sensor H loose or corroded","Sensor H internally faulty"],["Turn signal flashes fast, front lamps partly dead","Lamp body codes stored together with sensor U-codes","Service Driver Assist or surround camera message"],2,0,["U056D","U026B","U0268","U0075"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ H"],U026D:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor I","No manufacturer documents U026D publicly, and the camera filed under letter I is unknown. Among the image sensors that now sit on the bus as modules of their own is the driver-facing camera: Ford runs a driver status monitor camera module (CMR) on the 2021 Mustang Mach-E and later on F-150, Expedition, Navigator and Corsair.",["Wiring or connector to sensor I interrupted","Sensor I without supply or ground","Sensor I not responding because of software or configuration","Sensor I internally faulty"],["Camera-based function unavailable with a service message","Sensor not reachable in the module scan"],2,0,["U056E","U026E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ I"],U026E:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor J","U026E is not documented publicly by any manufacturer, so it is not known which camera letter J denotes. Exposed outside cameras show where such links are vulnerable. Prevost fits a side camera rear view system, eMirror, to H3-45 coaches from model year 2019 and to its X3 series.",["Water in an exposed camera housing or plug, corroded contacts","Camera lead damaged at a hinge, mirror arm or body passage","Sensor J without supply","Sensor J internally faulty"],["One camera image black or frozen","Fault more frequent in rain or after washing"],2,0,["U056F","U026D","U026F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ J"],U026F:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor K","Neither U026F nor the meaning of letter K appears in published manufacturer material. Some image sources are optional or arrive with towing equipment, and that matters before diagnosing a silent camera. GM ties the turn signal activated camera view of 2025–2026 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban, Yukon, Silverado EV and Sierra EV to option code TRG, the trailer camera provisions.",["Camera function expected although the vehicle lacks the option or configuration","Plug connection of an add-on or trailer camera open or corroded","Display or radio software not handling the camera input","Sensor K internally faulty"],["Extra camera view missing or greyed out","View works only with or only without a trailer connected"],2,0,["U0570","U026E","U0270"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ K"],U0270:["Lost Communication With Image Processing Sensor L","U0270 ends the image sensor series, and no vehicle maker documents it publicly, so the camera behind letter L is unknown. Twelve letters reflect how many image sensors a vehicle can carry, and they compete for a limited number of receiver inputs: Texas Instruments' DS90UB954 hub, for example, combines one or two camera or radar links.",["Sensor fitted or retrofitted without matching configuration, or configured but absent","Link cable or connector to sensor L interrupted","Sensor L without supply","Sensor L internally faulty"],["Function of sensor L unavailable with a service message","Fault right after retrofitting or replacing a camera"],2,0,["U0571","U026F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ L"],U0271:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Switch Module C","Seat control switch module C is a third switch unit with its own electronics that reports key presses to a seat module instead of carrying motor current. No manufacturer documents U0271 publicly, and which seat C serves is unpublished.",["Spread or loose terminals in the switch connector","Signal wire between switch and seat module chafed under the seat or in the door","Switch module C without supply or ground","Switch module C internally faulty"],["Seat does not move from this switch, other controls normal","Memory or comfort keys of this seat without function"],1,0,["U0272","U0260","U0261","U0208"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ C"],U0272:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Switch Module D","Seat control switch module D is the fourth switch unit in this series; no manufacturer documents U0272 publicly or says which seat it belongs to. Such switches need not sit on the seat at all. On 2021–2023 Escalade, Tahoe, Suburban and Yukon with the power-folding third-row bench (RPO AS8) the folding switches are in the overhead console and command the K169 folding third-row seat module;",["Wiring to a switch mounted away from the seat (console, roof, trim) interrupted","Seat module lost its learned positions or needs new calibration","Switch module D without supply or ground","Switch module D internally faulty"],["Rear or folding seat does not respond to its switch","Seat stops short of its end position"],1,0,["U0271","U0260","U0261","U0210"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ D"],U0273:["Lost Communication With Lighting Driver Control Module A","A lighting driver control module sits in or on a headlamp and powers its LED groups on command from a higher-level lamp or body controller. U0273 means that controller hears nothing from driver module A within its timeout.",["Moisture or corrosion at the headlamp connector of driver module A","Driver module A without supply or ground (fuse, splice)","Module software outdated or update interrupted","Driver module A internally faulty (often only with complete headlamp)"],["Lighting warning in the instrument cluster","Adaptive high beam, cornering light or light animation unavailable","LED segments on one headlamp dark or in a default setting"],2,0,["U0574","U0274","U0241","U0542"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ A"],U0274:["Lost Communication With Lighting Driver Control Module B","U0274 is stored when the second lighting driver control module stops answering on its network. Lincoln documents a B unit on the 2025 Navigator, listed as LDCMB and updated with the same release 25.10.08 as its three siblings, but gives no position for it.",["Bus wire or connector to driver module B open or corroded","Supply or ground of driver module B missing","Driver module B software not current after an update","Driver module B internally faulty"],["Lamp stays at one fixed brightness and ignores dimming","Lighting fault message","Adaptive light functions switched off"],2,0,["U0575","U0273","U0275"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ B"],U0275:["Lost Communication With Lighting Driver Control Module C","Driver module C is the third LED driver unit a lamp controller can address. Three or more of them appear where each headlamp has several separately driven zones, as on the 2025 Lincoln Navigator, whose release notes name LDCMC alongside A, B and D. U0275 means the controller no longer receives C's messages; the reason may be the bus, the supply or the module.",["Lamp harness or connector to module C damaged (e.g. after front-end repair)","Power or ground of module C interrupted","Module C internally faulty or overheated"],["Part of the headlamp light pattern missing or static","Warning for lighting system"],2,0,["U0576","U0274","U0276"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ C"],U0276:["Lost Communication With Lighting Driver Control Module D","U0276 closes the four-letter block: the controlling module has lost contact with lighting driver control module D. Lincoln names an LDCMD on the 2025 Navigator and updated it in the same over-the-air package as A to C; nothing more about its location is public, and no manufacturer documents U0276.",["Connector of module D loose, wet or corroded","Bus line to module D chafed or open","Module D internally faulty"],["Automatic or adaptive high beam deactivated, manual switching still works","Lighting warning in the cluster"],2,0,["U0577","U0275","U0273"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ D"],U0277:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module K","Ford uses seat control module K for a second-row seat: on the 2025 Lincoln Navigator, SCMK drives the power seat behind the driver, in SSM 54226 called the rear left-hand power seat module. Its update SCMK-25.5.5.3 was meant to make that seat store its memory positions reliably, and SSM 54226 deals with second-row seats stuck in their longitudinal position, B167F:11 stored in SCMK or SCML, which moved again only…",["Seat harness or connector under the second-row seat strained or unplugged","SCMK not configured or software update incomplete","Seat module fuse or supply open","Seat control module K internally faulty"],["Left second-row power seat does not move","Memory positions of that seat not stored or recalled"],2,0,["U0278","U0578","U024B","U0208"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ K"],U0278:["Lost Communication With Seat Control Module L","Seat control module L is the right-hand partner of K. On the 2025 Lincoln Navigator, Ford's SCML runs the second-row power seat on the passenger side; release SCML-25.5.5.3 targeted its memory function, and SSM 54226 lists it as the rear right-hand power seat module, with its own configuration app that must be run after a module change, for example when the seat ignores its fore-aft switch.",["Harness under the sliding seat damaged by seat movement","SCML configuration missing after replacement or update","Power or ground to SCML interrupted","Seat control module L internally faulty"],["Right second-row power seat inoperative","Seat memory on that seat not working"],2,0,["U0277","U0579","U024C","U0209"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מושב‏ L"],U0279:["Lost Communication With Haptic Control Module","A haptic control module produces vibrations or pulses that the occupants feel, for example in the steering wheel, a seat or the floor. Where it sits varies: the 2026 Range Rover has separate haptic floor modules under the carpet, while on the 2019–2022 Hyundai Palisade the haptic steering wheel motor is driven by the integrated central control unit, so there is no separate network node.",["Connector of the haptic module loose, e.g. after seat or carpet removal","Supply or ground of the haptic module interrupted","Vehicle configured for a haptic option the module does not match","Haptic module internally faulty"],["No vibration warning in steering wheel, seat or floor","Message about haptic or warning system in the cluster"],2,0,["U0277","U0278"],""],U027A:["Lost Communication With Battery Charger Control Module C","Module C is a third on-board charger in the same vehicle; A and B have U019B and U01BB. Several chargers on one bus need clearly separated roles, and a Lear patent shows one way: each unit reads a coded input at start-up, then joins the vehicle bus either as master with the master message set or as slave with the slave set. A slave whose input or wiring is wrong can thus vanish from the network.",["12 V supply or wake-up line of charger C missing","Bus connector at charger C corroded or not latched","Charger C coded or addressed wrongly after replacement","Charger C control electronics faulty"],["Reduced AC charging power or longer charging time","Charging fault message"],3,0,["U027B","U057B","U019B","U01BB"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ C"],U027B:["Lost Communication With Battery Charger Control Module D","U027B refers to a fourth charger unit. In multi-charger designs the units also split the control task; in a dual charger system patented by Lear, two chargers feed the battery in parallel, one regulating voltage and the other regulating current. If one partner falls silent, the remaining unit has to carry the job alone or charging is stopped.",["Low-voltage supply, fuse or wake-up of charger D missing","Bus wiring to charger D damaged or connector wet","Charger D control board faulty"],["Charging power lower than usual","Charging session aborted with a warning"],3,0,["U027A","U057C","U019B","U01BB"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ D"],U027C:["Lost Communication With Off-Board Charger Control Module","DC fast charging uses a charger outside the car, so the vehicle needs a controller that negotiates with the station. Ford has a module with almost this name in its battery-electric vehicles: the off-board charger controller (OBCC) of the Mustang Mach-E, E-Transit and F-150 Lightning.",["Supply or wake-up of the fast-charge controller missing","Controller software outdated or update failed","Bus wiring or connector to the controller faulty","Fast-charge controller internally faulty"],["DC fast charging fails or does not start","Charge failure notification on screen or in the app","AC charging still possible"],3,0,["U057D","U019B","P0CF4"],""],U0284:["Lost Communication With Active Grille Air Shutter Module A","The grille shutter actuator is a LIN node of the engine controller. GM's 2018 ECM tables set U0284 when the ECM loses the LIN link to shutter 1 for 3 counts in Run with at least 11 V; it is Type B, MIL after two trips. Ford's 2024 OBD summary lists it as a continuous monitor: entry 5 s after start at 11–16 V, fault when the AGS signal is missing over 10 s.",["Water intrusion and corrosion at the shutter actuator connector or its harness","Fault on a shared connection, e.g. with the generator (check U012D/U042E)","Unstable power supply to the actuator","Shutter actuator A internally faulty or damaged by impact"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Grille shutter warning, shutters do not open or close","Check charging system message when a shared connection is affected"],2,1,["U0285","U0585","P059F","P05A2","U012D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ A"],U0285:["Lost Communication With Active Grille Air Shutter Module B","Module B is the second shutter unit, typically the one behind the lower bumper opening. GM's 2018 ECM tables treat it as LIN device 1 (shutter 2): the ECM sets U0285 after 3 missed counts once the check has been enabled for 400 ms in Run at 11 V or more, Type B with MIL after two trips. Ford monitors it together with A in its OBD summary (signal missing over 10 s).",["Corrosion in the lower shutter harness or connector from water and salt","Lower shutter or its wiring damaged by impact or debris","Shutter actuator B internally faulty"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, often with P05AE","Lower grille shutters do not move","Active air flap warning message"],2,1,["U0284","U0586","P05AE","P05B1","U028B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ B"],U0286:["Lost Communication With Radiator Anti-Tamper Device","Some low-emission vehicles carry a catalytic radiator coating that breaks down ground-level ozone; BASF sells it as PremAir, and EPA and CARB grant 5 mg/mi credit for it. CARB requires the OBD system to watch such a direct ozone reduction system.",["Connector or wiring of the device at the radiator corroded or damaged","Anti-tamper device internally faulty","Radiator replaced and device missing or broken off"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Further codes for the ozone reduction system or radiator temperature"],2,1,["U0587","P00B1"],""],U0287:["Lost Communication With Transmission Fluid Pump Module A","An electric transmission fluid pump with its own control electronics keeps hydraulic pressure available whenever the engine stands still, in auto stop or electric driving. Stellantis calls it transmission fluid pump module 1; the TCM sets U0287 when it stops responding.",["Electric fluid pump or its integrated electronics failed","Pump connector not fully latched","Damaged high-voltage cable inducing interference on the pump circuit (hybrids)","Transmission control module software outdated"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and service transmission or hybrid message","Engine stop-start disabled","Limp mode on plug-in hybrids"],3,3,["U0588","U028A","P0B0D","P2797"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול משאבת שמן תיבה‏ A"],U0288:["Lost Communication With DC/AC Converter Control Module A","A DC/AC converter, usually called a power inverter, turns the vehicle's direct current into 120 V or 230 V alternating current for sockets in the cabin or the load bed. U0288 is logged when the module supervising those sockets stops receiving the cyclic frames of converter A.",["Body or gateway module configured for an outlet the vehicle does not have (false entry)","Outdated software in the converter or inverter system controller","Blown fuse, supply or bus wiring fault at converter A","Converter A internally failed"],["120 V or 230 V outlets without power","Outlet or power supply warning in the instrument cluster","Code stored without any noticeable symptom"],2,0,["U0289","U0589","U058A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A"],U0289:["Lost Communication With DC/AC Converter Control Module B","U0289 belongs to a second DC/AC converter, unit B, in vehicles that generate mains-voltage alternating current at two points, for example a small inverter for a console socket and a stronger one for the bed, or one converter per group of outlets. No manufacturer documents U0289 or describes a converter B in public material.",["Network configured for a second converter that is missing or not activated","No supply or ground at converter B (fuse, connector)","Bus wiring or connector to converter B damaged","Converter B internally failed"],["Some outlets dead while others still work","Power outlet warning message"],2,0,["U0288","U058A","U0589"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ B"],U028A:["Lost Communication With Transmission Fluid Pump Module B","An electric transmission fluid pump with built-in electronics holds clutch pressure and lubrication whenever the engine is stopped, in auto stop or electric driving. Module B is a second pump of this kind; U028A means the transmission or hybrid controller no longer hears its status frames. No manufacturer documents U028A or names a pump B publicly, so the reaction must be inferred from pump A.",["Electric pump B or its integrated electronics failed","Corroded or loose pump connector, oil wicking into the connector","Supply, ground or bus line to pump B interrupted","Transmission controller software outdated"],["Start-stop function no longer active","Electric driving blocked or engine keeps running","Transmission warning, harsh engagement after an engine stop"],3,3,["U0287","U058B","U0588","P0B0D","P2797"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול משאבת שמן תיבה‏ B"],U028B:["Lost Communication With Active Grille Air Shutter Module C","Shutter module C is a third, separately addressed flap actuator behind the grille or bumper, used where a front end divides its cooling air openings into several sections. Hyundai documents the code: its 2026 Palisade and Palisade Hybrid have left and right actuators for the lower active air flaps, and campaign 26-01-026H lists U028B together with U0285 and flap position codes when water enters the bumper connectors…",["Water ingress and corrosion at the bumper connector of shutter C","Front harness damaged by impact, stone chips or poor routing","Actuator C failed or seized","Fault in the controlling engine module or its LIN output"],["Check engine lamp on","Active air flap warning in the cluster","Lower flaps no longer move"],2,1,["U028C","U0285","U0284","U058C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C"],U028C:["Lost Communication With Active Grille Air Shutter Module D","Module D is the fourth grille shutter address in the code list and only matters on fronts with four independently driven flap units, for instance upper and lower flaps on each side. No manufacturer documents U028C or says where unit D sits, so its position is maker-specific.",["Moisture or corrosion at the connector of shutter D","LIN or supply wire to unit D damaged in the front end","Actuator D failed, for example after ice or impact","Wrong actuator variant or configuration after a repair"],["Check engine lamp on","Part of the shutters stays open or closed","Slightly longer warm-up or higher consumption"],2,1,["U028B","U0285","U0284","U058D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D"],U028D:["Lost Communication With Active Aerodynamic Feature Control Module A","Active aerodynamic features change the airflow around the body while driving, for example an extending front air dam, a movable wing or ride height that drops at speed. CARB defines them as active off-cycle technologies, cites grill shutters and speed-dependent ride height as examples and requires counters that record how long they are deployed.",["Element or its wiring damaged by kerbs, snow or debris","Water or corrosion at the module connector","Fuse, supply or ground of module A faulty","Control module A internally failed"],["Active aero warning message in the cluster","Element does not deploy or retract","Slightly higher consumption at highway speed"],2,0,["U028E","U028F","U0290","U0645"],""],U028E:["Lost Communication With Active Aerodynamic Feature Control Module B","U028E concerns a second aerodynamic control module, B, on vehicles that drive more than one active element or split one element into separately controlled halves. Ford's F-150 is a practical example of the latter: its active air dam has a left and a right actuator whose firmware Ford blamed for C0604 logged by the PCM (SSM 51718), and bulletin 24-2404 and its successors cure the warning Active Air Dam System Fault…",["Wiring or connector of module B damaged near the moving element","Outdated software in module B or the commanding controller","Supply or ground of module B interrupted","Module B internally failed"],["Active aero or air dam warning in the cluster","One side of an element stuck or misaligned"],2,0,["U028D","U028F","U0290","U0645"],""],U028F:["Lost Communication With Active Aerodynamic Feature Control Module C","A third aerodynamic control module, C, is found on vehicles that combine front elements with rear ones such as a deployable spoiler or an adjustable wing. Sports cars show what these rear parts do: the 2017–2019 Ford GT raises and lowers an active aero wing, and Ford's bulletin 20-2353 deals with that wing touching the body after long storage in its lowered position.",["Wiring chafed or broken at the moving rear element","Moisture in the connector of module C","Fuse, supply or ground of module C faulty","Module C internally failed"],["Spoiler or wing no longer moves","Active aero fault message, sometimes a speed limitation"],2,0,["U028D","U028E","U0290"],""],U0290:["Lost Communication With Active Aerodynamic Feature Control Module D","Module D is the last of four aerodynamic control addresses and fits vehicles in which aerodynamics are integrated with chassis functions. Ford's Mustang GTD is such a case: its hydraulic system serves both the suspension and the active aero elements, and service message SSM 55237 lists the warning Active Aero Fault together with suspension and front lift messages, caused by vehicle dynamics module software that…",["Software of module D or the vehicle dynamics controller","Bus or supply wiring to module D damaged","Moisture or corrosion at the connector of module D","Module D internally failed"],["Active aero fault message","Drive modes or top speed restricted","Aero element stuck in one position"],3,2,["U028D","U028E","U028F"],""],U0291:["Lost Communication With Gear Shift Control Module B","With shift-by-wire, the driver's lever, buttons or dial is an electronic module that sends the selected range to the transmission over the network. Gear shift control module B is a second unit of this kind; U0291 means the transmission controller has stopped receiving its messages.",["Loose or corroded connector at the second selector","Bus line to selector B chafed or interrupted","Selector variant or software not matching the transmission calibration","Selector module B internally failed"],["Gear selection at the selector has no effect","Transmission warning or flashing range display","Vehicle cannot be shifted out of Park or Neutral"],2,2,["U0103","U0592","U0404","P085E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B"],U0292:["Lost Communication With Drive Motor Control Module B","Electric and hybrid vehicles with a motor on each axle usually give the inverter of the second motor the address drive motor control module B. U0292 means the coordinating controller no longer receives its messages.",["Low-voltage harness of the second drive unit chafed","Blown supply fuse of module B","Connector at the inverter of module B loose or corroded","Inverter or control module B internally failed"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive","Drive system warnings, restricted gear selection","Only one axle driven, reduced power"],3,3,["U0110","U029B","U029C","U0593"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ B"],U0293:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Powertrain Control Module","The hybrid or EV powertrain control module coordinates engine, motors and high-voltage battery, so many controllers depend on its frames. Ford's 2019 hybrid OBD summary has the battery module set U0293 when HPCM messages are missing for 1 or 5 s, and the brake module set it because wheel torque data are lost; the 2014 list marks it with MIL.",["Supply relay or fuse of the hybrid powertrain module (e.g. IGCT relay in frost)","Software in the hybrid module, gateway or receiving module","Connector fault, including grease applied to module connectors","CAN wiring to the hybrid module damaged","Hybrid/EV powertrain control module internally failed"],["Check engine lamp or hybrid system warning","Vehicle does not become ready or will not start","Stop safely now message, loss of power"],3,3,["U0594","U0100","U0111","U0110"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מערכת ההנעה היברידי/חשמלי"],U0294:["Lost Communication With Powertrain Control Monitor Module","A powertrain control monitor module is a separate supervisor that recalculates torque, speed or driver demand and checks whether the main controller's commands stay within safe limits. U0294 is stored when that supervisor stops communicating, so the plausibility layer is missing. Ford's 2014 code list includes it lighting only the wrench symbol, never the MIL.",["Software of the monitoring or main controller (incl. cold-start behaviour)","Supply, ground or wake-up of the monitoring module faulty","Bus wiring or connector to the monitoring module damaged","Monitoring module internally failed"],["Wrench or drive system warning lamp","Reduced power or limp home","Gear selection refused, especially in cold weather"],3,2,["U0595","U0100","U0115","P060A"],""],U0295:["Lost Communication With AC/AC Converter Control Module","An AC/AC converter takes in alternating current and delivers alternating current at a different voltage or frequency, with no DC storage in between. In electric vehicles such a stage can be part of a charger: in patent US9973107B2 a matrix stage converts the three mains phases directly to a high-frequency waveform, which an isolating transformer passes on before rectification for the battery.",["Low-voltage supply or wake-up of the converter module missing","Bus wiring or connector to the converter damaged","Converter shut down after overheating or a coolant fault","Converter control module internally failed"],["AC charging not possible or interrupted","Charging or power supply warning"],3,0,["U0596","U0296","U0288"],""],U0296:["Lost Communication With AC/DC Converter Control Module A","An AC/DC converter rectifies alternating current; in plug-in vehicles the best known example is the on-board charger, which also runs in the opposite direction of an inverter feeding a motor. U0296 means converter module A no longer reports on the bus. CARB obliges plug-in hybrids to detect charger malfunctions that prevent full charging or limit the charge rate.",["Aftermarket device or Y-splitter on the diagnostic connector disturbing the bus","Outdated software in the converter or inverter module","Supply, ground or bus wiring of converter A faulty","Converter module A internally failed"],["ESC or hybrid system warning in the cluster","Pure electric driving not available","Charging from the grid not possible"],2,3,["U0297","U0597","U0598","U019B"],""],U0297:["Lost Communication With AC/DC Converter Control Module B","Converter B is a second AC/DC unit, typically an additional on-board charger that raises AC charging power when combined with the first. Patents show how such pairs are coordinated: in Porsche's US10029578B2 one charger leads and the other follows commands received over a communication link, while Hyundai's US10270273B2 has a master controller steering slave controllers for several power modules.",["Low-voltage supply or wake-up line of charger B missing","Communication line between the converters interrupted","Software or configuration does not match the fitted charger variant","Converter B internally failed"],["AC charging noticeably slower than usual","Charging system warning"],3,1,["U0296","U0598","U0597","U019B"],""],U0298:["Lost Communication With DC/DC Converter Control Module A","A DC/DC converter adapts one direct voltage to another. Hybrids and EVs use it to charge the 12 V system from the traction battery, while some start-stop cars use it to keep the voltage steady for sensitive electronics during an engine restart. U0298 means converter module A no longer answers on the bus. Ford's 2014 OBD code list contains U0298 without the MIL.",["Converter connector corroded, often from water in the battery area","Blown fuse or missing supply at converter A","Bus wiring to converter A damaged","Converter A internally failed"],["Start-stop no longer active","12 V battery discharging, charge warning","Electronics resetting during engine restarts"],2,0,["U0299","U0599","U01BD","P0A94"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ A"],U0299:["Lost Communication With DC/DC Converter Control Module B","A second DC/DC converter, B, appears where a single support stage cannot serve every consumer or where two networks are fed separately. FCA documents the code: in PCM reflash bulletins 18-023-19 Rev. B and 18-020-21, covering 2019 Cherokee models with the 3.2 V6 and stop-start, U0299 is named as loss of contact to DC-DC converter 2.",["Powertrain control module software (FCA update)","Supply, fuse or ground of converter B faulty","Bus wiring or connector to converter B damaged","Converter B internally failed, e.g. after overheating"],["Check engine lamp on","Engine does not always restart after auto stop","Start-stop function disabled"],2,1,["U0298","U059A","U0599","P0EA5","P0EA6"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ B"],U029A:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Sensor Module","The battery pack sensor module is the electronics inside the high-voltage battery that reports pack current and voltage; many designs house it together with the main contactors. U029A means the battery or vehicle controller no longer hears from it. Stellantis documents the code in the battery pack control module of the 2024 Dodge Charger with 400 V electric drive: bulletins 08-026-25 Rev. B and 08-126-25 Rev.",["Outdated software in the battery control module or sensor module","Code latched after programming because the network never went to sleep","Moisture or poor contact at the battery low-voltage connector or bus wiring","Battery pack sensor module internally failed"],["Wrench or turtle symbol, reduced power","Vehicle does not enable drive or stops charging","High-voltage system warning in the cluster"],4,2,["U059B","U0335","U0111","P2D3A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול חיישן מארז סוללת מתח גבוה"],U029B:["Lost Communication With Drive Motor Control Module C","Drive motor control module C is the inverter and controller of a third traction motor, so it only occurs on vehicles with three or four drive motors. Production examples are the tri-motor version of the GMC Hummer EV, which drives its rear axle with two motors, and Rivian's quad-motor R1T and R1S with one motor per wheel.",["Fuse, low-voltage supply or ground of module C faulty","Damaged or corroded bus wiring or connector at the drive unit","Software fault or interrupted programming of module C","Drive motor control module C internally failed"],["Reduced power warning, one motor disabled","Torque vectoring or all-wheel-drive functions unavailable","Drive system warning in the cluster"],4,2,["U029C","U0292","U059C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ C"],U029C:["Lost Communication With Drive Motor Control Module D","Letter D refers to the controller of a fourth drive motor, which presupposes individual-wheel drive. Rivian's quad-motor R1S is the familiar production case: each wheel gets its own frame-mounted Bosch motor, so torque can be split freely between all four corners at any time. U029C says module D has gone silent on the network. If it still sent frames with bad content, U059D would be stored instead;",["Fuse, low-voltage supply or ground of module D faulty","Bus wiring near the wheel drive unit chafed or wet","Software fault or failed update of module D","Drive motor control module D internally failed"],["Reduced power and loss of torque vectoring","Drive system warning in the cluster","Uneven traction when accelerating"],4,2,["U029B","U0292","U059D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ D"],U029D:["Lost Communication With NOx Sensor A","NOx sensor A is normally the engine-out or SCR inlet sensor; its control unit puts NOx and oxygen values on CAN. U029D means these frames have stopped. GM treats it as Type A: its 2016 diesel tables wait 10 s, the 2025 tables (25OBDG04A/B) about 1 s for most frames, at 11 to 18 V with the bus otherwise healthy; on the 2014 6.6 L LML the code also counted checksum errors.",["Water or corrosion in the NOx sensor module connector or harness","Blown fuse, open supply or ground of the sensor module","Sensor CAN wiring damaged or terminating resistor faulty","Engine control software with start-up timing fault","NOx sensor control unit internally failed"],["MIL on","SCR or NOx monitor not completed","Engine derate on some trucks"],2,3,["U029E","U02A1","U059E","U05A1","U030D","P2209","P2200"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן NOx‏ A"],U029E:["Lost Communication With NOx Sensor B","Sensor B usually measures NOx at the outlet, behind the SCR catalyst, so the SCR efficiency verdict depends on it. U029E is logged once its CAN messages fail to reach the engine controller. GM monitors the post-catalyst frames the same way as for sensor A and also treats a loss as Type A; Ford's 2023 diesel summary reacts after more than 1 s, and Ford's 2014 code list shows it with MIL.",["Sensor plugs swapped or not fully seated after service work","Water or corrosion in the NOx sensor connectors","Incomplete or wrong engine control module programming","NOx sensor B control unit internally failed"],["MIL on","SCR efficiency monitor not completed","Engine derate on some heavy trucks"],2,3,["U029D","U02A1","U059F","U05A2","U030E","P229E","P22A7"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן NOx‏ B"],U029F:["Lost Communication With Evaporative Emission System Leak Detection Control Module","Some evaporative systems run the leak test through a separate module that holds its own valve, pressure switch or sensor and reports results to the engine controller. U029F is stored when those reports no longer arrive.",["Damaged insulation or corroded strands in the module signal wire","Corrosion or water at the leak detection module connector","Supply or ground of the leak detection module interrupted","Leak detection module internally failed"],["MIL on","EVAP readiness not set","No noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["U05A0","U030A","P0455","P0456","P2401"],""],U02A0:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module D","Although it sits among lost-communication codes, U02A0 is a data error code. The expected slot in the invalid-data series, U04A4, had already gone to particulate matter sensor A, as Ford's 2014 code list and Volkswagen's 2014 Touareg data show, so module D's data fault landed here.",["Interface board D delivering corrupted or implausible data","Poor contact in the internal communication chain of the pack","Mismatched software between battery controller and interface modules","Damaged cell sense lead at module D"],["Hybrid or electric system warning","Reduced power or no charging","Engine runs more often on hybrids"],4,3,["U01A3","U033D","U04A3","U04A5","U04A4"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D"],U02A1:["Lost Communication With NOx Sensor C","A third NOx sensor, C, is fitted where the aftertreatment needs one more measuring point, typically behind a second SCR stage. U02A1 is set when its CAN messages no longer reach the engine controller. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG04B) wait longer than 10 s without any of its five messages, with 11 to 18 V and the bus up, and rate it Type B, so the MIL comes on after the second failed trip;",["Engine harness chafed on a hot component such as the EGR cooler","Blown fuse feeding the NOx sensor modules","Water or corrosion at the sensor C connector","NOx sensor C control unit internally failed"],["MIL on after two drives","Further NOx or PM sensor codes stored at the same time","SCR monitor for the second stage incomplete"],2,3,["U029D","U029E","U05A8","U05A9","U0352"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן NOx‏ C"],U02A2:["Lost Communication With Reductant Quality Module","The reductant quality module tells the engine or dosing controller whether the tank holds proper diesel exhaust fluid; in many trucks it is one tank sensor unit with level and temperature. U02A2 means its messages have stopped. Ford's 2023 diesel summary allows 5 s without them.",["Water in the reductant harness connectors at tank or pump","Defective DEF tank sensor unit with quality sensor","Missing supply voltage or wrong software version of the module","Damaged CAN wiring between tank sensor and controller"],["MIL and DEF system warning","Countdown to speed or restart limitation","DEF quality and level readings missing"],2,3,["U05A3","U030C","P203B","P206B","P21CD","P21DD"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול איכות אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U02A3:["Lost Communication With Particulate Matter Sensor","The particulate matter sensor behind the diesel particulate filter collects soot on a heated element; its own control unit reports the result over CAN, and the engine controller uses it to judge the filter. U02A3 means those frames have stopped. Ford's 2023 diesel summary sets it after 7 s at 11 to 16 V. GM waits 10 s and rates it Type B.",["Wrong particulate sensor variant fitted during repair","Chafed harness, blown fuse or corroded connector at the sensor unit","Engine control software with start-up timing fault","Particulate sensor control unit internally failed"],["MIL on","Particulate filter monitor not completed","Derate or inducement warning on some trucks"],2,3,["U05A4","U04A4","P24D0","P2002"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן חלקיקים"],U02A4:["Lost Communication With NH3 Sensor","An NH3 sensor reports ammonia downstream of the SCR catalyst, showing whether more reductant is dosed than the catalyst can use. Like a NOx sensor it has its own control unit on CAN; Bosch even sells a NOx sensor that delivers a selective ammonia signal alongside NOx and oxygen. U02A4 is set when the engine or dosing controller no longer receives any ammonia messages. No manufacturer documents U02A4 publicly.",["Engine calibration expects an ammonia sensor that is missing or different","Heat damage, water or corrosion at the sensor connector","Fuse, supply or ground of the sensor control unit faulty","NH3 sensor control unit internally failed"],["MIL on","SCR system warning","Higher reductant consumption possible"],2,1,["U05A5","U029E","U059F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן אמוניה"],U02A5:["Lost Communication With Reductant Heater Control Module","At roughly -11 °C diesel exhaust fluid turns solid, while EU type approval asked for usable fluid within 20 minutes of a start at -15 °C, so tank, pump and lines carry heaters. Some systems leave their switching to a separate heater control module that reports state and temperatures to the engine or dosing controller. U02A5 is set when this module goes silent. No manufacturer documents U02A5 publicly.",["Fuse, relay or supply of the heater module faulty","Water or salt corrosion at the module connector near the tank","Shared bus disturbed by another faulty module","Heater control module internally failed"],["MIL and DEF system warning","Dosing delayed in cold weather","Inducement countdown if it persists"],2,1,["U05A6","P20B9","P20BB","U02A2"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U02A6:["Lost Communication With Safety Integration Control Module","The Safety Integration Control Module is a name from the SAE code catalogue for which no carmaker publishes a role or a fitted model; the term points to a unit that bundles several safety functions, for instance restraint, braking and driver assistance data. U02A6 means another controller expects its cyclic messages and they no longer come.",["Fuse, supply or ground of the module faulty","Bus wiring or connector to the module damaged","Software or configuration fault after programming","Safety integration module internally failed"],["Several safety or assistance warnings at once","Driver assistance functions unavailable"],4,0,["U05A7"],""],U02A7:["Lost Communication With Engine Sound Control 1","Engine sound control means active sound design: a controller composes or amplifies engine sound from live data such as engine speed and torque and plays it through speakers or a structure-borne actuator, the way Volkswagen's Soundaktor or Kia's Active Sound System do. Where this runs in a separate unit, U02A7 records that unit 1 has stopped sending its network messages.",["Fuse, supply or ground of sound unit 1 faulty","Unit or function not enabled or wrongly configured","Bus wiring or connector to the unit damaged","Sound control unit 1 internally failed"],["Synthetic engine sound missing in the cabin","More audible drivetrain or road noise"],2,0,["U02A8"],"אבדה התקשורת עם בקרת צליל מנוע‏ 1"],U02A8:["Lost Communication With Engine Sound Control 2","A second engine sound control exists where one unit is not enough, for example when interior speakers and an exterior sound source are handled separately or two actuators sit at different points of the body. Active sound design covers both directions: inside it shapes what occupants hear, outside it can give a car a recognisable voice. U02A8 is stored when unit 2 drops off the network while unit 1 may still work.",["Fuse, supply or ground of sound unit 2 faulty","Water or corrosion at a connector in an exposed mounting point","Unit 2 coded as fitted but missing or disabled","Sound control unit 2 internally failed"],["Part of the engine sound effect missing","Code stored without other noticeable effect"],2,0,["U02A7"],"אבדה התקשורת עם בקרת צליל מנוע‏ 2"],U02A9:["Lost Communication With Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A","Water-cooled charge air coolers need an electric pump in the low-temperature circuit, normally run by the engine controller as a LIN node. U02A9 means the pump has stopped answering. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG04B) declare it after 2.5 s without a response while the pump is enabled and the supply is 11 to 18 V, and rate it Type A.",["Water or corrosion in the pump connector or an open inline connector","Terminals pushed out of the pump connector","Software of the LIN master controller needs an update","Charge air cooler pump electronics failed"],["MIL on","Reduced boost or hesitation at high load","Coolant warning or fan running at full speed on some models"],2,3,["U05AA","P023B","U0623","U0284"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ A"],U02AA:["Lost Communication With Engine Disconnect Clutch","In a parallel hybrid the engine disconnect clutch sits between crankshaft and motor-generator. Ford's patent US9296380B2 shows the layout: with the clutch open, the electric machine drives alone; closed, it lets the engine add torque or be started, and the controller exchanges signals with the clutch. Honda's two-motor hybrid uses a lockup clutch that couples the engine directly at higher speeds.",["Fuse, supply or ground of the clutch actuator faulty","Harness or connector at the transmission or hybrid module damaged","Software fault in actuator or hybrid controller","Clutch actuator electronics internally failed"],["Hybrid system warning, MIL possible","No electric-only driving or engine runs continuously","Rough or delayed engine starts while driving"],4,3,["U05AB"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מצמד ניתוק מנוע"],U02AB:["Lost Communication With Vehicle Thermal Management Control Module","A vehicle thermal management controller coordinates pumps, valves, fans and the refrigerant circuit that keep cabin, battery and drive electronics at temperature; Marelli markets such an integrated module for electric cars, ready for fast-charge preconditioning and OBD compliance. U02AB means this controller has stopped talking to the rest of the vehicle.",["Thermal management control module software needs an update","Fuse, supply or ground of the module faulty","Bus wiring or connector to the module damaged","Thermal management control module internally failed"],["Several warning messages in the instrument cluster","Climate control or battery conditioning limited","Reduced charging or drive power on electrified models"],4,2,["U05AC","U02AE","U0623"],""],U02AC:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control A","Boost control A is the actuator that sets boost, usually a vane or wastegate drive with its own electronics that receives targets and reports status over a data link. U02AC means the engine controller has stopped hearing from it. No manufacturer documents U02AC publicly.",["Corroded or loose actuator connector, chafed bus wires near the hot turbocharger","Actuator loses its supply or ground (fuse, relay, ground point)","Electronics inside the boost actuator failed, often from heat","Weak 12 V battery causing modules to drop off during cranking"],["Check engine lamp","Noticeably less boost and power, engine in reduced-power mode","Boost actuator values missing or frozen in the scan tool"],3,3,["U02AD","U010C","U0656","P00AF","P0045"],"אבדה התקשורת עם בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ A"],U02AD:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control B","A second boost actuator appears on engines with two chargers, either one per cylinder bank or in a staged layout where a high-pressure and a low-pressure stage share the work. BorgWarner's two-stage patent describes a valve that shifts exhaust gradually from the small to the large turbine; its setting decides which stage does the work.",["Damaged plug or harness at actuator B, heat-aged insulation","Supply or ground of actuator B interrupted","Electronics of actuator B failed","Replacement actuator not matched or not set up for position B"],["Check engine lamp","Weak pull in the speed range where the second stage normally takes over","Engine power limited"],3,3,["U02AC","U010D","U02B0","P00B0","P004A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ B"],U02AE:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Pump","The battery coolant pump circulates coolant through the high-voltage pack. Electrically commutated pumps like Bosch's PAD2 carry their own electronics, take a speed request by PWM or LIN and report back. U02AE applies when such a pump is a bus node and stops answering the controller that runs battery thermal management. No manufacturer documents U02AE publicly.",["Moisture or corrosion in the pump connector, pushed-out terminal","Pump electronics failed (seized rotor, internal fault)","LIN/bus wire, supply fuse or ground of the pump interrupted","Software fault in the battery or thermal management controller"],["Hybrid or battery warning, possibly with the MIL","Reduced charging rate or electric drive power, especially when hot","Battery temperature rises faster than usual"],2,3,["U0694","U0695","P0C47","U02BA","U02AB"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה"],U02AF:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor","In staged turbocharging a valve in the exhaust path decides how much gas passes through the small high-pressure stage and how much goes around it. GM's patent keeps this valve closed in one load and speed region, modulates it in a transition region and coordinates it with the variable vanes; Ford's two-stage patent opens the bypass fully and cuts torque when valve control is lost.",["Heat-damaged connector or wiring at the sensor near the exhaust","Position sensor electronics failed","Sensor supply or ground missing","Fault at the engine controller input"],["Check engine lamp","Boost limited, sluggish response at low and medium engine speed","Engine in reduced-power mode"],3,3,["P22D4","P22D5","P22D8","P22CF","U02B0"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו"],U02B0:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control B Position Sensor","This code covers the digital position feedback of the second boost actuator. Its A counterpart, U0656, appears in GM's 2025 engine tables: the ECM reads the vane position as SENT frames and fails the link when frames stop updating for more than 6.25 ms while the line sits steadily low or high, or when message errors pile up, 480 failures in 600 samples, rated Type A (lamp on the first trip).",["Signal line or connector of the B position sensor damaged or corroded","Position sensor of actuator B failed (often integrated in the actuator)","5 V reference or ground of the sensor missing","Engine controller input damaged"],["Check engine lamp on the first trip","Reduced power, boost no longer regulated by actuator B","Higher smoke or emissions on diesel engines"],3,3,["U0656","U02AD","P2586","P2587","P003B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ B"],U02B1:["Lost Communication With Comfort and Convenience Display A","Comfort and convenience displays are touch screens for climate, seats and similar settings, separate from the main infotainment screen. Stellantis calls them CCDM; on the Jeep Grand Wagoneer a front unit (CCDMF) is joined by a rear unit (CCDMR) for the second row, and the front one can lock out the rear. Which of them counts as A is not published.",["Loose or damaged connector behind the display, often after dash work","Fuse, supply or ground of the display interrupted","Display module or its firmware failed","Low battery voltage during start-up"],["Comfort display stays dark or does not react","Climate or seat settings cannot be changed from that screen"],2,0,["U02B2","U05B2"],""],U02B2:["Lost Communication With Comfort and Convenience Display B","Where a vehicle carries two comfort screens, display B is normally the second one, the rear panel from which back-seat passengers set climate and seats. U02B2 means that unit has dropped off the bus while display A may keep working. No manufacturer documents U02B2 or says which screen carries the letter B.",["Harness to the rear display pinched or unplugged in the console or seat area","Rear display module failed","Fuse or ground of the rear display interrupted"],["Rear comfort display blank or frozen","Rear climate or seat functions only adjustable from the front, or not at all"],2,0,["U02B1","U05B3"],""],U02B3:["Lost Communication With Driver Monitoring System Module","The driver monitoring module evaluates an interior camera that follows where the driver looks, how open the eyes are and how the body is held, to judge distraction and drowsiness; the EU's General Safety Regulation makes distraction warning mandatory on all new vehicles from July 2026. U02B3 is logged when this module stops talking to the network. No manufacturer documents U02B3 publicly.",["Deep battery discharge or replacement left the module offline","Connector at the camera or module loose, e.g. after steering column or dash work","Driver monitoring module or camera failed"],["Driver attention or drowsiness warning unavailable","Hands-free or lane assistance switched off with a service message","Stored driver profiles not recognised"],2,0,["U05B4"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול מערכת ניטור נהג"],U02B4:["Lost Communication With Front Radar Module A","At the front, radar modules measure range and speed of the traffic ahead, which adaptive cruise and automatic braking rely on; corner units also watch crossing traffic. U02B4 means module A no longer answers the assistance controller.",["Radar connector behind the bumper not latched, corroded or damaged after a collision","Supply, ground or fuse of the radar interrupted","Radar module failed","Low battery voltage at start-up"],["Adaptive cruise and collision warning unavailable","Driver assistance message in the cluster"],3,0,["U02B5","U05B5","U0235"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר קדמי‏ A"],U02B5:["Lost Communication With Front Radar Module B","U02B5 is set when front radar B stops answering on the network. It is one of the few codes in this group with a public manufacturer case: on the 2022 Jeep Grand Wagoneer, Stellantis STAR case S2208000105 reports Active Driving Assist as not ready while the central ADAS module (CADM) holds U02B5, because connector D1082A of the front long-range radar (LRRF), mounted behind the bumper, was not fully latched;",["Radar connector not fully latched (Stellantis LRRF connector D1082A)","Wiring or radar damaged by a front impact or bumper work","Radar module B failed"],["Driving assistant reported as not ready","Adaptive cruise and forward collision warning off"],2,0,["U02B4","U05B6","U0235"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר קדמי‏ B"],U02B6:["Lost Communication With Rear Radar Module A","Rear radar modules are hidden behind the bumper corners at the back and supply blind spot detection, which in its advanced form uses one sensor on each side, and rear cross traffic alert. U02B6 means rear radar A has stopped communicating.",["Wiring or connector in the rear bumper damaged, e.g. after a parking knock or bumper repair","Rear radar A failed (confirmed when the fault follows a left/right swap)","Water or corrosion in the radar connector"],["Blind spot warning unavailable on one side","Rear cross traffic alert off, assistance message"],3,0,["U02B7","U02B8","U02B9","U05B7","U0232"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר אחורי‏ A"],U02B7:["Lost Communication With Rear Radar Module B","U02B7 reports that rear radar B, the second corner unit at the back, has gone silent. Stellantis lists it together with U02B6 for the 2022-2023 Grand Cherokee and Wagoneer models in GPOP review 9100222 and relies on a side-to-side comparison: after a pin unlock the two rear corner radars are exchanged, so the fault either follows the sensor or stays on the harness side.",["Harness or connector on the side of radar B damaged or loose","Rear radar B failed","Radar replaced or swapped without completing the calibration drive"],["Blind spot lamp on one side stays off or shows a fault","Rear cross traffic alert unavailable"],3,0,["U02B6","U02B8","U05B8","U0233"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר אחורי‏ B"],U02B8:["Lost Communication With Rear Radar Module C","A third rear radar is only fitted where the usual left and right corner pair is extended, for instance by a sensor watching straight back or along a long body. No manufacturer documents U02B8 publicly or states where module C sits, and its invalid-data partner U05B9 is equally unpublished.",["Connector or wiring of radar C damaged or unplugged","Supply or ground of radar C missing","Rear radar C failed"],["Rear assistance functions partly unavailable, assistance message","Cross traffic or exit warning restricted"],3,0,["U02B9","U02B6","U05B9"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר אחורי‏ C"],U02B9:["Lost Communication With Rear Radar Module D","Rear radar module D completes a set of four rear sensors, a layout that only a few vehicles with extended rear sensing use. No manufacturer documents U02B9 publicly; there is no published fitting position, timeout or lamp rating. The code states that module D no longer responds on the bus.",["Wiring or connector of radar D damaged","Fuse, supply or ground of radar D interrupted","Rear radar D failed"],["Some rear assistance functions unavailable","Message about limited driver assistance"],3,0,["U02B8","U02B7","U05BA"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול רדאר אחורי‏ D"],U02BA:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B","Hybrid and electric cars cool their power electronics, such as inverter, DC/DC converter and on-board charger, with electric pumps that hang on a LIN line and report their state to a thermal or vehicle controller. U02BA means pump B of that loop no longer answers. No manufacturer documents U02BA publicly or says which pump bears the letter B.",["Loose or corroded pump connector, open or shorted LIN wire","Pump power supply or ground missing (fuse, relay, ground point)","Pump electronics failed or pump seized","Pump of another position fitted or controller software outdated"],["Warning for the hybrid/electric drive system, MIL possible","Reduced drive or charging power when the electronics warm up","Pump running constantly or not at all, 12 V battery drained"],3,3,["U063D","U02C1","P0CE9","U02AE"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B"],U02BB:["Lost Communication With EVAP System Purge Pump","The purge pump actively pushes fuel vapour from the charcoal canister into the intake, which turbocharged engines need because they often lack intake vacuum. GM fits it to models such as Blazer, Encore GX, XT4 and Silverado 1500 as a separate unit with its own electronics, linked to the ECM by LIN.",["Purge pump electronics failed (known GM failure, extended coverage)","LIN wire or pump connector damaged, corroded or unplugged","No supply from the actuator or powertrain relay, poor ground"],["Check engine light after two drives","Further EVAP or purge pump codes stored","Possible fuel smell; driving itself usually normal"],2,1,["P0441","P0496","P0455"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת טיהור מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)"],U02BC:["Lost Communication With Localization and Mapping Module","The localization and mapping module merges satellite positioning, correction data and vehicle motion signals with a detailed map, so that hands-free or automated driving knows its lane and the road ahead; Bosch offers such a GNSS-based unit for driver assistance and automation. U02BC means this module has stopped communicating.",["Ethernet harness routed too tight, connector strained or not latched","Bent or damaged Ethernet connector pins","Module supply missing or module internally faulty"],["Blind spot alert unavailable, service message in the cluster","Hands-free or advanced driver assistance disabled","Several ADAS and Ethernet codes stored at once"],3,0,["U05BD","U015C","U015D","U0081"],""],U02BD:["Lost Communication With Night Vision Control Module","The night vision control module evaluates an infrared camera, either a passive thermal unit that sees body heat or an active near-infrared system, picks out pedestrians and animals and passes image and warnings to the cluster or head-up display. U02BD is stored when a listening module, usually the body controller, hears nothing more from it.",["Misaligned or not fully seated terminals in the module connector","Bent pins on the night vision module","Module supply missing or module internally faulty"],["Night vision display stays dark or the function is unavailable","Pedestrian or animal warnings at night are missing","Matching night vision code stored in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["U05BE","B0125","U0140"],""],U02BE:["Lost Communication With Trailer Backup Assist Control Module","The trailer backup assist module steers the tow vehicle in reverse so the trailer follows a curve the driver chooses with a knob; with Ford's Pro Trailer Backup Assist the hitch angle comes from a target sticker filmed by the backup camera or from a trailer-mounted sensor. Ram names its unit TRSCM.",["Module software hangs and the unit drops off the bus (Ram 1500, 2021)","Fuse, supply or connector of the module faulty","CAN wiring to the module damaged"],["Trailer backup assist unavailable","Ram: throttle control message, MIL and rear park assist unavailable","Code stored in several modules at once"],2,1,["U05BF","U0131","U0121"],""],U02BF:["Lost Communication With Interior Lighting Control Module B","Many cars spread cabin lighting over several controllers; module B is a second unit beside module A (U024A), for example for ambient strips or a rear zone. Such nodes are usually LIN slaves of the body computer, a single-wire bus of up to about 19.2 kbit/s in which the master can detect nodes that fail. U02BF means module B no longer replies.",["LIN wire or connector of module B loose, damaged or corroded","Vehicle configuration does not match the module, module not reset after coding","Lighting module internally faulty or without supply"],["Some cabin or ambient lights stay dark","Colour or brightness of a light zone can no longer be changed"],2,0,["U024A","U05C0","U054B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת תאורה פנימית‏ B"],U02C0:["Lost Communication With Active Radiator Air Flow Control Module A","J2012 gives the active radiator air flow module its own codes, separate from the active grille shutter modules U0284 and U0285. A Hyundai patent shows the kind of hardware meant: a pair of flaps between bumper intake and radiator, fed by an air guide, whose opening meters the cooling air. U02C0 means module A of such a system has stopped answering the engine or thermal controller.",["Water ingress and corrosion at the front-end connector or harness","Flap unit or wiring damaged by stones or a minor collision","Actuator electronics of module A failed"],["Check engine light or warning lamp","Cooling flaps no longer move, slightly higher consumption"],2,1,["U05C1","U0284","U0285","P05AE"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול בקרת זרימת אוויר רדיאטור פעיל‏ A"],U02C1:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump C","U02C1 concerns the third networked pump of the electronics cooling loop, pump C, which has gone quiet on its data line. Vehicles with three such pumps assign them to different branches, and which branch pump C serves is the maker's choice; no manufacturer documents U02C1 publicly.",["Pump connector or LIN wire faulty","Look-alike pumps swapped between positions during service","Pump electronics or motor failed"],["Warning for the electric drive or charging system","Reduced power or charging rate under load or heat","Cooling fans running hard"],3,3,["U063D","U02BA","P0CEA","U0648"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C"],U0300:["Internal Control Module Software Incompatibility","U0300 is the general entry of the U03xx group: the module storing it finds that its own software, calibration or configuration does not fit, or that the modules around it run versions that do not belong together. It typically follows a module swap or flash. Ford's 2012 OBD summary uses it for a software version mismatch between electronic throttle processors, without MIL on Gen2 and with MIL on Gen3/Gen4.",["Module replaced without loading the latest software and configuration","Partner module left on an older software level after an update","Wrong module or part number fitted (e.g. with a replacement gearbox)","Programming aborted due to low voltage"],["Warning lamp or MIL, depending on the module","Function of the affected module limited, e.g. suspension levelling or throttle","Code appears right after module replacement or software update"],4,3,["U0301","U0302","U0304","P0606"],""],U0301:["Software Incompatibility With ECM/PCM","U0301 means a module has found that the engine or powertrain controller carries software or a calibration it cannot work with, most often after the ECM was replaced, flashed or coded for another variant. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 manual lists U0301 as a setup fault: tested between 9 and 16 V while the data link works, triggered by a module left unconfigured after fitting, repaired by programming rather than wiring work.",["ECM/PCM replaced or flashed without configuration","ECM and TCM on different software levels after an update","ECM coded for the wrong variant or modified by tuning","Volvo: entry left behind by a service software download"],["Check engine light or other warning lamps","Gearbox or other systems in a restricted mode","Code stored in several modules after ECM work"],4,3,["U0100","U0401","U0300","U0302"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)"],U0302:["Software Incompatibility With Transmission Control Module","U0302 points to a software or calibration conflict between the transmission controller and its partners. Volkswagen's 2014 Touareg and CC emission specification books show a typical trigger: the engine controller sets U0302 when it is coded for the wrong gearbox type, for instance it receives automatic transmission frames while coded for a manual, or is coded automatic in a manual car.",["Engine controller coded for the wrong transmission type","TCM or ECM replaced or updated without matching the partner","Programming of the TCM aborted"],["Check engine light on","Harsh or missing shifts, transmission in limp mode","Code appears after engine or transmission controller work"],4,3,["U0101","U0402","U0301","U0304"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת תיבת הילוכים"],U0303:["Software Incompatibility With Transfer Case Control Module","U0303 reports that the transfer case control module, which engages 4WD and selects the low range, runs software or a calibration another module rejects. No manufacturer documents U0303 publicly.",["Transfer case module replaced without programming or setup","Software variant does not match the transfer case or drivetrain","Engine, transmission or body controller updated, transfer case module not"],["4WD or service 4WD warning","Shifting between 2WD, 4WD or low range refused","Code appears after transfer case module work"],4,0,["U0102","U0403","U0300","U0302"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת תיבת העברה"],U0304:["Software Incompatibility With Gear Shift Control Module","U0304 is stored when a control unit, usually the transmission controller, finds that the software or calibration identity of the gear shift control module does not match what it expects. GM's generic U03xx procedure (Saab 9-5, 2011) treats such codes as configuration faults: checked at 9-16 V with normal bus traffic, no circuit test, cured by setup or programming.",["Shift selector generation or type does not match the TCM calibration (e.g. after replacement)","Shift module or TCM replaced or flashed without setup","Software update aborted, wrong file loaded"],["Gear ranges cannot be selected or the selector does not respond","Transmission warning or code shown on the selector display","Code appears right after a selector or TCM was replaced"],4,2,["U0103","U0404","U0302","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים"],U0305:["Software Incompatibility With Cruise Control Module","On current cars the cruise control module is mostly the radar unit of adaptive cruise control, which asks engine and brakes for speed changes to hold a chosen gap. U0305 is stored when another controller finds that this unit carries software or a calibration that does not belong to the vehicle, typically after a radar swap or a partial update. No manufacturer documents U0305 publicly.",["Radar/cruise module replaced or swapped from another car without programming","Wrong calibration from the factory or after an incomplete software update","Engine, brake or gateway module updated without the cruise module"],["Cruise control and adaptive distance control cannot be switched on","Driver assistance warning in the cluster, often also collision warning off","Code appears right after radar replacement, windscreen or bumper work"],4,0,["U0104","U0405","U0300","U0316"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת שיוט"],U0306:["Software Incompatibility With Fuel Injector Control Module","Some diesels fire their injectors through a separate fuel injector control module that raises the voltage and opens each injector when the engine controller commands it; Ford's 6.0 L Power Stroke used such a FICM at about 48 V, and GM's 2005 Duramax table watches its injector driver by a CAN status bit that must toggle every 20 ms.",["Used, remanufactured or wrong-variant injector module fitted without programming","Engine controller reflashed or replaced while the injector module kept old software","Programming of the injector module interrupted, e.g. by low battery voltage"],["Hard start or no start, engine may crank without firing","Rough running, misfire or reduced power","Further injector or injector module codes stored"],4,2,["U0105","U0406","U0301","U0307"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מזרק דלק"],U0307:["Software Incompatibility With Glow Plug Control Module 1","Glow plug control module 1 switches the glow plugs of a diesel and exchanges data with the engine controller, usually over LIN. U0307 means that the controller does not accept the module's software. Volkswagen's 2014 Touareg TDI specification book sets it when the software check carried out over the LIN message fails.",["Glow plug module software outdated or not matching the engine controller","Replacement glow module of another part number or engine variant fitted","Engine controller updated or replaced without updating the glow module","Disturbed LIN line corrupting the software check"],["Long cranking or no start in cold weather","White smoke and rough idle after a cold start","MIL and glow plug warning lamp on"],4,1,["U0106","U0407","U030B","P0670"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 1"],U0308:["Software Incompatibility With Throttle Actuator Control Module","U0308 flags that the throttle actuator control module carries software or a calibration that the engine controller does not accept. In most current cars throttle control lives inside the ECM/PCM, so a separate TAC module and this code are rare; no manufacturer documents U0308 publicly.",["Throttle or engine control module replaced or flashed without matching software","Wrong or outdated calibration loaded, e.g. by an engine tune","Programming aborted due to low voltage"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp mode with limited throttle opening","Code appears after module replacement or programming"],4,3,["U0107","U0408","U0301","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת"],U0309:["Software Incompatibility With Alternative Fuel Control Module","An alternative fuel control module runs the gaseous fuel side of a bi-fuel or dedicated LPG or CNG engine and works alongside the gasoline or diesel controller. CARB counts such engines as alternate-fueled vehicles that fall under OBD II.",["Gas system module software not released for the current engine controller calibration","PCM/ECM reflashed by a dealer without updating the gas system module","Gas system module replaced with a unit of another variant"],["Engine stays on or switches back to gasoline/diesel","MIL and gas system warning on","Rough running or hesitation in gas mode"],4,3,["U0108","U0409","U0300","U0301"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת דלק חלופי"],U030A:["Software Incompatibility With Evaporative Emission System Leak Detection Control Module","In some evaporative systems a dedicated module with its own pump or valve, pressure switch and electronics runs the leak test. U030A means that controller has found the module's software or calibration not to fit. No manufacturer documents U030A publicly.",["Leak detection module replaced with a unit of another part number","Engine controller reprogrammed with a calibration that expects other module software","Damaged signal wire corrupting the identification exchange"],["MIL on, usually without any drivability change","EVAP readiness monitor not completed","Further EVAP leak test codes may follow"],3,1,["U029F","P0455","P0456","U0301"],""],U030B:["Software Incompatibility With Glow Plug Control Module 2","U030B is the counterpart of U0307 for a second glow plug control module, used where an engine splits its glow plugs between two drivers, say one per bank. It is stored when the engine controller rejects the software or calibration identity of module 2, typically after only one of the two units was replaced or flashed. No manufacturer documents U030B publicly.",["Only glow module 2 (or only module 1) replaced, software levels now differ","Module of another part number or engine variant installed in position 2","Engine controller updated without the second glow module"],["Hard cold start, uneven running until warm","White smoke after starting in the cold","MIL and glow plug warning on"],4,1,["U019C","U049D","U0307","P0380"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 2"],U030C:["Software Incompatibility With Reductant Quality Module","The reductant quality module tells the SCR system whether the tank holds proper urea solution (DEF/AdBlue); in many trucks it sits in the tank unit together with level and temperature sensing. U030C means the engine or dosing controller has rejected its software or calibration, as after a tank or sensor replacement with the wrong part number. Ford's 2014 code interpretation flags U030C as a MIL code;",["DEF tank unit or quality sensor of a different part number installed","Engine or dosing controller updated, quality module left on old software","Programming interrupted or wrong file loaded"],["MIL and DEF/AdBlue system warning","Countdown to speed limitation or no-restart shown","Code appears after tank, heater or sensor replacement"],4,3,["U02A2","U05A3","U030F","P2BA9"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול איכות אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U030D:["Software Incompatibility With NOx Sensor A","NOx sensor A is in most layouts the upstream sensor ahead of the SCR catalyst; its own control unit measures NOx and oxygen and sends both on CAN. U030D shows that the engine controller does not accept the software or calibration of this smart sensor, a frequent result of fitting a sensor meant for another engine or model year. Ford's 2014 code interpretation lists U030D with the MIL marker.",["Replacement NOx sensor of another part number or software level fitted","Aftermarket sensor whose identification the controller rejects","Engine controller updated to a calibration that expects a newer sensor"],["MIL on, SCR or emission system warning","NOx and SCR readiness monitors incomplete","Possible DEF countdown or reduced power on some trucks"],2,3,["U029D","U059E","U030E","P2200"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול חיישן NOx‏ A"],U030E:["Software Incompatibility With NOx Sensor B","NOx sensor B is usually the downstream sensor after the SCR catalyst, the one whose reading reveals how well the catalyst converts and guides the correction of urea dosing. U030E is stored when its software or calibration identity does not match what the engine controller expects, for instance after a replacement sensor with another part number or a controller update the sensor does not support.",["Downstream NOx sensor replaced with a part of another number or software level","Upstream and downstream sensors swapped or coded to the wrong position","Engine controller update requiring a newer sensor version"],["MIL and SCR/emission warning","SCR efficiency monitor never completes","Possible DEF countdown on some trucks"],2,3,["U029E","U059F","U030D","P20EE"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול חיישן NOx‏ B"],U030F:["Software Incompatibility With Reductant Control Module","The reductant control module runs the urea side of an SCR system: pump, dosing valve, line heaters and level reading. U030F means the engine controller has found that this module's software or calibration does not belong with its own, for example after either unit was swapped or reflashed. No manufacturer documents U030F publicly, but how software-dependent the module is can be seen in bulletins.",["Dosing/reductant control unit software outdated or not released for the engine calibration","Dosing unit or DEF tank assembly with integrated controller replaced by another variant","Engine controller reprogrammed without the reductant control module"],["MIL and DEF/SCR warning in the cluster","Wrong or frozen DEF level display","Countdown to speed limit or reduced power"],4,3,["U010E","U040F","U030C","P20EE"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U0310:["Software Incompatibility With Fuel Pump Control Module","A fuel pump control module drives the in-tank pump at variable speed so that the pressure requested by the engine controller is reached. U0310 is set when the two controllers do not accept each other's software or calibration. No manufacturer documents U0310 publicly.",["Replacement or aftermarket pump module with software for another application","Engine controller reprogrammed, matching FPCM calibration not loaded","Interrupted programming of the pump module"],["Hard start or no start, stalling","Hesitation, lean running or misfire under load","MIL and fuel pressure codes"],4,3,["U0109","U0410","U0301","P0627"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת משאבת דלק"],U0311:["Software Incompatibility With Drive Motor Control Module","The drive motor control module, often built into the inverter, turns battery power into phase currents for an electric traction motor and reports torque and speed. U0311 means a partner, typically the hybrid or vehicle controller, rejects the module's software or calibration. No manufacturer documents U0311 publicly.",["Drive motor control module software behind the level the vehicle controller expects","Only one of two drive motor modules (front/rear) updated or replaced","Inverter or drive unit replaced without programming and setup"],["Reduced propulsion power or vehicle will not drive","Hybrid/EV system warning and MIL","Jerky acceleration or one-pedal driving switched off"],4,3,["U0110","U0411","U0312","U0293"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה"],U0312:["Software Incompatibility With Battery Energy Control Module A","Battery energy control module A supervises the high-voltage or 48 V battery: cell voltages, temperatures, current, state of charge and contactors. U0312 is stored when a partner, usually the hybrid or vehicle controller, refuses the BECM's software or calibration, for example after a pack or module replacement. Ford's 2014 code interpretation marks U0312 as a MIL code.",["BECM calibration outdated or not matching the hybrid controller software","Battery pack or BECM replaced without programming","Hybrid or vehicle controller updated without the BECM"],["Hybrid/EV system warning and MIL","Electric driving or charging limited or unavailable","Engine runs more often in hybrids"],4,3,["U0111","U0412","U0313","U0335"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ A"],U0313:["Software Incompatibility With Battery Energy Control Module B","Battery energy control module B is a second battery controller, for instance a sub-unit inside the pack that measures part of the cells for the main battery management. U0313 means the network does not accept its software or calibration. No manufacturer documents U0313 publicly. Mitsubishi's 2018 Outlander PHEV has such a pair: the main BMU expects frames from a sub-BMU and records U0112 after 0.3 s without them.",["Sub-module software outdated or faulty, newer level required","Module B or battery section replaced with a different variant","Main battery management updated without module B"],["Several warning lamps including MIL and hybrid system warning","Power or speed limited until the next restart","Electric operation or charging restricted"],4,3,["U0112","U0413","U0312","U0335"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ B"],U0314:["Software Incompatibility With Four-Wheel Drive Clutch Control Module","The four-wheel-drive clutch control module decides how much torque an on-demand coupling, such as a Haldex-type multi-plate clutch, passes to the secondary axle, using wheel speed, torque and brake data from other units. U0314 is stored when one of those partners rejects the module's software or calibration, for instance after the coupling, its controller or the engine controller was replaced or updated separately.",["Coupling or its controller replaced without programming or coding","AWD software level not matching engine, transmission or ABS software","Used module from a vehicle with another drivetrain variant"],["AWD/4WD warning, drive only on one axle","Reduced traction on slippery roads or when pulling away","Code appears after coupling or controller work"],4,2,["U0114","U0414","U0303","U0315"],""],U0315:["Software Incompatibility With Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Control Module","U0315 concerns the ABS control module, which on most cars also hosts traction and stability control. A partner module stores the code when the brake controller's software, calibration or option configuration does not fit, typically after a module was replaced without setup.",["ABS/EBCM replaced and not configured or programmed for the vehicle","Used unit from a vehicle with different equipment or drivetrain","Engine, steering or chassis module updated to a level the ABS unit does not support"],["ABS, traction control and stability warning lamps on","Stability and assistance functions switched off","Code present right after brake module replacement"],4,0,["U0121","U0415","U0316","U0318"],""],U0316:["Software Incompatibility With Vehicle Dynamics Control Module","U0316 means the vehicle dynamics control module, the electronic stability control unit, reports a software or calibration identity another module does not accept, typically after it was replaced or reflashed without setup. GM's U03xx procedure (Saab 9-5, 2011) runs at 9-16 V and sets such codes when a module is not configured properly; GM itself uses U0315 for its electronic brake module.",["Stability control module replaced or flashed without setup/coding","Software variant does not match vehicle equipment","Mazda: fault in DSC or SAS module reported to other units (U0316:09)"],["Stability or traction control warning light on","Driver assistance functions unavailable","Code stored in several modules at once"],4,0,["U0122","U0416","U0315","U0300"],""],U0317:["Software Incompatibility With Park Brake Control Module","U0317 tells that the park brake control module of an electric parking brake runs software or a calibration another module does not accept. Following GM's generic U03xx logic it is checked at 9-16 V with normal bus traffic, sets when a module is not configured properly and needs no wiring test; the cure is setup or programming. No manufacturer documents this J2012 meaning publicly.",["Park brake module replaced or flashed without setup","Mitsubishi: CAN time-out to the EPB ECU, e.g. connector unplugged","Software level of park brake module and partner module do not match"],["Park brake warning light or message","Automatic release or hill hold not working","Code appears after park brake module work"],4,0,["U0128","U0417","U0316","U0318"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת בלם חניה"],U0318:["Software Incompatibility With Brake System Control Module","U0318 indicates a software or calibration mismatch with the brake system control module, a unit J2012 separates from the ABS module (U0315) and the vehicle dynamics module (U0316). Which box that is depends on the maker; on brake-by-wire systems or electromechanical boosters it is often the controller that builds brake pressure.",["Brake system module replaced or flashed without setup","Software level does not match the ABS/ESC or engine controller","Programming aborted due to low battery voltage"],["Brake system warning light or message","Brake assist or regenerative braking functions unavailable","Code appears after brake module service"],4,0,["U0129","U0418","U0315","U0316"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מערכת בלם"],U0319:["Software Incompatibility With Steering Effort Control Module","U0319 is set when the steering effort control module, the unit that varies steering assist, for example with road speed, reports a software or calibration identity the network does not accept. J2012 keeps it apart from the power steering control module, which has its own code U0320.",["Steering module replaced or flashed without setup","Software variant does not match vehicle configuration","Programming aborted or wrong file loaded"],["Steering heavier or assist no longer speed-dependent","Steering warning light or message","Code appears after steering module work"],4,0,["U0130","U0419","U0320","U0318"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מאמץ היגוי"],U031A:["Software Incompatibility With Transmission Range Control Module","In shift-by-wire drivelines the transmission range control module carries out the driver's range request by mechanically engaging park, reverse, neutral or drive. U031A means a partner, such as the transmission or shifter controller, rejects its software or calibration. Ford's 2014 code interpretation lists U031A without the MIL marker.",["TRCM calibration outdated or faulty, newer release available","TRCM/range actuator replaced without programming and learn procedure","Transmission or shifter controller updated without the TRCM"],["Service transmission or shift system warning","Range changes refused, car stays in Park","Wrong range shown in the display"],4,2,["U019E","U049F","U0304","U0302"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים"],U031B:["Software Incompatibility With DC/DC Converter Control Module A","DC/DC converter module A moves energy between two voltage levels, in hybrids and mild hybrids typically from the high-voltage or 48 V battery to the 12 V system. U031B means another module does not accept the converter's software.",["48 V/HV battery or its management replaced by a newer version the converter software does not support","DC/DC converter replaced without programming or coding","Converter software behind the level of the other powertrain modules"],["Often no symptom, code found during service","12 V battery or charging warning possible","Mild hybrid functions such as start-stop or recuperation limited"],4,0,["U0298","U0299","U0312","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ A"],U031C:["Software Incompatibility With Brake System Control Module B","In GM's hybrid OBD tables brake system control module B is the electromechanical brake booster (Bosch iBooster), which builds brake pressure without engine vacuum and works hand in hand with the stability control unit. The 2016 to 2019 tables describe the check behind U031C: the stability module receives a compatibility index from the booster over CAN and compares it with its own configuration.",["Brake booster unit replaced or swapped without programming to the vehicle","Stability control module updated or configured for another booster variant","Programming interrupted, for example by low battery voltage"],["MIL on and brake or stability warning in the cluster","Changed pedal feel or reduced electric brake boost","Code appears right after brake booster or ESP module work"],4,3,["U01B4","U04B5","U0318","U0315"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ B"],U031D:["Software Incompatibility With Parking Assist Control Module A","Parking assist control module A evaluates the ultrasonic bumper sensors for park distance warnings and, on newer vehicles, supports low-speed helpers such as automated parking. U031D tells that another controller considers the software or configuration of this module wrong for the vehicle.",["Vehicle or PCM configuration lists a parking or trailer feature that does not match the fitted module","Parking assist module replaced or swapped without programming","Only some modules updated, leaving the parking module on an older level"],["Wrench lamp or service message without any drivability complaint","Park distance warning or trailer hitch assist not available","Code returns after clearing until the configuration is corrected"],4,0,["U0159","U045A","U031E","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ A"],U031E:["Software Incompatibility With Parking Assist Control Module B","Parking assist control module B is a second park aid unit, found where front and rear sensors are split between controllers or an automatic parking controller sits beside the distance warning; which unit gets the letter B is decided by each maker. U031E is set when a partner module rejects the software or setup of module B, mostly after a replacement or an incomplete update. No manufacturer documents U031E publicly.",["Second parking module replaced or taken from another car without programming","Module variant does not match the fitted sensor set or parking option","Software update of the parking module interrupted or incomplete"],["Park assist unavailable message in the cluster","No warning tones from front or rear sensors","Automatic parking function cannot be started"],4,0,["U0243","U0544","U031D","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ B"],U031F:["Software Incompatibility With Accessory Protocol Interface Module","The accessory protocol interface module (APIM) is the SYNC computer, as Ford calls it, behind the centre screen, which handles audio sources, phone, voice control and navigation. U031F tells that a connected unit finds the APIM software unsuitable.",["Replacement display or other unit needs a newer SYNC software level than installed","APIM replaced or swapped without module installation and configuration","SYNC update interrupted or installed only partly"],["Centre screen stays dark or keeps rebooting","No radio, phone or navigation functions","Rear camera picture or touch controls missing on the screen"],4,0,["U0253","U0554","U0300"],""],U0320:["Software Incompatibility With Power Steering Control Module","The power steering control module drives the electric assist motor and needs calibration data that suit the steering gear and the vehicle. U0320 is logged when another module refuses to work with its software. No manufacturer documents U0320 publicly, but GM and Volkswagen show the background.",["Steering gear or steering module replaced without loading matching calibration","Steering module software older than required by the other modules","Basic setting or adaptation after programming not carried out","Programming disturbed by voltage drop"],["Steering heavy or assist only partly available","Power steering warning lamp or message","Lane keeping or park steering functions switched off"],4,2,["U0131","U0420","U0319","U0328"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת הגה כוח"],U0321:["Software Incompatibility With Suspension Control Module A","Suspension control module A manages adjustable dampers, air springs or ride height, and on some cars it also leads active roll control; some code lists call it the ride level module. U0321 tells that a partner controller considers its software unfit. No manufacturer documents U0321 publicly.",["Replacement suspension or roll control unit carries a software level the partners do not accept","Only one of the linked chassis modules updated","Suspension module coded for another equipment level"],["Suspension warning in the cluster","Ride height cannot be adjusted or vehicle sits at one level","Firm or uneven damping, more body roll"],4,2,["U0132","U0421","U0300","U0316"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מתלים‏ A"],U0322:["Software Incompatibility With Body Control Module","The body control module switches lighting, locks, wipers and many comfort functions and often holds configuration data used by other units. U0322 tells that a controller has found the BCM software or setup unfit for the vehicle. The code without a letter is meant for cars with one body controller; where two are fitted, U0331 names body control module A and U0339 module B. No manufacturer documents U0322 publicly.",["BCM replaced or swapped without loading vehicle configuration","BCM updated while a connected unit such as a headlamp module kept old software","BCM programming interrupted by low voltage or lost connection"],["Headlamps, interior lights or wipers work wrongly or not at all","Central locking or remote key functions unreliable","Several body codes stored at the same time"],4,0,["U0140","U0422","U0331","U0339"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מרכב"],U0323:["Software Incompatibility With Instrument Panel Control Module","The instrument panel control module is the cluster with gauges, warning lamps and messages; it also passes data such as units or outside temperature to other modules. U0323 means the engine controller or another unit rejects its software or coding.",["Cluster not coded for the fitted equipment, for example the ambient temperature sensor","Start-up exchange interrupted by a missing fuse, disconnected infotainment unit or quick ignition off","Cluster replaced or updated without matching configuration","Retrofitted accessory such as an alarm kit disturbing the cluster data"],["MIL or several warning lamps such as TPMS and stability control on","Codes in engine, ABS and cluster that cannot be cleared","Outside temperature or other displays missing"],2,1,["U0155","U0423","U0301","U0322"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת לוח מחוונים"],U0324:["Software Incompatibility With HVAC Control Module","The HVAC control module reads cabin and outside temperatures and drives blend doors, blower, defrosting and the request for the A/C compressor. U0324 means another controller has found its software or calibration unfit for the vehicle. No manufacturer documents U0324 publicly; GM bulletins show how tightly the HVAC calibration is tied to other parts.",["HVAC module calibration outdated or not matching the vehicle options","Connected part replaced, such as antenna, display or compressor, without matching HVAC software","HVAC module replaced or taken from another car without setup"],["Heating, cooling or defrosting works only in part","Climate settings reset or remote start climate stays off","A/C compressor not requested"],4,0,["U0164","U0424","U032A","U0325"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מיזוג אוויר"],U0325:["Software Incompatibility With Auxiliary Heater Control Module","The auxiliary heater control module runs an extra heat source: a fuel-burning or electric coolant heater, or on electrified cars a high-voltage heater that warms the cabin while the engine is off. U0325 means a connected module rejects this unit's software. No manufacturer documents U0325 publicly.",["Heater unit or its controller replaced without programming or coding","Climate or vehicle software level does not match the heater variant","Retrofitted parking heater not coded into the vehicle network"],["No auxiliary or parking heat, cabin warms only with the engine running","Heater warning or service message","On plug-in hybrids the engine starts more often for heat"],4,0,["U0166","U0425","U0324"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת גוף חימום עזר"],U0326:["Software Incompatibility With Vehicle Immobilizer Control Module","The vehicle immobilizer control module checks the transponder or smart key and releases the engine controller only after a coded exchange. U0326 means that a controller, usually the engine controller, does not accept the immobilizer's software or stored codes, mostly once either unit has been renewed or reprogrammed. No manufacturer documents U0326 publicly.",["Engine controller or immobilizer unit replaced without pairing the security codes","Used module from another vehicle fitted, carrying foreign codes","Software of engine controller and immobilizer on incompatible levels after an update"],["Engine cranks but does not start, or starts and stalls at once","Security or key lamp flashes in the cluster","Keys are not recognised after module work"],4,0,["U0167","U0426","U0327","U0301"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אימובילייזר רכב"],U0327:["Software Incompatibility With Vehicle Security Control Module","The vehicle security control module handles theft protection: alarm, monitoring of doors, bonnet and tailgate and, at some makers, the key check that unlocks the engine. Chrysler, for example, gives this job to its wireless control module, and its lost-contact code U0168 calls that unit the vehicle security control module (18-023-13).",["Security or wireless control module replaced without programming and key learning","Engine or body controller updated while the security module kept old software","Aftermarket alarm or remote start interfering with the security data"],["No start or start refused although the key is accepted at the door","Alarm triggers without reason or cannot be armed","Security lamp flashing, remote locking unreliable"],4,0,["U0168","U0427","U0326"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אבטחת רכב"],U0328:["Software Incompatibility With Steering Angle Sensor Module","The steering angle sensor module reports wheel angle and turning speed over CAN, mainly to stability control and electric power steering. U0328 means a receiving module rejects the software or variant of this sensor. No manufacturer documents U0328 publicly.",["Steering angle sensor or column part replaced without calibration or setup","Sensor of another part number or software variant fitted","Brake or steering module software does not support the fitted sensor"],["ESC, traction control or lane assist warning lamps on","Steering assist uneven or the car pulls after alignment work","Code appears after wheel alignment or steering column repair"],4,2,["U0126","U0428","U0320","U0329"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול חיישן זווית הגה"],U0329:["Software Incompatibility With Steering Column Control Module","The steering column control module gathers the stalks and wheel buttons for indicators, wipers, horn and cruise control, and on newer cars it may also handle the heated wheel or pass on the steering angle. U0329 means a partner module rejects the software of this unit. No manufacturer documents U0329 publicly.",["Replacement steering column module of the wrong variant fitted","Module installation or programming after replacement not completed","Steering column module software older than the connected modules expect"],["Indicators, wipers or horn work only partly","Cruise control or wheel buttons without reaction","Assistance functions using steering column signals unavailable"],4,0,["U0212","U0429","U0328"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת עמוד היגוי"],U032A:["Software Incompatibility With A/C Compressor Control Module","The A/C compressor control module drives an electric refrigerant compressor, as used in hybrid and electric cars, and reports speed and status to the climate controller. U032A means that controller considers the compressor module's software or learned data invalid.",["Compressor module lost its adaptation and needs the calibration routine","Climate or compressor software below the level of an open update campaign","Electric compressor replaced without programming and calibration"],["Air conditioning blows warm, compressor does not run","Fault returns after a while even when cooling was restored","On electric cars battery cooling or preconditioning may be limited"],4,0,["U016B","U046C","U0324"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן"],U0330:["Software Incompatibility With Tire Pressure Monitor Module","The tyre pressure monitor module receives the radio messages of the wheel sensors, evaluates the pressures and, on many systems, works out which sensor sits on which wheel; from this it drives the warning lamp and cluster messages. U0330 is set when a partner controller finds the software or variant of this module unsuitable, usually after a replacement or a partial update. No manufacturer documents U0330 publicly.",["TPMS module replaced or taken from another vehicle without programming and coding","Module still on a software level that the partner controllers no longer accept","Module configured for another wheel, tyre or sensor variant"],["Tyre pressure warning lamp or TPMS fault message in the cluster","Tyre pressures not shown or shown on the wrong wheel","Code appears after work on the TPMS module or a software update"],4,0,["U0127","U0430"],""],U0331:["Software Incompatibility With Body Control Module A","Body control module A is the first of several body controllers on vehicles that spread lighting, locking, wipers and power distribution over more than one unit. With a single body controller the same mismatch is reported as U0322; U0339 covers unit B. U0331 means a partner module finds the software or configuration of unit A unfit.",["Body control module A replaced without loading the vehicle configuration","Programming aborted or corrupted by an outdated diagnostic tool release","Other body modules updated while unit A stayed on its old level"],["Lighting, locking or wiper functions fail or behave oddly","Keyless start or remote locking may not work","Several modules store network codes after body module work"],4,0,["U0141","U0339","U0322","U0422"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מרכב‏ A"],U0332:["Software Incompatibility With Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A","Multi-axis acceleration sensor module A measures yaw rate plus lateral and longitudinal acceleration for stability control and driver assistance; it can be a separate box or part of another controller. U0332 means a receiving controller rejects its software or variant. No manufacturer documents U0332 publicly.",["Sensor module replaced by a part with another software or variant","Brake or suspension controller updated without matching the sensor module","Yaw rate sensor learn skipped after programming"],["Stability control or traction control warning lamp on","Driver assistance functions unavailable","Code follows module replacement or software update"],4,0,["U0125","U014E"],""],U0333:["Software Incompatibility With Gear Shift Control Module B","With shift-by-wire, both the driver's selector and the unit that actually moves the range are electronic modules; module B denotes a second such unit, either a further selector or the shift actuator. U0333 means its software or calibration does not fit the partner controller.",["Selector or actuator of another generation or part number fitted","Transmission calibration specifies a different selector than the one fitted","Shift actuator ECU still on an outdated calibration"],["Range changes requested at this unit are ignored","Transmission warning or shift indicator fault","Vehicle stays in or returns to neutral or park"],4,2,["U0291","U0592","U0304"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B"],U0334:["Software Incompatibility With Radio","On current vehicles the radio is the infotainment head unit: besides audio it runs navigation, voice control, phone connection and the setting menus for other systems such as seat heating. U0334 is stored when a controller relying on these services rejects the radio's software. No manufacturer documents U0334 publicly.",["Radio update done out of sequence or with a skipped intermediate level","Head unit replaced by a variant for another market or equipment","Other modules updated while the radio stayed on an old level"],["No sound or missing functions on the head unit","Comfort settings shown greyed out in the radio menus","Code appears after a radio update or replacement"],4,0,["U0184","U0485"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול רדיו"],U0335:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Sensor Module","The battery pack sensor module is housed in the traction battery, where it measures pack current and voltage for the battery controller. U0335 records that this controller or another partner rejects the module's software. Ford's 2014 code interpretation lists U0335 for the hybrid battery pack sensor module without a MIL marker.",["Battery controller updated without matching the sensor module, or the reverse","Sensor module or contactor box replaced with a part on another software level","Programming of the battery modules interrupted"],["Vehicle will not enter ready mode or drives with reduced power","Charging does not start or stops early","Range and state of charge shown incorrectly"],4,2,["U029A","U059B","U0312","U034C"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול חיישן מארז סוללת מתח גבוה"],U0336:["Software Incompatibility With Restraints Control Module","The restraints control module reads the crash sensors and triggers airbags and belt tensioners according to a calibration written for one body style and equipment level. U0336 means a connected unit rejects the software or configuration of this module. Ford's 2014 code interpretation lists U0336 without the MIL marker.",["Replacement airbag module delivered with an older software level and not brought up to the vehicle level","Calibration for another body style, drive or equipment loaded","Used module from another vehicle installed"],["Airbag warning lamp stays on","Further restraint codes such as airbag circuit faults stored","Code appears right after airbag module replacement"],4,0,["U0151","U0452"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מערכת הריסון"],U0337:["Software Incompatibility With Battery Charger Control Module A","Battery charger control module A is the charger built into a plug-in car: it turns mains AC into DC for the traction battery and coordinates with the charging station and the battery controller. U0337 appears when a partner module refuses the charger's software or calibration. No manufacturer documents U0337 publicly.",["On-board charger left on an older software level after other modules were updated","Charger replaced without programming to the vehicle","Charger update interrupted, for example by low 12 V supply"],["Charging does not start or stops after a short time","Charging fault message that clears only after replugging","12 V battery drained after charging sessions"],4,0,["U019B","U049C","U01BB"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ A"],U0338:["Software Incompatibility With Remote Function Actuation Module","The remote function actuation module receives key fob, passive entry and, on newer cars, phone key signals and passes lock, unlock or start requests to the body controller. U0338 means a partner rejects its software. No manufacturer documents U0338 publicly.",["Replacement module shipped with software for another network layout","Software download aborted by low voltage, a lost link or a corrupted file","Module fitted but not configured or keys not programmed"],["Remote or keyless locking does not respond","Keyless start refused or key not detected","Module not reachable by the diagnostic tool after replacement"],4,0,["U0214","U0515"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול הפעלת פונקציה מרוחקת"],U0339:["Software Incompatibility With Body Control Module B","Body control module B is a second body controller that takes over part of the switching, for example in a rear or auxiliary junction box. U0339 means a partner module rejects its software or setup; U0331 covers unit A, U0322 vehicles with a single body controller.",["Body control module B carries a configuration that does not match the vehicle","Unit B left on an older software level after an update campaign","Auxiliary junction box replaced without programming"],["Functions switched by the second body module fail, such as lights or sill plate illumination","Depending on its tasks, engine may stall or not start","Network codes in several modules after body module work"],4,0,["U0142","U0443","U0331","U0322"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מרכב‏ B"],U033A:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module A","U033A is the one code of this row that a manufacturer names in public. Volvo's bulletins for the battery-electric VNR Electric truck (KC-2288 of 2023, CBR-2288 of June 2024, the latter also valid for the Mack LRe) list it among faults that turn active right after the ESCM has been reprogrammed, together with missing-message codes for interface modules A to D.",["Battery management unit left on its old software after another controller was reprogrammed","Programming session ended before all battery-related units were flashed","Interface module A replaced and not brought to the matching level"],["Code turns active directly after a module programming session","Missing-message codes for interface modules A to D stored at the same time","High-voltage battery warning until the battery unit is reprogrammed"],4,2,["U01A0","U04A1","U033B","U0300"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U033B:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module B","Module B is the second interface board, and on GM's eAssist mild hybrids it is also the last: bulletin PIT5513D lists exactly two, K112A and K112B, for 2016–2018 Silverado and Sierra and the 2018 LaCrosse, both under the same part number 24282084. Since one spare fits either slot, the part number alone does not tell which position a board serves.",["Board B replaced with a spare carrying another software level","Battery controller software older than the board it has to accept","Identical boards A and B swapped during pack repair"],["Hybrid system or battery warning, often with the check engine lamp on PHEVs","Electric assist or electric driving reduced","Fault follows work on the battery pack"],4,2,["U01A1","U04A2","U033A","U033C"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U033C:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module C","U033C names the third interface board. GM's closest published check is its own code P1EB1 in the VITM of the Volt: at power-up the controller compares its own software version with that of all slave boards and logs P1EB1 if any one does not fit, within 200 ms, with at least 9 V and no slave lost-communication fault active.",["Board C carries a software version the battery controller does not list as compatible","Battery controller updated while the boards stayed on the old level","Unstable low-voltage supply at power-up corrupts the version exchange"],["MIL possible on hybrids, as GM rates its comparable check Type A","Hybrid or high-voltage battery warning after switching on","Electric driving or charging restricted"],4,2,["U01A2","U04A3","U033B","U033D"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C"],U033D:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module D","On the first-generation Chevrolet Volt the monitoring electronics end at the fourth board. GM's 2012 Volt table refers to four slave units through its own codes: P1EB2 to P1EB5 report a slave that answered wrongly or not at all when a programming session ended, and U2603 to U2606, listed in GM's U-code catalogue for the 2011 Saab 9-4X as loss of hybrid battery interface control modules 1 to 4, block the software…",["Programming of the fourth board aborted or answered with an error","Replacement board D still on a superseded software version","Interrupted link to board D masks or disturbs the version check"],["Code appears after programming or replacing a battery section","Hybrid warning, MIL possible on plug-in hybrids","Reduced propulsion until all boards match"],4,2,["U01A3","U02A0","U033C","U033E"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D"],U033E:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module E","A fifth interface board exists, for example, in BMW's 330e plug-in hybrid of the F30 series: bulletin SI B61 25 17 lists voltage-measurement codes for cell supervision circuits 1 to 5 in the battery electronics SME, under BMW's own numbers 21F0C2 to 21F0C6. BMW replaces a CSC only if the fault is active, has been logged five times, or twice with the MIL lit, and once harness and cell voltages have been checked.",["Fifth supervision board replaced without matching the controller software","Battery controller not updated to the part numbers now installed","Boards of different production levels combined in one pack"],["Powertrain or hybrid warning, MIL possible on plug-in hybrids","Fault stored after a battery or BMS repair","Electric range or power temporarily limited"],4,2,["U01A4","U04A5","U033D","U033F"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ E"],U033F:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module F","Public documents name no vehicle that uses U033F, nor a pack with exactly six interface boards; F is simply the sixth address in the row. What is documented is how strictly battery software must follow the hardware. Hyundai's bulletin 18-HC-003 requires a BMS parameter update whenever a replacement lithium battery is installed in a 2011–2015 Sonata Hybrid or a 2015–2017 Tucson Fuel Cell.",["Battery parameters not updated after a pack or module replacement","Board F taken from another pack with a different software level","Battery controller on an outdated calibration"],["Limp-home mode or reduced electric power","Stop/start or electric assist disabled","Battery or hybrid warning after battery service"],4,2,["U01A5","U04A6","U033E","U0340"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ F"],U0340:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module G","G is the seventh board, a position GM's 2016–2019 plug-in hybrids really have: table 16OBDG02 describes eight interface modules on a UART daisy chain to the battery system module. That table publishes lost-contact and processor tests for every board, yet it holds no counterpart to the P1EB1 version check of the older VITM design and no U0340. For G, GM thus documents silence (U01A6), not a software conflict.",["Seventh board replaced by a unit with another software level","Battery system module reflashed without the boards being brought along","Disturbed daisy-chain link garbles the version data of board G"],["Hybrid warning, MIL possible depending on the maker","Electric mode limited or unavailable","Other battery diagnostics paused while the code is active"],4,2,["U01A6","U04A7","U033F","U0341"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ G"],U0341:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module H","Packs with eight boards end at H. Besides GM's 2016–2019 plug-ins, BMW's i3 is one: bulletin SI B61 02 16 lists eight cell supervision circuits for the i3 battery and, for boards built between December 2013 and September 2014, orders all of them renewed together once diagnosis calls for a CSC.",["Software of the last board does not match after a section replacement","Only some boards renewed where the maker requires a complete set","Service tool, adapter or tool software of the wrong generation used"],["Car cannot be made ready to drive","Code set after battery section work","Drive power reduced"],4,2,["U01A7","U04A8","U0340","U0342"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ H"],U0342:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module I","Mitsubishi shows that a replaced monitoring board must first be given its place in the pack. On the 2022 Outlander plug-in hybrid, numbering of the cell monitoring units (CMU) is done at the factory;",["Replaced board not numbered or registered in the battery controller","ID numbering run while charging or aborted before completion","Board of another battery variant fitted at position I"],["Battery warning after a module or CMU replacement","EV mode or charging restricted","MIL possible on plug-in hybrids"],4,2,["U01A8","U04A9","U0341","U0343"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ I"],U0343:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module J","J, the tenth board, only appears on larger packs. BMW's i8 is a documented example with more than ten: the parts list in bulletin SI B61 02 16 counts twelve cell monitoring circuits, and the battery electronics SME carries a voltage plausibility code for each of them, numbered 1 to 12 (21F0F3 to 21F0FE).",["Tenth board carries software the battery controller does not accept","Replacement boards from different production batches combined","Internal battery bus disturbs the identification of board J"],["Car will not become ready to drive","High-voltage system switches off, contactor opens","Drivetrain malfunction message"],4,2,["U01A9","U04AA","U0342","U0344"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ J"],U0344:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module K","Eleven boards or more are found in GM's Ultium packs: according to Wikipedia the Cadillac Lyriq carries twelve modules and the Hummer EV two layers of twelve, and the battery management works wirelessly.",["Battery controller software does not accept the monitoring unit","Released software update for the battery controller not yet installed","Monitoring unit K replaced and not registered"],["Vehicle does not become ready after switching on","Battery or propulsion warning","Charging may be refused"],4,2,["U01AA","U04AB","U0343","U0345"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ K"],U0345:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module L","L is the twelfth letter and thus the last board on packs with twelve, such as the twelve CSCs of BMW's i8, provided a maker counted them this way. The mismatch behind U0345 is easy to create during battery repair.",["Battery controller logic and pack generation do not match","Update for new-generation packs applied to an old-generation pack","Twelfth board replaced with a unit of another software level"],["Hybrid warning after high-voltage battery replacement","Electric assist reduced","MIL possible on hybrids"],4,2,["U01AB","U04AC","U0344","U0346"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ L"],U0346:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module M","With M the row passes the common twelve-board size. GM's 2018 hybrid table 18OBDG02 includes lost-contact codes for interface modules up to M (U01AC) in its bundle BICM Loss of Comm and adds that GM shares software across programs, so a code counts only where the program in question uses it. A matching bundle for software codes such as U0346 is not listed.",["Thirteenth board on a software level the controller rejects","Controller software variant for another pack configuration","Board installed in the wrong layer or position of a multi-layer pack"],["Battery or propulsion warning","Power or charging limited","Code seen only on very large packs"],4,2,["U01AC","U04AD","U0345","U0347"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ M"],U0347:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module N","N, the fourteenth slot, is not tied to any vehicle in public sources. What can be shown is how false mismatch codes arise in the workshop. Volvo notes for its electric VNR that many apparent data mismatches come from TEA2+ control units not reporting to the tester; switching the truck on and letting it power up, then starting and logging into the tool, and only then plugging in the interface avoids them.",["Stale or incorrectly started tester session reports a false mismatch","Programmable module installation skipped after a battery replacement","Board N really carries incompatible software"],["Code appears during or right after a tester session","Further network codes in the battery controller","Often no change in driving once programming is completed"],4,2,["U01AD","U04AE","U0346","U0348"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ N"],U0348:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module O","O stands for a fifteenth board; no public document links U0348 to a vehicle. That the software inside a cell monitoring unit can itself be the problem is shown by Honda's recall 15V602 of October 2015: in 6,786 Accord Hybrids of 2014–2015 the cell voltage sensor (CVS) could misread electrical noise from inverter and motor circuits, a side effect of a change made for digital TV reception in Japan, and switch the car…",["Firmware of the monitoring unit itself faulty and superseded","Board O missed a released software update","Pack boards on different update levels after a partial repair"],["Fail-safe mode with reduced speed and power","Engine switched off, electric drive only until the battery is drained","Hybrid warning with audible alert"],4,2,["U01AE","U04AF","U0347","U0349"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ O"],U0349:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module P","P is the sixteenth and final letter; the following number, U034A, already names an engine disconnect clutch, so a pack with more than sixteen boards would need maker codes. No vehicle is publicly linked to U0349.",["Battery firmware so old that over-the-air updates cannot be applied","Sixteenth board replaced without matching software","Code confused with U034A, which belongs to another component"],["Software updates fail or are not offered","Battery warning after battery service","Charging or power limited in severe cases"],4,2,["U01AF","U04B0","U0348"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ P"],U034A:["Software Incompatibility With Engine Disconnect Clutch","Parallel hybrids place a disconnect clutch between combustion engine and electric drive; it couples the engine in or separates it for electric driving. Where the clutch has its own actuator controller, U034A means the hybrid or transmission controller rejects that unit's software. No manufacturer documents U034A publicly.",["Hybrid, engine and transmission controllers on software levels that do not belong together","Clutch actuator or transmission unit replaced without programming","Programming of a powertrain module interrupted"],["Engine warning lamp or transmission warning on","Electric driving or engine start-stop unavailable","Harsh engagement or loss of drive until the next key cycle"],4,2,["U02AA","U05AB","P2885"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מצמד ניתוק מנוע"],U034B:["Software Incompatibility With Brake Booster Control","Brake booster control is the electromechanical brake servo that replaces the vacuum booster and lets regenerative braking be blended in; in the VW group it is unit J539, which holds the pedal travel sensor and the motor position sensor (self-study 861213).",["Faulty software level in the electromechanical brake booster","Brake booster unit replaced without programming or coding","Brake or engine controller updated without matching the booster"],["Engine warning lamp stays on after starting","Request-MIL code stored in the engine controller","Code returns after clearing until new booster software is installed"],4,1,["U025E","U055F","U031C"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול בקרת מגבר בלם"],U034C:["Software Incompatibility With Battery Energy Control Module C","Battery energy control module C is a third battery controller, found where a high-voltage battery is split into sections with their own management electronics. U034C means the leading controller or another partner rejects its software. No manufacturer documents U034C publicly or names a unit C.",["Battery controllers on software levels that do not match each other or the vehicle controller","Battery section or its controller replaced without programming","Battery software update aborted or only partly applied"],["Reduced drive power or no ready mode","Charging refused or slower than usual","High-voltage system warning in the cluster"],4,2,["U0312","U0313","U014A","U044B"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ C"],U034D:["Software Incompatibility With Vehicle Thermal Management Control Module","The vehicle thermal management control module commands pumps, valves and fans that keep battery, drive electronics and cabin at their target temperatures. U034D means a partner controller rejects its software or calibration. No manufacturer documents U034D publicly.",["Thermal management controller on an outdated software level","Thermal management module replaced without programming","High-voltage heater or another partner updated without matching the thermal controller"],["Weak cabin heating or cooling","Charging or drive power limited to protect the battery","Warning lamp with thermal or coolant codes stored"],4,2,["U02AB","U05AC","U032A"],""],U034E:["Software Incompatibility With Active Grille Air Shutter Module A","Active grille air shutter modules are small actuator controllers, usually LIN slaves of the engine controller, that open and close flaps in the front end to speed up warm-up and cut drag. U034E means the engine controller refuses the software of shutter module A. No manufacturer documents U034E publicly.",["Shutter actuator with an unsuitable firmware level fitted","Shutter assembly for another engine or model year installed","Engine controller updated to a level that expects a different shutter"],["Check engine lamp may light depending on the maker","Upper grille flaps stay open or closed","Slower engine warm-up in cold weather"],2,0,["U0284","U0585","U034F"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ A"],U034F:["Software Incompatibility With Active Grille Air Shutter Module B","Shutter module B is the second flap actuator; at GM it drives the lower shutter. U034F tells that its software or variant differs from what the engine controller has stored as valid, typically after a shutter with another part number or firmware was fitted. No manufacturer documents U034F publicly.",["Lower shutter actuator with early or unsuitable firmware","Lower shutter replaced by a part with another part number","Water in the lower connector disturbing the module and misread as a software fault"],["Lower grille flaps no longer move","Check engine lamp may light depending on the maker","Code appears after a lower shutter was replaced"],2,0,["U0285","U0586","U034E"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ B"],U0350:["Software Incompatibility With Active Grille Air Shutter Module C","Module C denotes one more flap actuator with its own bus address, needed where the front end splits its air openings into more sections, for example left and right lower flaps. U0350 indicates that the engine controller does not accept this unit's software. No manufacturer documents U0350 publicly.",["Side or lower flap actuator with another part number or firmware fitted","Left and right actuators swapped or mixed between model versions","Engine controller software expects a different shutter configuration"],["Air flap warning message in the cluster","One group of flaps remains in its last position","Check engine lamp may light depending on the maker"],2,0,["U028B","U058C","U0351"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C"],U0351:["Software Incompatibility With Active Grille Air Shutter Module D","Shutter module D is the fourth address the code list reserves for grille flap actuators and is relevant only where a front end has four independently driven flap groups. U0351 signals that the engine controller will not accept the software of that unit. No manufacturer documents U0351 or says where a unit D would sit, so the position is maker-specific.",["Flap actuator of group D with another part number or firmware fitted","Front end or bumper from another version fitted with different shutter equipment","Engine controller calibration expects a different number of shutter modules"],["One flap group no longer opens or closes","Air flap warning or check engine lamp depending on the maker","No noticeable change in driving"],2,0,["U028C","U058D","U0350"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D"],U0352:["Software Incompatibility With NOx Sensor C","NOx sensor C is a third smart NOx sensor with its own electronics, fitted on exhaust systems with a second SCR stage, where it watches the gas behind the last catalyst. U0352 means the engine controller declines the software or calibration of this sensor, for example after a part meant for another engine or model year was fitted. No manufacturer documents U0352 publicly.",["NOx sensor for another engine, model year or position fitted","Engine controller updated to a level that expects another sensor software","Sensor C swapped with the sensor of another position"],["Check engine lamp possible, depending on the maker's rating","SCR or catalyst readiness does not complete","Code appears right after a NOx sensor replacement"],4,0,["U02A1","U05A8","U05A9","U030D","U030E"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול חיישן NOx‏ C"],U0353:["Software Incompatibility With Ion Sense Module","An ion sense module places a small voltage across the plug gap after each spark and turns the resulting ion current into combustion, knock and misfire information for the engine controller; Ford's patent US20170030322A1 shows such a unit inside the ignition system.",["Engine controller or ion sense module updated without the matching partner software","Replacement ion sense module with another part number or calibration","Programming of one of the two units interrupted or incomplete"],["Check engine light","Misfire or knock codes stored at the same time","Code appears right after a module replacement or reflash"],4,3,["U0673","U0901","P0300"],""],U0354:["Software Incompatibility With Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Control Module","The inductive charger control module is the on-board part of a wireless charging system: a receiving coil under the floor picks up energy from a ground pad, and the module rectifies it and coordinates the process with battery management and charge controller. U0354 is stored when one of those partners finds that the module runs software or a calibration it does not accept, say after an exchange or a partial update.",["Inductive charger module replaced but not programmed or configured","Battery or charge controller updated to a level that expects other charger software","Software update of the charger module aborted"],["Wireless charging does not start","Charging warning in the display while cable charging still works"],4,0,["U014B","U044C"],"אי-התאמת תוכנה מול מודול בקרת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה"],U0400:["Invalid Data Received","U0400 is the unspecific entry of the invalid-data block. It says that a module receives messages from another node on time but rejects their content, without naming the sender; the codes from U0401 upward name the partner.",["Modules on different software levels after a partial update","Replaced module not programmed or configured","Disturbed bus signal from poor connections or low supply voltage"],["Code cannot be cleared or returns at once","Functions of the storing module limited or warning lamp on, depending on the vehicle"],4,0,["U0401","U0402","U0300","U0073"],""],U0401:["Invalid Data Received From ECM/PCM A","U0401 is stored by a module that keeps receiving the engine or powertrain controller's messages but finds their content faulty. Most often the transmission controller logs it; Ford's 2012 OBD summary names engine torque and pedal position as the data concerned.",["Software of the ECM/PCM or of the receiving module (update available)","ECM sends a signal flagged invalid, for example after its own sensor fault","Disturbed CAN traffic from connectors, wiring or low battery voltage","Engine control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light, often stored in the transmission controller","Harsh shifts or transmission limp-home mode","Adaptive cruise control switched off"],3,3,["U0100","U0301","U0402","U0400"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)‏ A"],U0402:["Invalid Data Received From TCM","U0402 is the reverse case of U0401: the engine controller or another listener receives the transmission controller's frames but rejects their content. GM's 2025 ECM checks counter, protection value and checksum of the estimated-gear and general transmission information signals, flags a fault at 8 errors among 18 checks, Type A after one trip; the body controller uses 15 of 16 and Type B.",["Software of PCM or TCM (update available)","Internal transmission fault making the TCM send implausible values","Disturbed CAN traffic from connectors, wiring or low voltage","Transmission control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light","Transmission stuck in a fixed gear (limp mode)","Harsh or delayed shifts"],3,3,["U0101","U0302","U0401","U0400"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מחשב תיבה (TCM)"],U0403:["Invalid Data Received From Transfer Case Control Module","U0403 points to data from the transfer case control module, the unit that engages four-wheel drive and selects the range: its frames keep coming, yet the listener rejects what they carry. In GM's 2025 tables the ECM watches the secondary-axle signals from this module for faulty rolling counter, protection value or checksum, needs 8 bad results out of 18 to fail and assigns Type B (MIL on the second trip), whereas…",["Software of the transfer case or drivetrain control module (update available)","Ignition voltage dropping out at fuse block terminals or relays","Faulty range position sensor making the module send implausible values","Transfer case control module internally faulty"],["Service 4WD message","Traction control or check engine light on","Driveline bumps or clicking from the transfer case motor"],2,1,["U0102","U0303","U0400"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת תיבת העברה"],U0404:["Invalid Data Received From Gear Shift Control Module A","Gear shift control module A is the electronic selector of shift-by-wire cars: lever, dial or buttons that report the chosen range as data. U0404 means its messages still arrive but the receiver, usually the transmission controller, rejects them. GM's 2025 ECM checks counter and protection fields of the selector's position-sensor and self-check signals, fails a signal after 4 errors in 10 or 8 in 18 checks;",["Software of TCM or gateway (update available)","Position sensor or electronics in the selector delivering implausible values","Connector or bus line at the selector loose or corroded","Gear shift module internally faulty"],["Selector fault message or flashing range indicator","Range cannot be selected or vehicle stays in Park","Check engine light"],3,3,["U0103","U0304","U0592","U0402"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ A"],U0405:["Invalid Data Received From Cruise Control Module","Today the module behind this code is usually the distance radar of adaptive cruise, the unit that asks the engine controller for speed and torque changes. U0405 is set when those requests arrive but fail the receiver's integrity checks. Saab's 2011 code list breaks it down into sub-codes 71 (invalid data), 72 (message counter) and 74 (checksum).",["Engine controller software detecting the fault falsely (update available)","Radar or cruise module sending implausible requests, for example after misalignment or damage","Disturbed CAN traffic from connectors or wiring"],["Adaptive cruise control unavailable","Check engine light that does not go out after clearing"],2,1,["U0104","U0305","U0401"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שיוט"],U0406:["Invalid Data Received From Fuel Injector Control Module","U0406 means a receiving controller, normally the ECM/PCM, gets messages from the fuel injector control module that arrive but fail its checks: wrong counter, checksum, range or a signal marked invalid. Ford's 2012 OBD summary shows the U04xx principle with U0401: the TCM stores it when the ECM sends invalid or faulted torque or pedal data. A separate injector module exists only on some designs;",["Corroded or loose connector, damaged bus wire to the injector module","Low supply voltage at the injector module","Software levels of injector module and ECM do not match","Injector control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light on","Rough running, misfire or hard start","Reduced power"],3,3,["U0105","U0306","U0401","U0407"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מזרק דלק"],U0407:["Invalid Data Received From Glow Plug Control Module","U0407 is stored when the engine controller receives data from the glow plug control module that it rejects as implausible. Volkswagen lists the code in the 2014 Touareg diesel OBD chart as Invalid Data Received From Glow Plug Control Module 1, criterion implausible messages received. On that engine the glow unit talks to the ECM over LIN;",["LIN wire or connector between glow module and ECM corroded or loose","Glow plug control module internally faulty","Voltage dip during glow check or cranking","Glow module software does not match the ECM"],["Check engine or glow plug light on","Hard starting in cold weather","White smoke and rough idle after cold start"],2,1,["U0106","U0307","U0406"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מצת להט"],U0408:["Invalid Data Received From Throttle Actuator Control Module","U0408 points to messages from the throttle actuator control module that the receiver, usually the ECM/PCM, judges invalid: implausible content, a failed checksum or counter, or a value outside its range. Most vehicles integrate throttle control in the engine controller, so a separate TAC module and therefore this code are uncommon; no manufacturer documents U0408 publicly.",["Damaged bus wire or poor connector contact at the throttle module","Throttle actuator control module internally faulty","Software of throttle module and ECM do not match","Low or unstable supply voltage"],["Check engine light on","Limp mode with reduced throttle response","Unstable idle or stalling"],2,3,["U0107","U0308","U0401","U0406"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת"],U0409:["Invalid Data Received From Alternative Fuel Control Module","U0409 is logged when the engine controller receives data from the alternative fuel control module that fail its validity checks. Such a module runs the gas side of bi-fuel CNG or LPG vehicles. In Ford's 2000 bi-fuel OBD description the AFCM passes the requested mode (ALT or GAS) and supply status between the gas metering unit and the PCM, which then switches the petrol injectors on or off;",["Corroded connector or damaged wiring of the retrofit or factory gas system","Faulty gas rail pressure/temperature sensor delivering implausible values","Alternative fuel control module faulty or wrongly configured"],["Check engine light on","Engine stays on or switches back to petrol","Gas gauge or fuel mode indicator incorrect"],4,1,["U0108","U0309","U0406","U0410"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלק חלופי"],U040A:["Invalid Data Received From Air Conditioning Control Module","J2012 separates the air conditioning control module, which governs the refrigerant side with compressor, pressures and, in electrified cars, an electric compressor drive, from the HVAC module that handles blower, flaps and set temperature (invalid data from that one is U0424).",["Software of the A/C control module or of the receiver out of step","Faulty pressure or temperature input making the module send invalid values","Disturbed bus line, poor ground or low supply voltage at the module","A/C control module internally faulty"],["Air conditioning blows warm, compressor stays off","Windows demist slowly"],2,0,["U010F","U0164","U0424"],""],U040B:["Invalid Data Received From Exhaust Gas Recirculation Control Module A","U040B refers to an exhaust gas recirculation system driven by its own electronics on the bus, for example a smart EGR valve actuator that receives position targets and returns its measured position. The code is set when that unit's replies reach the engine controller but fail plausibility or protection checks, so the controller can no longer verify how much exhaust gas flows back.",["Electronics or position sensor of the EGR actuator A delivering implausible values","Heat-damaged connector or bus line at the EGR unit","Software of engine controller and EGR module A out of step","EGR control module A internally faulty"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or rough idle","EGR flow codes stored alongside"],3,3,["U010A","U040C","P0400","P0401"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת סחרור גזי פליטה‏ A"],U040C:["Invalid Data Received From Exhaust Gas Recirculation Control Module B","U040C concerns a second, separately networked EGR control unit, B. Two units appear on engines with separate high- and low-pressure recirculation paths, common on modern diesels, or with one EGR valve per cylinder bank; which one counts as B is up to the maker.",["Electronics or position sensor of EGR actuator B delivering implausible values","Connector or bus line in the branch of module B damaged by heat or moisture","Module B with software that does not match the engine controller"],["Check engine light","Reduced power, more smoke or higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["U010B","U040B","P0400"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת סחרור גזי פליטה‏ B"],U040D:["Invalid Data Received From Turbocharger/Supercharger Control Module A","Turbocharger/supercharger control module A is in practice an electronic charger actuator that sets the vanes of a variable-geometry turbine or a wastegate on command and reports position and status back. U040D means those reports arrive but the engine controller judges them invalid. No manufacturer documents U040D publicly.",["Electronics of the turbo actuator degraded by heat","Sticking vanes or linkage making the actuator report implausible positions","Connector or sensor bus line at the actuator damaged"],["Check engine light","Noticeably reduced power (limp mode)","Boost pressure codes stored alongside"],3,3,["U010C","U040E","P0046","P0234"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מגדש‏ A"],U040E:["Invalid Data Received From Turbocharger/Supercharger Control Module B","U040E is reserved for a second charger control module, B, on engines that run two separately actuated chargers: twin or sequential turbo layouts, or a turbocharger combined with an electrically driven or clutched supercharger. The engine controller sets it when module B's position or status messages keep coming but are judged invalid.",["Electronics or position feedback of charger actuator B faulty","Connector or bus line of module B damaged by heat","Module B with software that does not match the engine controller"],["Check engine light","Reduced power, especially at higher load"],3,3,["U010D","U040D","P0234"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מגדש‏ B"],U040F:["Invalid Data Received From Reductant Control Module","On a diesel with SCR, the reductant control module looks after the urea circuit, chiefly the pump, dosing and heater control, and reports pressure and status to the engine controller. U040F means its messages arrive but fail validation. GM's 2025 ECM tables check counter and checksum of the DEF information and dosing status frames, count 6 errors among 15 or 3 among 10 checks as a failure;",["Pump motor controller in the reductant module reporting an invalid control signal","Corroded connector or damaged bus line at the tank-mounted module","Software of the reductant module or ECM out of step","Reductant control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light","DEF/AdBlue warning with countdown to a speed limit","Further SCR or reductant pump codes stored"],3,3,["U010E","U030F","U05A3","U05A6"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U0410:["Invalid Data Received From Fuel Pump Control Module","U0410 means the engine controller receives data from the fuel pump control module that it cannot trust, such as a bad checksum, counter or an out-of-range value. Many cars drive the in-tank pump through such a module to set the low-side pressure on demand.",["Damaged bus wire or corroded connector to the fuel pump module (often near the tank)","Poor power or ground of the fuel pump module","Pump module and ECM software do not match after replacement","Fuel pump control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light on","Fuel pressure codes such as P2635 set together","Hesitation, stalling or reduced power"],2,3,["U0109","U0310","U0409"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת משאבת דלק"],U0411:["Invalid Data Received From Drive Motor Control Module","U0411 is stored when a controller, typically the engine or hybrid controller, receives messages from the drive motor control module (the inverter electronics of an electric traction motor) that it judges invalid. Volkswagen lists it in its 2014 hybrid OBD charts: for the Touareg Hybrid on implausible messages from the motor module, for the Jetta Hybrid on an incorrect CAN data length code.",["Damaged pins or poor contact in harness connectors near the drive motor (Bentley case)","Faulty motor temperature sensor circuit making the module send invalid data","Software of motor module and hybrid controller do not match","Drive motor control module internally faulty"],["Engine or drive system warning light on","Electric drive unavailable, engine runs constantly","Reduced power"],4,3,["U0110","U0311","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה"],U0412:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Energy Control Module A","U0412 is stored when the hybrid or engine controller receives data from battery energy control module A, the management unit of the high-voltage battery, that it rejects as invalid. Volkswagen's 2014 Jetta Hybrid OBD chart sets it on implausible received data.",["Software error in hybrid controller or battery management (FCA: reflash HCP/AHCP)","Bus wiring or connector fault between battery module and hybrid controller","Weak 12 V battery disturbing module start-up","Battery energy control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light on, code may become permanent","Charging or electric driving limited","Hybrid system warning message"],4,3,["U0111","U0312","U0413","U0411"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ A"],U0413:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Energy Control Module B","U0413 is the counterpart of U0412 for battery energy control module B, used where the high-voltage battery has a second management unit or a split controller. Volkswagen's 2014 Jetta Hybrid chart sets it on implausible data, while the 2014 Touareg Hybrid chart uses U0413 for its single battery module, which shows that the A/B assignment is maker-specific.",["Software error in battery management or junction box (Audi: SVM update)","Bus wiring or connector fault at the battery module","Battery energy control module B internally faulty"],["Drive system or engine warning light on","Electric driving or charging restricted","Code stored in engine and electric drive controllers"],4,3,["U0112","U0313","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ B"],U0414:["Invalid Data Received From Four-Wheel Drive Clutch Control Module","U0414 is set when a listener, usually the engine controller, receives frames from the four-wheel-drive clutch control module but cannot trust what they carry. That module regulates an on-demand coupling feeding torque to the secondary axle and reports its state on the bus. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) test the secondary-axle signal every 12.5 ms for faulty rolling counters, protection values or checksums;",["Four-wheel-drive clutch module sends faulty values (internal fault, moisture)","Disturbed CAN traffic from connectors, wiring or low supply voltage","Clutch module and receiver on software levels that do not match"],["AWD or 4WD warning in the cluster","Drive on the primary axle only","Check engine light after two trips"],3,3,["U0114","U0314","U041E","U0403"],""],U0415:["Invalid Data Received From Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Control Module","U0415 means a module accepts frames from the ABS control module only to find their content invalid, typically wheel speeds or brake status with a wrong counter, checksum or a value flagged as unavailable. GM's Saab 9-5 list (2011) splits it into sub-types 72 (message counter) and 74 (checksum) for the electronic brake module. Ford's 2014 code list gives it both MIL and wrench lamp.",["Software of the receiving module (TCM, AWD, steering) too strict or faulty; update available","ABS module passing on implausible values, for example from a faulty wheel speed sensor","Disturbed CAN traffic from water in connectors, wiring or low voltage"],["ABS, traction or stability warning lamps","Check engine light and Service Transmission message (model-specific)","AWD, steering or camera functions limited"],3,3,["U0121","U0315","U045B","U0416","U0418"],""],U0416:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Dynamics Control Module","U0416 points at the vehicle dynamics control module, the stability control unit that brakes single wheels and trims engine torque. A receiver logs the code when that unit's frames arrive but fail the plausibility check. GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 list adds sub-types 72 (counter wrong) and 74 (checksum error); Ford's 2014 code list carries U0416 without a lamp.",["Weak or recently disconnected 12 V battery disturbing the stability unit's data","Software of the receiving assistance module (radar, camera) needs an update","Steering angle or sensor calibration lost after battery work","Missing or damaged wire or connector in the bus branch"],["Adaptive cruise or emergency brake assist unavailable","Stability or brake warning in the cluster"],2,0,["U0122","U0316","U0415","U0418"],""],U0417:["Invalid Data Received From Park Brake Control Module","U0417 covers implausible data from the park brake control module, the controller of an electric parking brake that clamps the rear calipers by motor and reports apply state and faults on the bus. A receiver stores it when these frames arrive with a bad counter, checksum or an invalid value. No manufacturer explains U0417 in public documents.",["Low battery voltage or a voltage dip corrupting park brake messages","Park brake control module or its actuator feedback faulty","Connector or wiring fault in the park brake bus branch"],["Park brake warning lamp or message","Auto hold or hill start assist unavailable","Code only stored in history without current fault"],2,0,["U0128","U0317","U0418"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת בלם חניה"],U0418:["Invalid Data Received From Brake System Control Module A","U0418 says a node rejects the content of frames from brake system control module A, on many cars the unit that combines ABS, stability control and brake boost. GM's 2025 tables are detailed: the engine controller tests brake status signals for bad counters, protection values or checksums, 8 faults in 18 checks give Type A with MIL after one trip;",["Low battery voltage (below about 10 V) during start or standstill","Engine or transmission controller software reacting too sensitively; update available","Loose connector or harness fault disturbing the chassis bus","Brake system control module internally faulty"],["Check engine light","Adaptive cruise, stop-start or driver assistance unavailable","Brake or stability warning in the cluster"],3,3,["U0129","U0318","U04B5","U0415","U0416"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ A"],U0419:["Invalid Data Received From Steering Effort Control Module","U0419 concerns the steering effort control module, which varies the assistance or steering ratio the driver feels. Ford uses that name for the controller of its adaptive steering: bulletin 16-2066 on the 2016 Edge and MKX stores C1B00 in the steering effort control module (SECM) and replaces the steering wheel that houses the actuator.",["Steering effort module or its actuator reporting implausible values","Clock spring, connector or bus wiring fault in the steering branch","Module not calibrated or configured after replacement"],["Steering system warning in the cluster","Steering ratio or assistance no longer speed-dependent"],4,0,["U0130","U0319","U0420"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מאמץ היגוי"],U041A:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Module","U041A refers to the battery isolation or voltage stabilization module, which separates an auxiliary battery or sensitive loads from the starter circuit, so a restart after an automatic engine stop leaves the rest of the electrical system at stable voltage. GM's patent US 9,803,608 builds such an isolator from MOSFET switches.",["Poor ground connection of the isolation module","Weak auxiliary battery making the module report implausible values","Battery isolator or stabilizer internally faulty"],["Automatic stop-start not available","Battery or charging system message"],2,0,["U061E"],""],U041B:["Invalid Data Received From Exhaust Gas Sensor Module A","U041B names exhaust gas sensor module A, an electronic unit that heats and evaluates an exhaust probe, usually a wide-band oxygen sensor, and sends the result as bus data. The engine controller sets the code when the module still talks but its values fail plausibility, carry wrong counters or report the sensor as not ready. No manufacturer documents U041B publicly.",["Heat-damaged sensor harness or connector at the sensor module","Aged or contaminated probe giving implausible readings","Exhaust gas sensor module internally faulty"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel use or regeneration problems on diesels"],3,1,["U011A","U046E","U016D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן גזי פליטה‏ A"],U041C:["Invalid Data Received From Rocker Arm Control Module A","U041C relates to rocker arm control module A, the controller that switches oil-actuated rocker arms to change valve lift or shut cylinders down. The engine controller stores it when the module's lock-state or feedback frames arrive with implausible content, wrong counters or invalid values. No manufacturer documents U041C publicly, and it is open which engines use a separate module.",["Low oil pressure or sticking switching solenoid causing implausible lock-state feedback","Rocker arm control module A internally faulty","Connector or bus wiring fault at module A"],["Check engine light","Cylinder deactivation or valve lift switching locked out","Higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["U011B","U041D","U011C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נדנד שסתומים‏ A"],U041D:["Invalid Data Received From Rocker Arm Control Module B","U041D is the counterpart for rocker arm control module B, used where the switching of rocker arms is split, for instance by cylinder bank. The code tells that the engine controller still receives B's messages, but their lift or lock status cannot be trusted. Comparing with U041C helps: B alone points to that module, its harness branch or its solenoids, both together to the shared supply or the bus.",["Switching solenoid or oil supply on the B side faulty","Rocker arm control module B internally faulty","Shared supply or bus fault (then usually with U041C)"],["Check engine light","Uneven running or higher fuel use"],3,1,["U011C","U041C","U011B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נדנד שסתומים‏ B"],U041E:["Invalid Data Received From All Wheel Drive Control Module","U041E concerns the all-wheel-drive control module, the unit that manages a complete AWD or transfer case system rather than a single clutch (U0414). A receiver logs it when that module's torque, mode or status frames arrive but are invalid.",["Transfer case shift motor or module connector not fully seated","Transfer case motor or position sensor faulty, making the module send invalid status","All-wheel-drive control module internally faulty"],["4WD or AWD service light","Check engine light (model-specific)","Four-wheel-drive modes unavailable"],2,3,["U011D","U0414","U0403","U0418"],""],U041F:["Invalid Data Received From Throttle Actuator B Control Module","U041F addresses throttle actuator B control module, a separately housed driver for a second electronic throttle. Most engines use one throttle driven directly by the engine controller; a separate driver for the first throttle is covered by U0408. The engine controller sets U041F when B's position or status frames arrive but disagree with plausibility checks or carry bad counters.",["Position feedback of throttle actuator B implausible (sensor or gearbox wear)","Throttle actuator B control module internally faulty","Connector or bus wiring fault at module B"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or limp-home mode"],3,3,["U011E","U0408","U0308","U0107"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מפעיל מצערת‏ B"],U0420:["Invalid Data Received From Power Steering Control Module A","U0420 is stored when a listener gets frames from power steering control module A, the electric assist unit on rack or column, yet judges their content unusable. GM's 2025 tables name several listeners: the ECM tests the steering wheel information for bad counter, protection value or checksum and needs 8 failures within 18 samples for a Type C fault with no MIL;",["Low battery voltage during cranking corrupts steering module start-up data","Steering module or receiving module software needs an update","Corroded connector or poor ground at the steering module"],["Adaptive cruise, lane keeping or emergency braking unavailable","Stability control or steering warning in the cluster","Code returns after cold starts with a weak battery"],4,0,["U0131","U0320","U0428","U0415","U045C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת הגה כוח‏ A"],U0421:["Invalid Data Received From Suspension Control Module A","Suspension control module A runs air springs, ride height or adjustable dampers and broadcasts level and status data. U0421 tells that a receiving module gets these frames but finds them corrupt or implausible.",["Suspension module software hang, cleared by a power reset","Low supply voltage or weak battery during start-up","Internal fault of the suspension control module"],["Service air suspension or leveling warning","Ride height no longer adjusts","Stability or brake system message alongside"],4,2,["U0132","U0321","U043A","U0422"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מתלים‏ A"],U0422:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module","U0422 applies to cars with a single body controller; with several, U0431 names body control module A and U0443 to U0446 modules B to E. A receiver logs it when BCM frames arrive but carry unusable content. GM's 2025 ECM checks body information frames with 8 faults in 18 samples and serial data frames with 3 in 10, after 5 s at 11 V or more, as Type B, so the MIL follows a second faulty trip.",["Battery disconnect or low voltage leaves default values in BCM messages","Missing or wrong BCM configuration such as VIN, tire size or vehicle options","BCM or receiver software fault, cured by an update"],["Check engine light on some vehicles","Cruise control or driver assistance unavailable","Wrong outside temperature or A/C not working"],4,1,["U0140","U0322","U0431","U0443"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב"],U0423:["Invalid Data Received From Instrument Panel Cluster Control Module","The instrument cluster does more than display: it sends outside temperature, display and chime status or confirmations from its menus to other units. U0423 marks cluster frames that arrive but fail the receiver's checks. In GM's 2025 driver assistance controller EOCM3, 8 of 10 bad frames on chime state, display status or speed limit confirmations set a Special Type C fault that turns adaptive cruise off.",["Battery, fuse or display disconnected so the cluster sends start values","Software fault in cluster or receiving module","Another node on the same bus disturbing the cluster's messages"],["Stability, tire pressure or assistance warnings that cannot be cleared","Adaptive cruise or auto high beam unavailable","Check engine light on some makes"],4,1,["U0155","U0323","U0424"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת לוח מחוונים לוח מחוונים"],U0424:["Invalid Data Received From HVAC Control Module","The HVAC control module reports climate requests and, on newer layouts, also the voltages of switches on the climate faceplate that it measures itself. U0424 says a receiver rejects these frames.",["HVAC control module or faceplate electronics faulty","Low battery voltage or a reset of the HVAC module during start-up","HVAC or BCM software level that needs an update"],["Climate controls or buttons react incorrectly or not at all","A/C or defrost not available","Check engine light on some makes"],4,1,["U0164","U0324","U0466","U046C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מיזוג אוויר"],U0425:["Invalid Data Received From Auxiliary Heater Control Module","U0425 concerns the auxiliary heater control module, the controller of an extra heat source such as a fuel-fired coolant heater on a diesel. The HVAC or engine controller sets it when the heater's status frames arrive with implausible content. No manufacturer documents U0425 publicly; GM's 2013 bulletin PIP5094 merely includes it in a long list of codes for which terminal fit should be checked before circuit tests.",["Auxiliary heater control unit faulty or locked after an internal fault","Low supply voltage at the heater, for example from a weak battery","Loose terminals or corrosion in the heater's bus connector"],["Auxiliary or parking heater does not start","Slow warm-up and weak cabin heat in cold weather"],4,0,["U0166","U0325","U0424"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גוף חימום עזר"],U0426:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Immobilizer Control Module","The vehicle immobilizer control module reads the transponder in the key and passes a coded release to the engine controller. U0426 is logged when that release or status message arrives but cannot be accepted, so the handshake fails even though the module is still talking.",["Ignition feed voltages do not match the key position, often due to aftermarket equipment","Damaged key transponder or key not matched to the vehicle","Immobilizer module or antenna faulty"],["Engine cranks but does not start, or no start at times","Security or key warning lamp flashing","Key hard to remove from the ignition"],4,0,["U0167","U0326","U0427"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אימובילייזר רכב"],U0427:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Security Control Module","The vehicle security control module looks after theft protection: alarm, door, bonnet and tailgate monitoring and, with some makers, the key authorisation for the engine. U0427 marks messages from this module that reach a partner but fail its checks. No manufacturer documents U0427 publicly; GM's 2013 bulletin PIP5094 only names it among many codes for which terminal fit comes before circuit tests.",["Security control module faulty or reset during start-up","Aftermarket alarm or remote start interfering with the module or its supply","Poor terminal fit or corrosion at the module connector"],["Alarm triggers falsely or cannot be armed","Remote locking or keyless functions unreliable","Engine start refused on vehicles where the module joins the key check"],4,0,["U0168","U0327","U0426"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אבטחת רכב"],U0428:["Invalid Data Received From Steering Angle Sensor Module","U0428 is for a separately networked steering angle sensor module, usually on the column, feeding angle and rate to stability control, assistance and stop-start. GM's 2025 brake module counts wrong checksums or counters in its frames (8 of a 16 window) and reacts at once to a cleared validity bit or a data mask stuck at zero, all Type C without MIL.",["Steering angle sensor not calibrated after replacement or alignment work","Software in the engine, brake or steering controller misjudging the sensor data","Steering angle sensor module faulty"],["Stability control or steering warning lamp","Stop-start stops the engine at the wrong moment or stays off","Check engine light on some vehicles"],4,1,["U0126","U0328","U0420","U0429"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן זווית הגה"],U0429:["Invalid Data Received From Steering Column Control Module","U0429 covers the steering column control module (SCCM), which reads stalks and wheel buttons and on many cars also houses the steering angle sensor. A partner logs the code when SCCM frames are received but rejected. Ford's 2024 OBD summary lists U0429_48 in the supervision layer of the PCM's throttle monitor as a non-MIL fault.",["Vehicle configuration not restored or aligned after a module repair","Software fault in PCM, steering unit or column module","Steering column control module or its angle sensor faulty"],["Steering or power steering warning lamp","Cruise control or stalk functions unavailable","Driver assistance systems switched off"],4,0,["U0212","U0329","U0428","U0420"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת עמוד היגוי"],U042A:["Invalid Data Received From V2X Module","The V2X module is the radio node for vehicle-to-everything messaging with other cars, roadside units and the network, via DSRC/ITS-G5 or cellular C-V2X. U042A tells that another module gets frames from it but cannot use their content. No manufacturer documents U042A publicly.",["V2X module or receiver software fault","V2X module faulty, for example after a supply interruption","Antenna or positioning input problem leading to invalid status data"],["Connected traffic or hazard warnings missing","Message about unavailable connected services"],4,0,["U011F","U0198"],""],U042B:["Invalid Data Received From Chassis Control Module A","Chassis control module A is a generic name for a controller that coordinates chassis functions, and the job behind the letter varies by brand. GM's documents give one concrete owner: the 2020 ten-speed transmission controller (20OBDG03A) treats the integrated chassis control module (ICCM) as chassis control module A and watches its frame $1F7; an L20 engine controller of 2016 also listens to this module.",["Software fault in the chassis module or the receiving controller","Low voltage or reset of the chassis module during operation","Chassis control module A faulty"],["Chassis, stability or suspension warning","Chassis functions such as damping or traction aids limited"],4,2,["U012A","U042C","U012B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שלדה‏ A"],U042C:["Invalid Data Received From Chassis Control Module B","U042C refers to a second chassis controller, labelled B, where chassis tasks are split between two units. It is stored when that module's frames still arrive but carry a bad counter, checksum or implausible values. No manufacturer documents U042C or the B module publicly; the only public assignment found concerns module A, which GM's 2020 transmission tables equate with the integrated chassis control module.",["Software fault in chassis module B or the receiver","Supply, ground or gateway problem affecting the module's messages","Chassis control module B faulty"],["Chassis or suspension warning in the cluster","Chassis function handled by module B inactive"],4,2,["U012B","U042B","U012A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שלדה‏ B"],U042D:["Invalid Data Received From Active Vibration Control Module","The active vibration control module drives active engine mounts or inertial actuators that push against engine vibration in counter-phase, useful with cylinder deactivation. It needs engine speed and other data from the bus and reports its own status back. U042D says a partner receives its frames but finds them invalid. No manufacturer documents U042D publicly.",["Control unit software not matching replaced mounts or actuators","Active vibration control module faulty","Low supply voltage or poor connection at the module"],["Noticeable vibration or humming at idle","More body vibration when cylinders are deactivated"],4,0,["U012C","P0A14"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת רעידה פעילה"],U042E:["Invalid Data Received From Generator A Control Module","U042E points to the regulator of generator A, on many Ford models a smart alternator that the PCM commands over a LIN line and that answers with load, temperature and fault status. The PCM stores U042E when those answers come back distorted or implausible; if they stop altogether, U012D is set instead, and U0284 often joins because grille shutters may share the line.",["Chafed or shorted LIN wire between PCM and generator","Water intrusion or corrosion in a connector of the LIN circuit","Faulty voltage regulator of the generator"],["Check charging system message or battery lamp","Battery runs down, starting problems","Grille shutter codes stored at the same time"],2,0,["U012D","U0284","U044D","U012F"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גנרטור‏ A"],U042F:["Invalid Data Received From Camshaft Position Control Module","U042F concerns a camshaft position control module, used where an electric motor with its own electronics moves the phaser instead of an oil valve. The engine controller commands a target angle and receives actual position and status; U042F means those replies arrive but fail plausibility or protection checks, while U012E is set when they stop.",["Electric valve timing control module faulty","Supply, ground or connector fault at the module","Engine controller software misjudging the module data"],["Check engine light","Reduced power and rougher idle","Higher fuel consumption"],4,3,["U012E","P0010","U0101"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מצב גל זיזים"],U0430:["Invalid Data Received From Tire Pressure Monitor Module","U0430 means that a receiver gets frames from the tire pressure monitor module but rejects what they contain, such as wheel pressures, sensor identifiers or a system status outside the permitted range, or a broken message counter. A stand-alone evaluation unit exists for example in the 2020 Jeep Gladiator Rubicon, whose TPM module FCA reflashed to add the selectable tire fill alert (bulletin 08-023-20).",["Outdated or unsuitable software in the tire pressure module","Wheel sensors not learned after tire or wheel change, module sends default values","Poor supply, ground or connector at the tire pressure module"],["TPMS malfunction lamp on or flashing","Tire pressures missing or shown as dashes in the cluster"],2,0,["U0127","U0330","U0431"],""],U0431:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module A","U0431 points at body control module A on vehicles that split body functions over several controllers; with a single BCM the code is U0422, and units B to E have U0443 to U0446. Mitsubishi documents it in the all-wheel-drive ECU, which reads body data from the ETACS unit, among them the stop light switch, and sets U0431 when that signal is abnormal;",["Software of the receiving module (e.g. AWD unit) misreads body data, reflash needed","Body control module A software or coding faulty","Supply or ground problem at body control module A"],["All-wheel-drive or 4WD warning lamp on","Ignition or comfort functions do not switch on","Further body-related warnings in the cluster"],4,0,["U0141","U0331","U0422","U0443"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב‏ A"],U0432:["Invalid Data Received From Multi-axis Acceleration Sensor Module A","Multi-axis acceleration sensor module A is the inertial unit that reports yaw rate plus lateral and longitudinal acceleration to stability control, airbag and assistance systems. U0432 is logged when its frames arrive but fail integrity tests. In GM's 2019 tables the XT4 brake module checks the IMU frames for a rolling count that stops changing and for a checksum mismatch;",["Corroded connector or terminals in the sensor module harness","Software in the receiving module (PCM, brake module) needs an update","Internal fault or loose mounting of the inertial sensor module"],["Stability control, ABS or AWD warnings","Start-stop or driver assistance functions unavailable","Several chassis codes stored at once"],4,2,["U0125","U0332","U014E","U0418"],""],U0433:["Invalid Data Received From Front Distance Range Sensor - Single Sensor or Center","U0433 concerns the forward distance sensor of adaptive cruise control when there is only one or when it sits in the middle, usually a long-range radar behind the grille. A receiver stores it when the radar's object frames fail their protection checks or carry implausible values.",["Radar misaligned after front-end work or impact, sending implausible objects","Radar or assistance controller software out of step","Low supply voltage or poor connector at the radar"],["Adaptive cruise control switched off","Forward collision warning or emergency braking unavailable"],4,0,["U0235","U043B","U043C"],""],U0434:["Invalid Data Received From Active Roll Control Module","The active roll control module drives actuators that twist the anti-roll bars on both axles against body lean, hydraulically in older designs and electrically in newer ones. U0434 tells that a receiver, for instance the chassis or brake controller, gets this module's status or torque frames but cannot trust their content. No manufacturer documents U0434 publicly.",["Roll control module software fails to initialise reliably","Weak supply to the roll control actuators or module","Internal fault of the roll control module or actuator"],["Suspension or chassis warning in the cluster","Noticeably more body roll in corners"],4,2,["U0133","U043A","U0421"],""],U0435:["Invalid Data Received From Power Steering Control Module - Rear","U0435 refers to the rear power steering module, the controller of active rear-wheel steering. A receiver sets it when the module's status or angle frames arrive but are unusable. GM bulletin 17-NA-130 explains one case on the 2016-17 Cadillac CT6: during a remote start the rear steer module had not yet initialised while the brake module already expected its data, so the EBCM stored U0435 and showed a Service Soon…",["Rear steering module not yet ready when receivers expect data, e.g. at remote start","Software error in rear steering or brake module","Low voltage or poor connector at the rear steering unit"],["Service Soon or rear steering fault message","Larger turning circle, rear wheels held straight"],4,2,["U0134","U0420","U0428"],""],U0436:["Invalid Data Received From Differential Control Module - Front","U0436 concerns the front differential control module, a controller that locks or meters the front axle differential, for example the electric locker of an off-road vehicle. A receiver records the code when lock status, clutch torque or diagnostic frames from this module look implausible. No manufacturer documents U0436 publicly.",["Fault in the locking module electronics, e.g. degraded measuring resistor","Corroded or damaged harness and connector near the front axle","Differential module software mismatch"],["Front locker or 4WD function unavailable","ABS, stability or drivetrain warning"],4,2,["U0135","U0437","U0136"],""],U0437:["Invalid Data Received From Differential Control Module - Rear","The rear differential control module runs an electronic limited-slip differential or the rear clutch of an on-demand all-wheel drive. U0437 is set when a receiver gets its frames but finds torque, clutch state or counter values invalid. No manufacturer documents U0437 publicly with thresholds.",["Rear differential module software needs reprogramming","Corrosion at the module mounted on or near the rear axle","Faulty clutch actuator or motor feeding implausible status"],["Service AWD or rear axle message","All-wheel drive or limited-slip function inactive"],4,2,["U0136","U0436","U0135"],""],U0438:["Invalid Data Received From Trailer Brake Control Module","U0438 names the trailer brake control module, which applies the electric brakes of a towed trailer in step with the vehicle's braking; park brake data has a code of its own, U0417. Ford uses U0438 explicitly: SSM 52184 connects U0438:82 stored by the cluster of some 2023 F-150 PowerBoost hybrids, built from 24 to 26 October 2022, with a Trailer Brake System Fault message caused by the cluster configuration, which is…",["Receiving module (instrument cluster) wrongly configured","Loose or wrongly tightened body ground","Internal fault of the trailer brake control module"],["Trailer brake system fault message","Trailer brake gain cannot be set or trailer brakes inactive","Further network warnings in the cluster"],2,0,["U0137","U0417","U064D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת בלם גרור"],U0439:["Invalid Data Received From All Terrain Control Module","U0439 relates to the all terrain control module, which manages drive modes for snow, sand, mud or rock and passes the chosen setting to powertrain, brake and suspension controllers. A receiver sets it when mode request, switch state or status frames from this module look invalid. No manufacturer documents U0439 publicly.",["Terrain or 4WD mode switch stuck or obstructed by trim","All terrain module software or variant coding wrong","Poor supply, ground or connector at the module"],["Check 4x4 or terrain system message","Drive mode selection does not respond"],2,2,["U0138","U0437","U043A"],""],U043A:["Invalid Data Received From Suspension Control Module B","Suspension control module B is a second chassis controller, often the one that runs adjustable dampers while module A handles levelling. U043A is logged when its frames reach a receiver but fail integrity checks.",["Damper module resets or hangs, sending frozen counters","Low supply voltage at the suspension module","Software of suspension and brake modules not matched"],["Service suspension or ride control warning","Ride noticeably firmer or softer than usual"],4,2,["U0139","U0421","U0434"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מתלים‏ B"],U043B:["Invalid Data Received From Front Distance Range Sensor - Left","U043B covers the left front distance sensor, usually a short-range corner radar that widens the view of adaptive cruise and collision assistance beyond the central long-range unit; that one has U0433, the right corner U043C. A receiver sets U043B when the left sensor's object or status frames arrive but fail plausibility or protection checks. No manufacturer documents U043B publicly.",["Left corner radar misaligned or damaged after a bumper impact","Corner radar software not matching the assistance controller","Moisture or corrosion in the left sensor connector"],["Adaptive cruise or lane change assistance unavailable","Message to clean or check front sensors"],4,0,["U023D","U043C","U0433"],""],U043C:["Invalid Data Received From Front Distance Range Sensor - Right","U043C is the right-hand counterpart: invalid frames from the right front distance sensor, a corner radar on cars that pair one long-range radar with two short-range units. Finding only U043C points at that sensor, its plug or its mounting area, for example after a light knock on the right bumper corner; U043B and U043C together suggest a shared supply, bus segment or a software issue in the receiver.",["Right corner radar knocked out of alignment or damaged","Shared supply or bus segment fault when both corner codes appear","Moisture or corrosion in the right sensor connector"],["Assistance functions using the right front view switched off","Sensor blocked or check sensor message"],4,0,["U023E","U043B","U0433"],""],U043D:["Invalid Data Received From Accelerator Pedal Module","U043D applies where the accelerator pedal is a networked module that sends pedal position as messages instead of two analogue voltages. The engine or vehicle controller stores it when those messages carry an implausible position, redundant values that disagree or a broken counter. No manufacturer documents U043D publicly;",["Poor pin contact at the pedal module or its receiver connector","Internal fault of the accelerator pedal module","Pedal module and engine controller software not matched"],["Reduced power or limp-home mode","Engine or drivetrain warning lamp on","Pedal response delayed or ignored"],2,3,["U013C","P2138","P2122"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול דוושת גז"],U043E:["Invalid Data Received From Vacuum Sensor A","Vacuum sensor A reports the vacuum in a brake booster or vacuum reservoir; U043E is meant for designs in which this sensor sends digital messages and a receiver judges them invalid. No manufacturer documents U043E publicly.",["Faulty sensor electronics giving wrong vacuum values","Oil or dirt in the sensor, check valve or vacuum hose","Poor terminal tension at the sensor connector"],["Brake assist warning message","Hard brake pedal or vacuum pump running often"],2,0,["U013D","U043F","P0556","P0557"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן ואקום‏ A"],U043F:["Invalid Data Received From Vacuum Sensor B","U043F is the counterpart for vacuum sensor B, used where a second vacuum signal exists, for example a redundant booster sensor or one watching a separate reservoir. A receiver records it when B's digital vacuum value arrives invalid. Comparing with U043E narrows the search: B alone points at that sensor or its wiring branch, both together at a shared supply, the bus or a genuine vacuum shortage.",["Faulty vacuum sensor B or its electronics","Damaged wiring branch or connector to sensor B","Actual vacuum leak making both sensors disagree"],["Brake assist or vacuum system warning","Start-stop or other vacuum-dependent functions inactive"],2,0,["U013E","U043E","P0557"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן ואקום‏ B"],U0440:["Invalid Data Received From Pedestrian Alert Control Module","U0440 points at the pedestrian alert control module, which drives the external speaker of electric and hybrid vehicles. FMVSS 141 in the US demands an audible signal while the vehicle stands with its propulsion active and at speeds below 30 km/h, so the module needs speed, gear and propulsion state and reports its own status back. A receiver sets U0440 when the module's frames arrive with invalid content.",["Loose or vibrating connector at the alert module","Alert module software not matched to the vehicle","Internal fault of the pedestrian alert module"],["Pedestrian alert system warning in the cluster","No external sound at low speed"],2,0,["U013F"],""],U0441:["Invalid Data Received From Emissions Critical Control Information","U0441 does not name one controller: the title refers to emissions-critical control information, the data powertrain units exchange for emission-relevant functions. A receiver logs it when such a message arrives but fails plausibility, counter or checksum tests; if the information stops altogether, U0113 applies. Ford's 2014 OBD-II code list marks U0441 for the MIL, whereas U0113 carries no lamp flag there.",["Software of the powertrain unit sending the emission data is outdated or mismatched","Fault in the powertrain CAN wiring or connectors corrupting messages","Low or unstable supply voltage at the sending or receiving unit"],["Check engine light on","Additional powertrain or network codes stored","Emissions inspection not passed while the code is present"],4,1,["U0113","U0401","U0442"],""],U0442:["Invalid Data Received From ECM/PCM B","ECM/PCM B stands for a second engine or powertrain controller where a car carries more than one such unit; U0442 means its frames reach a receiver with invalid content, while U0115 means they stop arriving.",["Control logic in the engine or powertrain software too sensitive, update available","Software levels of sending and receiving units do not match after an update","Bus wiring, connector or supply fault at the second powertrain controller"],["Check engine light on","Fail-safe mode with limited engine speed or lack of power","Transmission codes stored alongside engine codes"],4,3,["U0115","U0401","U0441"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מחשב מנוע (ECM/PCM)‏ B"],U0443:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module B","U0443 is set when a receiver gets frames from body control module B but rejects their content. The letters B to E come into play when a vehicle spreads body electronics such as lighting, locks, wipers or power distribution over several controllers; module A has U0431, a single BCM U0422, and lost contact with B is U0142. No car maker explains publicly which unit carries the letter B.",["Software of module B or of the receiver sets the code without a real fault","Loose connector or damaged network wiring at body control module B","Supply or ground problem at body control module B"],["Single comfort or lighting functions unavailable","Code stored as history right after start-up without complaint"],2,0,["U0142","U0431","U0444","U0422"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב‏ B"],U0444:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module C","Body control module C is the third body controller in vehicles with distributed body electronics; U0444 records invalid content in its frames, U0143 lost contact. Ford documents the code: TSB 24-2116 covers 2023 F-150 trucks with the 3.5L PowerBoost hybrid that warn of a trailer brake fault even with no trailer hitched, while the trailer module stores U0444:82, possibly next to U0140:87 and U0143:87.",["Gateway module software level corrupts or delays forwarded messages","Software of the receiving module (e.g. trailer module) misjudges the data","Supply, ground or connector fault at body control module C"],["Trailer brake fault message although no trailer is connected","Lost-communication codes for the BCMs stored together with U0444"],4,0,["U0143","U0140","U0443","U0445"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב‏ C"],U0445:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module D","U0445 belongs to body control module D, a fourth controller for body functions that only vehicles with heavily distributed body electronics need. A receiver sets it when D's frames arrive but their content fails range, counter or checksum tests; complete silence from D is U0144. No manufacturer documents U0445 publicly, and no maker states what D controls.",["Software of module D or of the receiver not matching after an update","Damaged bus wiring or corroded connector on the branch to module D","Internal fault or poor supply at body control module D"],["A body function handled by module D works erratically or not at all","Warning messages in the instrument cluster"],4,0,["U0144","U0444","U0446"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב‏ D"],U0446:["Invalid Data Received From Body Control Module E","U0446 refers to body control module E, the last letter in the series that starts with U0431 for module A. It is logged by a receiving controller when module E is present on the bus but delivers values or protection fields that cannot be trusted; if E stops sending, U0145 is stored instead. No manufacturer documents U0446 publicly.",["Software of the single reporting module misreads the data of module E","Fault in the network branch or connector leading to module E","Low supply voltage or poor ground at body control module E"],["Individual body or comfort functions inoperative","Code present in one or several receiving modules"],4,0,["U0145","U0445","U0431"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מרכב‏ E"],U0447:["Invalid Data Received From Serial Data Gateway Module A","As the central gateway, serial data gateway module A links the vehicle networks and forwards messages between them. U0447 means a receiver gets gateway frames with failed protection; for lost contact the code is U0146.",["Gateway hardware or software fault, update or replacement of the gateway","Receiver software logs the code without a real fault (history entry)","Low battery voltage or poor ground at the gateway during wake-up or power mode changes"],["Several warning messages in the instrument cluster at once","Adaptive cruise or camera-based assistance unavailable","Check engine light on in vehicles that rate the fault as MIL-relevant"],4,1,["U0146","U0448","U0422"],""],U0448:["Invalid Data Received From Serial Data Gateway Module B","U0448 concerns serial data gateway module B, a second gateway that some architectures add next to the central unit to bridge further networks; U0147 is lost contact with it. A receiver stores U0448 when B's frames arrive but alive counter, checksum or message authentication do not match. No manufacturer documents U0448 publicly.",["Software level of gateway B not matching the other modules","Supply or ground fault at gateway B","Internal fault in gateway module B"],["Warnings from several systems at the same time","Assistance or comfort functions on the networks behind gateway B unavailable"],4,0,["U0147","U0447","U0449"],""],U0449:["Invalid Data Received From Serial Data Gateway Module C","U0449 points at serial data gateway module C; its lost-contact partner is U0148. The receiver logs it when C keeps transmitting, yet the content breaks the rules agreed for that message, for instance a wrong length, a frozen counter or a bad checksum. No manufacturer documents U0449 publicly.",["Gateway C software sends frames in a layout the receiver does not expect","Wiring, termination or connector fault on a network served by gateway C","Low voltage or poor ground at gateway C"],["Several unrelated warnings in the cluster","Functions on one network segment unavailable"],4,0,["U0148","U0448","U044A"],""],U044A:["Invalid Data Received From Serial Data Gateway Module D","U044A covers serial data gateway module D. A receiver records it when D's frames carry implausible values or violate their counter or checksum; if they stop, U0149 is the matching code. No manufacturer explains U044A publicly, but Stellantis shows which unit can hold the letter D: for the 2021 Jeep Grand Cherokee, case S2108000139 describes the driver assistance module logging U0149-00, which Stellantis words as…",["Receiver software (e.g. camera or assistance module) misjudges gateway data at start-up","Software or configuration of gateway D not matching the vehicle","Supply, ground or bus wiring fault at gateway D"],["Brief assistance unavailable message at start-up","Driver assistance or display functions limited"],4,0,["U0149","U0449","U0451"],""],U044B:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Energy Control Module C","A third battery controller, module C, appears where a pack is divided into separately managed sections or a vehicle has more than one battery system. A receiver, typically the hybrid or vehicle controller, sets U044B when C's frames on cell voltages, temperatures, state of charge or contactor status fail validity checks; U014A is lost contact, U0412 and U0413 cover modules A and B.",["Software of battery module C not matching the vehicle controller","Faulty cell or temperature sensing inside the pack section managed by C","Bus wiring, connector or 12 V supply fault at module C"],["Hybrid or battery system warning","Reduced electric power or range","Functions supplied by the affected battery switched off"],4,2,["U014A","U0412","U0413","U034C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אנרגיית סוללה‏ C"],U044C:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charging Module","U044C covers the module that controls inductive charging of the high-voltage battery: a receiver coil and electronics on the vehicle take energy from a ground pad without a cable and must agree with the charger on alignment, power and battery limits. A receiver such as the battery or vehicle controller stores U044C when the module's frames arrive but hold invalid status or power values; U014B is lost contact.",["Poor alignment or disturbed link between vehicle unit and ground pad","Software of the inductive charging module not matching the battery controller","Internal fault or overheating of the inductive charging module"],["Wireless charging does not start or stops early","Charging system message in the display"],4,0,["U014B","U044B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול טעינה אינדוקטיבית סוללת מתח גבוה"],U044D:["Invalid Data Received From Generator B Control Module","U044D names the generator B control module. Ford uses the A version for its LIN-controlled alternator: in SSM 50737, 2021-22 F-150 trucks with the 2.7L EcoBoost warn about the charging system and store U012D and U042E in the PCM because a LIN wire rubs through to ground close to the engine mount on the left. A B unit would then be the regulator of a second alternator, as found on trucks with dual generators;",["Chafed or shorted LIN wire to the second alternator","Faulty voltage regulator of alternator B","Second alternator not configured correctly in the engine computer"],["Battery or charging system warning","Low charging voltage under high electrical load"],2,0,["U012F","U042E","U012D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גנרטור‏ B"],U044F:["Invalid Data Received From Mirror Control Module B","U044F is stored when a controller receives data from mirror control module B that it cannot use; U014D is lost contact, U0514 covers module A. Depending on design, mirror modules adjust, fold and heat the exterior mirrors, store memory positions or run an interior mirror with camera display.",["Vehicle configuration does not match the fitted mirror modules","Damaged wiring in the door hinge area or loose mirror connector","Internal fault of mirror control module B, often after water entry"],["Mirror adjustment, folding or memory function inoperative","Camera mirror display or automatic dimming unavailable"],2,0,["U014D","U0514","U0213"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מראה‏ B"],U0451:["Invalid Data Received From Serial Data Gateway Module E","U0451 is the code for serial data gateway module E, the fifth gateway letter; lost communication with it is U0150. It is logged by a receiver that still hears E but finds its data implausible or its protection fields wrong. No manufacturer documents U0451 publicly, and five gateways in one vehicle are rare.",["Receiver software stores the code sporadically without a real fault","Software level of gateway E not matching after an update","Bus wiring, supply or ground fault at gateway E"],["Code stored without noticeable fault","Warnings from systems on the networks behind gateway E"],4,0,["U0150","U044A","U0447"],""],U0452:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints Control Module","The restraints control module decides on airbag and belt tensioner deployment; in many GM vehicles it also sends yaw rate, lateral and longitudinal acceleration and post-crash data to other units. U0452 means a receiver rejects these frames; U0151 is lost contact. GM's 2025 tables show the checks: the ECM tests the alive counter and protection field, 8 failures in 18 samples or 4 in 10 set a Type C code without MIL;",["Restraints control module software needs reprogramming","Receiver stores the code as history after start-up or network wake-up without a real fault","High CAN bus load, poor ground or connector fault on the restraints network branch"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Emergency call or crash notification message","Adaptive cruise or stability functions unavailable"],4,0,["U0151","U0453","U0455","U0432"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מערכת הריסון"],U0453:["Invalid Data Received From Side Restraints Control Module - Left","U0453 concerns a side restraints control module for the left side, used where side impact sensing or the firing of side and curtain airbags is handled by a separate unit next to the main restraints module. A receiver, usually the main restraints module, sets U0453 when the left unit's crash or status data are invalid; U0152 is lost contact, U0454 covers the right side. No manufacturer documents U0453 publicly.",["Loose or corroded connector of the left side unit, for example under the seat or in the B-pillar","Software or configuration of the left unit not matching the main restraints module","Internal fault of the left side restraints unit, often after a side impact"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side or curtain airbag on the left possibly not available"],4,0,["U0152","U0454","U0452"],""],U0454:["Invalid Data Received From Side Restraints Control Module - Right","U0454 is the right-hand counterpart of U0453. Where a separate side restraints unit on the right evaluates side impact sensing or fires the right side and curtain airbags, a partner, normally the central airbag controller, stores U0454 when it judges that unit's messages corrupt or implausible. Contact itself still exists; a silent right unit would be U0153. No manufacturer documents U0454 publicly.",["Loose or corroded plug of the right side unit, for example under the right seat or in the B-pillar","Software or configuration of the right unit not matching the central airbag controller, often after a module swap","Internal fault of the right side restraints unit, for instance after a side impact on the right"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side or curtain airbag on the right possibly unavailable"],4,0,["U0153","U0453","U0452","U0455"],""],U0455:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints Occupant Classification System Module","The occupant classification module reads sensors in the front passenger seat and reports to the restraints controller if the seat is vacant, occupied by a child seat or by an adult; FMVSS 208 lets carmakers switch the passenger airbag off automatically on that basis. U0455 means the restraints controller still receives this classification but finds it invalid, whereas U0154 is total loss of contact.",["Restraints controller software needing an update and as-built configuration","Damaged or unplugged seat harness of the passenger seat, for example after seat removal or adjustment","Faulty occupant classification module or seat sensor mat"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Passenger airbag on/off indicator wrong or flashing","Emergency call function reported as unavailable"],4,0,["U0154","U0452","U0453","U0454"],""],U0456:["Invalid Data Received From Coolant Temperature Control Module","U0456 means a module receives messages from the coolant temperature control module but rejects them as invalid; U0116 is the lost-contact twin. Such a controller runs electronically managed cooling, for example an electric coolant pump whose built-in electronics, as Bosch describes for its PAD2 pump, take speed commands over PWM or LIN and report back.",["Coolant in the plug or pigtail of the electric water pump","Blown fuse or weak supply of the pump or cooling control module","Faulty electronics of the electric coolant pump or cooling module"],["Engine or coolant temperature warning","Reduced engine power as protection","Check engine lamp on some models"],2,3,["U0116","P25AF"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת טמפרטורת נוזל קירור"],U0457:["Invalid Data Received From Information Center A","Information center A is the first of two driver information displays defined alongside the instrument cluster, in practice often the central screen or head unit of the infotainment system. U0457 is stored when a listener still hears this display but rejects what it sends, for example because a message counter or checksum fails, the kind of protection AUTOSAR specifies for safety-related frames;",["Software fault or version mismatch in the display or head unit","Poorly seated fuse or weak supply of the display unit","Connector or bus wiring fault at the display"],["Central display showing wrong, frozen or no content","Network malfunction message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0156","U0458","U0423"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מרכז מידע‏ A"],U0458:["Invalid Data Received From Information Center B","U0458 covers the second driver information display, information center B, which J2012 keeps apart from center A, the instrument cluster and the head-up display; which physical screen a maker calls B, for example a passenger or rear-seat display, is its own decision.",["Software fault or unsuitable software level in display B","Loose connector or damaged bus wiring to display B","Internal fault of display B"],["Second display blank, frozen or showing wrong values","Functions operated through that display unavailable"],2,0,["U0157","U0457","U0423"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מרכז מידע‏ B"],U0459:["Invalid Data Received From Head Up Display","The head-up display shows speed, route arrows or warnings as a virtual image in the windscreen. It takes most content from other modules and reports its own state, such as brightness, image position, page or standby, back over the vehicle bus or a LIN link to the cluster. U0459 is set when a partner receives HUD data that fail its checks; U0158 means the HUD is not heard at all.",["Software of the cluster or HUD handling messages badly, for example around standby","HUD shutting down or sending fault status because of heat","Connector or LIN/bus wiring fault at the HUD"],["Head-up display blank or frozen","Brightness, position or page settings have no effect"],2,0,["U0158","U0423","U0457"],""],U045A:["Invalid Data Received From Parking Assist Control Module A","Parking assist module A evaluates the ultrasonic sensors and in newer cars requests steering or braking for automated parking. U045A flags invalid data from it; U0159 is lost contact, U0544 covers module B.",["Parking assist module software needing an update","Water or corrosion in ultrasonic sensor plugs or the bumper harness","Receiver storing the code as harmless history after a software change"],["Park assist or automatic parking unavailable","Parking sensor indicator flashing or false obstacle warnings","Emergency braking or collision warning message"],2,0,["U0159","U0544","U0243"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ A"],U045B:["Invalid Data Received From Anti-Lock Brake System (ABS) Control Module B","ABS module B is a second brake controller, found where braking has to survive a single fault. Bosch pairs an electromechanical booster or its integrated power brake with ESP for that purpose and, for automated driving, adds a separate redundant brake unit; its 2018 show message was that automated driving needs redundancy.",["Software levels of brake module A and B or the automation computer not matching","Weak supply or ground of brake module B","Internal fault of brake module B"],["Brake system or ABS warning","Automated or hands-off driving functions unavailable"],4,2,["U015A","U0415","U0121","U045C"],""],U045C:["Invalid Data Received From Power Steering Control Module B","Power steering module B is the second controller of a redundant electric steering system. Bosch presented a fail-operational EPS for highly automated driving in 2017: if one path fails, the system can still steer the car to a safe stop or spare the driver a sudden rise in steering effort.",["Software or calibration of steering module B not matching module A","Voltage dips or poor ground at the second steering path","Internal fault of steering module B"],["Steering system warning","Lane centring or automated steering unavailable","Steering assist reduced in some cases"],4,2,["U015B","U0420","U0131","U045B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת הגה כוח‏ B"],U045D:["Invalid Data Received From Automated Driving System Control Module A","Automated driving system control module A is a computer that merges radar and camera data and plans braking and steering for features such as adaptive cruise, lane centring and emergency braking. U045D means a partner hears it but gets implausible content; U015C is lost contact. Stellantis documents the code.",["Outdated software in the front long-range radar or ADAS module","Strained or badly routed Ethernet cable with poor pin contact at the ADAS modules","Internal fault of the ADAS control module"],["Automatic emergency braking unavailable message","MIL on in affected Stellantis models","Adaptive cruise and lane centring disabled"],4,3,["U015C","U045E","U045F"],""],U045E:["Invalid Data Received From Automated Driving System Control Module B","Control module B is the second unit of a split automated driving computer, and the two halves check each other. Stellantis documents U045E in STAR case S2508000095 for 2024-26 Jeep Wagoneer and Grand Wagoneer: the CADM and the global navigation and motion module store U045E-00 next to U015D-00, Ethernet link errors and time synchronisation faults, and the freeze-frame data name failed message checks on two internal…",["Ethernet cable routed too tight, straining plugs and pins at the ADAS modules","Harness clip at the ADAS decision module outside the specified distance","Internal fault of ADAS control module B"],["Blind spot alert unavailable message","Blind spot lamps in the mirrors stay lit","Driver assistance features disabled"],4,2,["U015D","U045D","U0460"],""],U045F:["Invalid Data Received From Automated Driving System Interface Module A","Interface module A sits between an automated driving computer and the base vehicle: it turns the computer's steering, braking and propulsion requests into commands the vehicle's own controllers accept and reports their state back. Bosch places this act layer at the end of its sense-think-act chain.",["Software of interface module A not matching the automation computer or actuator controllers","Connector, bus wiring or supply fault at interface A","Internal fault of interface module A"],["Automated driving or advanced assistance refuses to engage","Takeover request or warning to the driver"],4,2,["U015E","U0460","U045D"],""],U0460:["Invalid Data Received From Automated Driving System Interface Module B","Interface module B is the second, redundant link between an automated driving computer and the brakes, steering and propulsion. Bosch says plainly that automated driving is impossible without redundancy, which is why it doubles brake and steering paths. U0460 applies when B still communicates but its data are corrupt or implausible, for example out-of-sequence counters or CRC errors;",["Software level of interface module B not matching after an update","Loose plug or supply dips at interface B","Internal fault of interface module B"],["Automated driving unavailable or takeover request","Assistance functions limited"],4,2,["U015F","U045F","U045E"],""],U0461:["Invalid Data Received From Audible Alert Control Module","The audible alert control module produces warning chimes, for an unfastened belt, an open door or lights left on; in GM's list of U codes for the 2011 Saab 9-5 the matching node is called chime alarm control module. U0461 is stored when a partner, often the body controller or instrument cluster that requests or confirms the tones, receives status frames from this module that fail plausibility;",["Software of the chime module or requesting unit not matching","Loose plug or weak supply of the chime module","Internal fault of the audible alert module"],["Warning chimes missing, wrong or sounding constantly","Belt reminder without sound"],2,0,["U0160","U0440"],""],U0462:["Invalid Data Received From Compass Module","The compass module measures the earth's magnetic field, usually with two perpendicular sensors in the interior mirror or overhead console, and sends the heading to a display or navigation unit. Gentex patented a mirror compass of this kind with automatic calibration, compensation for magnetic disturbances inside the car and a link to the vehicle bus.",["Compass calibration lost or disturbed by magnetic influences, for example after a battery change or roof-mounted accessories","Loose plug at the interior mirror or overhead console","Internal fault of the compass module or mirror electronics"],["Compass display shows dashes or wrong heading","Heading jumps while driving"],1,0,["U0161","U0463","U0464"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מצפן"],U0463:["Invalid Data Received From Navigation Display Module","The navigation display module is the screen part of a navigation head unit that shows maps and route guidance. U0463 marks invalid data from it, while U0162 means it is silent and U0464 concerns the navigation control unit.",["Software fault or mismatch in the head unit or display","Fuse, relay or supply problem of the display unit","Connector or bus wiring fault at the display"],["Navigation map or screen blank or frozen","Warnings of systems that share data with the head unit"],2,0,["U0162","U0464","P0463"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תצוגת ניווט"],U0464:["Invalid Data Received From Navigation Control Module","U0464 is stored when a module still hears the navigation control module but rejects its content: a frame whose checksum fails, a message counter that no longer advances, or position, heading and route values outside their defined range. Typical listeners are the instrument cluster or head-up display, which repeat turn arrows, and on some cars predictive cruise or shift logic that reads the map ahead.",["Navigation unit software or map update fault sending implausible values","Loose connector or damaged bus wiring at the navigation unit or head unit","Weak 12 V battery or voltage dips during start-up corrupting frames","Internal fault in the navigation control module"],["Turn arrows missing in the cluster or head-up display","Vehicle position on the map jumps or is wrong","Route guidance stops or restarts unexpectedly"],2,0,["U0163","U0463","U046B","U0162"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ניווט"],U0465:["Invalid Data Received From PTO Control Module","U0465 flags implausible data from the power take-off (PTO) controller. That unit switches in an engine-driven output for dump beds, aerial lifts or pumps and asks the engine for a working speed. The engine or body controller logs it when PTO state or speed requests arrive corrupted or contradictory.",["Damaged or corroded wiring and connectors of the body-mounted PTO module","Mismatched configuration after installing or changing the body equipment","Voltage drops while the PTO and hydraulic loads are running","Internal fault in the PTO control module"],["PTO cannot be engaged or disengages on its own","Working engine speed for the body equipment is not held","PTO warning or message in the cluster"],3,0,["U0117","P064B","U0645"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת PTO"],U0466:["Invalid Data Received From HVAC Control Module - Rear","U0466 concerns the rear HVAC control module, the second climate controller in vans, minivans and large SUVs that runs its own blower, blend flaps and often a separate control panel for the back rows. A receiver such as the front climate unit or the body controller sets the code when the rear module's frames carry bad checksums, stalled counters or settings it cannot accept. No manufacturer documents U0466 publicly.",["Loose or corroded connector at the rear HVAC module, often in the rear trim or headliner","Software mismatch after replacing or programming one of the climate modules","Weak battery or voltage dips at the module","Internal fault in the rear HVAC control module"],["Rear climate controls do not respond","Rear blower or temperature stuck at one setting","Climate warning or fault message in the display"],2,0,["U0165","U0424","U0164","U0664"],""],U0467:["Invalid Data Received From Fuel Additive Control Module","U0467 belongs to diesels that use a fuel-borne catalyst. A separate fuel additive control module meters a metal-based additive from its own reservoir into the fuel after refuelling, so that soot trapped in the particulate filter ignites at about 350-450 °C instead of above 600 °C.",["Corroded connector or damaged wiring at the additive pump module near the tank","Faulty additive level sensor feeding implausible values into the module","Module not adapted after refilling the additive or replacing the particulate filter","Internal fault in the fuel additive control module"],["Check engine lamp or particulate filter warning","Regeneration becomes more frequent or incomplete","Reduced engine power once the filter loads up"],3,3,["U0118","P2584","P2585"],""],U0468:["Invalid Data Received From Fuel Cell Control Module","U0468 marks invalid data from the fuel cell control module, the master controller of a hydrogen car, managing air and hydrogen supply, heat and water in the stack and the split of electrical power between stack, buffer battery and drive. Partners such as the motor inverter, battery management or the hydrogen storage unit reject its frames when checksums, counters or power requests do not hold up.",["Fuel cell control unit software needing an update from the manufacturer","Weak 12 V battery or poor ground disturbing the controller","Connector or bus wiring fault between the fuel cell unit and its partners","Internal fault in the fuel cell control module"],["Fuel cell system warning in the cluster","Reduced power, driving on the buffer battery only","Vehicle does not reach READY"],4,3,["U0119","U0293"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת תא דלק"],U0469:["Invalid Data Received From Starter / Generator Control Module","U0469 means the engine controller or gateway receives data from the starter/generator control module but cannot trust it. On 48 V mild hybrids this electronics sits in the belt starter generator, which cranks the engine, recuperates and charges both networks.",["Outdated software in the starter/generator control module","Other CAN or sensor faults disturbing the hybrid bus, with the generator only reporting the effect","48 V battery or 12 V supply problem upsetting the generator electronics","Internal hardware fault in the belt starter generator"],["Electrical system fault message and yellow or red battery symbol","Start-stop and recuperation no longer work","12 V battery not charged while driving"],3,3,["U0120","P0CA7","U0029","U0028"],""],U046A:["Invalid Data Received From Sunroof Control Module","U046A is logged when a module, usually the body controller or the overhead console, gets data from the sunroof control module that fails its checks: position and motion reports that contradict each other, a counter that stops changing or a bad checksum. The sunroof module drives the glass panel and sun blind and tracks their end positions.",["Water in the roof module or its connector from blocked sunroof drains","Lost end-position learning after battery disconnection or panel work","Chafed wiring or loose connector in the headliner","Internal fault in the sunroof control module"],["Sunroof does not open or close with its switch","Convenience closing by key or rain sensor no longer works","Panel stops midway or reverses unexpectedly"],2,0,["U0169","U0140"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גג שמש"],U046B:["Invalid Data Received From Global Positioning System Module","U046B indicates that position, speed or time data from the global positioning system module fail plausibility in a receiving unit: a corrupt frame, a counter that stalls, or coordinates that cannot match the movement the car measures through its wheel speeds. The receiver feeds navigation, telematics, emergency call and map-based assistance.",["Damaged GPS antenna, cable or connector giving poor or jumping fixes","Software fault in the GPS or telematics module","Low battery voltage or poor ground at the module","Internal fault in the GPS module"],["Vehicle position on the map is wrong, jumps or freezes","Connected services or emergency call show no location","Clock or time zone set incorrectly"],2,0,["U016A","U0464","U0198"],""],U046C:["Invalid Data Received From A/C Compressor Control Module","U046C means that the electric A/C compressor's controller, i.e. the inverter spinning the high-voltage compressor in hybrids and EVs, sends data a receiver refuses: speed, power draw or status with bad checksums, frozen counters or values outside their range. Receivers are the climate controller and the hybrid or engine controller, which also use the refrigerant circuit to cool the traction battery.",["Damaged or chafed low-voltage harness or connector at the electric compressor","Compressor inverter software fault or mismatch after service","Weak 12 V supply disturbing the compressor electronics","Internal fault in the compressor control electronics"],["Air conditioning blows warm or switches off intermittently","Battery cooling limited, slower DC charging in hot weather","Climate or hybrid system warning in the cluster"],4,2,["U016B","U032A","U0424","U010F"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן"],U046D:["Invalid Data Received From Fuel Pump Control Module B","U046D is about module B, the second of two fuel pump drivers, used on vehicles with two in-tank pumps or a saddle tank; for module A the matching code is U0410. A receiver, normally the engine controller, logs it when the module's reports, such as delivered pump output or its own fault status, arrive corrupt or implausible. No manufacturer documents U046D publicly.",["Poor ground or corroded connector at the second fuel pump driver","Damaged feedback or bus wiring between pump module B and the engine controller","Worn pump B drawing excess current and upsetting the driver's reports","Internal fault in fuel pump control module B"],["Check engine lamp on","Hesitation or power loss under heavy load","Long cranking or stalling"],2,3,["U016C","U0410","P027B","P26EA"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת משאבת דלק‏ B"],U046E:["Invalid Data Received From Exhaust Gas Sensor Module B","U046E points to the B unit among exhaust gas sensor modules, a second smart device that warms a probe in the exhaust, interprets its signal, typically from a wide-band oxygen or NOx sensor, and transmits readings and readiness as bus data. The engine or aftertreatment controller sets it when frames still arrive but fail checksum or counter tests, or values such as NOx level or the ready flag are not credible.",["Heat-damaged or corroded connector and harness at the sensor module","Aged or contaminated probe making the module report implausible values","Calibration mismatch after replacing the sensor module","Internal electronics fault in exhaust gas sensor module B"],["Check engine lamp on","Exhaust aftertreatment or emission warning","Higher fuel or urea consumption from substitute values"],2,1,["U041B","U016D","U011A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן גזי פליטה‏ B"],U0471:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor A","U0471 is logged when the airbag controller still receives telegrams from restraints sensor A but rejects their content, for example because of a parity error, a reading outside the sensor's range or values that contradict the other crash sensors. Lost contact would be U0170.",["Water or corrosion at the connector of a front satellite sensor in the engine bay","Sensor or its bracket deformed by a minor frontal impact","Replacement sensor of the wrong part number or orientation fitted"],["Airbag warning lamp stays on","Fault code stored in the restraints control module, sometimes with an internal sensor code"],3,0,["U0170","U0472","U0452","U0151"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ A"],U0472:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor B","U0472 points to restraints sensor B: the airbag controller hears it but discards the transmitted values as corrupt or implausible, whereas U0171 would mean silence. Chrysler's NHTSA filing PE11-019 lists sensor B as the right-hand up-front satellite measuring acceleration on its 2007-2008 Jeep models, paired with internal fault B1B71.",["Front sensor not tightened to specification or loosened after body repair","Chafed or corroded harness between front sensor and airbag controller","Measuring element of the right front satellite defective"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Frontal crash detection possibly degraded until repair"],3,0,["U0171","U0471","U0473","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ B"],U0473:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor C","U0473 means the restraints controller receives sensor C but cannot use what it sends. In Chrysler's lists from investigation PE11-019, C is the first left-side satellite acceleration sensor, present already on the four-sensor Wrangler JK; its internal fault is B1B72, while U0172 covers lost contact.",["Sensor wire pinched or chafed under the B-pillar or sill trim","Side sensor loose because a stud, nut or screw is missing","Sensor damaged by a previous side impact"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Left side and curtain airbag readiness uncertain"],3,0,["U0172","U0474","U0476","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ C"],U0474:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor D","U0474 flags unusable data from restraints sensor D. Chrysler's lists in NHTSA file PE11-019 assign D to the second left-side satellite acceleration sensor (internal fault B1B73, lost contact U0173). It appears only for the 2007-2008 Compass and Patriot, which carry six satellites, and is absent from the four-sensor Wrangler list.",["Cracked solder joint inside the satellite sensor","Connector or wiring fault at the rear side sensor behind the pillar trim","Restraints controller configured for a different sensor layout"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Side impact sensing on the left reduced"],3,0,["U0173","U0473","U0477","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ D"],U0475:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor E","U0475 reports corrupt or implausible data from restraints sensor E; U0174 would be the lost-contact code. No manufacturer publicly ties letter E to a mounting point. Chrysler's restraint fault lists in NHTSA file PE11-019 even skip it, jumping from the second left-side sensor D to the first right-side sensor F.",["Damaged two-wire sensor line or connector","Internal fault in the satellite sensor itself","Restraints controller coding does not match the installed sensors"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller only"],3,0,["U0174","U0474","U0476","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ E"],U0476:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor F","U0476 is stored when restraints sensor F still reports but its values fail the receiver's checks. Chrysler's lists in NHTSA investigation PE11-019 make F the first right-side satellite acceleration sensor, fitted even to the four-sensor Wrangler JK; internal fault B1B75, lost contact U0175. The side has little crush space, so this sensor must deliver usable data within milliseconds.",["Wiring or connector fault at the right side sensor under the pillar or sill trim","Right side sensor damaged or misaligned after a side impact or body repair","Internal fault in the satellite sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right side and curtain airbag readiness uncertain"],3,0,["U0175","U0473","U0477","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ F"],U0477:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor G","U0477 concerns restraints sensor G, whose messages arrive but are judged invalid; U0176 is lost contact. In Chrysler's lists from NHTSA investigation PE11-019, G names the second satellite on the right flank, an acceleration sensor with internal fault B1B76, and appears only on the six-sensor Compass and Patriot.",["Sensor of an unsuitable part number installed","Trapped or chafed sensor line causing corrupted telegrams","Sensor reporting values outside its measuring range"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Right rear side impact sensing reduced"],3,0,["U0176","U0476","U0474","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ G"],U0478:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor H","U0478 flags invalid data from restraints sensor H, the counterpart of lost-contact code U0177. No manufacturer publishes which sensor carries the letter H; the Chrysler fault tables filed with NHTSA under PE11-019 stop at G. An H implies at least eight satellites.",["Moisture or a damaged seal affecting a door-mounted pressure sensor","Sensor line damaged, for example in a door hinge harness","Restraints controller coded for a sensor set that is not fitted"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code present only in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U0177","U0477","U0479","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ H"],U0479:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor I","U0479 records that restraints sensor I sends data the airbag controller refuses; U0178 would be silence. No public source assigns the letter I to a mounting point, and a ninth peripheral sensor is rarely documented.",["Damaged line or connector to the sensor","Sensor disturbed by loose cargo or a poor mounting location","Internal sensor fault"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U0178","U0478","U047A","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ I"],U047A:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor J","U047A means the airbag controller receives restraints sensor J but its content fails validation; lost contact is U0179. Which component carries the letter J is not published anywhere. Pedestrian protection is one source of extra inputs: Bosch fits either acceleration sensors or an air-filled tube with a pressure sensor at each end into the front bumper, lets the airbag controller evaluate them and can raise the hood…",["Bumper-mounted sensor damaged by a parking knock or bumper repair","Line or connector fault on the sensor circuit","Controller coding does not match the fitted sensors"],["Airbag or pedestrian protection warning shown","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U0179","U0479","U047B","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ J"],U047B:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor K","U047B: restraints sensor K is heard but its values are rejected; U017A covers lost contact. No manufacturer documents the letter K publicly, so its position stays open. Eleven satellites point to a large system, yet not every function needs one of its own: Bosch's AB premium controller can house rollover and inertial sensing internally and accepts as many as 18 PSI5 sensors.",["Corroded or loose connector in the sensor line","Defective satellite sensor","Restraints controller software evaluating the sensor incorrectly"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U017A","U047A","U047C","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ K"],U047C:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor L","U047C sets when restraints sensor L still communicates but delivers unusable data; U017B is the lost-contact partner. L is the twelfth sensor letter, and twelve is exactly the number of PSI5 sensor interfaces Bosch quotes for its standard airbag control unit; more requires the premium version. No carmaker publishes what sits behind L.",["Damaged shielding or twisted pair causing checksum errors","Defective satellite sensor","Controller coding not matching the sensor equipment"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U017B","U047B","U047D","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ L"],U047D:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor M","U047D reports invalid data from restraints sensor M; U017C is lost contact. A thirteenth satellite exceeds the twelve sensor interfaces of Bosch's standard airbag control unit, so a system using M needs a larger controller such as Bosch's AB premium with up to 18. No manufacturer discloses which component is M.",["Sensor variant not matching the vehicle configuration","Damaged satellite sensor","Restraints controller software misinterpreting the sensor data"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U017C","U047C","U047E","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ M"],U047E:["Invalid Data Received From Restraints System Sensor N","U047E closes the sensor series: restraints sensor N still sends, but its data are rejected; U017D is lost contact, and the following codes U047F and U0480 move on to belt pretensioner modules. Fourteen external sensors is precisely the maximum Bosch states for its airbag control unit for commercial vehicles.",["Corroded connector or damaged line to the sensor","Outdated restraints controller software or wrong sensor configuration","Defective satellite sensor"],["Airbag warning lamp on","Code stored in the restraints controller"],3,0,["U017D","U047D","U047F","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן מערכת כריות האוויר‏ N"],U047F:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Belt Pretensioner Module A","U047F concerns seat belt pretensioner module A, a belt retractor with its own motor and electronics rather than a purely pyrotechnic tensioner fired by the airbag unit. Such reversible retractors take up slack before a possible crash, during emergency braking or evasive steering, and can warn by pulsing the strap, as ZF LIFETEC describes for its ACR8.",["Software fault in the belt pretensioner module or its bus partner","Supply or bus wiring fault at the retractor in the B-pillar or seat","Internal fault in the motorised retractor module"],["Warning that proactive occupant protection is faulty","No belt pre-tensioning during hard braking","Airbag or restraint warning possible"],3,0,["U017E","U0480","U017F","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות‏ A"],U0480:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Belt Pretensioner Module B","U0480 mirrors U047F for seat belt pretensioner module B: the receiver gets its messages but finds them invalid, whereas U017F would mean silence. Honda's patent US 7,686,118 shows how such a unit is tied in: a dedicated electric belt controller drives the retractor motor, sits on the vehicle LAN, takes collision warnings from the brake control unit and receives the buckle signal routed through the airbag controller.",["Software fault in pretensioner module B or the unit sending it data","Faulty input relayed through the module, such as the buckle signal","Internal fault in the motorised retractor"],["Belt pre-tensioning or haptic belt warning unavailable","Restraint system warning message"],3,0,["U017F","U047F","U017E","U0452"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול קדם-מותחן חגורת בטיחות‏ B"],U0481:["Invalid Data Received From Automatic Lighting Control Module","U0481 means a module still receives frames from the automatic lighting control module but refuses their content, for instance an ambient-light value outside its range, a frozen message counter or a failed checksum; silence from that unit would be U0180. The unit decides from a light sensor, often housed with the rain sensor behind the windscreen, when the headlamps come on. No manufacturer documents U0481 publicly.",["Light or rain/light sensor delivering values outside its range, e.g. after heat soak or windscreen replacement","Software or configuration of the lighting module not matching the receiving module","Corroded or loose connector on the bus line to the module"],["Automatic headlamp function unavailable, lights must be switched manually","Exterior lighting warning or message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0180","U0483","U0482","U0140"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת תאורה אוטומטית"],U0482:["Invalid Data Received From Headlamp Leveling Control Module A","U0482 is stored when messages from headlamp leveling control module A arrive but fail the receiver's integrity or plausibility checks; complete loss of contact is U0181, and U048B covers a second leveling unit. Such a module takes axle ride-height signals and moves the beam actuators so that a loaded boot or hard braking does not lift the cut-off line, as Hella explains; dynamic versions also react to acceleration.",["Bent or faulty axle ride-height sensor feeding implausible values into the module","Leveling module software computing or transmitting wrong values","Basic setting of the leveling system not performed after repair or replacement"],["Headlamp leveling warning in the cluster","Beam height no longer adapts to load and may dazzle or fall short","Inclination display or related functions show fixed values"],2,0,["U0181","U048B","U018A","U0483"],""],U0483:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Control Module - Front","U0483 means the front lighting control module, which switches low and high beam, daytime running and turn lamps or drives the LED channels in the headlamps, is still on the bus but delivers data the receiver rejects. U0182 would be the silent module, U0484 the rear counterpart. GM's Saab list names the front lighting control module among its partners.",["Weak battery or voltage dips during cranking upsetting the lighting module","Lighting module software or calibration fault","Moisture or corrosion at the module or headlamp connector"],["Headlamps or daytime running lamps flicker or flash","Exterior lighting warning in the cluster","Front lamps stay in a fixed default state"],2,0,["U0182","U0484","U0481","U0140"],""],U0484:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Control Module - Rear A","U0484 is set when frames from rear lighting control module A are received but carry values the listener cannot accept; U0183 stands for lost contact, while rear module B has U0252 and U0553. Such modules drive tail, stop and turn lamps or LED segments at the back and report their status.",["Software error in the rear lighting module or a module not updated to the current level","Chafed or broken wires in the tailgate or boot lid harness","Water ingress at a rear lamp connector"],["Rear light system warning although the lamps may still work","Turn, stop or tail lamp failures not reported or lamps in default mode"],2,0,["U0183","U0553","U0252","U0483"],""],U0485:["Invalid Data Received From Radio","U0485 means the radio or centre stack still transmits but a receiving module rejects its frames. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG03B, 25OBDG04B) describe the body control module checking alive rolling counters, protection values, checksums and CRCs of centre-stack signals, among them HVAC control requests: 8 failures in 10 samples, for some signals 14 in 18 or 15 in 16, set it at least 5 s after power-up, with the partial…",["Radio or infotainment software level with known message errors, fixed by an update","Radio resetting or waking late so that counters and checksums no longer match","Low supply voltage or a disturbed bus connection to the centre stack"],["Radio resets, black screen or audio sources inoperative","Climate controls on the screen do not respond","MIL on some vehicles"],2,1,["U0184","U0334","U0487","U0424"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: רדיו"],U0486:["Invalid Data Received From Antenna Control Module","U0486 points to the antenna control module: its frames still arrive, yet the receiver, typically the radio or a keyless-entry controller, discards them as corrupt or implausible. U0185 would mean silence. Such modules sit in the roof fin, rear screen or bumper and amplify, combine or switch signals for radio, satellite, navigation, phone or remote key, and some raise a powered mast.",["Water reaching the antenna module through a roof leak or failed fin seal","Internal fault of the antenna amplifier or module","Damaged coaxial or bus connector between antenna module and receiver"],["Poor or no radio, satellite or navigation reception","Remote key does not unlock or works only at short range"],2,0,["U0185","U0485","U0258"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת אנטנה"],U0487:["Invalid Data Received From Audio Amplifier A","U0487 means the external audio amplifier A keeps sending frames, but the radio or gateway finds their content invalid; once the amplifier vanishes from the bus, U0186 applies, and amplifier B has U0262 and U0563. Amplifiers return status such as mute state, sound settings and diagnostic results to the head unit. No manufacturer documents U0487 publicly.",["Backed-out or spread pin in the amplifier or MOST connector","Amplifier software level not matching the head unit","Poor supply or ground at the amplifier"],["No sound or radio muted","Static or crackling from the speakers, sometimes when tapping the dash"],2,0,["U0186","U0563","U0262","U0485"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מגבר שמע‏ A"],U0488:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Disc Player/Changer Module A","U0488 is logged when the first networked disc drive, module A, still reports on the bus but its data fail the receiver's checks; U0187 would mean the drive is silent, while U0489, U048A and U0491 cover drives B to D.",["Disc player hung internally, cleared by a power cycle","Poor supply or ground at the disc player","Disc player itself defective"],["CD or DVD playback unavailable","Other audio sources keep working"],2,0,["U0187","U0489","U048A","U0491"],""],U0489:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Disc Player/Changer Module B","U0489 refers to disc player/changer module B, a second drive in the same network, such as a changer added to a radio that already plays CDs or a DVD unit for the rear seats. The receiver still hears it but rejects the content, whereas loss of contact is U0188; drive A has U0488.",["Replacement changer fitted without removing the transport lock","Mechanical or internal fault in the changer","Vehicle coded for a second drive that is missing or of another type"],["Second disc drive does not accept or play discs","Disc error message on the display"],2,0,["U0188","U0488","U048A","U0491"],""],U048A:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Disc Player/Changer Module C","U048A stands for a third disc player or changer, module C. It is set when that unit's frames reach the receiver but fail its checks; silence would be U0189. Three networked drives in one vehicle are rare. Luxury cars with a DVD changer in addition to the head unit come closest: Audi's update 72K1 for the 2019 A8 replaced the changer mounting because its trim cover could come loose.",["Wrong vehicle coding after a retrofit or removal of a disc unit","Supply, ground or bus connection fault at the third drive","Internal fault of the disc unit"],["Disc playback from that unit unavailable","Code present without any noticeable fault on cars without such a unit"],2,0,["U0189","U0489","U0488","U0491"],""],U048B:["Invalid Data Received From Headlamp Leveling Control Module B","U048B concerns the second headlamp leveling control module, B, whose messages reach the receiver but are discarded as corrupt or implausible; if B fell silent, U018A would be logged, while module A has U0482 and U0181. A second address is needed where each headlamp carries its own electronics or a central unit works with lamp-side controllers. No maker assigns the letter publicly or documents U048B.",["Software of the lamp-side or leveling module misjudging actuator feedback","Setup or configuration of the headlamp module not completed after assembly or replacement","Moisture or poor contact at the connector of the second headlamp"],["Headlamp leveling or adaptive lighting warning","Beam height on one side no longer adjusted"],2,0,["U018A","U0482","U0181"],""],U0491:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Disc Player/Changer Module D","U0491 belongs to a fourth networked disc player or changer, module D: frames from that drive still arrive, yet the radio or gateway rejects their content. Its lost-contact partner is U0190; drives A to C have U0488, U0489 and U048A.",["Vehicle coding or head-unit software expecting a fourth disc drive that is absent or different","Disc drive D hung up or internally faulty","Poor supply, ground or bus link at the drive"],["Discs in that drive cannot be played","Code stored without noticeable fault on cars lacking such a drive"],2,0,["U0190","U0488","U0489","U048A"],""],U0492:["Invalid Data Received From Television","U0492 is set when a television tuner keeps transmitting but the module listening to it, usually the head unit or a display controller, cannot use what arrives, for instance because values lie outside their defined range, a message counter stalls or a checksum is wrong.",["Tuner or head-unit software with faulty TV data, cured by an update","Internal fault of the TV tuner","Supply, ground or bus connection fault at the tuner"],["No TV picture or a frozen, blurred image","Radio and other media sources keep working"],2,0,["U0191","U0485","U0497"],""],U0493:["Invalid Data Received From Personal Computer","U0493 covers a personal computer sharing the vehicle network, a slot in the J2012 list that hardly any production car fills. The nearest real case is a fleet or police vehicle with a laptop or mobile data terminal wired into the car: Ford's 2027 Police Interceptor Utility offers an Integrated Computer Screen that mirrors a laptop stowed in the cargo bay, and a Vehicle Integration System that lets upfitters read the…",["Aftermarket computer installation or interface box sending non-conforming frames","Software or configuration of the connected computer","Wiring or connector fault at the vehicle interface"],["Functions of the connected computer that rely on vehicle data fail","Often no noticeable fault in the vehicle itself"],2,0,["U0192","U0499"],""],U0494:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Audio Control Module A","U0494 is stored when digital audio control module A still communicates but supplies data the receiver will not accept. In GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 and 9-4X lists the matching lost-contact code U0193 belongs to the digital radio receiver, at that time the separate XM satellite tuner.",["Receiver software or activation state producing unexpected values","Supply, ground or bus fault at the receiver's connector","Digital radio receiver internally defective"],["Satellite or digital radio channels missing or showing errors","Analogue radio and other sources unaffected"],2,0,["U0193","U0495","U0496"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ A"],U0495:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Audio Control Module B","U0495 is the invalid-data code for a second digital audio unit, module B. Where slot A is used at all, it tends to be the digital or satellite radio receiver, as in GM's Saab lists; for B no public code list or bulletin names a concrete device, and no maker documents U0495.",["Coding or software mismatch about which device occupies slot B","Damaged or pinched bus wiring disturbing several modules","Internal fault of digital audio module B"],["One digital audio source unavailable","Often stored together with other network codes"],2,0,["U0194","U0494","U0193"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ B"],U0496:["Invalid Data Received From Subscription Entertainment Receiver Module","U0496 points to the subscription entertainment receiver: a tuner whose programmes, typically SiriusXM satellite radio in North America, play only with a paid, activated account. Its frames still reach the radio, but their content fails the checks; complete silence would be U0195.",["Subscription or activation state not refreshed, receiver reports unexpected status","Internal binding failure of the receiver","Supply, ground or bus fault at the receiver"],["Only preview channels or no satellite channels at all","Terrestrial radio and media work normally"],1,0,["U0195","U0494","U0486"],""],U0497:["Invalid Data Received From Entertainment Control Module - Rear A","U0497 concerns rear entertainment control module A, which lets people in the back choose media, listen on headphones and watch their own screens independently of the front. It is set when that unit's data reach the head unit or gateway but fail the plausibility, counter or checksum test; U0196 means contact is lost. In the Saab code lists GM published for 2011, that partner is the rear audio control module.",["Software of the rear unit or the head unit mishandling shared video or audio data","Internal fault of the rear entertainment unit or its media player","Supply, ground or bus connection fault at the rear unit"],["Rear screens show a rolling or missing picture","Rear headphones or controls without function","Front audio system usually keeps working"],2,0,["U0196","U0485","U0491"],""],U0498:["Invalid Data Received From Telephone Control Module","U0498 is logged when the telephone control module, the hands-free or Bluetooth unit, still sends frames but the head unit or body controller rejects their content. For Chrysler the lost-contact partner U0197 is the hands-free phone module (HFM); its bulletins 08-112-14 (2013-2015 Town & Country, Grand Caravan, Wrangler, Challenger and others) and 08-055-17 Rev.",["Hands-free module software fault, cured by reprogramming","Module not booting fully or resetting, so its status values are invalid","Internal hardware fault of the telephone module"],["Bluetooth pairing or hands-free calls fail","Phone menu unavailable or stuck on a loading message"],2,0,["U0197","U0499","U0485"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת טלפון"],U0499:["Invalid Data Received From Telematic Control Module","U0499 means the telematic control module, which carries the cellular modem for remote services and, in the EU, the 112 eCall required by Regulation 2015/758, sends data a receiver rejects. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG04B) let the object calculation module EOCM3 check ARC, checksum or MAC on the telematics unit's precise positioning frames (heading, latitude, longitude): 6 of 10 faulty, judged over 8 s of a 10 s window,…",["Telematics module software sending faulty or unprotected frames, fixed by an update","Corrupted positioning data from the telematics unit (GPS antenna or receiver issues)","Internal fault of the telematics module"],["Super Cruise or adaptive cruise unavailable on GM vehicles","Connected services or an infotainment service message","Often no noticeable effect, code cannot be cleared"],2,0,["U0198","U0498","U0493"],""],U049A:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module A","U049A reports implausible data from door control module A, usually the driver's door: the unit that runs window lift, lock and mirror and reads the door switches. The body controller or gateway still hears it but rejects the content because a value is undefined, a counter jumps or a checksum fails.",["Chafed wires or loose pins in the door harness between body and door","Driver door module internally faulty, for example after water ingress","Wrong configuration or software after module replacement or retrofit"],["Driver window or mirror switches without function","Central locking ignores the driver's door"],2,0,["U0199","U0501","U0502","U0140"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ A"],U049B:["Invalid Data Received From Tachograph Module","U049B is set when the tachograph still transmits but its data are rejected. In trucks and buses EU Regulation 165/2014 has the device record speed, distance and driving times from a motion sensor, and units such as Continental VDO's DTCO 4.1a pass these values on through two CAN interfaces. Engine, transmission or body controllers then rely on the tachograph speed, so implausible frames matter beyond the logbook.",["Tachograph calibration or parameters not matching the vehicle, e.g. after a tyre or axle change","Faulty motion sensor or sensor wiring producing implausible speed values","Internal fault of the tachograph unit"],["Speedometer or tachograph speed missing or erratic","Cruise control, speed limiter or shift behaviour affected","Tachograph fault message"],4,0,["U019A","P0500"],""],U049C:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Charger Control Module A","U049C means the on-board charger, battery charger control module A, is heard on the bus but reports values the battery controller considers invalid. Ford's 2019 OBD summary for hybrid and plug-in vehicles has the BECM set it when the charger's CAN signal shows invalid states for 5 s; U019B is the same charger missing for 5 s.",["Charger module software reporting invalid states, cured by reprogramming","Software levels of charger and battery controller not matching","Internal fault of the on-board charger"],["High-voltage battery does not charge, error shown at the charging station","Charge fault message or wrench lamp in the cluster","Driving itself unaffected"],4,0,["U019B","U0412","U0293"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ A"],U049D:["Invalid Data Received From Glow Plug Control Module 2","U049D is logged when a controller, normally the engine control module, still hears from the second glow plug control module but cannot trust what it reports, for instance because a counter, checksum or plug status value is out of line. A second unit is found on diesels that split their glow plugs between two drivers. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; it mirrors U0407, which covers module 1.",["Corroded or loose connector or data wire at glow plug module 2","Supply voltage sagging while the glow plugs draw high current","Glow plug control module 2 internally faulty","Module or engine controller software not matched after replacement"],["Check engine or glow plug warning light on","Long cranking or misfire on cold starts","White smoke until the engine warms up"],2,1,["U019C","U030B","U0407"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מצת להט‏ 2"],U049E:["Invalid Data Received From Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor","Direct ozone reduction (DOR) means a catalytic coating on the radiator, sold by BASF as PremAir, that turns ground-level ozone into oxygen while air flows through the core. CARB grants an emissions credit for it and, under section (e)(14) of 1968.2, wants OBD to watch the coating on cars that claim the credit; a temperature sensor on the radiator serves this purpose.",["Radiator temperature sensor electronics faulty","Damaged connector or wiring near the radiator (impact, corrosion)","Replacement radiator or sensor not matching the original DOR version","Sensor or engine controller software version not matching"],["Check engine light on without noticeable drivability change","Emissions inspection failed or readiness not set"],2,1,["U019D","P2567","P2568"],""],U049F:["Invalid Data Received From Transmission Range Control Module","The transmission range control module (TRCM) is the shift-by-wire actuator that physically moves the transmission between P, R, N and D after the driver selects a range electronically. U049F is stored by a module that receives TRCM messages whose content it rejects. Ford lists U049F in its 2014 OBD code chart without the MIL marker it gives to other codes such as U04A4.",["TRCM electronics or actuator position sensing faulty","Outdated TRCM calibration (GM 16-NA-373 calls for reprogramming)","Bus wiring or connector fault at the transmission-mounted module","Low or unstable battery voltage while shifting"],["Shift system or transmission service message","Vehicle stays in Park or does not engage the selected range","Gear indicator disagrees with the selected range"],4,2,["U019E","U031A","U04BD"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת טווח תיבת הילוכים"],U04A0:["Invalid Data Received From Engine Coolant Pump Control Module","Engines with an electric main coolant pump carry a pump whose built-in electronics set the speed on request and send back status and fault information. Rheinmetall, for example, builds such pumps for main engine cooling with a LIN interface and extensive self-diagnosis, and Hella notes that electric pumps can stay off after a cold start so the engine warms faster.",["Pump electronics faulty, often after overheating or coolant ingress","LIN or CAN wire or connector at the pump corroded or loose","Pump running dry or blocked (air in system, debris), reported as error state","Pump or engine controller software not matched after replacement"],["Check engine or coolant temperature warning","Engine runs hot or the cooling fan runs continuously","Reduced engine power to protect the engine"],2,3,["U019F","U0672"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע"],U04A1:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module A","U04A1 means the battery management controller keeps receiving messages from interface control module A, one of the slave boards that measure cell voltages and temperatures inside the high-voltage pack, but rejects their content as invalid.",["Software issue in battery management or cell module controllers (VW ID.4 CMCe case, helpline first)","Interface control module A internally faulty","Loose or corroded connector on the pack-internal data link to module A","Weak 12 V battery disturbing the start-up of the battery electronics"],["Electrical system or high-voltage battery warning in the cluster","Reduced drive power","Charging interrupted or refused"],4,3,["U01A0","U033A","U04A2","U04A5","U04A9","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U04A2:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module B","U04A2 covers the second interface board of the high-voltage pack, module B: its frames reach the battery controller but carry implausible content. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. The closest published logic is GM's 2016 hybrid table 16OBDG02, where the battery systems module talks to eight interface boards, A to H, over a serial UART daisy chain.",["Poor contact in the chain connection between interface boards A, B and C","Interface control module B internally faulty","Outdated calibration in the battery controller"],["Hybrid or EV system warning, MIL on plug-in hybrids","Electric range or power reduced"],4,3,["U01A1","U033B","U04A1","U04A3","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U04A3:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module C","U04A3 concerns interface module C. Such boards do more than measure: they also switch the balancing resistors that bleed charge from individual cells. CARB 1968.2 section (e)(15.2.3) requires hybrid OBD to confirm that cell balancing still holds the cell voltages where intended, and GM checks this per board in 16OBDG02 by closing the odd and even balancing gates in turn and comparing readings, for module C under…",["Interface control module C faulty (measurement or balancing stage)","Damaged cell sense lead or connector at module C","Interference or contact fault on the pack-internal data link"],["Hybrid or EV warning, MIL on plug-in hybrids","Power limited, state of charge shown inaccurately"],4,3,["U01A2","U033C","U04A2","U02A0","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C"],U04A4:["Invalid Data Received From Particulate Matter Sensor A","Diesel particulate matter (PM) sensors have their own control unit that measures soot on the element and sends the result to the engine controller. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG04A) check the alive rolling count, protection value and checksum of about twenty soot sensor signals and set U04A4 after 3 bad frames in 10, with battery voltage of at least 11 V for 5 s;",["PM sensor control unit or sensing element faulty (heat, soot, moisture)","Replacement sensor of the wrong variant or not yet matched","Damaged wiring or connector between sensor unit and engine controller","Low supply voltage disturbing the sensor unit"],["Check engine light on","Particulate filter monitor not completing, readiness missing","Usually no change in how the engine runs"],2,1,["U02A3","U04B2","U05A4","P24AF"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן חלקיקים‏ A"],U04A5:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module E","Module E is the fifth interface board in a high-voltage pack, and U04A5 says its data reach the battery controller in a form that fails the checks. This is one of three letters Volkswagen spells out: for the ID.4 of model years 2021 to 2024 the on-car analysis list of July 2024 groups U04A5 with U04A1 and U04A9, all stored in address 8C, and asks dealers to phone the VW helpline before any repair.",["Software issue in the battery electronics (VW ID.4, clarify with helpline)","Interface control module E internally faulty","Contact fault on the internal link to module E"],["Electrical system warning message","Drive power or charging limited"],4,3,["U01A4","U033E","U02A0","U04A6","U04A1","U04A9"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ E"],U04A6:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module F","U04A6 is set when interface control module F delivers messages the battery controller cannot accept. A board like this checks itself as well: in GM's 16OBDG02 table every interface module, F included, runs four processor performance tests once at each ignition change, for example confirming that its analogue-to-digital converter shows no stuck bits when the input is forced to its limits, Type A after 8 failures in…",["Processor or converter fault on interface board F","Contact fault on the internal data link to module F","Supply dropouts of the battery electronics during switch-on"],["Hybrid or EV warning, MIL on plug-in hybrids","Reduced power output"],4,3,["U01A5","U033F","U04A5","U04A7"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ F"],U04A7:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module G","U04A7 points to interface module G. In a modular battery management system each board sits at a different potential: the ground of the top module can be hundreds of volts above that of the bottom one, so the boards talk through isolated links such as optocouplers or radio.",["Moisture or corrosion at internal connectors (leaking pack seal)","Failing isolated communication stage on board G","Interface control module G otherwise defective"],["Battery or hybrid system warning","Charging or drive power limited","Fault may come and go with humidity or temperature"],4,3,["U01A6","U0340","U04A6","U04A8"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ G"],U04A8:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module H","U04A8 is the invalid-data code for interface module H. In GM's 2016 hybrid table 16OBDG02, H is the last of eight boards that the battery systems module reaches through a daisy chain; a pack of that design needs no higher letter. GM explains that a break anywhere in such a chain cuts off every board behind it, so lost contact is reported for the first board that cannot be recovered.",["Interface control module H internally faulty","Connector or lead fault at the last board of the chain","Faulty cell input on board H producing impossible values"],["Hybrid system warning, MIL on plug-in hybrids","Reduced propulsion power"],4,3,["U01A7","U0341","U04A7","U04A9"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ H"],U04A9:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module I","U04A9 refers to interface module I, the ninth position in the series. It is the third of the codes Volkswagen lists for the ID.4: in the dealer analysis list of July 2024, U04A9 appears beside U04A1 and U04A5 as a CMCe fault in address 8C, valid for model years 2021 to 2024, with an electrical system message as the complaint.",["Software issue in the battery electronics (VW ID.4 case)","Interface control module I internally faulty","Contact fault on the pack-internal link to module I"],["Electrical system warning message","Charging or power restricted"],4,3,["U01A8","U0342","U04A8","U04AA","U04A1","U04A5"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ I"],U04AA:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module J","U04AA flags invalid data from interface module J, the tenth slot. From here on the series only matters for packs with ten or more monitored sections; a nine-module ID.4 battery or an eight-board GM pack like the one in table 16OBDG02 has no J at all. GM's Ultium family, by contrast, assembles packs from anywhere between six and 24 modules of one design, per Wikipedia, and the larger ones clearly exceed ten.",["Disturbed isolated data link inside the pack","Damaged connector at module J","Interface control module J faulty"],["Battery or EV system warning","Power or charging rate reduced"],4,3,["U01A9","U0343","U04A9","U04AB"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ J"],U04AB:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module K","U04AB means interface module K, the eleventh, delivers data the battery controller judges invalid. What those boards report, cell voltages and temperatures, are exactly the inputs that CARB rule 1968.2, paragraph (e)(15.2.3)(A)(iv), names for monitoring in a hybrid energy storage system;",["Faulty temperature or voltage input on board K","Contact fault on the internal data link to module K","Interface control module K internally faulty"],["MIL (plug-in hybrid) or battery warning (EV)","Charging blocked or slowed","Reduced acceleration"],4,3,["U01AA","U0344","U04AA","U04AC"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ K"],U04AC:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module L","U04AC covers interface module L, the twelfth letter. Twelve is a common pack size: Wikipedia gives twelve modules for the larger ID.4 battery and for the Ultium pack of the Cadillac Lyriq. Where one board serves each module, L would be the last board present there. Whether a maker actually wires it that way is not public; the 2024 Volkswagen list names only A, E and I for that car, and no source names U04AC.",["Interface control module L faulty","Loose plug on the internal link to module L","Fault at the pack's external low-voltage connector"],["High-voltage battery warning","Power reduced, possibly no charging"],4,3,["U01AB","U0345","U04AB","U04AD"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ L"],U04AD:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module M","With U04AD the series reaches module M, the thirteenth interface board, which only exists in packs larger than the common twelve-module layout. One example of such a size is GM's Hummer EV: Wikipedia describes its Ultium battery as 24 modules in two layers that can be switched from parallel to series for 800 V fast charging.",["Corrupted frames on the internal link (counter or checksum errors)","Interface control module M faulty","Measurement input on board M reporting impossible values"],["Battery system warning","Fast charging slower or refused"],4,3,["U01AC","U0346","U04AC","U04AE"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ M"],U04AE:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module N","U04AE stands for invalid data from interface module N, the fourteenth. Like the other high letters it can only appear on a large pack, and no manufacturer documents it publicly. What changes for the workshop is mostly practical: the board sits inside the sealed high-voltage battery, so after reading the freeze-frame data and ruling out the 12 V supply and the low-voltage connectors outside the pack, every further…",["12 V supply or low-voltage plug of the pack at fault (check first)","Interface control module N faulty","Contact fault on the internal link to module N"],["Battery or EV system warning","Output and charging power limited"],4,3,["U01AD","U0347","U04AD","U04AF"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ N"],U04AF:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module O","U04AF concerns interface module O, the fifteenth board. In practice a data fault of this kind often follows work on the pack: if a replaced board and the battery controller interpret messages differently, frames arrive formally intact but fail range or counter checks. The software sibling U0348 and a search for available updates therefore belong next to this code, as does U01AE for a module that stopped sending.",["Software levels of replaced board and battery controller do not match","Interface control module O faulty","Plug not fully seated after pack repair"],["Battery warning shortly after a battery repair","Reduced power or charging"],4,3,["U01AE","U0348","U04AE","U04B0"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ O"],U04B0:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module P","U04B0 closes the series: interface module P is the sixteenth and last letter the code lists provide for these boards, with U01AF for lost contact and U0349 for a software mismatch. Packs with more than sixteen monitored sections do exist, such as Ultium batteries with up to 24 modules, so either several modules share one board or the maker uses its own codes beyond P; which applies is not published.",["Interface control module P faulty","Contact fault on the internal link to module P","Battery controller software misreading module P"],["High-voltage system warning","Power and charging limited"],4,3,["U01AF","U0349","U04AF","U04B1"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ P"],U04B1:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Monitor Module","Despite its place after the high-voltage interface series, U04B1 usually concerns the 12 V side: in GM's 2024 OBD table 24OBDG07 the battery monitor module is the intelligent battery sensor on the 12 V battery, read by the body control module over LIN.",["Body control module configuration lost or mismatched after reprogramming (Alfa Romeo)","Intelligent battery sensor on the negative terminal faulty","LIN lead or plug at the battery sensor damaged or corroded"],["Check engine light (GM Type B, after two trips)","Start-stop disabled or charging strategy of the generator changed"],2,1,["U01B0","U04C0"],""],U04B2:["Invalid Data Received From Particulate Matter Sensor B","U04B2 is the B counterpart of U04A4, intended for vehicles that carry a second smart PM sensor, for instance one per exhaust line or one ahead of and one behind a filter. Messages from sensor B still reach the engine controller, but their content is rejected. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the public examples all use the single sensor A.",["Control unit or element of PM sensor B damaged by heat, soot or moisture","Wiring or connector of sensor B chafed or corroded","Sensors A and B swapped or wrong variant fitted"],["Check engine light on","Particulate filter readiness not set"],2,1,["U01B1","U04A4"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן חלקיקים‏ B"],U04B3:["Invalid Data Received From Planetary Gear Set Control Module","Several hybrid transmissions use planetary gear sets whose shift elements are switched to change the operating mode; two-mode hybrids, for example, combine two extra planetary sets with four clutches to move between electric, power-split and fixed-gear driving. Where a separate module controls such a set and reports its state, U04B3 marks messages from that module that arrive but carry implausible data.",["Planetary gear set control module or its position sensing faulty","Bus wiring or connector at the transmission damaged or oil-soaked","Software of module and hybrid controller not matching"],["Hybrid system or transmission warning","Reduced power or electric-only driving unavailable"],4,3,["U01B2"],""],U04B4:["Invalid Data Received From Brake Blending Actuator","In hybrid and electric cars, brake blending decides how much of the requested deceleration the drive motor recovers as energy and how much the friction brakes supply; at low speed the hydraulic brakes take over completely. An electromechanical booster such as Bosch's iBooster, paired with a matching ESP, is rated for blending up to about 0.3 g of regenerative deceleration.",["Blending actuator or its pedal/position sensing faulty","Chassis bus wiring or connector fault","Brake and drive controller software not matching after update or replacement","Low 12 V supply affecting the actuator electronics"],["Brake system or hybrid warning light on","Little or no regenerative braking, shorter range","Brake pedal feels different or harder"],4,3,["U01B3","U04B5"],""],U04B5:["Invalid Data Received From Brake System Control Module B","Brake system control module B is a second brake controller. Bosch, for instance, adds a second, redundant brake unit to its Integrated Power Brake on automated vehicles so the car can still be stopped if the main unit fails, and the iBooster plus ESP pairing serves the same purpose.",["Brake control module B internally faulty","Chassis or private brake bus wiring or connector fault","Software of the two brake modules not matching after update or replacement","Weak supply on the redundant power path"],["Brake, ABS or stability control warning","Driver assistance or automated driving functions unavailable"],4,2,["U01B4","U031C","U0418"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מערכת בלם‏ B"],U04B6:["Invalid Data Received From Catalyst Heater Control Module","An electrically heated catalyst brings the converter to working temperature right after a cold start. Vitesco's EMICAT heater runs at 12, 24 or 48 V and can draw up to 300 A, has been ordered for 48-volt mild hybrid diesel vans with production planned from 2022, and in high-voltage hybrids is fed by a dedicated DC/DC converter.",["Heater control electronics or DC/DC stage faulty","High-current connection to the heater loose or overheated, giving implausible feedback","Bus wiring or connector near the hot exhaust damaged","Module and engine controller software not matching"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst monitor readiness not set","Engine may idle longer at raised speed after cold start"],4,1,["U01B5"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גוף חימום ממיר קטליטי"],U04BA:["Invalid Data Received From Switch Input Module A","A switch input module collects the positions of several buttons and reports them to other control units as network frames. U04BA means that frames from module A keep arriving, but the receiver, usually the body controller, rejects their content: a switch state outside the defined values, a wrong message counter, a failed checksum or an unexpected length.",["Switch module or receiving controller with incompatible software or coding after repair","Switch input module A internally faulty (moisture, damaged switch contacts)","Corroded connector or chafed data lead corrupting the frames"],["Buttons served by the module inoperative or acting intermittently","Code stored in the body controller without a warning lamp"],2,0,["U01B7","U04BB","U04BC"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול כניסת מתג‏ A"],U04BB:["Invalid Data Received From Switch Input Module B","U04BB concerns the second switch input module. A receiving controller still hears module B on the bus, but the switch information inside its frames fails the plausibility, counter or checksum test.",["Replacement switch module of the wrong variant or not coded to the vehicle","Switch input module B internally faulty","Loose or corroded plug between satellite and main module"],["A group of buttons in one panel not responding","Functions switching on by themselves or not switching off"],2,0,["U01B8","U04BA","U04BC"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול כניסת מתג‏ B"],U04BC:["Invalid Data Received From Switch Input Module C","With a third switch input module, addressing becomes a weak point. Several near-identical switch units often hang on one LIN line as slaves, and each needs its own node address, assigned either by part variant or by an auto-addressing routine at start-up.",["Two switch units with the same LIN node address after replacement or failed auto-addressing","Switch input module C internally faulty","Interference on the shared LIN line, e.g. damaged insulation"],["Buttons of module C ignored while other switch groups work","Button presses assigned to the wrong function"],2,0,["U01B9","U04BA","U04BB"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול כניסת מתג‏ C"],U04BD:["Invalid Data Received From Park Lock/Pawl Control Module","With park-by-wire, an electronic unit drives an actuator that pushes the parking pawl into the toothed park wheel on the gearbox output and pulls it out again; there is no mechanical link to the selector. Software holds back engagement until the vehicle has stopped, since the pawl would otherwise ratchet over the teeth.",["Pawl position sensing or actuator inside the module faulty","Bus wiring or connector at the transmission corroded or loose","Weak 12 V battery during park lock actuation","Software or learned values missing after module replacement"],["Warning to secure the vehicle or apply the parking brake","Vehicle will not shift out of Park","Park not confirmed on the display"],4,2,["U01BA","U049F"],""],U04BE:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Charger Control Module B","U04BE is logged when a module receives data from battery charger control module B that it cannot accept. Charging hardware can come in more than one stage: the Audi e-tron, for example, was sold in Europe with 11 kW AC charging as standard and 22 kW as an option. Which unit counts as A or B is up to the maker.",["On-board charger B internally faulty (Polestar 3 analogy, grid disturbances)","Charger or charging-control software out of date","Bus wiring or plug at the charger damaged"],["AC charging slow, interrupted or impossible","DC fast charging usually still works","Charging fault message"],4,0,["U01BB","U049C","U057B","U057C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ B"],U04BF:["Invalid Data Received From Drive Motor A Clutch Actuator","Some electric and hybrid drivetrains can separate a drive motor from its wheels with a clutch so that an unused axle does not drag the motor along. A Rivian patent describes such a disconnect without a position sensor: the motor speed is brought within a small window of the output speed before engaging, and the control system judges success from how the motor responds to the load.",["Clutch actuator motor or its electronics faulty","Worn or sticking disconnect clutch giving a state that does not match the command","Bus wiring or connector at the drive unit damaged","Software of actuator and drive controller not matching"],["Drive system or all-wheel-drive warning","Reduced power or one motor not used","Clunk or jerk when the motor is coupled"],4,2,["U01BE","U0411"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מפעיל מצמד מנוע הנעה‏ A"],U04C0:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Management Control Module","The battery management control module behind U04C0 is not always the main controller of the high-voltage battery. Mazda uses the code on the CX-90 (2024–2026) and CX-70 (2025–2026) plug-in hybrids for their backup power unit: the PCM stores U04C0:00, which Mazda describes as an internal malfunction there, often together with P143B, U3008 or U3003 and a lit hybrid system warning.",["Weak backup sub battery (Mazda CX-90/CX-70 PHEV, AGM YTZ7S)","Battery management or backup power unit internally faulty","Bus wiring or connector fault to the module"],["Hybrid system warning light on","Further codes for the backup power supply stored"],2,0,["U01BF","U04B1","U0412"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ניהול סוללה"],U0500:["Invalid Data Received From Communication Module","The public code lists checked do not carry U0500 at all, so neither its status as a generic code nor its wording can be confirmed. In the generic numbering, an invalid-data code usually mirrors the lost-communication code of the same module 0x301 lower (U0200 to U0501, U0199 to U049A); for U0500 that partner would be U01FF, which is not assigned in those lists either, so a reserved slot is likely.",["Code read with a manufacturer-specific definition that differs from the generic list","Scan tool decoding the stored fault number incorrectly","Telematics or communication unit sending corrupted frames (analogy to U0499)"],["Code present without any noticeable fault","Remote app, emergency call or online services unavailable (if it concerns the telematics unit)"],3,0,["U0499","U0198","U0400"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תקשורת"],U0501:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module B","Many cars give each door its own electronics: a door unit receives commands over CAN and drives window lift, lock and mirror, as a Yazaki patent describes with a LIN sub-bus inside the door. Module A has its invalid-data code in U049A; U0501 is the same check for the second door unit.",["Water ingress into the door module through a failed door membrane","Broken wires in the harness grommet between body and door","Door module not programmed or configured after replacement"],["One door not following central locking","Window, mirror or door-ajar display of that door erratic"],2,0,["U0200","U049A","U0502"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ B"],U0502:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module C","For door control module C the letter is a weak guide. In the generic list its lost-communication partner is U0201, yet GM's 2011 Saab 9-5 code list uses U0201 for the transfer case control module. So on some makes the slot is not a door at all, and the vehicle's own fault text decides.",["Door control module C internally faulty","Damaged wiring in the door hinge area","Manufacturer uses this code slot for another module"],["Lock, window or mirror of one door working only sometimes","Stored code without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0201","U0501","U0503"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ C"],U0503:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module D","U0503 is the invalid-data code for door control module D. It is rarely seen in published service material: Ford, the most visible user of lettered door modules, labels the latch controllers of its four-door electronic-latch cars E to H (DCME–DCMH, e.g. Mustang Mach-E), leaving D unused there. In a four-door car with one unit per door, D would typically be the last of the four, but that is not fixed.",["Door control module D internally faulty or water-damaged","Broken data lead in the door harness grommet","Weak 12 V battery causing faulty frames during wake-up"],["One door not unlocking or locking with the others","Window switch on that door ignored"],2,0,["U0202","U0502","U0504"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ D"],U0504:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module E","U0504 is the one door code of this series with a public manufacturer case. Ford names the electronic door latch controllers DCME to DCMH, and its programming applications list DCME as door control module E. In 2024–2026 Lincoln Nautilus and 2025–2027 Aviator, latch software stored B1262:92 in several of these modules, and U0504 could appear in the gearshift module, which evidently uses door status.",["Door latch module software (Lincoln Aviator/Nautilus, update DCME–DCMH)","Door control module E internally faulty","Damaged wiring between body and door"],["Door fault warning in the cluster","Transmission Not In Park or Hill Start Assist Not Available messages (Lincoln)","Door latch or electronic door release erratic"],2,0,["U0203","U0503","U0505"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ E"],U0505:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module F","At Ford, F is the second of the electronic latch modules (DCMF). Its typical troubles are documented, though not with U0505 itself: 2020–2023 Aviators logged latch circuit codes in DCME–DCMH when low battery voltage met fault thresholds set too low (SSM 50556), and Mach-E cars raised false alarms through latch module software (SSM 51292). Both show that supply voltage and software are where such modules fail.",["Low 12 V battery voltage disturbing the latch module (Ford/Lincoln)","Outdated latch module software","Door control module F internally faulty"],["Door ajar or door fault warning","False alarm after locking"],2,0,["U0204","U0504","U0506"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ F"],U0506:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module G","G is the seventh door slot and in practice belongs to cars that number their door electronics from E upwards. Ford does so with DCMG, the third of four latch modules in Mach-E, Aviator and Nautilus; Ford service messages name DCMG together with its siblings whenever latch software is updated. GM's Saab 9-5 code list contains no partner entry U0205, so the slot appears unused there.",["Latch module software needing update (Ford DCMG)","Weak 12 V supply during locking or wake-up","Door control module G internally faulty"],["Door not opening with the electronic handle","Door fault message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0205","U0505","U050C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ G"],U0507:["Invalid Data Received From Folding Top Control Module","The folding top control module runs the power soft top or retractable hardtop of a convertible: it moves the top through hydraulics or motors, watches latch and position sensors and blocks the sequence when something is in the way. Other units need its status, for example to drop the windows, warn while driving or release the trunk lid. U0507 is logged when that status arrives in an unusable form.",["Top control module software error (BMW F33/F83 example)","Damaged wiring to top position or latch sensors in the folding area","Water reaching the module from a leaking top drain"],["Top refuses to open or close or stops midway","Top not secure warning while driving"],3,0,["U0206","U0508"],""],U0508:["Invalid Data Received From Moveable Roof Control Module A","The moveable roof control module drives an electric sunroof or panoramic glass panel, typically through a cable-driven motor with stored end positions and pinch protection. GM uses the same module name: its Saab 9-5 code list files the loss of contact with this module as U0207, the partner of this code. U0508 is stored when the roof module's position and status frames arrive but fail validation.",["Roof module software or lost initialisation of end positions","Water damage from blocked roof drains","Damaged wiring or connector in the headliner"],["Sunroof stuck, moving jerkily or one-touch function lost","Roof not closing with the remote key"],2,0,["U0207","U050B","U046A"],""],U0509:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module A","Seat control module A is usually the electronics of the first powered seat, often the driver's memory seat. The Saab 9-5 code list published by GM spells this out: there, the lost-communication partner U0208 is the memory seat control module. Its frames carry seat positions for memory recall, heating or ventilation states and switch inputs;",["Seat module configuration or software not matching the vehicle","Under-seat harness or connector damaged by seat travel or objects","Seat control module A internally faulty"],["Seat memory positions not recalled","Seat heating or ventilation unavailable"],2,0,["U0208","U050A","U0511"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ A"],U050A:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module B","For seat control module B there is a fairly clear manufacturer assignment. Ford calls the front passenger seat unit SCMB, for example in the 2024–2026 Lincoln Nautilus, where it held B120A:2A with an inoperative heated seat (SSM 54647), while the driver side is the DSM.",["Seat module configuration lost or wrong after programming (Ford SCMB)","Harness under the passenger seat pinched or connector loose","Seat control module B internally faulty"],["Passenger seat heating or adjustment not working","Seat settings missing in the center display"],2,0,["U0209","U0509","U0512"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ B"],U050B:["Invalid Data Received From Moveable Roof Control Module B","A second moveable roof module only makes sense where the roof has more than one powered element, for instance a sliding front glass panel plus a separately driven rear panel or sunshade, or a large panoramic roof split into sections. U050B records that data from this second unit reached the network but was unusable.",["Second roof drive lost its end-position learning","Moveable roof control module B faulty, often after water entry","Connector or lead to the rear roof drive damaged"],["Rear roof panel or shade not moving while the front one works","Panel stopping part-way"],2,0,["U020A","U0508"],""],U050C:["Invalid Data Received From Door Control Module H","Door control module H, the last door slot, is used by Ford in two different ways. In the Mach-E, Aviator and Nautilus it is the fourth electronic latch module, DCMH, updated together with DCME–DCMG.",["Power sliding door latch or adjustment fault feeding wrong states (Ford Transit)","Latch module software (Ford DCMH)","Worn wiring in the sliding door track or hinge"],["Power sliding door moving only partly or not at all","Door ajar or door fault message"],2,0,["U020B","U0506","U049A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת דלת‏ H"],U050D:["Invalid Data Received From Wireless Accessory Charging Module A","The wireless accessory charging module is the inductive pad for phones, almost always following the Qi standard, which Toyota was first to offer from the factory, on the 2013 Avalon. The module reports charging state, phone detection and faults to the infotainment or body controller, which shows the charging icon. Ford calls it WACM;",["Charging module software outdated or mismatched","Module overheating, e.g. blocked fan or foreign object on the pad","Wireless charging module A internally faulty"],["Phone not charging on the pad or charging icon missing","Repeated phone position warnings"],1,0,["U020C","U050E"],""],U050E:["Invalid Data Received From Wireless Accessory Charging Module B","U050E belongs to a second inductive charging pad, found in cars that offer one pad up front and another for the rear seats or a second front position. Each pad runs its own transmitter coil, object detection and temperature monitoring, so a fault in B leaves pad A working.",["Metal object or card on the second pad triggering protection","Software of charging module B not matching the vehicle","Wireless charging module B internally faulty"],["Second charging pad inactive while the first works","No charging indication for the rear or second pad"],1,0,["U020D","U050D"],""],U0511:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module C","Seat control module C usually serves a seat beyond the two front ones. GM's Saab 9-5 code list assigns the partner slot U0210 to the rear seat heating control module, and Ford labels its rear seat electronics with later letters altogether (SCMK and SCML for the second-row power seats of the 2025 Navigator, SCMJ for the third-row fold module), so module C is anything but uniform.",["Harness pinched by rear seat folding or rail mechanism","Configuration of the rear seat module missing after replacement","Seat control module C internally faulty"],["Rear seat heating not switching on","Power folding or adjustment of a rear seat inoperative"],2,0,["U0210","U0512","U050A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ C"],U0512:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module D","U0512 has a documented GM case that goes beyond comfort functions. On the 2020 Cadillac CT5 with option UGN, the image processing module, which handles camera data for driver assistance, could set U0512 and display Service Driver Assist.",["Software in the receiving module (Cadillac CT5 image processing module)","Seat module D configuration or software mismatch","Damaged harness or connector under the seat"],["Service Driver Assist message (Cadillac CT5)","Driver assistance features temporarily unavailable","Seat functions served by module D not responding"],2,0,["U0211","U0511","U050A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ D"],U0513:["Invalid Data Received From Yaw Rate Sensor Module","A yaw rate sensor reports how quickly the body rotates about its vertical axis, and stability control weighs that rotation against steering angle, wheel speeds and sideways acceleration. U0513 means frames from a separate yaw rate sensor module do arrive, but the receiver rejects them: value out of range, invalid-status bit, wrong counter or checksum. No manufacturer publishes setting criteria for this code.",["Sensor element drifting or giving an offset the receiver flags as implausible","Loose mounting or corroded connector at the sensor module","Sensor module or brake controller software/configuration not matching after replacement","Disturbed CAN signals (wiring, terminating resistor, interference)"],["ESC/stability control and traction control warning lamps on","Stability control interventions unavailable","Driver assistance relying on vehicle motion data switched off"],2,2,["U0123","U0536","U0125","U0416"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן קצב סבסוב"],U0514:["Invalid Data Received From Mirror Control Module A","J2012 provides two mirror control units, and U0514 concerns unit A: its frames keep arriving, but the receiver finds the content unusable, for instance a signal flagged invalid, a wrong counter or checksum, or a value outside the defined range. FCA ties the letter to the cabin mirror.",["Software error in the mirror module sending invalid signal values","Vehicle configuration in the BCM not matching the fitted mirror variant","Mirror control module A internally faulty","Loose or corroded connector at the mirror (headliner or door)"],["Often no noticeable effect; code found only during a scan","Auto-dimming or camera mirror view unavailable","Mirror memory or folding function not working"],2,0,["U0213","U044F","U014D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מראה‏ A"],U0515:["Invalid Data Received From Remote Function Actuation Module","The remote function actuation module picks up the radio signals of key fobs and, on newer vehicles, of a phone used as a key, and hands lock, unlock, liftgate or remote start requests to the body controller. U0515 means its messages reach the network but fail the receiver's checks.",["Module software hanging or outdated, e.g. after an over-the-air update","Chafed or pinched data wire to the receiver module in the roof area","Supply interruption or internal fault of the receiver module"],["Key fob or phone-as-a-key not working or only intermittently","Passive entry or remote start unavailable","Network codes stored in several body modules at the same time"],2,0,["U0214"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול הפעלת פונקציה מרוחקת"],U0516:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch A","Here a door switch is a networked switch pack in a door trim panel that reports window, lock or mirror requests as data instead of through separate wires. U0516 is stored when frames from switch unit A arrive but fail the receiver's validity checks. No manufacturer publishes which door letter A stands for or documents this code;",["Electronics of switch unit A faulty (moisture, cracked solder joints)","Damaged data or ground wire in the door harness","Replacement switch of the wrong variant or software level"],["Buttons on one door switch pack without function","Window or lock on that door only operable from other switches"],2,0,["U0215","U0517","U0518"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ A"],U0517:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch B","Door switch B is the only letter of this series with a published manufacturer assignment. FCA bulletin 08-013-15 for the 2014 Jeep Cherokee (KL) gives the partner code U0216 as lost communication with the driver door switch; it showed up after the battery had been disconnected, together with a Start/Stop Not Available message, and was cured with new BCM software and a restored proxi configuration.",["BCM software or vehicle configuration out of step after battery disconnection (FCA KL)","Driver door switch pack faulty, e.g. after liquid ingress","Chafed data or ground wire between body and driver door"],["Driver's master window switches or window lockout not working","Lock or mirror adjustment from the driver's door unavailable","Start/Stop Not Available message (FCA, with partner code)"],2,0,["U0216","U0516","U0518"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ B"],U0518:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch C","U0518 is set when a receiving controller gets data from door switch unit C that it cannot trust. Which door that is remains unpublished, and no manufacturer documents the code. Door switch packs are usually LIN slaves, and LIN protects every frame with a parity-checked identifier and a checksum; NXP's keypad design even reports bit, checksum, parity and no-response errors back in its status bytes.",["Partly broken data or ground wire in the door hinge area","Supply dips while motors start (weak battery, poor ground)","Switch unit C internally faulty"],["Controls on one door respond only sometimes","Fault appears when the door is opened or closed"],2,0,["U0217","U0517","U0519"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ C"],U0519:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch D","Door switch unit D reports the positions of its buttons as coded data. Inside such packs several contacts often share one input through resistor networks or comparators, as Microchip explains for the switch interface of its LIN chips ATA6641/ATA6642, and the stages of a window rocker are distinguished by voltage level.",["Worn, sticky or wet contacts producing impossible switch combinations","Electronics of switch unit D faulty","Poor ground or damaged data wire to the switch"],["Window moves the wrong way or not at all from this switch","Express function triggered or missing unexpectedly"],1,0,["U0218","U0518","U051A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ D"],U051A:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch E","U051A concerns door switch unit E. On a car with four side doors, A to D would already be enough for one unit per door, so E suggests an additional switch location; no manufacturer documents this code or says what E means.",["Switch unit E internally faulty or water-damaged","Fault on the LIN sub-bus wiring between door controller and switch","Switch variant not matching the vehicle configuration"],["Switch at an additional door position without function","Window at that position operable only from the driver's door"],2,0,["U0219","U0519","U0521"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ E"],U0521:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch F","Door switch unit F lies beyond the usual four side doors. Vans and large SUVs may carry further switch panels, for example at sliding doors or for a third seat row, but no manufacturer states which position F denotes or documents this code.",["Switch unit F internally faulty","Worn wiring or contacts at a sliding or rear door transition","Switch or controller software not matching after replacement"],["Switch panel at a sliding door or rear row not working","Windows or locks served by that panel do not respond to it"],2,0,["U0220","U051A","U0522"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ F"],U0522:["Invalid Data Received From Door Switch G","J2012 provides seven door switch units, and G is the last of them. Few vehicles need that many networked switch packs, and no manufacturer publishes what G stands for or documents U0522. Where such a unit exists it works like its siblings: it supplies its button states when asked, and the receiver ignores them once a frame is malformed, out of range or carries an invalid counter.",["Switch variant or body controller configuration not matching","Switch unit G internally faulty","Data or supply wire to switch unit G damaged"],["One additional switch panel ignored by the vehicle","Code appears after a switch or module replacement"],2,0,["U0221","U0521","U0516"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מתג דלת‏ G"],U0523:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor A","A door window motor in the J2012 sense is a lift motor with its own electronics that talks to the network, usually as a LIN slave of a door or body controller. Such a unit reports where the glass is, based on its Hall pulses, whether it stopped for an obstacle or a stall and whether its sensor or supply has failed, as NXP's MM908E624 reference design (AN3147) shows.",["Electronics or Hall sensor in window motor A faulty","Window position not learned after battery disconnection or repair","Damaged LIN, supply or ground wire to the motor"],["Window moves only while the switch is held","Express up/down or comfort closing unavailable","Window stops part way"],2,0,["U0222","U0524","U053A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ A"],U0524:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor B","U0524 means the master accepts frames from window motor B but not what they say. A common reason is a position value the controller cannot reconcile. Smart lift motors count Hall pulses between a learned lower and upper end, and Atmel's anti-pinch application note AVR480 describes acquiring such parameters during initialisation and spotting a defective Hall sensor from a run of apparent direction changes.",["End positions lost after battery disconnection, motor or regulator work","Hall sensor in motor B faulty, giving erratic position counts","Regulator cable or glass clamp slipped, so travel no longer matches"],["One-touch operation lost on that window","Window stops short of the top or reverses near the seal"],2,0,["U0223","U0523","U0525"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ B"],U0525:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor C","Data from window motor C include what the door controller needs for automatic closing, which in the United States falls under FMVSS 118. A window able to close without the switch being held must stop and reverse before it presses on a test rod of 4 to 200 mm with 100 N or more, and then open again by at least 125 mm or far enough for a 200 mm rod.",["Motor C electronics sending corrupted status","Voltage drop at the motor during start-up (weak battery, poor ground)","Chafed LIN wire in the door harness"],["Automatic closing on locking does not close this window","Window only operable with the switch held"],2,0,["U0224","U0524","U0526"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ C"],U0526:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor D","Not every lift motor carries Hall sensors. Patent US11611297 describes a cheaper approach in which the controller derives speed, current and how quickly current changes from the ripple that commutation leaves in the motor current, and recognises a pinch from those values.",["Position counting from current ripple disturbed (brush wear, supply noise)","Window motor D or its electronics faulty","Poor ground or connector at the door"],["Window halts part way or misjudges its end position","Express and comfort closing unavailable"],2,0,["U0225","U0525","U0527"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ D"],U0527:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor E","U0527 is logged when a receiver rejects the content sent by window motor E. Mechanics can play a part. Subaru's bulletin 07-189-21 for the 2020 Legacy and Outback deals with front regulators whose glass tilted in the sash frame and bound, so the anti-entrapment function reacted erratically and the glass closed slowly or not at all; revised regulator and motor assemblies fixed it.",["Glass binding in the run channel or sash, distorting motor load","Window motor E electronics faulty","Worn or damaged regulator mechanism"],["Window reverses without an obstacle while closing","Glass closes slowly or stops before the seal"],2,0,["U0226","U0526","U0528"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ E"],U0528:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor F","Window motor F is one of the slots beyond the four usual side doors; it could serve, for instance, powered rear quarter glass or a sliding door window, but no manufacturer documents which window F stands for or publishes U0528.",["Replacement motor with a different variant or node configuration","Window motor F internally faulty","Damaged wiring at a sliding door or rear body transition"],["An additional power window moves only partly or not at all","Code appears after a motor has been replaced"],2,0,["U0227","U0527","U0529"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ F"],U0529:["Invalid Data Received From Door Window Motor G","With G, J2012 reaches the seventh and last window motor slot, more than most vehicles will ever use. No manufacturer publishes U0529 or names a window for G. Should the code appear, it follows the logic of its siblings: motor G is heard on the network, yet its frames are rejected because of a checksum or counter error, a signal marked invalid or a value outside the agreed range.",["Weak supply or ground causing faults under starting current","Window motor G or its electronics faulty","Motor electronics overheated after repeated operation"],["Window stops responding after several operations","Automatic functions of that window disabled"],2,0,["U0228","U0528","U0523"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מנוע חלון דלת‏ G"],U052A:["Invalid Data Received From Heated Steering Wheel Module","The heated steering wheel module powers the heating mat in the rim and reports its state, such as heater on or off, the requested level and the rim temperature read by an embedded thermistor, to the body or climate network. A receiver that gets these frames but finds the content implausible (temperature out of range, bad checksum or counter, wrong length) logs U052A;",["Rim temperature sensor drifting or open, giving implausible values","Worn clock spring or steering wheel wiring to the heater circuit","Heated steering wheel module internally faulty","Module software or configuration not matching after programming"],["Heated steering wheel stays cold or switches off early","Heater indicator or menu shows no or wrong status"],2,0,["U0229"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול גלגל הגה מחומם"],U052F:["Invalid Data Received From Object Detection Maintenance Control Module A","Object detection maintenance control modules appear in the generic code list, but no manufacturer has published what they do or when this fault sets. The name points to a unit that keeps cameras, radar or lidar used for object detection usable, for example by running washers, air jets or heaters.",["Software or configuration mismatch of maintenance module A","Internal fault of the maintenance module (e.g. moisture ingress)","Wiring or connector fault on the module's data line"],["Sensor blocked or sensor cleaning message","Driver assistance features temporarily unavailable","Sensor washing or heating not working"],4,0,["U022E","U0530","U022F"],""],U0530:["Invalid Data Received From Object Detection Maintenance Control Module B","Module B of this family is a second maintenance controller for object detection sensors, for instance one serving another sensor group or the other side of the vehicle. The generic definition offers no public explanation, and no manufacturer document names U0530.",["Software level of module B not matching the receiving controller","Module B internal fault, e.g. after water or road salt exposure","Intermittent contact in the data line or connector to module B"],["Message that a sensor or assistance function is unavailable","Automatic sensor cleaning on one side or sensor group not working"],4,0,["U022F","U052F","U022E"],""],U0531:["Invalid Data Received From Rear Gate Module","The rear gate module runs a powered liftgate or tailgate: motor drive, latch, pinch sensing and the requests from switches or key fob. U0531 is stored when its messages reach other controllers with content they refuse. No manufacturer documents U0531 itself, but its lost-communication partner U0230 appears in several bulletins. GM's Saab 9-5 code list calls the unit liftgate control module;",["Water ingress or corrosion in connectors at the liftgate","Liftgate module software fault (update available on some models)","Broken wires in the harness passing through the liftgate hinge area","Hinge or drive damage after repeated obstruction while closing"],["Power liftgate does not open or close electrically","Liftgate reverses at the fully closed position","Interior lamps or other body functions fail at the same time (shared LAN)"],2,0,["U0230","U053A","U0541"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול שער אחורי"],U0532:["Invalid Data Received From Rain Sensing Module","The rain sensing module behind the windshield measures how much infrared light wet glass scatters and, in most designs, also reads ambient light for automatic headlamps. Melexis describes such a unit as an optical front end, a microcontroller and a LIN system basis chip linking it to the body controller.",["Rain and light sensor electronics faulty","Sensor badly coupled to the glass or wrong variant after windshield replacement","Corroded connector or chafed LIN wire at the windshield headliner","Body controller software evaluating the sensor frames incorrectly"],["Automatic wipers do not react to rain or wipe on a dry screen","Automatic headlamps switch late, early or not at all"],2,0,["U0231","U0481"],""],U0533:["Invalid Data Received From Side Obstacle Detection Control Module A","Side obstacle detection modules are the corner radars behind the rear bumper that watch blind spots and crossing traffic. GM and Ford give letter A to the left unit: the 2011 Saab 9-5 code list names U0232 for the left side-object module, and Ford bulletin 24-2180 (Expedition/Navigator 2022-2024) logs U0232 in Ford's IPMA camera module together with faults of the left radar.",["Mud, ice or damage at the left rear radar, bracket or bumper cover","Water or corrosion in the radar connector or harness","Radar module software or configuration fault"],["Blind spot monitoring unavailable message","Left mirror warning indicator inoperative","Rear cross traffic alert switched off"],2,0,["U0232","U0534","U0233"],""],U0534:["Invalid Data Received From Side Obstacle Detection Control Module B","Module B is the right-hand rear corner radar in GM and Ford numbering: Saab's 2011 list calls U0233 the right side-object module, and Ford's Expedition/Navigator bulletin 24-2180 pairs U0233 with the right sensor. Toyota uses U0233 for the master sensor of the Tacoma blind spot system, where bulletin T-SB-0063-19 had both sensors replaced and re-aimed with a reflector tool.",["Moisture or corrosion at the right radar connector","Right radar damaged or misaligned after a bumper impact","Internal fault or outdated software in the right radar module"],["Right mirror blind spot indicator not working","Cross traffic alert unavailable","Service message for the blind spot system"],2,0,["U0233","U0533","U0232"],""],U0535:["Invalid Data Received From Convenience Recall Module","A convenience recall module keeps driver profiles and moves seat, mirrors, adjustable pedals or steering column back to stored positions, typically on a memory button or when the key fob linked to a profile unlocks the car. Ford's patent filing lists profiles covering seat, mirror, pedal and steering adjustment, and a Lear/Ford patent places a memory seat module with position sensors on the seat frame;",["Seat, mirror or pedal position sensor reporting implausible values","Memory module internally faulty or stored profiles corrupted","Pinched or corroded wiring under the seat or in the door","Module not configured or positions not relearned after replacement"],["Memory buttons or key-linked profiles do not restore positions","Seat or mirrors move to wrong positions or stop part-way"],2,0,["U0234","U0509"],""],U0536:["Invalid Data Received From Lateral Acceleration Sensor Module","Lateral acceleration tells the stability system how hard the car is being pushed sideways in a bend; set against yaw rate and steering input it reveals whether the vehicle still follows the driver.",["Acceleration sensor element faulty or out of calibration","Module mounted loosely or in the wrong orientation after repair work","Corrosion or moisture at the module connector (often under seats or console)","Software or coding mismatch between sensor module and receiver"],["ESC and traction control lamps lit","No stability or traction intervention when cornering","Hill hold or adaptive cruise may be unavailable"],2,2,["U0124","U0513","U0125","U0416"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן תאוצה צידית"],U0537:["Invalid Data Received From Column Lock Module","The column lock module drives the electric bolt that blocks the steering shaft when the car is parked and frees it before the engine may start. U0537 records that a partner module, such as the body controller or keyless start unit, received lock status messages it cannot trust. No manufacturer explains this exact code publicly.",["Column lock module software or calibration fault (reprogramming)","Weak 12 V battery or voltage drops during start","Lock module not paired/learned to the body or immobilizer module after replacement","Mechanical or internal fault of the lock actuator"],["Engine does not start or start is refused","Steering wheel remains locked","Steering column lock service message"],2,0,["U0236","U0422","U0140"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול נעילת עמוד"],U0538:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Audio Control Module C","Digital audio control modules are the networked parts of a sound system such as amplifiers, signal processors or media interfaces; the letters A to D merely count them. Ford groups U0237 and U0238, the lost-communication codes for modules C and D, with DSP trouble: 2020–2021 Escape, 2021 F-150, Mach-E, Expedition, Explorer and 2020–2022 Edge could lose all sound while chimes moved to the cluster, cured by a…",["Audio module software fault, as in Ford's DSP cases","Module C internally faulty","Poor fuse contact or low supply voltage at the module"],["No sound or missing speaker channels","Warning chimes only from the instrument cluster"],2,0,["U0539","U0494","U0495","U0487"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ C"],U0539:["Invalid Data Received From Digital Audio Control Module D","Ford assigns the D slot fairly clearly: on 2024–2026 Nautilus, 2025–2026 Aviator with the 28-speaker system and 2025–2026 Navigator, the audio control module stores U0238 when it cannot reach the digital signal processor (SSM 54751, 54752). The first check there is pulling the DSP fuse for one minute;",["Digital signal processor module faulty","Poor blade contact at the DSP fuse or supply interruption","DSP or audio control module software fault"],["No audio from the speakers although the radio display works","Sound drops out intermittently or some channels are missing"],2,0,["U0238","U0538","U0495"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת שמע דיגיטלי‏ D"],U053A:["Invalid Data Received From Entrapment Control Module A","Entrapment control modules handle pinch protection for powered closures where it is not built into the drive, typically sliding doors, liftgates or roofs with sensing edges. For windows, roof panels and partitions FMVSS 118 sets the goal: stop and reverse before 100 N act on the test rod.",["Entrapment control module A internally faulty or with wrong software","Damaged pinch sensor edge feeding implausible values into the module","Bus wiring to the module damaged, e.g. in a liftgate or door hinge"],["Power closure will not close automatically","Closure reverses without an obstacle"],3,0,["U0239","U0541","U0531"],""],U053B:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Module A","Image processing modules evaluate camera data for assistance functions, and module A is the one most often named in service literature. GM's 2025 brake controller tables (25OBDG04A) check protection values and rolling counters in messages from the object fusion controller (EOCM); 3 errors in a window of 16 frames set U053B as Type C without MIL, and the test pauses outside 9 to 16 V.",["Software in image processing module A (update available, e.g. Ford Maverick)","Steering angle not relearned after battery disconnect or transport mode (Jeep Compass)","Front camera not calibrated after windshield or module replacement","Supply voltage outside the valid window during start-up"],["Lane keeping or adaptive cruise unavailable message","Remote park assist or automatic hitch function refused","Code stored without noticeable symptoms"],2,0,["U023A","U053C","U053D","U0566"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ A"],U053C:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Module B","U053C is documented by GM on cars with Super Cruise. On the 2023 Cadillac Lyriq it could set at start-up and remain current for as long as half an hour, keeping Super Cruise unavailable; an ignition cycle cleared it in some cases only (PIC6500). Revision PIC6500A widened the list of codes stored by that module and told technicians not to replace the controller, and PIC6500B closed the case in 2024.",["Software behaviour at start-up between the image processing modules (GM Super Cruise)","Stored history code unrelated to the actual fault (GM PIC6607)","Fault in module B or its network connection"],["Super Cruise Unavailable message","Adaptive cruise or Service Driver Assist message","Surround view camera display faulty (other makes)"],2,0,["U023B","U053B","U053D","U0567"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ B"],U053D:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Module C","No manufacturer text cites U053D. GM does show which unit occupies slot C: bulletin 21-NA-209 for the 2021 Escalade identifies U023C as the code for a silent K157 video processing module, where a software fault left the radio screen black with a crossed-out camera symbol until a fuse reset and reprogramming. The Lyriq bulletin PIC6500A also lists U023C among codes held by its camera processing unit.",["Software anomaly in the video/image processing module C","Module locked up, cleared by power reset (fuse) and reprogramming","Damaged video or network cable to module C"],["Black or missing camera image on the central display","Camera-based assistance functions unavailable"],2,0,["U023C","U053B","U053C","U0568"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול עיבוד תמונה‏ C"],U0541:["Invalid Data Received From Entrapment Control Module B","Entrapment control module B is the second slot for a separate pinch-protection unit. Some designs detect a person before contact: a capacitive strip changes its electric field as a hand approaches, and the attached electronics pass the result to the closure controller either as a switched output or as LIN or SAE J2602 data, as a review of tailgate anti-pinch approaches explains;",["Capacitive sensor strip or its electronics delivering implausible values","Sensor connector not fully seated or corroded","Software or calibration of module B not matching after replacement"],["Power liftgate or sliding door stops or reverses without contact","Automatic closing refused with a warning"],3,0,["U0240","U053A","U0531"],""],U0542:["Invalid Data Received From Headlamp Control Module A","Headlamp control modules run adaptive lighting such as swivelling, levelling, matrix segments and LED daytime lights, frequently with one module per headlamp. U0542 means a receiver, for example the body or lighting master module, gets messages from module A that fail its checks. No manufacturer publishes text for U0542.",["Headlamp module A software (reprogramming released)","Headlamp or module replaced without coding/configuration","Moisture or corrosion at the headlamp connector"],["Check headlamp or lighting system warning","Adaptive or cornering light not working on one side","Daytime running light or position light affected"],2,0,["U0241","U0543","U0242"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת פנס ראשי‏ A"],U0543:["Invalid Data Received From Headlamp Control Module B","Headlamp control module B is the second light controller, usually serving the headlamp opposite module A. Bentley's 2019-2020 Continental GT campaign (2056293/1) handles the two as light control left and right, at diagnostic addresses 29 and 39, and both needed new software when the outer daytime running lights failed. Jaguar's 2020 XE likewise names HCMA and HCMB (SSM74402).",["Different or outdated software in headlamp module B compared with A","Headlamp B replaced without coding","Internal fault in headlamp module B"],["Lighting system warning in the cluster","Matrix or bending light on one side fixed to low beam","Daytime running light on one side out"],2,0,["U0242","U0542","U0241"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת פנס ראשי‏ B"],U0544:["Invalid Data Received From Parking Assist Control Module B","Parking assist control modules evaluate the ultrasonic sensors in the bumpers and work out distances or steering paths. Mercedes-Benz lists U0544 in its Intelligent Predictive Repair guide for its eight-gear DCT (models 118, 177, 247; document LI27.00-P-077141): the transmission controller stores U054487 when data from the PARKTRONIC unit are implausible, and failure type 87 points to a missing message.",["Internal or software fault in parking assist module B","Messages from module B missing or delayed (bus fault, module reset)","Damaged bumper harness or sensors causing module B to send invalid data"],["Parking sensors or park assist switched off with warning","Automatic parking manoeuvre not available","Transmission control unit stores the code (Mercedes DCT)"],2,0,["U0243","U045A","U0159"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת סיוע חניה‏ B"],U0545:["Invalid Data Received From Running Board Control Module A","Power running boards deploy when a door opens and retract when it closes or the vehicle moves; a running board control module (Ford: RBM) drives the motors and reports position and faults. U0545 means its data reach other modules but are rejected.",["Software fault in the running board or hosting seat module","Low battery voltage event corrupting module data","Implausible motor position feedback from dirt, ice or corrosion at the board"],["Running boards do not deploy or retract, fault message in the cluster","Running board setting changes from Auto to Off by itself"],2,0,["U0244","U0552"],""],U0546:["Invalid Data Received From Entertainment Control Module — Front","The front entertainment control module is the media unit for the front row, usually the head unit or a separate media controller that also supplies rear systems. Visteon's patent describes this layout: a main unit for the front seats and an entertainment module for rear passengers, each with its own microcontroller, trade commands and status as multiplex messages, with the front unit steering sources for the rear.",["Head unit or media controller software fault","Front entertainment unit internally faulty","Damaged media bus wiring or connector behind the dash"],["Rear entertainment loses its source or control from the front","Wrong or frozen media information on displays"],2,0,["U0245","U0497","U054A"],""],U0547:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module E","Seat control module E belongs to the higher letters used once a car has more seat electronics than a driver and a passenger unit. Ford uses the E slot for a climate seat controller on the 2016 Lincoln MKX, where weak seat cooling was fixed by updating the as-built configuration of the SCME (SSM 46279).",["Wrong as-built configuration or software in the seat module","Seat temperature sensor or thermoelectric element giving implausible values","Loose or corroded connector under the seat"],["Seat heating or ventilation switches off or stays at one level","Seat climate setting on the screen does not match the seat"],2,0,["U0246","U0548","U0509"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ E"],U0548:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module F","For seat control module F no manufacturer publishes an official assignment, and U0548 appears in no bulletin. Ford's naming shows how far seat letters reach: B for the front passenger, G and H for multi-contour units, J for third-row power folding and K/L for the second-row power seats of the 2025 Navigator (SSM 54226), so F is one more seat node, possibly in a rear row.",["Seat module F internally faulty","Harness pinched in seat rails or folding mechanism","Module not configured to the vehicle after replacement"],["Functions of one particular seat unavailable","Seat switch or screen control for that seat does not react"],2,0,["U0247","U0547","U054C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ F"],U0549:["Invalid Data Received From Remote Accessory Module","No manufacturer explains in public what the remote accessory module is; the term shows up only in code lists, together with its lost-communication partner U0248. Going by the name, it is a body-side unit controlling accessories away from the main controllers, and it is distinct from the accessory protocol interface module covered by U0554.",["Remote accessory module internally faulty","Retrofitted or upfitter equipment disturbing the module's data","Low battery voltage or power interruption while the module was active"],["An accessory function controlled by this module does not work","Code stored without noticeable effect"],2,0,["U0248","U0554"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול אביזרים מרוחק"],U054A:["Invalid Data Received From Entertainment Control Module — Rear B","Some vehicles carry two rear entertainment units, for instance one screen per front headrest or separate units for second and third rows, which J2012 numbers Rear A and Rear B. GM's Saab 9-5 code list shows such a split: U0196 for the rear audio control module and U0249, the lost-communication partner of U054A, for a rear radio audio control module.",["Rear entertainment unit B internally faulty","Strained wiring through seat, headrest or headliner to unit B","Software level of unit B not matching the front unit"],["Second rear screen shows no picture or wrong source","Headphones or remote of that screen do not respond"],2,0,["U0249","U0497","U0546"],""],U054B:["Invalid Data Received From Interior Lighting Control Module A","Interior lighting control module A runs cabin illumination such as dome, footwell and ambient light strips, in newer cars often RGB LED nodes on a LIN line below the body controller. Microchip's reference ambient lighting module shows the data involved: the master sends a command frame with zone, colour shares and intensity and asks for a status frame in return, each protected by a LIN checksum at 10.4 kbit/s.",["LED driver node or lighting module internally faulty","Chafed LIN line or loose connector in trim or headliner","Wrong vehicle configuration for the lighting variant"],["Interior or ambient lights stay off or flicker","Ambient colour or brightness differs from the setting"],2,0,["U024A","U05C0"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת תאורה פנימית‏ A"],U054C:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module G","Ford gives seat control module G a fixed meaning: SCMG is the driver's multi-contour seat module with massage and lumbar functions. Ford's TSB 19-2293 covers vehicles from the 2013 MKZ to the 2019 F-150 and Navigator with intermittent massage and lumbar operation, B1471 and U024B/U024C, caused by fretting terminals at the SCMG and SCMH connectors and fixed with new pigtails and a rerouted harness.",["Fretting corrosion at the multi-contour seat module connector","Seat module misconfigured after a software update","Multi-contour seat module internally faulty"],["Driver seat massage or lumbar adjustment works only intermittently","Seat contour settings cannot be operated from the touchscreen"],2,0,["U024B","U054D","U0548"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ G"],U054D:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module H","Seat control module H is Ford's multi-contour module for the passenger seat (SCMH), the counterpart of SCMG. On 2022 Explorer and Aviator an intermittent passenger massage function without any stored code was traced to the configuration of both modules; first no fix was available, later reprogramming plus the configuration apps solved it (SSM 50591, 51927).",["Passenger seat module configuration not matching the vehicle","Fretting corrosion at the passenger seat module connector","Passenger multi-contour seat module internally faulty"],["Passenger seat massage starts and stops on its own","Passenger lumbar or contour adjustment does not respond"],2,0,["U024C","U054C","U054E"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ H"],U054E:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Module J","Ford calls the module that folds the third-row seats electrically both PFSM and seat control module J (SCMJ). On 2025–2026 Expedition and Navigator its software left the seats unwilling to fold when 3L, Both or 3R was pressed, restored by a relearn in which Both is held for one minute and then five seconds more (SSM 53681), and caused misaligned upright seats after an obstruction reset (SSM 54613).",["Power fold seat module software fault","Seat end positions lost after an obstruction event or power loss","Harness to the third-row seats damaged in the cargo area"],["Third-row seats do not fold or unfold electrically","Seats stop part-way or end up misaligned"],1,0,["U024D","U054D","U0511"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מושב‏ J"],U054F:["Invalid Data Received From Side Obstacle Detection Control Module C","Some vehicles carry more than two side obstacle radars, adding units for wider coverage of lane changes and crossing traffic. Ford names them side obstacle detection control modules C and D (SODCMC, SODCMD) next to the left and right units SODL and SODR.",["Module C not configured or VIN not written after replacement","Software level of module C outdated or incompatible","Harness or connector fault at module C"],["Side assistance or blind spot warning message","Lane change or cross traffic warnings partly unavailable"],2,0,["U024E","U0550","U024F"],""],U0550:["Invalid Data Received From Side Obstacle Detection Control Module D","Module D is the fourth radar of a side obstacle system, in Ford terms SODCMD alongside SODL, SODR and SODCMC. Which corner it serves depends on the vehicle and is not stated in the public Ford bulletins. U0550 has no published manufacturer description; a module receiving data from unit D sets it when that data proves invalid, for example a signal outside its range or a sequence error.",["Radar D or its bracket damaged by a bumper impact","Water ingress or corrosion at the module D connector","Replacement module D without vehicle configuration"],["Side assistance or cross traffic alert switched off","Warning message about a blocked or faulty sensor"],2,0,["U024F","U054F","U024E"],""],U0551:["Invalid Data Received From Impact Classification System Module","An impact classification system module helps the restraint system judge what kind of collision is under way, for example frontal, side or angled, and how severe it is, so that the right airbags and pretensioners fire at the right stage. U0551 means another module, typically the airbag or restraint controller, receives messages from this unit whose content fails its plausibility or integrity checks.",["Internal fault in the impact classification module","Module or restraint controller not configured/programmed after replacement or crash repair","Damaged wiring or connector after collision or interior work"],["Airbag/SRS warning lamp on","Restraint system message in the instrument cluster","Passenger airbag status indicator behaving abnormally"],4,0,["U0250","U0452","U0151"],""],U0552:["Invalid Data Received From Running Board Control Module B","A second running board controller only makes sense where each side of the vehicle has its own electronics. A 2004 Ford patent for powered boards has one central module drive the left and right boards separately, so a design with one node per side is plausible, but no manufacturer publishes which side B would be.",["Battery undervoltage or discharged battery disturbing the running board electronics","Running board module software fault (Ford fixes comparable faults by reprogramming)","Corroded connector or chafed wiring at the board motor under the body","Running board control module B internally faulty"],["Running board on one side no longer deploys or retracts","Running board setting changes from Auto to Off without driver input"],2,0,["U0251","U0545"],""],U0553:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Control Module — Rear B","Rear lighting control module B is a second controller for the rear lamps. U0553 is set when its messages are received but their content is implausible. No manufacturer documents U0553 publicly, yet the partner code U0252 hints at what the module often is: GM's list for the Saab 9-5 calls U0252 the trailer interface control module, and Ford links U0252 and U0137 on 2021–2024 F-150, Expedition, Navigator and the 2024…",["Trailer or rear lighting module software hung or outdated (Ford remedy is reprogramming)","Loose or badly tightened ground connection","Corrosion or short at the trailer socket feeding back into the module","Rear lighting control module B internally faulty"],["Trailer lamps or trailer brake function reported as faulty","Individual rear lamps not working","Several warning messages after battery or ground work"],2,0,["U0252","U0484","U0137"],""],U0554:["Invalid Data Received From Accessory Protocol Interface Module","Accessory protocol interface module is Ford's name for the SYNC computer (APIM), which, at least in the first SYNC generation, sits apart from the audio control module and talks to the high- and medium-speed CAN buses.",["Outdated or faulty SYNC/APIM software (often fixed by an over-the-air or dealer update)","APIM configuration not matching the vehicle equipment after replacement or update","Receiving module (e.g. ABS) evaluating APIM data with outdated software"],["Drive mode or vehicle settings chosen on the touchscreen are not applied or fall back","Wrong or incomplete information on the center display","Code stored in another module without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0253","U031F"],""],U0555:["Invalid Data Received From Remote Start Module","A remote start module lets the engine run from a key fob or app for heating or cooling and must work around the immobilizer while doing so; it may be a factory part, a dealer accessory or an aftermarket box tied into the CAN network. GM lists the remote start module as its own node (Saab 9-5 2011: U0254).",["Aftermarket remote starter or other add-on device on the CAN bus sending non-conforming messages","Software of the remote start module not matching the vehicle gateway","Poor splices or connectors from the remote starter installation"],["Engine does not start or shuts down again when started remotely","Code found during an all-systems scan with no noticeable fault","Module programming at the workshop does not complete"],2,0,["U0254"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול התנעה מרוחקת"],U0556:["Invalid Data Received From Front Display Interface Module","The front display interface module is the screen unit in the center of the dash; GM calls the matching node info display module (Saab 9-5 2011, U0255), Ford uses FDIM. The display mostly shows what other modules feed it. Ford examples: on the Escape (2016–2019) and Focus/C-Max (2016–2018) the FDIM ramps its backlight up and down in auto-dim mode, which looks like flicker but is normal (SSM 47748);",["Display module software fault or level not matching the infotainment unit","Wrong configuration of display or infotainment module after replacement or update","Front display module internally faulty (touch sensor or electronics)"],["Touchscreen does not respond or reacts to inputs that were not made","Wrong or incomplete content shown on the center display"],2,0,["U0255","U0558","U0557"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול ממשק תצוגה קדמית"],U0557:["Invalid Data Received From Front Controls Interface Module A","Front controls interface module A is the button panel in the center stack that reads keys and knobs for audio and climate and passes them on as bus messages; Ford calls it FCIM, GM the infotainment faceplate control module (Saab 9-5 2011, U0256).",["Control panel electronics locking up under high bus load","Control panel software fault or mismatch with the infotainment unit","Stuck button or liquid spilled into the panel producing invalid key states","Front controls interface module A internally faulty"],["Radio or climate buttons work only intermittently or not at all","Several warning lamps or messages appear together with the button failure"],2,0,["U0256","U055E","U0558"],""],U0558:["Invalid Data Received From Front Controls/Display Interface Module","Simpler infotainment systems put buttons and a small screen into one unit, the front controls/display interface module. Ford calls it FCDIM, used for example with the 4-inch audio display, and the GM-built 2011 Saab 9-5 lists U0257 for its info display module/infotainment faceplate control module.",["Software fault in the combined controls/display unit (Ford remedy is reprogramming)","Unit programmed with a calibration for a different equipment level","Front controls/display interface module internally faulty"],["Radio presets cannot be stored or recalled, preset keys act erratically","Small audio display blank or showing wrong settings"],2,0,["U0257","U0556","U0557"],""],U0559:["Invalid Data Received From Radio Transceiver","Despite the name, the radio transceiver is not the audio tuner but the module that exchanges radio signals with keys and wireless accessories. Ford's name is RTM: on 2021–2022 Bronco Sport, jammed passive-key frequencies or a weak key battery could trigger No Key Detected, solved by placing the key in the console backup spot close to the RTM (SSM 50341);",["Radio interference or weak key battery producing implausible receiver data","Accessory keypad or remote on a frequency the transceiver does not support","Transceiver software or configuration fault","Radio transceiver module internally faulty"],["No Key Detected or similar key message in the cluster","Keyless entry or remote functions work poorly or not at all","Wireless keypad cannot be paired"],2,0,["U0258"],""],U055A:["Invalid Data Received From Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module A","Special purpose vehicle control modules are add-on controllers that body builders and upfitters fit to police cars, ambulances, utility trucks and similar conversions. U055A means frames from module A arrive but their content fails the receiver's checks.",["Upfitter module programmed or configured for a different vehicle software level","Vehicle modules updated without matching the upfitter module","Poorly made bus connection or splice in the body builder's wiring","Special purpose module A internally faulty"],["Upfitter equipment (lights, outputs, interlocks) works erratically or not at all","Code stored without warning lamp"],2,0,["U0259","U055B","U055C","U055D"],""],U055B:["Invalid Data Received From Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module B","U055B concerns the second slot reserved for special purpose controllers. A receiving module gets frames from controller B, but a signal lies outside its permitted span, a counter or checksum is wrong, or the frame length does not match. No manufacturer documents U055B publicly.",["Second add-on controller set up with wrong address or message set","Software of add-on controller B and vehicle modules not matched","Unstable supply or ground at controller B, e.g. on a shared accessory feed","Controller B internally faulty"],["One group of conversion functions fails while others still work","Fault entry in the receiving module, usually without warning lamp"],2,0,["U025A","U055A","U055C","U055D"],""],U055C:["Invalid Data Received From Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module C","With U055C a module rejects the content of messages sent by special purpose controller C, the third of four slots for conversion electronics. No maker publishes a code-specific description. Ford's body builder bulletin for the 2023 Super Duty points to a typical pitfall: the factory interface module, the infotainment unit and the body control module all need matching software before the upfitter tool can talk to…",["Software levels of conversion controller and vehicle modules out of step","Conversion equipment added or changed without updating controller C","Damaged bus wiring in the conversion harness"],["Functions controlled by the conversion do not respond as configured","Code appears after a software update or conversion work"],2,0,["U025B","U055A","U055B","U055D"],""],U055D:["Invalid Data Received From Special Purpose Vehicle Control Module D","U055D is the last of the four special purpose controller codes. It is stored when frames from controller D reach the network but carry values the receiver rejects. No manufacturer documents it; even Ford, which names slot A in its 2024 summary as a non-MIL check, says nothing about B to D.",["Incomplete or interrupted software update of controller D","Voltage dip from heavy conversion loads corrupting controller D's output","Controller D internally faulty"],["Individual conversion functions fail intermittently","Fault entry without effect on engine or brakes"],2,0,["U025C","U055A","U055B","U055C"],""],U055E:["Invalid Data Received From Front Controls Interface Module B","Where the front switches are split over two panels, the second one is front controls interface module B. Ford uses exactly this name (FCIMB): on 2023 Transit vans with SYNC 3 Lite, rear-only parking aid and no front sensors, the parking aid disable switch sits in the FCIMB;",["Receiving module configured for different equipment and misreading the panel B data","Software fault in the second control panel","Loose connector or damaged wiring behind the second panel"],["Switches on the second front panel have no effect","Indicator lamps in the switches do not match the actual function state"],2,0,["U025D","U0557"],""],U055F:["Invalid Data Received From Electronic Brake Booster Control Module A","An electronic brake booster replaces the vacuum servo: a travel sensor reads the pedal and an electric motor supplies the assist, as in Bosch's iBooster, which also lets the brake system blend in regenerative braking and back up the stability control unit. U055F is set when booster A transmits but its data, such as pedal travel, assist status or pressure request, fail the receiver's checks.",["Booster control unit or its pedal travel sensor faulty","Supply interrupted or weak battery during start or service work","Booster and ABS/ESC software not matched","Bus wiring or connector at the booster damaged"],["ABS, brake or stability warning lamps on","Harder pedal or changed pedal feel","Regenerative braking or driver assistance functions limited"],4,2,["U025E","U0560","U0415","U0129"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מגבר בלם אלקטרוני‏ A"],U0560:["Invalid Data Received From Electronic Brake Booster Control Module B","A second brake booster unit mainly appears in architectures built for automated driving, where a single electronic brake must not be a single point of failure. Bosch, for example, pairs its integrated power brake with a separate redundant brake unit that can stop the car if the primary unit fails.",["Secondary brake unit B internally faulty","Software of the two brake units not matched after update or replacement","Separate supply or ground of unit B faulty"],["Brake system warning lamp or message on","Driver assistance or automated functions unavailable"],4,2,["U025F","U055F","U0415"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מגבר בלם אלקטרוני‏ B"],U0561:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Switch Module A","Modern power seat switches are often small control units of their own: they read the keys and send the result to the seat module over LIN instead of switching motor current directly. A Lear patent describes a seat electronics unit with a LIN driver that acts on commands from such an external switch.",["Seat switch module software fault (e.g. switch stays in sleep mode)","Switch part or software level not matching the seat module","Loose or corroded connector at the seat or door switch","Seat control switch module A internally faulty"],["Seat cannot be adjusted with the switch","Seat settings such as lumbar not shown or not selectable on the screen"],1,0,["U0260","U0562"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ A"],U0562:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Control Switch Module B","Switch module B is a second, separate seat switch unit, for the passenger side or another seat row; which position B denotes is not published by any manufacturer. Mercedes counts its seat switch groups by position, front left being SSE-VL, which points to one unit per seat.",["Receiving seat module not configured for the installed switch and seat equipment","Software fault in the second seat switch module","Connector or harness under a movable seat damaged by seat travel or objects"],["Passenger or rear seat does not move when its switch is pressed","Seat moves only in some directions"],1,0,["U0261","U0561"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מתג בקרת מושב‏ B"],U0563:["Invalid Data Received From Audio Amplifier B","Premium sound systems often use an external amplifier away from the head unit, and large installations can need a second one, audio amplifier B. Such amplifiers are network nodes: the head unit sends volume and other commands over CAN instead of an analog level, and the amplifier reports its status back, as a patent on modular vehicle amplifiers explains.",["Amplifier B software not matching the head unit software level","Aftermarket amplifier or audio interface on the vehicle bus sending non-conforming data","Audio amplifier B internally faulty or overheated"],["Some speakers or the subwoofer silent while others play","Volume or sound settings react incorrectly"],2,0,["U0262","U0487"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מגבר שמע‏ B"],U0564:["Invalid Data Received From Speech Recognition Module","In-car voice control lets the driver place calls, pick stations or play music by spoken command, in newer systems even in natural sentences. Some makers house it in a module of its own: FCA put Uconnect voice recognition into a hands-free module (HFM) on 2012–2017 Journey, Charger and 300;",["Speech recognition software outdated or faulty (fixed by reflashing)","Unsupported language selection or mismatch between module and head unit settings","Speech recognition module internally faulty"],["Voice control does not respond to the steering-wheel button","Voice commands misrecognized or system stuck while loading"],2,0,["U0263","U0554"],""],U0565:["Invalid Data Received From Camera Module — Rear","The rear camera module delivers the reversing picture and, on some vehicles, data that other controllers reuse. U0565 is logged by a receiver that gets its frames but judges the content implausible.",["Rear camera module software level not matching the receiving module (Ford remedy is reprogramming)","Receiver flags the camera data too strictly although the picture is fine (Jeep Gladiator 2024 radio)","Water or corrosion in the camera plug or tailgate harness","Rear camera module internally faulty"],["Hands-free driving or lane centering unavailable (Ford BlueCruise vehicles)","Reversing picture missing, frozen or without guide lines","Code stored in radio or driver-assist module without noticeable fault"],2,0,["U0264","U053B","U0566"],""],U0566:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor A","At GM, image processing sensor A is the front camera behind the windshield; its partner U0265 is called Front View Camera – Windshield in GM bulletins. GM's 2025 OBD tables show how U0566 is detected: the brake module and the EOCM3 driver-assist controller check rolling counters, checksums and message authentication on the camera's frames.",["Windshield camera software resets or sends faulty protection values (GM remedy is reprogramming)","Front camera internally faulty when the fault recurs often (GM then replaces it)","Supply voltage dips or bus disturbances during start"],["Service Driver Assist or Steering Assist Reduced message","Adaptive cruise and automatic braking functions unavailable","MIL possible only through accompanying brake-module code P25A2"],3,0,["U0265","U053B","U0567","U056B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ A"],U0567:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor B","Image processing sensors are cameras that interpret their own picture and send results, not raw video, onto the bus. U0567 is set when frames from sensor B arrive but fail the receiver's checks, for instance a wrong CRC or a counter that jumps or repeats.",["Sensor B software not matching the receiver after an update or replacement","Loose connector or damaged wiring causing corrupted frames","Image processing sensor B internally faulty"],["Assistance or night-view function served by sensor B switched off","Camera-related service message in the instrument cluster"],3,0,["U0266","U0566","U0568"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ B"],U0568:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor C","U0568 means a receiver gets messages from image processing sensor C whose content it cannot trust. SAE only numbers these sensors; no manufacturer publishes which physical camera is C, and the partner U0267 appears in no public bulletin either. Typical consumers of a camera's object list are lane departure warning, traffic sign recognition and glare-free high beam.",["Software mismatch between sensor C and the receiving controller","Intermittent contact in the sensor connector or bus wiring","Image processing sensor C internally faulty"],["Lane departure warning or traffic sign display unavailable","Automatic high beam falls back to manual switching with a warning"],3,0,["U0267","U0567","U0569"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ C"],U0569:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor D","Sensor D's frames reach the receiver, but their content fails its plausibility or protection checks. Which camera carries letter D is not published, and U0569 itself appears in no bulletin. GM ties the partner code U0268 to its active-safety network: on 2015–2020 Cadillac Escalade models, a front fascia harness chafed at the right end of the bumper bar could blow fuses and set U0268 together with U0265, U0269 and…",["Front fascia or bumper harness chafed through (GM Escalade 2015–2020 pattern)","Blown fuse leaving the sensor with unstable supply","Image processing sensor D internally faulty or damaged in a collision"],["Surround-view, park-assist or adaptive-cruise service messages","Front park, turn, daytime or cornering lamps out at the same time","Several camera and radar codes stored together"],2,0,["U0268","U0568","U056A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ D"],U056A:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor E","U056A is the invalid-data code for image processing sensor E: the module still talks, but the receiver rejects what it says. No brand documents U056A itself. GM lists the partner U0269 among codes held by the active safety controller of many 2013–2018 models with driver-assist packages, among them Escalade, ATS, CT6, Malibu, Volt and Acadia.",["Faulty diagnostic interface or cable on the object detection bus pins (false codes)","Fault on the dedicated object detection bus wiring","Sensor E software fault or internal defect"],["Object detection or Service Active Safety message","Scan tool cannot reach radars and front camera","Code returns only when one particular tester is connected"],2,0,["U0269","U0569","U056B","U0075"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ E"],U056B:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor F","At GM, the partner of U056B – U026A – belongs to the front camera module B174W. A 2023 GM note for 2022–2023 Cadillac XT5 and XT6, Chevrolet Equinox and GMC Acadia and Terrain blames U026A plus the front-camera warning on terminals in that camera that were pushed back or absent, which then has to be replaced.",["Pushed-in or missing terminals in the front camera connector (GM 2022–2023)","Front camera software fault, fixed by reprogramming","Front camera module internally faulty"],["Service Front Camera message","Lane keeping, lane departure or forward collision alert unavailable"],3,0,["U026A","U0566","U056A","U056C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ F"],U056C:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor G","Image processing sensor G is sending frames that the receiving module refuses. Neither U056C nor a camera position for G is documented by a manufacturer. Its partner U026B, however, is on GM's list for 2015–2020 Escalades whose front fascia harness rubbed through at the right bumper bar: blown fuses F10DL, F19DR, F43UA or F46DR, dead front park, turn, daytime and cornering lamps, and messages for surround vision,…",["Bumper or fascia harness rubbed through, shorting circuits and fuses","Camera connector disturbed or misassembled after body repair","Image processing sensor G internally faulty"],["Surround view shows a black segment or is unavailable","Blown fuses and front lamps out at the same time"],2,0,["U026B","U056B","U056D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ G"],U056D:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor H","U056D is reported when sensor H's messages carry data that fail checks such as a CRC, an alive counter or an authentication value. AUTOSAR's end-to-end protection names the fault types behind this: repeated, lost, delayed, corrupted or masqueraded frames. GM uses the partner U026C on its object detection bus and lists it next to U0075, a bus-off code for a whole network.",["Sensor H software computing counters or checksums incorrectly","Poor contact at sensor H connector while the rest of the bus is fine","Image processing sensor H internally faulty"],["Single assistance function unavailable while others work","U056D stored without bus-off or other lost-communication codes"],3,0,["U026C","U056C","U056E","U0075"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ H"],U056E:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor I","The higher letters of the image-sensor series cover the further cameras that newer vehicles add. One growing group looks into the cabin: driver monitoring cameras check whether the driver is watching the road, as Super Cruise does at Cadillac, starting with the 2017 CT6, or Ford's BlueCruise, which uses a module on the steering column of the 2021 Mustang Mach-E and F-150;",["Sensor I software level not matching the receiving controller","Connector disturbed behind trim, dash or steering column panels","Image processing sensor I internally faulty"],["Hands-free or attention-dependent assistance not offered","Driver attention warning inactive or showing a fault"],3,0,["U026D","U056D","U056F"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ I"],U056F:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor J","U056F concerns image processing sensor J, whose messages arrive but are not plausible. No manufacturer publishes this code, its partner U026E, or which camera carries the letter J. Cameras increasingly replace glass: Lexus put cameras in place of door mirrors on the ES sold in Japan from October 2018, later joined by Hyundai's Ioniq 5 and Audi's Q8 e-tron.",["Software mismatch after an update of camera or display unit","Damaged wiring or connector at an exposed camera position (mirror housing, door)","Image processing sensor J internally faulty"],["Camera view black, frozen or replaced by a warning","Camera-related message in the instrument cluster"],3,0,["U026E","U056E","U0570"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ J"],U0570:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor K","Sensor K's frames reach the bus but are discarded as invalid. U0570 and its partner U026F are not documented by any vehicle maker, so the camera behind letter K is unknown. One use for additional image sensors is towing: a Magna patent describes satellite cameras fitted to the trailer whose images are merged with the picture of the car's own reversing camera into a see-through trailer view while driving forward,…",["Corroded or loose plug where an add-on or trailer camera connects","Additional camera not configured or software not matching the vehicle","Image processing sensor K internally faulty"],["Extra camera view (for example trailer view) missing or black","Code appears mainly with a trailer or accessory connected"],2,0,["U026F","U056F","U0571","U0565"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ K"],U0571:["Invalid Data Received From Image Processing Sensor L","U0571 closes the image-processing-sensor block; the next number, U0572, already belongs to a vehicle motion control module. An image processing sensor computes objects inside the camera itself, for instance with a system-on-chip as in Bosch's multi purpose camera or with Mobileye's EyeQ processors, the first generation of which launched in 2008.",["Processing software in sensor L faulty or not matching the receiver","Wiring or connector fault corrupting the sensor's messages","Image processing sensor L internally faulty"],["Assistance function using sensor L unavailable","Code stored without warning lamp"],3,0,["U0270","U0570","U053B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן עיבוד תמונה‏ L"],U0572:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Motion Control Module A","A vehicle motion control module sits above the individual chassis controllers and coordinates steering, brakes, damping and drive torque. ZF's cubiX software works this way and went into production in the Lotus Eletre; Hitachi Astemo describes a central controller that sends time-referenced instructions to several actuator modules.",["Software of motion control module and chassis controllers not matched","Motion control module A internally faulty","Implausible sensor input to the module (yaw, steering angle) leading to invalid outputs","Disturbed chassis network or gateway"],["Chassis or stability warning message","Rear-axle steering, active roll control or drive modes switched off","Car drives with basic stability control only"],4,2,["U0573","U0416","U0415","U0122"],""],U0573:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Motion Control Module B","U0573 is the B variant: invalid data from a second vehicle motion control module. A second unit makes sense where coordination tasks are split, for example lateral and longitudinal motion, or where a backup must take over for automated driving.",["Lost time synchronisation between module B and the actuator controllers","Modules A and B on different software levels","Motion control module B internally faulty"],["Warning about reduced chassis or assistance functions","Automated or semi-automated driving functions unavailable"],4,2,["U0572","U0416","U0420"],""],U0574:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Driver Control Module A","Lighting driver control modules switch and dim individual LEDs or LED segments in modern headlamps. Lincoln's 2025 Navigator has four of them, labelled A to D, and an over-the-air release (25.10.08) for all four adjusted headlamp colour and brightness at start-up; NHTSA's summary adds an intermittent resistance fault that dropped the lamps to their lowest setting.",["Lighting driver module software needing an update (Lincoln remedy over the air)","Moisture or poor contact at the headlamp connector","Lighting driver control module A internally faulty (often only with the headlamp)"],["Adaptive or glare-free high beam unavailable","Headlamp colour or brightness wrong, lamps at reduced level"],2,0,["U0273","U0575","U0542"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ A"],U0575:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Driver Control Module B","U0575 flags implausible data from lighting driver control module B. Matrix headlamps split the high beam into many LEDs that a control unit switches individually; Audi introduced the first such glare-free system on the 2013 A8 with 25 segments per lamp. With several driver modules on board, the controller in charge expects regular and consistent status from each of them.",["Software of driver module B outdated or inconsistent with the other modules","Defective LED segment producing fault reports the receiver cannot match","Lighting driver control module B internally faulty"],["Glare-free high beam switched off with a lighting message","Individual LED segments dark or flickering"],2,0,["U0274","U0574","U0576"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ B"],U0576:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Driver Control Module C","Lighting driver control module C is sending data that the receiver discards. The US standard FMVSS 108 explains why this matters for an adaptive driving beam: the system must recognise malfunctions, including a blocked sensor, switch to manual beam control until the fault is gone and show the driver a warning.",["Driver module C software fault, curable by an update","Unstable supply or ground at the headlamp","Lighting driver control module C internally faulty"],["Lighting system warning in the instrument cluster","Automatic high beam replaced by manual switching"],2,0,["U0275","U0575","U0577"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ C"],U0577:["Invalid Data Received From Lighting Driver Control Module D","U0577 is the code for invalid messages from lighting driver control module D, the last of the four-letter block; U0276 is its lost-communication partner. LED matrix drivers can be chained: TI's TPS92662 addresses up to 31 devices over one multi-drop UART line, can use CAN transceivers for a sturdier physical layer, and also drives sequential turn signals and animated daytime lights.",["Driver module D software not at the level of the other lighting modules","Fault on the serial link between lighting controller and driver chips","Lighting driver control module D internally faulty"],["Sequential indicator or animated daytime light not working","Lamp lit only in a basic setting"],2,0,["U0276","U0576","U0574"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת נהג תאורה‏ D"],U0578:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Module K","Ford assigns letter K to a defined seat: on the 2025 Lincoln Navigator, seat control module K (SCMK) is the rear left power seat module of the second row. Its software update SCMK-25.5.5.3 removed a short delay in seat operation and made the memory function of that seat store positions reliably.",["Seat module K software fault (Ford remedy is a software update)","Seat module K not configured for the installed second-row seat equipment","Connector under the second-row seat loose or damaged"],["Left second-row power seat responds late or does not move fore and aft","Memory positions of that seat not saved"],2,0,["U0277","U0579","U054E"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מושב‏ K"],U0579:["Invalid Data Received From Seat Module L","Seat control module L (SCML) is Ford's right-hand counterpart to SCMK: on the 2025 Lincoln Navigator it runs the passenger-side power seat of the second row. Ford pushed SCML-25.5.5.3 over the air so that this seat keeps its memory settings consistently; the release note page itself is headed with the PCM by mistake but names seat control module L in the text.",["Seat module L software fault (fixed by an over-the-air update)","Seat module L configuration missing or wrong for the seat equipment","Seat module L internally faulty"],["Right second-row power seat does not move with its switch","Stored seat positions on the passenger side lost"],2,0,["U0278","U0578"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מושב‏ L"],U057B:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Charger Control Module C","Charger C is the third on-board charger slot. Some vehicles split AC charging over several units: the extended-range Ford F-150 Lightning, for example, offers 19.2 kW through a dual on-board charger. A Porsche patent describes such a group, in which only one charger is wired to the inlet and acts as master while the others are linked to it only by a communication line.",["Charger C internally faulty","Charger C on a different software level than master or charging controller","Communication line between the chargers damaged"],["AC charging slower than expected","Charging fault message in the display or app"],4,0,["U027A","U057C","U049C","U04BE"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ C"],U057C:["Invalid Data Received From Battery Charger Control Module D","U057C covers the fourth charger slot. Large chargers are often built from parallel power modules: Hyundai's patent for a vehicle-mounted charger gives each module its own slave controller that reports to a master, which can drop to a single module once the battery reaches the constant-voltage phase. If the reports from unit D are implausible, the master cannot decide how to share current and stores U057C;",["Power module or slave controller D faulty","Charger software not matched across units","Overheating of unit D due to coolant or fan problems, corrupting its status data"],["Charging power lower than usual or charging stops","Charging system warning"],4,0,["U027B","U057B","U049C","U04BE"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ D"],U057D:["Invalid Data Received From Off-Board Charger Control Module","Despite its name, the off-board charger control module sits inside the vehicle: it conducts the dialogue with an external DC fast charger, which under CCS runs as power line communication on the control pilot contact (ISO 15118, DIN 70121) and under CHAdeMO over a CAN link in the connector. Ford calls this unit the off-board charger controller (OBCC) on the Mustang Mach-E and E-Transit;",["Fault or outdated software in the charging station","Dirty or damaged communication contacts in plug or inlet","Vehicle charging controller software not compatible with the station"],["DC fast charging aborts or does not start","Charging works at other stations"],2,0,["U027C","U049C","P0CF4"],""],U0580:["Invalid Data Received From Haptic Control Module","A haptic control module produces vibrations the driver feels, in the steering wheel, seat or a touch surface, mainly as a warning. Hyundai and Genesis use a separate haptic steering controller: on the 2015–2016 Genesis and 2017–2018 G80, B247100 for a vibration motor fault brought on the warning lamp and the controller was replaced (19-BE-001, 19-BE-001-G).",["Poor contact in the vibration motor circuit making the module report implausible status","Haptic controller internally faulty or on an old software level","Alert type setting (chime or vibration) not matching between modules"],["Steering wheel or seat no longer vibrates during lane or other warnings","Haptic system warning lamp or message in the cluster"],2,0,["U0279"],""],U0585:["Invalid Data Received From Active Grille Air Shutter Module A","Active grille shutters close the front opening to cut drag and speed warm-up; CARB counts them as an off-cycle CO2 technology. The shutter actuator is usually a LIN slave of the engine controller. GM's 2025 ECM tables check the rolling counter, protection value and checksum of shutter module A's status frame and set U0585 after 3 bad frames in 10, with battery voltage of 11 V or more for 5 s;",["Shutter actuator A with faulty firmware or internal fault (GM PIT6133)","LIN wiring or connector at the front end damaged or wet","Replacement actuator of the wrong variant"],["Check engine light on","Shutters stay in a fixed position","Slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["U0284","U0586","P059F","P05A2","U058C"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ A"],U0586:["Invalid Data Received From Active Grille Air Shutter Module B","Vehicles with two shutter assemblies, typically one in the upper grille and one in the lower bumper opening, report the second one as module B. U0586 means the engine controller gets status frames from that actuator but cannot trust them.",["Lower shutter actuator B with faulty firmware or internal fault","Wiring or connector in the lower bumper area damaged by road debris or water","Upper and lower actuator swapped or wrong part fitted"],["Check engine light on","Lower shutter does not move"],2,1,["U0285","U0585","P05AE","P05B1","U058D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ B"],U0587:["Invalid Data Received From Radiator Anti-Tamper Device","Some low-emission vehicles have a radiator coated with a catalyst that converts ground-level ozone, known as direct ozone reduction (DOR) or by BASF's trade name PremAir; it earns an emissions credit, and CARB then requires the OBD system to monitor it.",["Radiator replaced with an uncoated part or sensor moved from another radiator","Anti-tamper sensor internally faulty","Corroded connector or wiring at the radiator"],["Check engine light on","No noticeable change in driving or cooling"],2,1,["U0286","P00B1","P00B6"],""],U0588:["Invalid Data Received From Transmission Fluid Pump Module A","An electric transmission fluid pump keeps clutch and line pressure up while the engine is stopped by start-stop or in electric hybrid driving. Many such pumps have their own electronics and report speed, current and faults to the transmission or hybrid controller. U0588 means those reports arrive but cannot be trusted. Ford's 2014 OBD code list includes U0588 as a continuously monitored code without MIL.",["Electric pump or its integrated controller faulty","Pump connector not fully latched or wet","Pump and transmission controller software not matched"],["Start-stop function disabled","Service transmission or hybrid system message","Limp mode with limited gears on some hybrids"],3,2,["U0287","U058B","P0B0D","P2797","U0402"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול משאבת שמן תיבה‏ A"],U0589:["Invalid Data Received From DC/AC Converter Control Module A","A DC/AC converter turns the vehicle's DC supply into household-style AC for power outlets in the cabin or truck bed. Ford calls the 7.2 kW Pro Power Onboard unit of the 2021 F-150 PowerBoost direct current/alternating converter module A (DCACA) and fixed a service message there by reprogramming the PCM and the DCACA.",["Converter or receiving module software out of date (Ford DCACA reprogramming)","Body control module configured for an outlet option the vehicle does or does not have","Converter internally faulty or overheated"],["Power outlets dead or switching off under load","Message that the onboard power system needs service"],2,0,["U0288","U058A","P0364"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A"],U058A:["Invalid Data Received From DC/AC Converter Control Module B","U058A refers to a second DC/AC converter. Two converters can make sense when outlets in the cab and in the cargo bed are fed separately or when a high-power unit is added to a small one. GM's 2023 Silverado and Sierra 1500 illustrate how optional such hardware is: because of the chip shortage, trucks built from September 2022 left the factory with the inverter for the 120 V instrument panel and bed outlets inactive…",["Configuration not updated after fitting or retrofitting converter B","Converter B internally faulty or overheated","Bus wiring to converter B damaged"],["One group of outlets dead while others work","Outlet warning or service message"],2,0,["U0289","U0589","P0364"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ B"],U058B:["Invalid Data Received From Transmission Fluid Pump Module B","Some transmissions carry a second electrically driven oil pump with its own electronics, labelled module B, alongside or instead of a first one. Its job is to hold clutch pressure and lubrication while the combustion engine is off, so the receiving transmission or hybrid controller depends on the speed, current and fault status the pump reports.",["Integrated electronics of electric pump B faulty","Pump B connector or pass-through in the transmission case wet or loose","Pump firmware and transmission controller software not compatible"],["Start-stop or electric drive mode unavailable","Transmission warning message","Delayed engagement after an engine restart"],3,2,["U028A","U0588","P0B0D","P2797"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול משאבת שמן תיבה‏ B"],U058C:["Invalid Data Received From Active Grille Air Shutter Module C","A third grille shutter unit appears on vehicles that split the lower intake into several flaps. Hyundai is the clearest case: on the 2026 Palisade and Palisade Hybrid, the lower active air flaps use left and right actuators, and campaign 26-01-026H lists U028B, lost communication with shutter module C, among codes that light the engine lamp after water entered bumper connectors and corroded them.",["Water ingress and corrosion at the lower bumper connectors (Hyundai 26-01-026H)","Shutter actuator C with internal electronics fault","Actuator of wrong variant or position fitted after a bumper repair"],["Check engine light on","Active air flap warning message","Lower flaps stay in one position"],2,1,["U028B","U058D","U0585","U0586"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C"],U058D:["Invalid Data Received From Active Grille Air Shutter Module D","Module D is the fourth shutter position the code list reserves; it only matters on front ends with four separately driven flap sets, for instance two upper and two lower ones. No manufacturer documents U058D or names a shutter D in public material, so its exact placement remains maker-specific.",["Shutter D wiring or LIN connector damaged by road debris or moisture","Actuator D electronics faulty","Engine controller configured for a shutter layout that does not match the vehicle"],["Check engine light on some vehicles","One flap set does not move"],2,1,["U028C","U058C","U0586"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D"],U0592:["Invalid Data Received From Gear Shift Control Module B","Shift-by-wire cars turn the driver's lever, dial or buttons into network messages; where two such units exist, or the selector is split from a park-lock unit, the second one is module B. U0592 says its messages arrive but carry an implausible selector position, a frozen counter or a bad checksum, so the receiver cannot rely on the requested gear.",["Selector module B electronics or position sensing faulty","Bus wiring or gateway path between selector and transmission controller disturbed","Software of selector, gateway or TCM out of date"],["Vehicle will not shift out of Park","Transmission fault message in the cluster","Restricted gear selection"],2,2,["U0291","U0404","U0103","U0402"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B"],U0593:["Invalid Data Received From Drive Motor Control Module B","Electric vehicles with one motor per axle typically report the second inverter and motor as drive motor module B; on the 2019 Audi e-tron that is the rear unit, whose loss Audi logs as U0292 when a chafed low-voltage harness cuts it off. U0593 is set when that module keeps transmitting but its torque or status data are untrustworthy.",["Low-voltage harness to the second drive unit chafed or connector loose","Drive motor B inverter or receiver software out of date","Inverter B internally faulty"],["Drive system warning, reduced power","Reduced or no regenerative braking","Vehicle drives on one axle only"],3,3,["U0292","U0411","U059C","U059D"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ B"],U0594:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Powertrain Control Module","The hybrid or EV powertrain controller coordinates engine, motors and battery, so many modules read its messages. Ford's hybrid OBD summary explains that the ABS module logs U0594 when wheel-torque or driver-demand signals from the HPCM are flagged invalid, unknown or faulted; Ford's 2014 list carries it with MIL and its 2024 summary sets U0594_48 for bad monitoring data with MIL and wrench lamp.",["Fault inside the hybrid system makes the controller mark its signals invalid (e.g. MGU connector on Ram eTorque)","Software of the hybrid controller or the receiving module out of date","CAN wiring or termination disturbed"],["Check engine light and hybrid or electrical system warning","Reduced power or stalling on some hybrids","Stored code without symptoms (Ford Escape, F-150 Lightning)"],3,3,["U0293","U0401","U0415","U059B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מערכת ההנעה היברידי/חשמלי"],U0595:["Invalid Data Received From Powertrain Control Monitor Module","A powertrain control monitor module is an independent supervisor that recomputes torque, engine speed or pedal requests and compares them with what the main controller commands, so that unintended acceleration or deceleration can be caught. U0595 is stored when that supervisor's results arrive but cannot be trusted.",["Software mismatch between monitor module and main powertrain controller","Monitor module internally faulty","Supply voltage dips or bus disturbances corrupting messages"],["Wrench or powertrain warning lamp on","Reduced power or limp mode"],3,2,["U0401","U0594"],""],U0596:["Invalid Data Received From AC/AC Converter Control Module","An AC/AC converter changes alternating current of one voltage or frequency into another without handing it to the battery first. In vehicles, such a stage can sit in a charger, for example a matrix converter that turns three-phase grid power directly into high-frequency AC for an isolating transformer, as in patent US9973107B2, or it can adapt power for on-board outlets.",["Converter control electronics faulty or overheated","Converter and receiving module software not matched","Bus wiring to the converter damaged"],["Charging or outlet power interrupted","Warning about the charging or power system"],3,0,["U0589","U0597"],""],U0597:["Invalid Data Received From AC/DC Converter Control Module A","In plug-in hybrids and electric cars the AC/DC converter is normally the on-board charger: it rectifies mains power and controls the current into the traction battery. CARB requires plug-in hybrids to detect charger faults that stop charging or reduce its rate. U0597 is logged when the charger's messages about state, voltage or current fail validation at the battery or vehicle controller.",["Third-party dongle or Y-splitter on the diagnostic connector disturbing the bus (Volvo TJ 36559)","On-board charger electronics faulty or overheated","Charger or battery controller software out of date"],["AC charging stops or runs at reduced rate","Electric-only mode unavailable on plug-in hybrids","Warning lamps such as ESC or check engine"],3,1,["U0296","U0598"],""],U0598:["Invalid Data Received From AC/DC Converter Control Module B","A second AC/DC converter exists where makers raise AC charging power by fitting two charger units; the F-150 Lightning, for instance, can be ordered with two 40-amp charger units that together reach 19.2 kW.",["Second charger unit faulty or overheated","Software of the charger pair not matched after a replacement","Communication line between the chargers damaged"],["AC charging only at roughly half power","Charging system warning"],3,0,["U0597","U0296"],""],U0599:["Invalid Data Received From DC/DC Converter Control Module A","On start-stop vehicles a DC/DC converter can hold the 12 V supply for sensitive electronics while the starter pulls the voltage down; on hybrids it feeds the 12 V network from the high-voltage battery.",["Engine controller software miscalculating the converter's protection value (GM 20-NA-191)","DC/DC converter A electronics faulty","Weak 12 V battery causing deep voltage dips during cranking"],["Auto start/stop disabled","Check engine light after repeated failures"],2,1,["U0298","U059A","P0A94"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ A"],U059A:["Invalid Data Received From DC/DC Converter Control Module B","Converter B is a second DC/DC unit, used when one voltage support stage is not enough or when separate networks need their own supply. FCA is the only maker that names it publicly: in powertrain module updates for the 2019 Jeep Cherokee with the 3.2-litre V6 and engine stop-start (18-023-19 and follow-ups such as 18-020-21), the PCM lists both U0599 and U059A for invalid data from DC-to-DC converters A and B, plus…",["Powertrain controller software evaluating converter B data incorrectly (FCA 18-023-19)","Second DC/DC converter faulty","Wiring or ground connection of converter B poor"],["Check engine light","Engine does not restart after a stop-start event","Stop-start function withdrawn"],2,1,["U0299","U0599"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת ממיר DC/DC‏ B"],U059B:["Invalid Data Received From Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Sensor Module","The battery pack sensor module measures pack voltage and current and often sits in the switch box that holds the main contactors, reporting to the battery management controller. Audi uses U059B00 for an implausible signal from the high-voltage battery switch box on the 2024 Q8 e-tron family: after a stop at an AC charging point the car refused to enable its drive and the cluster asked the driver to stop safely, with…",["Over-sensitive battery management software (Audi 2073482)","Current or voltage sensing in the switch box faulty","Battery-internal communication line or connector disturbed"],["Drive system cannot be activated","Drive system and electrical system fault messages","Charging interrupted"],4,2,["U029A","U0594","P0AA1"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול חיישן מארז סוללת מתח גבוה"],U059C:["Invalid Data Received From Drive Motor Control Module C","A third drive motor controller exists only on tri-motor or quad-motor vehicles, where one axle carries two motors for torque vectoring. Examples are GMC's Hummer EV in tri-motor form and Rivian's quad-motor R1T with a motor at each wheel. U059C is stored when module C still talks but sends torque, speed or status values the vehicle controller cannot accept.",["Inverter or controller of motor C faulty","Low-voltage harness or connector at drive unit C damaged","Software level of motor C not matching the vehicle controller"],["Propulsion system warning and reduced power","Torque vectoring or a drive mode unavailable"],4,2,["U029B","U0593","U059D","U0411"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ C"],U059D:["Invalid Data Received From Drive Motor Control Module D","Module D only exists where four drive motors are fitted, one per wheel. Rivian's R1T and R1S Quad-Motor are production examples: each wheel has its own motor, so a single faulty controller costs one corner of drive, not a whole axle. U059D records that the fourth controller keeps sending frames whose torque, speed or diagnostic content fails the receiving controller's checks.",["Inverter or controller of the fourth motor faulty","Signal wiring at the wheel motor damaged by road debris or water","Motor controller software not updated together with the others"],["Reduced power warning","Off-road or performance modes locked"],4,2,["U029C","U059C","U0593"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת מנוע הנעה‏ D"],U059E:["Invalid Data Received From NOx Sensor A","NOx sensor A usually sits upstream of the SCR catalyst. Its attached electronics turn the probe current into NOx and oxygen readings and broadcast them on CAN. Here those frames still arrive, yet the receiver rejects them.",["Sensor control unit of NOx sensor A faulty (heat, moisture, internal error)","Replacement sensor of a different part number or software level","Corroded connector or damaged CAN/supply wiring at the sensor","Engine controller software needing an update"],["Check engine light after the second faulty trip","SCR and NOx sensor monitors stay incomplete","Engine usually runs normally"],2,3,["U029D","U059F","U05A8","U05A1","U030D","P2200"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן NOx‏ A"],U059F:["Invalid Data Received From NOx Sensor B","Sensor B is normally the tailpipe NOx sensor behind the SCR catalyst, so its readings decide whether the catalyst efficiency test passes. The code means its CAN frames are present but unusable. GM's 2025 diesel tables run the same counter, protection value and checksum test as for sensor A, here on the post-catalyst signal set, and treat it as Type B.",["Engine controller calibration known to flag false faults (FCA reflash)","Control unit of the downstream NOx sensor damaged","Chafed wiring or water in the connector near the exhaust"],["Check engine light on","SCR efficiency monitor not completing","No noticeable change in power"],2,3,["U029E","U059E","U05A8","U05A2","U030E","P229E"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן NOx‏ B"],U05A0:["Invalid Data Received From Evaporative Emission System Leak Detection Control Module","Some fuel systems hand the tank leak test to a separate module with its own pump, valve, pressure sensor and processor. Stoneridge patent US11773809 describes such a unit: it wakes hours after shutdown while the engine controller sleeps, runs the test alone and later passes pressure results over CAN or LIN, from which the OBD system decides on a fault code.",["Leak detection module electronics or its pressure sensor failing","Corrosion at the module connector near the tank or canister","Module and engine controller software levels do not match"],["Check engine light on","EVAP readiness not set, emissions inspection may fail"],2,1,["U029F","U030A","P0455","P0456"],""],U05A1:["NOx Sensor A Received Invalid Data From ECM/PCM","Here the fault is judged inside NOx sensor A: its control unit relies on engine controller frames, for instance the release to heat the probe once condensation is no longer a risk, and it reports back when those inputs are missing or make no sense. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary groups U05A1 with P2200 under the upstream NOx module checks.",["Engine controller software or configuration sending wrong values to the sensor","Intermittent CAN connection to the sensor causing timeouts","Sensor control unit misjudging correct data"],["Check engine light on","NOx reading for sensor A stays invalid on the scan tool","SCR monitors not completing"],2,3,["U059E","U05A2","U05A9","U029D","P2200"],""],U05A2:["NOx Sensor B Received Invalid Data From ECM/PCM","This is the downstream counterpart of U05A1: the tailpipe NOx sensor B finds the frames it gets from the engine controller missing or implausible and reports it. Ford's 2023 diesel summary documents it for the 3.0 L and 6.7 L engines next to P229E in the tailpipe NOx controller checks, using the same criteria as for the front sensor, an erroneous signal such as a dew point release with ignition off, or more than 1 s…",["Damaged harness to the rear sensor, exposed to road spray and heat","Engine controller software sending implausible commands","Fault inside the sensor B control unit"],["Check engine light on","SCR efficiency monitor incomplete"],2,3,["U059F","U05A1","U05A9","U029E","P229E"],""],U05A3:["Invalid Data Received From Reductant Quality Module","A reductant quality module checks that the tank holds proper diesel exhaust fluid, a 32.5 % urea solution. SSI's TULC sensor, for example, derives concentration from the speed of sound and reports it with level and temperature over J1939 CAN to the dosing control unit. This code means those reports arrive but are rejected.",["Dosing control unit software misreading the module (FCA reflash)","Quality sensor fouled by crystals or contaminated fluid","Corroded connector at the DEF tank sender"],["Check engine light and DEF warning","Reductant consumption faults stored alongside","Possible speed or restart limitation if not fixed"],2,3,["U02A2","U030C","P207F"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול איכות אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U05A4:["Particulate Matter Sensor Received Invalid Data From ECM/PCM","A diesel particulate matter sensor has its own control unit, which needs engine controller data to run its measuring and burn-off cycles. U05A4 is reported when that unit cannot accept what the engine controller sends.",["Engine controller software issue (FCA PCM update)","Damaged CAN or supply wiring to the PM sensor unit","PM sensor control unit faulty or wrong variant"],["Check engine light on","Several particulate matter sensor codes stored at once","Particulate filter monitor not completing"],2,1,["U04A4","U02A3","U04B2","P24AF"],""],U05A5:["Invalid Data Received From NH3 Sensor","An ammonia (NH3) sensor behind the SCR catalyst tells the controller whether too much urea is dosed and ammonia slips through. Like NOx sensors it carries its own electronics and talks over CAN; Bosch even offers NOx sensors that add a selective ammonia signal. U05A5 means the ammonia data come in but fail validation.",["Engine calibration does not match the sensor fit (with or without NH3 sensor)","Ammonia sensor control unit faulty","Damaged wiring or connector at the ammonia sensor"],["Check engine light on","Code appears right after an engine software update","SCR dosing runs without ammonia feedback"],2,1,["U02A4","U059F"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן אמוניה"],U05A6:["Invalid Data Received From Reductant Heater Control Module","Diesel exhaust fluid freezes at about -11 °C, and EU rules demanded that it be usable within 20 minutes after a start at -15 °C, so tanks, pumps and lines get electric heaters. Where these heaters are driven by a separate control module, it reports heater states, temperatures and faults to the engine or dosing controller over the bus. U05A6 is stored when those reports arrive but are inconsistent or corrupt.",["Heater control module electronics faulty","Water or salt corrosion at module connector or bus wiring","Software levels of heater module and engine controller do not fit"],["Check engine light or DEF system warning","Delayed DEF dosing after cold starts"],2,1,["U02A5","P20B9","U05A3"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת גוף חימום אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U05A7:["Invalid Data Received From Safety Integration Control Module","The Safety Integration Control Module appears in the SAE code catalogue, yet no carmaker explains in public what this unit does or which models carry it; the name suggests a controller that ties several safety functions together. U05A7 is stored by a receiving module that still gets the unit's frames but refuses what they contain.",["Software fault or outdated software in the safety integration module","Module replaced or reprogrammed without matching vehicle configuration","Corrupted frames from wiring, connector or termination faults on the bus","Low supply voltage during start or after battery discharge"],["Warning message about safety or assistance systems","Individual assistance functions unavailable","Further network codes stored in several modules"],3,0,["U02A6"],""],U05A8:["Invalid Data Received From NOx Sensor C","A third NOx sensor appears on exhaust systems with two SCR stages, where sensor C watches the gas after the second catalyst. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG04B) are the public example: the engine controller checks alive rolling count and checksum of the post-second-catalyst NOx signals, eight failures in 18 samples or three in ten depending on the signal, with battery voltage of at least 11 V for 5 s, and logs U05A8 as…",["Control unit of NOx sensor C faulty","Harness or connector of the rearmost sensor damaged","Sensors swapped between positions during repair"],["Check engine light after two trips","SCR monitor for the second catalyst incomplete"],2,3,["U02A1","U05A9","U059E","U059F","U0352"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: חיישן NOx‏ C"],U05A9:["NOx Sensor C Received Invalid Data From ECM/PCM","With this code the third NOx sensor, fitted after a second SCR stage, reports that it cannot use the frames the engine controller sends it, such as heater release or operating state. No manufacturer documents U05A9 publicly.",["Intermittent bus connection to sensor C","Engine controller not configured for the third sensor","Sensor C control unit rejecting valid data"],["Check engine light on","No NOx value from sensor C on the scan tool"],2,3,["U05A8","U05A1","U05A2","U02A1"],""],U05AA:["Invalid Data Received From Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump","Engines with a water-cooled charge air cooler use an electric pump, often a LIN slave of the engine controller, to move coolant through the low-temperature circuit. CARB requires the charge air cooling to be checked for performance and its electronic parts to be monitored. U05AA is set when the pump reports speed, current or fault bits that do not make sense.",["Pushed-out or corroded terminals at the pump connector","Fault elsewhere on the shared LIN bus or in the master module software","Pump electronics or motor faulty"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power in hot conditions","Coolant warning or radiator fan running at full speed"],2,3,["U02A9","P023B"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)"],U05AB:["Invalid Data Received From Engine Disconnect Clutch","In parallel hybrids the engine disconnect clutch sits between engine crankshaft and electric machine; opened, it lets the car drive electrically with the engine off, closed, it starts the engine or adds its torque. Ford's patents describe the clutch being prestroked so it is filled with pressure before an engine start is requested, and being advanced before the hydraulic pump spins down.",["Clutch actuator electronics or position sensor faulty","Actuator and hybrid controller software not matched or adaptation lost","Wiring or connector at the transmission bell housing damaged"],["Hybrid system warning and check engine light","Electric driving unavailable, engine runs continuously","Jerky engine starts"],4,3,["U02AA"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מצמד ניתוק מנוע"],U05AC:["Invalid Data Received From Vehicle Thermal Management Control Module","Electrified cars increasingly run cabin, battery and drive-unit cooling from one thermal management controller that commands pumps, valves, fans and the refrigerant circuit; suppliers such as Hirain and Marelli sell such units, Marelli explicitly with OBD compliance.",["Thermal management controller software out of date","Faulty temperature or pressure sensor feeding the controller","Controller internally faulty"],["Various warning messages in the cluster","Reduced charging or drive power","Climate control not working properly"],3,2,["U02AB"],""],U05B2:["Invalid Data Received From Comfort and Convenience Display A","Stellantis calls its touch screens for climate, seat and similar comfort settings Comfort and Convenience Display Modules (CCDM); the Jeep Grand Wagoneer has one up front and a second one for rear passengers. U05B2 is logged when a receiver gets traffic from display A whose content is implausible. Which of the screens carries letter A is not published.",["Display firmware with known faults, newer part number available","Display configuration not matching vehicle equipment, proxi alignment missing","Touch panel or display electronics defective","Loose or corroded connector at the display"],["Climate or seat settings change without input","Display shows functions the vehicle does not have","Comfort controls on the screen respond late or not at all"],2,0,["U02B1","U05B3","U02B2"],""],U05B3:["Invalid Data Received From Comfort and Convenience Display B","Display B is the second comfort screen on vehicles fitted with more than one, typically a rear unit from which back-seat occupants adjust climate and seats. U05B3 is set when its frames arrive but do not pass the receiver's validity checks, whereas U02B2 would mean that display B has fallen silent. No carmaker publishes U05B3 or states which screen counts as B.",["Rear comfort display with old firmware sending spurious commands","Replacement display not configured to the vehicle","Chafed or loose wiring to the rear console display"],["Rear climate settings change by themselves","Rear comfort screen does not accept inputs","Front display shows rear functions as unavailable"],2,0,["U02B2","U05B2","U02B1"],""],U05B4:["Invalid Data Received From Driver Monitoring System Module","A driver monitoring system films the driver's face with an infrared camera to judge attention and drowsiness. Toyota launched it in 2006, Cadillac relies on one to allow hands-free Super Cruise, and EU Regulation 2019/2144 covers it. Subaru stores up to five driver profiles in its DMS control unit and asks technicians to save them before service (bulletin 07-175-20);",["Low 12 V state of charge or recent battery replacement","Camera or infrared emitters covered, dirty or misaligned","Module software or calibration not matching the ADAS controller","Driver monitoring module internally defective"],["Hands-free or lane assistance not available","Driver attention warning inactive or triggered without reason","Service message for driver assistance in the cluster"],2,0,["U02B3"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול מערכת ניטור נהג"],U05B5:["Invalid Data Received From Front Radar Module A","Front radar modules measure distance and closing speed of objects ahead for adaptive cruise, emergency braking and lane change support. Mercedes-Benz documents this code on the 2026 CLA electric (series 174): the driver assistance controller N62/5 stores U05B555 when the front radar on the outer left delivers implausible data because it has not been configured.",["Radar sensor not configured or calibrated in the assistance controller (Mercedes N62/5)","Outdated software in the driver assistance controller","Radar knocked out of alignment after bumper damage or repair","Radar connector behind the bumper loose or wet"],["Driver assistance unavailable message that does not clear","Adaptive cruise and emergency braking switched off","Lane change or blind spot functions on the front left limited"],3,0,["U02B4","U05B6","U05B7","U05B8","U0433"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר קדמי‏ A"],U05B6:["Invalid Data Received From Front Radar Module B","Letter B on a front radar points to different hardware depending on the brand. At Mercedes-Benz, U05B655 on the 2026 CLA electric marks implausible data from the front radar on the outer right, again with sub-code 55 for a sensor that was never configured, and it shares the remedy of the left unit: calibrating control unit N62/5 per LI54.71-P-080345.",["Right front radar not configured after production or replacement (Mercedes)","Long-range radar connector not fully latched (Stellantis D1082A)","Radar cover dirty, iced or damaged","Radar module internally defective"],["Adaptive cruise control not available","Forward collision warning switched off","Lane centring or active driving assist not ready"],3,0,["U02B5","U05B5","U0433"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר קדמי‏ B"],U05B7:["Invalid Data Received From Rear Radar Module A","Rear radar modules are hidden in the corners of the rear bumper and feed blind spot warning, rear cross traffic alert and the exit warning that watches for cyclists when a door opens. Mercedes-Benz stores U05B755 on the 2026 CLA electric when the rear radar on the outer left sends implausible data because it is not configured; the driver assistance controller N62/5 then keeps several functions offline.",["Left rear radar not configured in the assistance controller","Rear bumper repaired or repainted, sensor mount or cover altered","Moisture or corrosion at the rear radar connector"],["Blind spot indicator on the left stays off","Rear cross traffic and exit warnings unavailable","Assistance unavailable message in the instrument cluster"],3,0,["U02B6","U05B8","U05B9","U05BA","U0533"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר אחורי‏ A"],U05B8:["Invalid Data Received From Rear Radar Module B","Module B is the right-hand rear corner radar in the only public manufacturer use: Mercedes-Benz lists U05B855 for the outer right rear sensor of the 2026 CLA electric. The fault type 55 reads as not configured, so the content is rejected because the controller N62/5 has no valid setup for that sensor, not because the radar is broken.",["Right rear radar not configured, calibration of the assistance controller missing","Initial calibration of the controller's acceleration sensor not completed","Right rear radar internally defective"],["Blind spot indicator on the right stays off","Assistance warnings reappear on every start","Rear cross traffic alert missing on the right"],3,0,["U02B7","U05B7","U05BA","U0534"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר אחורי‏ B"],U05B9:["Invalid Data Received From Rear Radar Module C","A third rear radar is only needed on vehicles whose rear coverage goes beyond the usual pair of corner sensors, for example to watch longer flanks or the area directly behind. No manufacturer publishes U05B9 or the position of a rear radar C, and its lost-communication partner U02B8 has no public bulletin either.",["Rear radar C not configured or calibrated after replacement","Sensor position or cover changed by rear body repair","Wiring or connector fault at rear radar C"],["Rear assistance warnings partly unavailable","Service message for driver assistance"],3,0,["U02B8","U05BA","U05B7"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר אחורי‏ C"],U05BA:["Invalid Data Received From Rear Radar Module D","Rear radar module D is the fourth unit in the rear numbering and is reserved for layouts with an unusually dense sensor set at the back. Neither U05BA nor the matching lost-communication code U02B9 is described by any manufacturer in public, so there are no published thresholds or fitting positions.",["Rear radar D not coded to the vehicle","Assistance controller software rejects data from module D","Rear radar D internally defective"],["Individual rear warnings such as exit warning not available","Assistance message in the instrument cluster"],3,0,["U02B9","U05B9","U05B8"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול רדאר אחורי‏ D"],U05BD:["Invalid Data Received From Localization and Mapping Module","Hands-free and highly automated driving needs to know the car's position to lane level and the road ahead from a detailed map. GM handles this in a separate map module (K179) for Super Cruise: it holds a LiDAR-surveyed map that decides where the system may be engaged and receives map and GPS correction data over the air while driving.",["Map database outdated because over-the-air updates could not complete","Poor satellite reception or faulty GNSS antenna and cable","Module software not matching the assistance controller","Localization and mapping module internally defective"],["Hands-free driving not offered on mapped roads","Service driver assist message","Lane-level guidance or map-based speed adaptation missing"],2,0,["U02BC","U0464"],""],U05BE:["Invalid Data Received From Night Vision Control Module","Night vision systems show the road beyond the headlight beam, either passively with a thermal camera that picks up heat from people and animals or actively with near-infrared illumination. The control module processes the picture, detects pedestrians and sends image and warning data to the cluster or head-up display. U05BE means those messages arrive but are judged invalid. No maker documents U05BE itself.",["Bent pins or loose terminals at the night vision module connector","Night vision module software fault","Infrared camera or its video link delivering faulty data"],["Night vision image missing or frozen","Pedestrian and animal warnings at night unavailable","Night vision fault message in the cluster"],2,0,["U02BD"],""],U05BF:["Invalid Data Received From Trailer Backup Assist Control Module","Trailer backup assist lets the driver reverse a trailer by turning a knob rather than the wheel; the vehicle measures the hitch angle and steers for the chosen path. Ford's Pro Trailer Backup Assist reads the angle from a target sticker via the rear camera or from a sensor on the trailer, and a Ford patent caps the steering command according to how fast the hitch angle changes, so the rig does not jackknife.",["Internal software fault in the trailer backup assist module","Implausible hitch angle input from trailer target, camera or trailer sensor","Trailer profile incomplete or measured dimensions wrong","Module supply interrupted or connector loose"],["Trailer backup assist cannot be activated or cancels","Rear park assist temporarily unavailable","Warning messages in other modules, on some trucks with MIL"],2,0,["U02BE","U0565"],""],U05C0:["Invalid Data Received From Interior Lighting Control Module B","Cars with extensive ambient and cabin lighting split it across several controllers; module B is the second of these, for instance for the rear cabin, the doors or a separate light strip, while A runs the main zone. These nodes usually hang on a LIN line below the body controller, which sends them colour and brightness commands and polls their status;",["LED controller of lighting module B defective","LIN line or connector to module B damaged, for example in a door hinge area","Replacement module B not configured for its zone"],["Ambient light zone stays dark or flickers","Wrong colour or brightness in part of the cabin","Lighting settings in the menu not applied to all zones"],2,0,["U02BF","U054B","U024A"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת תאורה פנימית‏ B"],U05C1:["Invalid Data Received From Active Radiator Air Flow Control Module A","Besides shutters in the visible grille, some cars meter cooling air with flaps placed directly in front of the radiator, behind the bumper intake. Hyundai's patent US11225900B2 describes such an arrangement with two adjacent flaps between bumper opening and radiator plus an air guide steering air towards them.",["Flap actuator A electronics faulty","Connector behind the bumper wet or corroded","Flap blocked by debris or ice so the actuator reports implausible positions"],["Warning lamp on some vehicles","Flap stays open, slightly higher consumption"],2,1,["U02C0","U0585"],"התקבלו נתונים שגויים מ: מודול בקרת זרימת אוויר רדיאטור פעיל‏ A"],U0600:["Lost Communication With Engine Oil Pressure Sensor A","Newer engines often use a digital oil pressure sensor that sends its value over a SENT line (SAE J2716) instead of an analog voltage. SENT is a one-way link with a 5 V supply, a signal wire and ground; each frame carries a CRC and a status nibble. U0600 means the engine controller no longer receives valid frames from oil pressure sensor A.",["Open, shorted or chafed SENT signal, supply or ground wire","Oil pressure sensor electronics failed","Oil or corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light on","Oil pressure warning or no oil pressure reading"],2,3,["P0520","U0601","U0609"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ שמן מנוע‏ A"],U0601:["Lost Communication With Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A","Particulate filter pressure sensor A measures the pressure drop across a diesel or gasoline particulate filter, the basis for soot load estimates and filter monitoring. Digital versions report over SENT.",["SENT line, 5 V supply or ground interrupted or shorted","Sensor internal fault switching off its output (heat, moisture)","Corroded connector near the exhaust"],["Check engine light, on GM already in the first trip","Filter regeneration may run on a model only or be blocked","Reduced power on some diesels"],2,3,["U0602","U0696","U0697","P2452","P2453"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ A"],U0602:["Lost Communication With Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B","Pressure sensor B serves a second particulate filter or a second measuring point, for example on engines with one gasoline particulate filter per bank. The code means its digital SENT output has stopped delivering usable frames to the engine controller. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary lists U0602 with P245E in the check for SENT-type filter pressure sensors A to D, running continuously and needing 5 s to register;",["Damaged SENT, supply or ground wire to sensor B","Sensor B electronics failed","Loose or corroded connector at sensor B"],["Check engine light on","Particulate filter monitor for the affected branch incomplete"],2,1,["U0601","U0696","U0697","P245E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ B"],U0603:["Lost Communication With Fuel Pressure Sensor A","Fuel pressure sensor A reports fuel or rail pressure, which the controller needs for injection quantity and pump control. When the sensor is digital, it transmits over a point-to-point SENT line instead of an analog voltage, and U0603 means its frames no longer arrive in usable form: wire open or shorted, signal stuck high or low, CRC errors or an internal sensor fault. No manufacturer documents this code publicly;",["SENT signal, 5 V supply or ground wire faulty","Fuel pressure sensor electronics failed","Loose, corroded or fuel-contaminated connector"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp mode","Hard start, stalling or no start"],2,3,["U0604","P0190","U0600","U0601"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ דלק‏ A"],U0604:["Lost Communication With Fuel Pressure Sensor B","Sensor B is the second fuel pressure measuring point, for example a low-pressure sensor in the feed line of a direct injection engine or a second rail on V engines; which pressure it reads depends on the maker. U0604 flags that this digital sensor has stopped sending valid SENT frames to the engine controller. Nobody publishes a manufacturer description for this code.",["Damaged signal, supply or ground wire to sensor B","Sensor B failed internally","Sensor A and B connectors swapped or loose"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation or reduced power under load"],2,3,["U0603","P018A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ דלק‏ B"],U0605:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Sensor A","The air conditioning controller needs refrigerant pressure or temperature to run the compressor and protect the circuit. Where this information comes over a serial link such as LIN, a single master polls the slave and expects an answer in a fixed schedule; U0605 means refrigerant sensor A no longer answers properly.",["Open or shorted LIN, supply or ground wire to the sensor","Refrigerant sensor electronics failed","Electric compressor shorted internally, high-voltage A/C fuse open (Mazda PHEV)"],["A/C does not cool","Compressor switched off by the controller"],3,0,["U0626","U0627","P0530","P0D6D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן גז מזגן‏ A"],U0606:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch A","Many electronic throttle bodies now report the blade angle as digital SENT frames (SAE J2716) instead of two analog voltages. U0606 means the engine controller no longer receives valid frames from position sensor A.",["SENT signal, 5 V supply or ground wire to the throttle body open, shorted or chafed","Loose, corroded or water-soaked throttle body connector","Sensor electronics in the throttle body failed (replacement usually as a complete throttle body)","Engine controller SENT input or software fault"],["Check engine light, on Ford also the wrench lamp","Reduced power or limp mode with limited throttle response","Rough or unstable idle"],2,3,["P0120","P0121","P0122","P0123","P0124","U0607","U0608","U0681"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ A"],U0607:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch B","Position sensor B is the redundant second track of a throttle or pedal unit. On SENT throttle bodies both tracks often share one sensor chip and even one frame (the dual throttle format A.1 of J2716), so a broken line usually drops A and B together. U0607 alone points to a fault confined to the second channel or its decoding.",["Second sensor channel inside the throttle or pedal unit failed","Damaged SENT line, supply or ground (often sets U0606 as well)","Spread or corroded terminal at the sensor connector","Engine controller software decoding the second channel wrongly"],["Check engine light, on GM in the first trip","Limited power because the redundancy check is lost"],2,3,["P0220","P0221","P0222","P0223","P0224","U0606","U0608","U0682"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ B"],U0608:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch C","Sensor C usually belongs to a second throttle body, as on engines with one throttle per bank or two throttles in parallel. Ford's 2020 to 2024 gasoline summaries spell this out: on dual-throttle applications the SENT sensor of throttle body B reports as sensor C, and U0608 sets with MIL and wrench lamp when wiring or the SENT device has been faulty for more than 4 s.",["Wiring fault on the SENT harness branch to the second throttle body","Position sensor electronics of the second throttle body failed","Corroded or loose connector at throttle body B"],["Check engine light and, on Ford, wrench lamp","Reduced power, uneven running between banks"],2,3,["P0225","P0226","P0227","P0228","P0229","U0606","U0607","U0688"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ C"],U0609:["Lost Communication With Manifold Absolute Pressure/Barometric Pressure Sensor","A digital manifold pressure sensor sends pressure, often with an intake temperature value, as SENT frames; chips built for this, such as Infineon's KP276, add a status nibble with error flags and a CRC to every frame. U0609 is stored when those frames stop arriving or cannot be used.",["SENT line stuck low, open or chafed, or supply/ground missing","Sensor reports an internal fault (moisture, oil or soot ingress)","Corroded or loose sensor connector"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or limited boost","Rough running or harder starting at altitude"],2,3,["P0105","P0106","P0107","P0108","U060A","U067F"],""],U060A:["Lost Communication With Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B","MAP sensor B is a second manifold pressure sensor, found for example on V engines with a separate intake plenum per bank or on engines measuring before and after the throttle. U060A applies when this sensor is digitally connected and the controller stops receiving usable SENT frames from it, whether because of a dead line, a broken frame or the sensor's own error code;",["Open, shorted or chafed wire to MAP sensor B","MAP sensor B electronics failed or reporting an internal error","Corroded or loose connector at sensor B"],["Check engine light","Reduced power on the affected bank or intake path"],2,3,["P2A0A","P2A0B","P2A0C","P2A0D","P2A0E","U0609"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B"],U060B:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor A","Boost sensor A measures charge air pressure after the compressor and is often a SENT pressure sensor with built-in temperature measurement. U060B means the engine controller no longer hears from it. Audi documents the code for the 2022 to 2025 Q5 and SQ5 family (bulletin 2074392): the MIL comes on and the engine control unit stores U060B00 against G31, the boost pressure sender, either intermittent or static.",["Wires broken by vibration right behind the sensor connector","Boost sensor electronics failed","Loose terminal or oil in the connector"],["Check engine light","Noticeably less power, boost held low","Fault may come and go with engine vibration"],2,3,["P0235","P0236","P0237","P0238","P025E","P023D","U060C","U060D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ A"],U060C:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor B","Boost sensor B is needed where charge pressure is measured twice: on twin-turbo V engines with one charge path per bank, on two-stage systems between the stages, or after the charge air cooler in addition to sensor A. When it is a digital SENT device, its frames carry pressure, often a temperature value, a status nibble and a CRC.",["Damaged wiring to boost sensor B, often near hot turbo plumbing","Boost sensor B electronics failed","Loose or oil-soaked connector at sensor B"],["Check engine light","Reduced power with boost limited"],2,3,["P0239","P0240","P0241","P0242","P025F","P023E","U060B","U060D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ B"],U060D:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C","A third boost sensor C appears only on complex charging layouts, for instance sequential or two-stage turbo systems with pressure taps between and after the stages, or engines that add an electric compressor.",["Open or shorted SENT, supply or ground wire to sensor C","Sensor C sending only its error value","Corroded connector at sensor C"],["Check engine light","Power loss when the affected stage would build boost"],2,3,["P25F2","P25F3","P25F4","P25F5","U060B","U060C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ C"],U060E:["Lost Communication With Crankcase Pressure Sensor","A crankcase pressure sensor lets the engine controller check the positive crankcase ventilation for leaks or a disconnected hose, which CARB 1968.2 requires. Ford fits it in two versions. The analog one reports circuit low, high and range faults; the SENT one uses P051A and U060E.",["Damaged SENT, supply or ground wire to the crankcase pressure sensor","Oil or moisture in the sensor connector","Crankcase pressure sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Crankcase ventilation monitor does not complete"],2,1,["P051A","P051B","P051C","P051D","P051E","P04DB","P2C90"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה"],U060F:["Lost Communication With Mass or Volume Air Flow Sensor A","Modern hot-film air flow meters often transmit digitally; Bosch lists SENT, frequency and LIN outputs, and many units also carry pressure, temperature or humidity. U060F means sensor A's messages are missing. GM's 2025 tables run it on LIN: no answer to the pressure request for at least 62.5 ms or to the temperature/humidity request for 250 ms, Type A or B by calibration.",["Water, corrosion or loose terminals in the air flow sensor connector","LIN or SENT line, battery feed or ground to the sensor interrupted","Air flow sensor electronics failed","Sporadic communication error without hardware fault (cleared and rechecked)"],["Check engine light, often together with an air flow circuit code","Engine runs on a modelled air mass, with reduced response","Rough idle or hesitation"],2,3,["P0100","P0101","P0102","P0103","P0104","P0068","U0610"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן זרימת אוויר (MAF)‏ A"],U0610:["Lost Communication With Mass or Volume Air Flow Sensor B","Air flow sensor B is the second meter on engines that measure each intake path separately, typically one per bank on V engines with two air boxes. In GM's documents 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07, written for an engine with two throttle bodies, U060F stands for bank 1 and U0610 for bank 2: the code sets when the digital sensor itself reports a time overflow or a maximum-period violation for 1.5 s with battery voltage above 9…",["Signal, supply or ground wire to air flow sensor B damaged","Air flow sensor B electronics failed or contaminated","Moisture or loose terminal at sensor B connector"],["Check engine light after the second trip on GM","Uneven running or slightly reduced power"],2,3,["P010A","P010B","P010C","P010D","P010E","P010F","U060F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן זרימת אוויר (MAF)‏ B"],U0611:["Lost Communication With Intake Air Temperature Sensor 1 Bank 1","Intake air temperature is often no longer a separate NTC wire to the controller but a value inside a digital frame: combined air flow meters send it over LIN or SENT, and pressure chips such as Infineon's KP276 digitize an attached NTC and pass it on in the same SENT message. U0611 concerns sensor 1 of bank 1, typically the upstream sensor in the air filter or air flow path.",["Wiring fault to the combined sensor that carries the temperature value","Electronics of the combined air flow or pressure sensor failed","Corroded or loose connector in the intake path"],["Check engine light, on GM after two trips","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],1,1,["P0110","P0111","P0112","P0113","P0114","U0612","U0613","U060F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר יניקה‏ 1 (בנק 1)"],U0612:["Lost Communication With Intake Air Temperature Sensor 1 Bank 2","Bank 2 needs its own intake temperature sensor only where the engine has two separate air paths, as on V engines with one air box and throttle per bank. U0612 is the lost-communication code for that sensor 1 of bank 2. GM's 23OBDG07/24OBDG07 treat it as the bank 2 twin of U0611: the second bank's temperature message is missing, or its line is reported stuck high or low, and the MIL follows after two trips.",["Wiring fault on the bank 2 intake sensor branch","Bank 2 temperature sensor or its host sensor failed (on Ford the air flow sensor B)","Corroded connector on the bank 2 intake"],["Check engine light","Little effect on driving; with Ford's air flow sensor B reduced response possible"],1,1,["P00AA","P00AB","P00AC","P00AD","P00AE","U0611","U0614","U0610"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר יניקה‏ 1 (בנק 2)"],U0613:["Lost Communication With Intake Air Temperature Sensor 2 Bank 1","Intake air temperature sensor 2 sits further downstream than sensor 1, for example after the charge air cooler or in the manifold, where it is frequently combined with a pressure sensor (a TMAP unit). Digital versions send the temperature together with pressure; Melexis' MLX90818 can carry a medium temperature in its SENT frame and replaces the value with a reserved error code when measurement fails.",["Damaged wiring to the combined temperature/pressure sensor","Temperature element or electronics of the combined sensor failed","Oil from the charge air path in the connector"],["Check engine light, on GM after two trips","Possible spark retard or boost reduction as a precaution"],2,1,["P0095","P0096","P0097","P0098","P0099","U0611","U0614"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר יניקה‏ 2 (בנק 1)"],U0614:["Lost Communication With Intake Air Temperature Sensor 2 Bank 2","This is the bank 2 counterpart of U0613: the downstream intake temperature sensor of the second bank, usually after that bank's charge air cooler or in its manifold half, delivers its value digitally and the controller has stopped receiving it. Typical carriers are TMAP-style sensors whose SENT frames hold pressure and temperature, protected by a CRC and status bits, as described for Infineon's KP276.",["Wiring fault to the bank 2 combined temperature/pressure sensor","Bank 2 combined sensor failed","Corroded or oily connector at the bank 2 sensor"],["Check engine light","Little effect on driving, occasionally less boost"],2,1,["P00A5","P00A6","P00A7","P00A8","P00A9","U0612","U0613"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוויר יניקה‏ 2 (בנק 2)"],U0615:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A","Engines with split cooling circuits often route coolant through an electrically driven valve that reports its position and status digitally. U0615 is stored when the engine controller gets no answer from bypass valve A.",["Moisture or corrosion in the valve connector (Ram bulletin 08-171-26)","LIN, supply or ground wire to the valve open, shorted or chafed","Valve actuator electronics failed (valve no longer answers)","LIN master in the engine controller faulty"],["Check engine light","Little or no cabin heat","Engine warms up slower or coolant temperature behaves unusually"],2,1,["P2681","P2682","P2683","P0E75","U0616","U0617","U0618","U063B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ A"],U0616:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B","Valve B is a second electronically controlled coolant valve, for example one that splits flow between the block and the head or toward a heater or oil cooler; which valve carries the letter B depends on the manufacturer. No manufacturer documents U0616 publicly.",["Damaged signal, supply or ground wire in the branch to valve B","Loose, corroded or wet connector at valve B","Electronics in valve B failed","Controller software or configuration does not match the fitted valve"],["Warning lamp, often without a noticeable change in driving","Unusual warm-up behaviour or coolant temperature swings"],2,1,["P0E7B","P0E7C","P0E7D","P0E7E","U0615","U0617","U0618","U063C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B"],U0617:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C","Unlike its LIN-based neighbours, GM uses U0617 for a coolant bypass valve whose position sensor transmits SENT frames (SAE J2716) to the engine controller. The tables 25OBDG03B and 25OBDG04B count a failure when the input hardware flags a message fault, when pulses arrive but the newest frame is older than 6.25 ms, or when the SENT pin voltage stays above or below a controller limit while frames go stale.",["SENT signal, 5 V supply or ground wire of the valve position sensor open or shorted","Corroded or loose connector at the valve","Position sensor inside the valve failed (usually replaced with the valve)","SENT input of the engine controller faulty"],["Check engine light (on GM after two trips, on 2019 calibrations after one)","Slow warm-up or reduced heater output","Possibly further coolant valve codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["U0615","U0616","U0618","U063F","P0128"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ C"],U0618:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D","Bypass valve D is a fourth smart coolant valve and appears only on engines with several separately controlled coolant paths. GM's 2025 table 25OBDG03B is the one public document found that uses U0618: the engine controller polls the valve over LIN and expects its response frame (BRV_Rsp).",["LIN wire, supply or ground to valve D interrupted or chafed","Poor contact at the valve connector","Valve D actuator electronics failed","Fault on the shared LIN bus or in the LIN master (several LIN codes)"],["Check engine light after two trips","Unusual coolant temperature or warm-up behaviour"],2,1,["U0615","U0616","U0617","U063B","P0128"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D"],U0619:["Lost Communication With Reductant Level Sensor A","Reductant level sensor A reports how much diesel exhaust fluid (DEF, AdBlue) is left in the SCR tank. Newer tank units are smart sensors: a sensing element plus electronics that transmit level, temperature and often concentration as digital frames over CAN, SENT or LIN.",["Corroded, water-soaked or loose connector at the DEF tank sensor","Data line, supply or ground of the tank sensor chafed or broken along the frame","Electronics of the tank level sensor failed (often replaced as a tank sender unit)","Controller software or configuration not matching the installed sensor"],["Check engine light or SCR warning","DEF gauge blank or frozen at a fixed value","No warning before the DEF tank runs empty"],2,1,["P203A","P203B","P203C","P203D","P203E","P203F","U061A","U061B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A"],U061A:["Lost Communication With Reductant Level Sensor B","Some SCR tanks carry more than one level measurement, for example a second sensing element, a second tank chamber or a separate sender; which point counts as B is the manufacturer's choice, and no public document assigns it. U061A is stored when the controller stops receiving usable digital frames from level sensor B while sensor A may still report normally.",["Open or chafed wire in the branch that feeds only level sensor B","Water or corrosion in the connector of sensor B","Level sensor B electronics failed"],["Check engine light or DEF system warning","DEF level shown wrongly or not at all"],2,1,["P21A8","P21A9","P21AA","P21AB","P21AC","P21C6","U0619","U061B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B"],U061B:["Lost Communication With Reductant Level Sensor C","Level sensor C is a third level input of a reductant system and exists only on layouts with more than one tank or measuring point. No manufacturer publicly documents U061B or explains which part carries the letter C. The code says that this third sensor's digital messages have stopped or keep arriving corrupted, so its reading is treated as unknown.",["Damaged pins, corrosion or water in the connector of sensor C","Harness to the additional tank or measuring point damaged","Internal failure of level sensor C"],["Malfunction indicator lamp","Implausible DEF quantity on the display"],2,1,["P21AD","P21AE","P21AF","P21B0","P21B1","U0619","U061A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ C"],U061C:["Lost Communication With Reductant Temperature Sensor A","Reductant temperature sensor A tells the controller how warm the diesel exhaust fluid is. That value decides when tank and line heaters must run, when dosing may begin after a cold start, and the concentration reading relies on it, since it is calculated from how fast sound travels through the fluid. On digital units the temperature element shares a housing with the level or quality measurement;",["Connector of the combined DEF tank sensor corroded or loose","Damaged data, supply or ground wire to the sensor","Sensor electronics failed, sometimes after freeze damage"],["Check engine light","DEF heater or SCR dosing starts late or not at all in cold weather","DEF quality reading unavailable"],2,1,["P2042","P2043","P2044","P2045","P2046","P205A","U061D","U0619"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A"],U061D:["Lost Communication With Reductant Temperature Sensor B","Temperature sensor B is a second temperature input of the reductant system. Where it sits depends on the maker: at another spot in the tank unit, in the pump or supply module, or along the dosing line. Volvo's truck tank sensor, for instance, measures temperature at two points on its circuit board, yet sends everything over one CAN connection and reports a lost connection as U02A2 rather than with this code.",["Wiring to the second temperature point (pump module or dosing line) damaged","Connector of temperature sensor B corroded or not latched","Temperature sensor B or the module housing it failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp","Line or pump heating may not work properly in frost"],2,1,["P2ACC","P2ACD","P2ACE","P2ACF","P2AD0","U061C","U02A2"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B"],U061E:["Lost Communication With Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Module","A battery isolation or voltage stabilization module separates a second 12 V battery or protected loads from the starter circuit, so that cranking during an automatic restart does not drag the voltage of the rest of the vehicle down. A GM patent (US 9,803,608) describes such an isolator built from MOSFET switches. U061E means the powertrain controller has lost contact with this module.",["Poor ground connection of the isolator circuit (Ford ground GD132)","Weak or deeply discharged auxiliary battery","Battery isolator module itself failed","Communication wire or connector to the module damaged"],["Powertrain malfunction (wrench) lamp on Ford trucks","Additional battery or isolator code such as P2C44"],2,0,["P2C43","P2C44","P2C45","P2C46","P2C47","P25FF","U041A"],""],U061F:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 1 Sensor 1","Many current exhaust temperature sensors are active: a thermocouple probe, often type N, feeds a small electronics module that turns the reading into SENT or CAN messages, as in the Sensience 22J sensor. U061F means valid messages from the bank 1, position 1 sensor (normally the most upstream one) have stopped.",["Sensor harness rubbing through on a bracket or subframe edge (Bentley V8)","Connector or module of the sensor damaged by exhaust heat","Internal fault of the active sensor that shuts its SENT output off","Missing 5 V supply or ground from the controller"],["Check engine or emission warning lamp","Further codes for the controller input or the second bank","Particulate filter regeneration may be postponed"],2,1,["P0544","P0545","P0546","P2080","P2081","P2478","U0620","U0621"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],U0620:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 1 Sensor 2","Sensor 2 on bank 1 is the next exhaust temperature measuring point downstream of sensor 1; on diesels it usually sits ahead of the particulate filter or the SCR catalyst, depending on how the maker numbers its sensors. U0620 is the lost-communication code for this point when it is a digital sensor: its frames have stopped, are too old, or its own diagnosis has switched the SENT output off.",["Signal, supply or ground wire of the sensor damaged near the exhaust","Moisture or corrosion in the underbody connector","Sensor electronics module failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp in the first trip on GM diesels","Diesel particulate filter or SCR warnings may follow"],2,1,["P2031","P2032","P2033","P2084","P2085","P2479","U061F","U0622"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],U0621:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 2 Sensor 1","U0621 mirrors U061F on bank 2: messages from the first exhaust temperature sensor of the second cylinder bank no longer reach the controller, so the code only appears on V engines or other layouts with two exhaust paths.",["Harness rubbed through on the subframe or a wheel-arch bracket","Electronics of the bank 2 sensor failed","Connector not latched or corroded"],["Emission warning lamp on","Code logged as intermittent first, later static"],2,1,["P0547","P0548","P0549","P2082","P2083","P247C","U061F","U0622"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],U0622:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 2 Sensor 2","U0622 covers the second exhaust temperature measuring point on bank 2 when it is a digital sensor that transmits its value as SENT or CAN messages. The controller sets it once those messages stop or keep failing their checks, for instance after a broken signal wire, a lost 5 V supply or a fault inside the sensor module, an electronics box that on active sensors must tolerate up to 140 °C beneath the car.",["Sensor wiring chafed or melted along the bank 2 exhaust","5 V supply or ground to the sensor interrupted","Heat-damaged electronics module of the sensor"],["Malfunction indicator lamp","Exhaust temperature for bank 2 sensor 2 missing in live data"],2,1,["P2034","P2035","P2036","P2086","P2087","P247D","U0620","U0621"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],U0623:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump A","Coolant pump A is an electric pump whose speed is set over a digital link, typically LIN, and which reports its status back. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG03A, 25OBDG04B) call it the auxiliary electric water pump and fail U0623 as Type B when its response frame is absent for 2.5 s although the LIN channel is ready and either the actuator relay or the powertrain relay is energised.",["Chafed or pinched LIN harness shared with other actuators (GM 23-NA-102)","Outdated hybrid or inverter controller software (Stellantis 08-399-25)","Blown fuse, relay or open supply/ground to the pump","Pump electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Reduced cabin heat or failed scheduled preconditioning on plug-in hybrids","Other LIN device codes (grille shutters, fans) stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2600","P2601","P2602","P2603","U0624","U062F","U0632","U0633"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A"],U0624:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump B","Some engines carry a second electric coolant pump, for instance one that keeps coolant moving through the turbocharger after shutdown or feeds a separate heater or low-temperature loop. Which pump is B is decided by the manufacturer. No manufacturer documents U0624 publicly; GM uses U0623 and U062F for its LIN pumps instead. The code means that pump B no longer answers on its data link.",["Signal, supply or ground wire to pump B damaged","Fuse or relay feeding pump B open","Pump electronics failed, sometimes after overheating or a seized rotor"],["Warning lamp","Reduced heater output or higher component temperatures after shutdown"],2,1,["P261A","P261B","P261C","P261D","U0623","U062F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B"],U0625:["Lost Communication With Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor Bank 1","Direct-injection engines increasingly use rail pressure sensors that send pressure, and sometimes fuel temperature, digitally via SENT. U0625 says the engine controller has lost this link for the bank 1 sensor. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG03A) set it when the SENT line stays low with at most four pulses received, in 400 of 500 samples taken every 6.25 ms, Type A;",["SENT signal wire shorted to ground or to voltage, or open","Fuel or oil contamination, corrosion or loose pins in the sensor connector","Rail pressure sensor electronics failed (on some engines only with the rail)","SENT input of the engine controller faulty"],["Check engine light in the first trip","Reduced power, rough running or hard starting","Further SENT codes such as U101B stored at the same time"],2,3,["P0190","P0191","P0192","P0193","P0194","U0665","U0670"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסילת דלק (בנק 1)"],U0626:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor A","Without a refrigerant pressure reading the climate controller cannot protect the compressor or schedule the condenser fan. When pressure sensor A digitizes its value itself and transmits it as a LIN or SENT frame, U0626 marks that the frame has stopped arriving; which point of the circuit gets the letter A is up to the manufacturer. No manufacturer documents U0626 publicly.",["LIN wire to the sensor pinched, chafed or cut (Audi documents this for G395)","Corroded, loose or pushed-back terminals at the sensor connector","Sensor supply voltage missing or ground intermittently open","Sensor electronics failed, often after moisture or refrigerant leaking at the sensor"],["A/C compressor stays off, no cooling","A/C fault message or flashing A/C indicator","Other LIN devices on the same line may also report no communication"],2,0,["U0627","U0628","U0605","P0530","P0531","P0532","P0533","P05E1"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ A"],U0627:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Temperature Sensor A","Refrigerant temperature matters most where a controller adjusts superheat itself, as with electronic expansion valves and heat pumps; it also guards against overheated discharge gas. U0627 is set once the digital temperature value from sensor A is no longer received. Many suppliers build temperature and pressure into one housing; Sensata, for example, offered such R744 sensors with LIN, PWM or analog output.",["Connector, LIN line or supply of a combined pressure/temperature sensor faulty","Temperature channel or sensor electronics failed","Climate or thermal controller no longer polls the sensor (software or LIN master fault)"],["Reduced cooling or heat-pump output","Heat-pump mode unavailable, auxiliary heater takes over","A/C fault message"],2,0,["U0626","U0629","U0605","P0EBC","P0EBD","P0EBE","P0EBF"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גז מזגן‏ A"],U0628:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B","A second pressure transducer appears mainly in heat pumps and CO2 (R744) systems, where both the low and the high side are measured to control efficiency and detect leaks; the Sensata R744 presentation lists heat-pump control and leak diagnosis among those uses. U0628 means that the digital pressure value from sensor B no longer reaches its controller.",["Damaged LIN, supply or ground wire in the branch to sensor B","Wet, corroded or loose connector at sensor B","Sensor B electronics failed"],["Heat pump does not heat, cabin heating relies on the auxiliary heater","Weak or no A/C cooling","A/C or thermal system warning message"],2,0,["U0626","U0629","P2515","P2516","P2517","P2518","P05E2","P2CD4"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ B"],U0629:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Temperature Sensor B","A second refrigerant temperature point is typical where an electronic expansion valve meters flow, for instance at the evaporator or chiller outlet, so that superheat can be calculated from temperature and pressure. U0629 is logged when the controller stops getting answers from temperature sensor B over its serial link.",["LIN line or connector at temperature sensor B open, shorted or corroded","Combined pressure/temperature unit B failed (often together with U0628)","Fuse or supply feed for sensor B open"],["Battery cooling or heat-pump mode unavailable","Uneven or reduced A/C performance"],2,0,["U0627","U0628","P0EC1","P0EC2","P0EC3","P0EC4"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גז מזגן‏ B"],U062A:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve Actuator A","Heat pumps and battery-cooling circuits need valves that redirect refrigerant, for example hot gas from the outer heat exchanger to an inner one when the system switches from cooling to heating. Suppliers such as Egelhof build these as motor-driven switching valves that replace two or more solenoid valves and are commanded digitally, partly via LIN. U062A is set when actuator A no longer answers its controller.",["LIN, supply or ground wire to valve actuator A damaged","Moisture or corrosion in the actuator connector","Actuator electronics failed","Software fault in the controlling module (reprogramming may be needed)"],["Switching between cooling and heat-pump mode fails","No cabin heat from the heat pump or no cooling in one branch","Thermal system warning, possibly reduced charging or drive power"],3,0,["U062B","U062C","U062D","U062E","P2611","P2612","P2613","P266F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ A"],U062B:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve Actuator B","Valve B is a further refrigerant switching point, for instance one that opens or closes a rear evaporator or a battery chiller path; the assignment of letters differs from maker to maker. U062B records that actuator B has stopped responding to its digital commands. While A still answers, the shared LIN master and the main feed are probably sound and the search narrows to B's branch.",["Wiring fault in the branch to valve actuator B","Loose or corroded connector at actuator B","Actuator B electronics or motor unit failed"],["One cooling branch (rear A/C or battery chiller) does not work","Several heat-pump modes unavailable at once with a multi-way valve","Thermal system warning message"],3,0,["U062A","U062C","U062D","P0EE2","P0EE3","P0EE4","P0EE5","P0EE6"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ B"],U062C:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve Actuator C","A third distribution valve only exists in elaborate thermal systems that combine cabin cooling, heat pump, dehumidification and battery conditioning in one refrigerant loop. U062C is stored when valve actuator C fails to reply on its serial line. In such layouts several actuators often hang on one LIN segment;",["Shared LIN segment, splice or supply feeding valve C damaged (often with U062D)","Connector at actuator C loose, wet or corroded","Actuator C electronics failed"],["A single heat-pump or dehumidifying mode no longer works","Windows fog more easily in heating mode","Climate system warning or reduced comfort without warning"],3,0,["U062A","U062B","U062D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ C"],U062D:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve Actuator D","Actuator D is the fourth refrigerant switching valve and appears only in loops with many separately controlled paths; because a single multi-way unit can replace up to four solenoid valves, many vehicles never use the letter D. U062D means the controller sent requests to valve D and got no valid answer within its expected schedule. No manufacturer documents U062D publicly.",["Supply or ground of actuator D missing (no current draw when commanded)","LIN line to actuator D open or shorted","Actuator D electronics failed"],["One refrigerant path cannot be opened or closed","Reduced heating or cooling in certain modes"],3,0,["U062A","U062B","U062C"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום חלוקת גז מזגן‏ D"],U062E:["Lost Communication With A/C Refrigerant Expansion Valve Actuator","An electronic expansion valve uses a geared or stepper motor to set the refrigerant flow into an evaporator or battery chiller, guided by pressure and temperature readings instead of a thermostatic bulb. Units such as Egelhof's EXV and KXV accept their target position over LIN and carry a position sensor, so they can also shut a branch completely. U062E is logged when that actuator stops answering.",["LIN, supply or ground wire to the expansion valve damaged","Connector at the valve wet or corroded (often near the evaporator or chiller)","Expansion valve motor electronics failed","Software fault in the thermal or powertrain controller"],["No cooling at the affected evaporator or chiller","Cooling-system warning, possibly reduced drive or charging power on electrified vehicles","Heat pump unavailable"],3,2,["U062A","U062B","U0626","U0627"],""],U062F:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump C","GM assigns coolant pump C to the pump of its low-temperature coolant loop, a separate circuit that runs well below engine temperature. The 2020 table 20OBDG04 fails U062F once LIN communication errors reach three counts, provided the bus itself is not already faulted (U1345), the pump is configured as present and run/crank voltage is at least 11 V.",["LIN wire, supply or ground to the low-temperature loop pump damaged","Corroded or loose pump connector","Pump electronics failed","LIN master in the engine controller faulty"],["Check engine light after two trips","Parts on the low-temperature loop may run hotter than normal"],2,1,["U0623","U0624","U0649","U0698","U0699"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C"],U0630:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4","Engines with split or multi-zone cooling may measure coolant temperature at more than three points, and a sensor that sends its value as a digital message instead of a resistance can be checked for silence. U0630 means the engine controller no longer receives such messages from coolant temperature sensor 4. No manufacturer documents U0630 publicly, and where sensor 4 sits is not standardised.",["Data, supply or ground wire to sensor 4 open or shorted","Corroded or loose sensor connector","Sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Cooling fan may run more than usual"],2,1,["U0631","P01E3","P2182","P0115","P0128"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4"],U0631:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5","Sensor 5 is the highest-numbered engine coolant temperature input in the J2012 list and is found only on engines that monitor many coolant zones, for example block, head, radiator outlet and separate loops. U0631 records that the controller has stopped receiving digital messages from that sensor. No manufacturer documents it publicly.",["Wiring to sensor 5 damaged (open, short, chafing)","Connector at sensor 5 corroded or not latched","Sensor 5 electronics failed or sending corrupt frames","Shared supply or data line fault (often with U0630)"],["Check engine light","Fan running more often or longer"],2,1,["U0630","P01E3","P2182","P0115","P2181"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5"],U0632:["Lost Communication With Fan 1","Many radiator fans now contain their own speed controller and take commands over LIN instead of relays. U0632 is set when fan 1 stops responding. GM (25OBDG03A, 25OBDG04B) fails it as Type B after 2.5 s without the fan's response frame and then suspends the fan speed checks P0494 and P30EE; the 2023/24 tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 allow three missed frames.",["Fan harness chafed or pinched near the radiator or plenum (Audi bulletins)","Fan power feed (fusible link) or ground open","Outdated software in the controller that runs the LIN bus (Mercedes PTCU)","Electronics in fan 1 failed (replaced as fan assembly)"],["Fan running continuously at full speed, loud","Check engine light and coolant warning message","On some Audi models limited engine speed or drive system fault message"],2,3,["U0633","U067C","P0480","P0691","P0692","P0494","P0495"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מאוורר‏ 1"],U0633:["Lost Communication With Fan 2","U0633 is the counterpart for a second LIN-controlled radiator fan. GM's 2025 table 25OBDG04B checks the frame CFM2_RSP and fails after 2.5 s of silence as Type B; 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 count three missing frames, and on those engines fans 3 and 4 have their own codes on another LIN line. In the Outlander PHEV 2023 Mitsubishi's fan 2 is the left-hand unit.",["Fan 2 harness rubbing on the frame rail or radiator support","Loose or corroded fan 2 connector","Power feed or ground of fan 2 interrupted","Fan 2 controller electronics failed"],["Remaining fan runs at full speed or noise from the fan area","Warning lamp; on Audi models limited performance and engine speed","Rising coolant temperature in slow traffic"],2,3,["U0632","U067D","P0481","P0693","P0694"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מאוורר‏ 2"],U0634:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor A","Liquid-cooled traction batteries check how warm the coolant is where it enters or leaves the pack to decide whether to cool or heat. Where that sensor is a digital node rather than a plain thermistor, the battery or thermal controller can detect when its messages stop, and U0634 records exactly that for sensor A. No manufacturer documents this code publicly;",["Data, supply or ground wire to sensor A damaged","Connector at the battery coolant line corroded or loose","Sensor A electronics failed","Battery or thermal management controller fault"],["Hybrid or battery warning lamp, on hybrids also the MIL","Reduced charging power or limited electric performance"],3,3,["U0635","P0C42","P0C43","P0C44","P0C45","P0C46","U0636","U0694"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U0635:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor B","Sensor B is the second battery coolant temperature point, commonly placed on the opposite side of the pack from sensor A so the controller can see how much heat the coolant picks up. U0635 means sensor B no longer delivers digital messages. No public manufacturer document uses the code.",["Wiring branch to sensor B open, shorted or chafed","Moisture or corrosion at the sensor B connector","Sensor B failed"],["Battery or hybrid system warning","Battery cooling runs more often or charging power is reduced"],3,3,["U0634","P0CD5","P0CD6","P0CD7","P0CD8","P0CD9","U0637"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U0636:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Control Valve A","Battery thermal loops use motor-driven valves to send coolant through the chiller, the heater or a bypass, or to link the battery loop with the drive unit circuit. Many of these valves have a small controller of their own: Hutchinson's rotary three-way valve for electric vehicles talks LIN, and Thomas offers its coolant valves with PWM, LIN or CAN control and an optional self-diagnosis.",["LIN, supply or ground wire to valve A damaged","Corroded or loose valve connector","Valve A actuator electronics failed","Thermal or battery controller software fault"],["Battery or hybrid system warning","Reduced fast-charging power or limited drive power when the battery is hot or cold","Cabin heating or cooling behaving differently"],3,3,["U0637","P0CDF","P0CE0","P0CE1","P0CE2","P0CE3","P0CE4","U0634"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U0637:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Control Valve B","Valve B is a second smart valve in the battery coolant loop, for example a mixing valve that blends chilled and warm coolant or a switch-over valve to the drive unit circuit. U0637 is set when valve B goes silent on its data link while the controller may still talk to valve A. No manufacturer documents U0637 publicly, so which function the letter B stands for varies.",["Wiring branch to valve B open, shorted or chafed","Valve B connector loose or corroded","Valve B actuator failed, sometimes after a jammed valve body"],["Battery or hybrid system warning","Limited charging or drive power in hot or cold weather"],3,3,["U0636","P0D1A","P0D1B","P0D1C","P0D1D","P0D1E","U0635"],"אבדה התקשורת עם שסתום בקרת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U0638:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor A","The coolant loop that serves the inverter and other high-voltage electronics needs its own temperature reading so the controller can size pump speed and decide when to derate. When sensor A on that loop is a bus node that sends its value digitally, for instance over LIN, the receiving controller notices when frames stop coming, and U0638 records that silence. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Data, supply or ground line to sensor A open, shorted or chafed","Corroded or loose connector at the electronics coolant line","Internal electronics of sensor A failed","Fault or outdated software in the controller that polls the sensor"],["Hybrid system warning, on hybrids usually the MIL as well","Reduced electric drive power, especially under load or in hot weather","Electronics coolant pump running continuously at high speed"],3,3,["U0639","U063A","P0CEE","P0CEF","P0CF0","P0CF1","P0CF2","P2D2A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ A"],U0639:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B","A second temperature point in the electronics cooling loop, labelled B, lets the controller compare inlet and outlet or watch a separate branch, and the pair is checked against each other by P2D2A. U0639 means that sensor B, read as a digital bus participant, has gone quiet while the bus itself is still working. No manufacturer documents U0639 publicly, so its exact mounting point stays vehicle-specific.",["Harness to sensor B damaged, for example near hoses or brackets","Moisture or bent pins in the sensor B connector","Sensor B itself no longer transmits","Bus master controller fault"],["Hybrid or EV system warning lamp","Correlation checks between the electronics coolant sensors disabled","Occasional power limitation on long climbs or fast charging"],3,3,["U0638","U063A","P2B20","P2B21","P2B22","P2B23","P2D2A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B"],U063A:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C","Sensor C is the third digitally connected temperature sensor in the cooling loop for the hybrid or EV power electronics. It is found where a system splits the loop further, for example to give a DC/DC converter or onboard charger its own reading. U063A is stored when its frames stop arriving. No public manufacturer documentation names this code or the location of sensor C.",["Open or chafed wire in the branch that feeds sensor C only","Sensor C connector unplugged after service work or corroded","Sensor C electronics defective"],["Hybrid or EV warning lamp","Possible reduction of charging or drive power"],3,3,["U0638","U0639","P2B24","P2B25","P2B26","P2B27"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C"],U063B:["Lost Communication With Coolant Bypass Valve Actuator A","Rotary coolant valves are often moved by a smart actuator that takes its target angle over LIN and reports back. U063B covers the case where actuator A no longer replies. Mercedes-Benz uses it in the drivetrain controller N127 (PTCU, CPC3) for the control valve of the high-temperature circuit;",["Outdated drivetrain controller software (Mercedes PTCU version 22A)","Damaged, chafed or corroded LIN wiring or intermediate connectors","Electronics in valve actuator A failed","Missing supply voltage or ground at the actuator"],["Check engine light with coolant service message","Radiator fan permanently running at full speed and noisy","Further LIN codes (fan, coolant pumps, exhaust flap) stored together"],2,1,["U063C","P0E75","P0E76","P0E77","P0E78","P0E79","P0E7A","U0615"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור‏ A"],U063C:["Lost Communication With Coolant Bypass Valve Actuator B","U063C is the counterpart for the second networked coolant bypass actuator, B. Stellantis lists it for the 3.0-litre Hurricane straight six: bulletin 18-071-26 (2025 Ram 1500) and bulletins 18-082-26 and 18-083-26 (2025 Jeep Wagoneer and Grand Wagoneer) name U063C next to the circuit and performance codes P0E7C to P0E7F of the same valve.",["Powertrain control module software (Stellantis 18-071-26, 18-082-26, 18-083-26)","Bus, supply or ground wire to actuator B damaged","Loose or corroded actuator B connector","Actuator B electronics failed"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Codes P0E7C to P0E7F for bypass valve B stored at the same time","Irregular warm-up or weak cabin heat"],2,1,["U063B","P0E7B","P0E7C","P0E7D","P0E7E","P0E7F","P0E80","U0616"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור‏ B"],U063D:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump A","The first electric pump of the power electronics loop, A, circulates coolant through the inverter, DC/DC converter and similar parts. Pumps of this class, such as Bosch's PAD2, take their speed command via PWM or LIN and run their own diagnosis; with LIN the controller also expects regular status replies. U063D is set when pump A stops answering. No manufacturer documents U063D publicly.",["Blown fuse or open supply/ground to electronics coolant pump A","LIN wire to the pump open, shorted or chafed","Pump electronics failed, often after running dry or overheating","Fault in the hybrid or thermal controller acting as bus master"],["Hybrid system warning and MIL","Reduced electric drive power or engine kept running on hybrids","Inverter or electronics overtemperature messages"],2,3,["U02BA","U02C1","P0CE9","P0CEA","P0CEB","P0CEC","P0CED","P2C68"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ A"],U063E:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve Actuator A","Exhaust heat recovery passes hot exhaust through a coolant heat exchanger after a cold start, so the engine and cabin warm up sooner; a flap later diverts the gas around it. When that flap's actuator is a LIN slave, losing it gives U063E.",["Actuator electronics damaged by heat near the exhaust","LIN or supply wiring under the vehicle damaged or corroded","Water ingress or corrosion in the actuator connector","Weak 12 V supply interrupting LIN communication"],["MIL after two drive cycles","Slower engine and cabin warm-up in cold weather","Engine runs longer on hybrids to reach operating temperature"],2,1,["U066C","P237C","P237D","P237E","P237F","P2C22","P2C23","P00E3"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום מעקף מחליף חום פליטה‏ A"],U063F:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor","The coolant flow control valve meters how much coolant passes through the engine, and its position sensor often transmits over SENT, a one-way digital protocol with a frame every few milliseconds. U063F flags the loss of that stream.",["Engine harness chafed through to the SENT, supply or ground wire (GM 21-NA-149)","Corroded or loose connector at the flow control valve","Position sensor electronics in the valve failed (usually replaced with the valve)","SENT input of the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light after two trips","Coolant temperature control less precise, slower warm-up or higher temperatures"],2,1,["P2B5D","P2B5E","P2B5F","P2B60","P2B6D","P2B58","P2B61","U0617"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע"],U0640:["Lost Communication With EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit","Many fuel tank pressure senders also measure the temperature of the vapor in the tank, and when such a sender reports digitally, typically over SENT, both values share one data stream. U0640 is stored when the engine controller no longer receives valid temperature data from this sensor. Despite the word circuit in the title, the fault concerns the digital link;",["Interference or chafing on the shared signal line of the tank pressure/temperature sender","Loose or corroded connector at the tank sender","Electronics of the sender failed (only if the code is stored permanently)","Engine controller software or input fault"],["Check engine light on","Often stored together with U0641","Evaporative system monitor does not complete"],2,1,["U0641","U0642","P2024","P2025","P2026","P2027","P2028"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מעגל חיישן טמפרטורת אדי דלק אדי דלק (EVAP)"],U0641:["Lost Communication With EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch Circuit A","Pressure sensor A is the main input for the evaporative leak test that CARB 1968.2 (e)(4) requires: with the system sealed, the controller follows how pressure in tank and canister rises or falls. Newer designs often use a relative pressure sensor with SENT output; Melexis' MLX90821, for example, spans about −0.06 to 0.26 bar in its SENT version and can add a media temperature.",["Electrical interference or damage on the sensor signal line","Connector at the tank or canister sensor loose, wet or corroded","Pressure sensor A itself no longer sends","Sensor supply or ground missing"],["MIL on","EVAP leak monitor not ready, possible inspection failure","No noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["U0640","U0642","P0450","P0451","P0452","P0453","P0454"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מעגל חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ A"],U0642:["Lost Communication With EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch Circuit B","A second EVAP pressure sensor, B, appears where one reading is not enough, for instance when tank and canister are separated by an isolation valve and each side needs its own value, as in sealed tanks of plug-in hybrids that see higher pressures. Which location is called B is up to the manufacturer. U0642 is the lost-communication code for this sensor when it reports digitally;",["Signal, supply or ground line to sensor B open or chafed","Corroded or unplugged connector at sensor B","Sensor B electronics failed","Receiving controller input or software fault"],["MIL on","EVAP monitor incomplete","On sealed tanks possibly a delayed fuel door release"],2,1,["U0641","U0640","P24D5","P24D6","P24D7","P24D8","P24D9"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מעגל חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ B"],U0643:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger A Temperature Sensor","This sensor reports a temperature at charger A, whose exact measuring point the J2012 title leaves open; depending on the design it can watch the compressor outlet or the hot side. GM's tables define charger A as the first one in the exhaust path on series layouts and the bank 1 charger on parallel ones.",["Wiring near the charger damaged by heat or chafing","Connector loose or corroded","Sensor electronics failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on","Reduced boost and power","Further boost-related codes stored"],2,3,["U0689","P2B6E","P2B6F","P2B70","P2B71","U0644"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ A"],U0644:["Lost Communication With Wastegate Position Sensor A","Pneumatic wastegates have largely given way to electric actuators, and these carry a position sensor so the controller knows how far the bypass flap around the turbine is open. GM reads that sensor on charger A over SENT and, in the 2025 table 25OBDG03B, stores U0644 when message faults appear or a frame is older than 3.13 ms in 10 out of 12 samples taken every 100 ms, with relay voltage of at least 11 V and the…",["Engine harness chafed at brackets or covers","Connector at the wastegate actuator loose or corroded","Position sensor in the actuator failed","Low supply voltage or poor ground"],["MIL on from the first trip","Reduced engine power, boost limited","Several other engine codes when the harness is damaged"],2,3,["U0674","P2AB7","P2AB8","P2AB9","P2B81","P2B93","U0643"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ A"],U0645:["Lost Communication With Active Air Dam Module","An active air dam is a motor-driven panel below the front bumper that drops at highway speed to cut drag and retracts for low speed or rough ground. Its small control module talks to the powertrain controller over a serial line; on the 2.7L F-150 Ford runs it on a LIN bus shared with the generator and the grille shutters. U0645 is logged once that module no longer replies.",["Air dam unit with built-in module failed (early Ram 1500 DT)","Air dam damaged by curb, snow or debris impact","Water or corrosion in the air dam connector","Shared LIN wire chafed to ground near the engine mount (Ford F-150 2.7L)"],["Air dam stays in one position","Check engine light on some trucks (Ram)","Charging system warning if the shared LIN line is shorted (Ford)"],2,1,["C0601","C0602","C0603","C0604","C0630","U0284","U0285"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מודול סכר אוויר פעיל"],U0646:["Lost Communication With Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A","In these titles, motor electronics stands for the power electronics that feed an electric drive motor in a hybrid or EV, and coolant pump A is the main electric pump of that loop. When it is commanded by LIN rather than a plain PWM wire, the controlling module can tell when the pump stops talking, which is what U0646 stores. No manufacturer documents U0646 publicly;",["Fuse, relay or power feed of motor electronics pump A interrupted","LIN line between controller and pump damaged","Integrated pump controller failed"],["Hybrid or EV system warning and MIL","Limited drive motor torque or power","Motor electronics over-temperature message, see P0A7C"],2,3,["U0647","U0648","P0A05","P0A06","P0A07","P0C73","P0E4F","P2D00"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ A"],U0647:["Lost Communication With Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B","Cars fitted with two or more drive units, or with separate loops for the motor and its inverter, may fit a second networked pump in the motor electronics circuit, called B. U0647 is logged when this pump no longer returns its status frames. Public manufacturer documentation for U0647 does not exist.",["Wiring branch or fuse that serves only pump B open","Pump B connector corroded or not fully seated","Pump B electronics failed"],["Hybrid or EV warning lamp, MIL on hybrids","Power limited on one drive unit"],2,3,["U0646","U0648","P0B38","P0B39","P0B3A","P0C74","P0E50","P2D05"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B"],U0648:["Lost Communication With Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C","U0648 belongs to a third digitally controlled pump in the motor electronics cooling, labelled C, which only more elaborate layouts carry, for example a generator inverter with its own loop. The fault means the pump has dropped off the bus. No carmaker publishes a description of U0648, so which component pump C cools has to be taken from the vehicle's own service information.",["Data or supply line to pump C damaged","Shared fuse or ground point of the pumps faulty (several pump codes at once)","Pump C controller failed"],["Hybrid or EV warning lamp","Reduced power from the electric machine cooled by pump C"],2,3,["U0646","U0647","P2BD4","P2BD5","P2BD6","P2BD7","P2D0A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C"],U0649:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump D","Coolant pump D is the fourth auxiliary electric pump in the generic lettering that runs from A (U0623) through B and C (U0624, U062F) to E (U0698). What D circulates is up to the manufacturer; GM, for example, assigns C to its low-temperature loop, while Mercedes uses the E code for a pump of its low-temperature circuit. U0649 is set when pump D, controlled over LIN or a similar link, no longer sends a response.",["LIN, supply or ground wire to pump D damaged","Corroded pump D connector","Pump D electronics failed","Controller acting as LIN master faulty or needing a software update"],["Warning lamp, depending on manufacturer the MIL","Components on the affected loop run warmer than normal"],2,1,["U0623","U0624","U062F","U0698","P2B66","P2B67","P2B68","P2B6A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D"],U064A:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor A","Battery management needs the pack current to count charge in and out and to judge state of charge and state of health. Many packs measure it with a self-contained sensor that sends its value over CAN; LEM's CAB series, for example, transmits on high-speed CAN at 500 kbit/s and is built for ASIL C.",["CAN, supply or ground wiring of sensor A inside or at the pack damaged","Current sensor A failed","Moisture or corrosion at the pack's low-voltage connector","Battery energy control module fault or software"],["Hybrid or EV battery warning, on hybrids also the MIL","Strongly reduced drive power or charging refused","Implausible state-of-charge display"],4,3,["U064B","U064C","P0ABF","P0AC0","P0AC1","P0AC2","P0AC3","P0B13"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U064B:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor B","Some packs carry a second current sensor, B, often a different measuring principle than A, so that the battery controller can cross-check the two through P0B13 and still have a value if one fails. U064B is stored when that second digital sensor goes silent. No manufacturer publishes U064B. With only one remaining sensor the controller loses its redundancy;",["Bus or supply wiring of sensor B damaged","Current sensor B failed","Missing or faulty CAN termination in the pack sub-network"],["Battery system warning lamp","Correlation check between the current sensors no longer possible","Possibly reduced charging or drive power"],4,3,["U064A","U064C","P0B0E","P0B0F","P0B10","P0B11","P0B12","P0B13"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U064C:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor C","A third pack current sensor, C, appears where a battery has parallel strings or a separate measuring point, for instance in a battery junction box, that each need their own current value. U064C means that this sensor no longer delivers its data frames to the battery controller. No manufacturer documents U064C or the place of sensor C publicly.",["Data or supply wiring of sensor C damaged","Current sensor C failed","Loose connector at the battery junction box"],["Battery warning lamp","Reduced power and slower charging"],4,3,["U064A","U064B","P2BE4","P2BE5","P2BE6","P2BE7"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C"],U064D:["Lost Communication With Trailer Brake Control Switch","Trucks with a factory trailer brake controller carry a dash switch with gain buttons and a manual slider that lets the driver apply only the trailer brakes. On current designs this switch is a small electronic unit that reports to the brake controller, which is why GM's 2024 campaign N242442100 for the 2022 Silverado and Sierra pairs a new switch with reprogramming of the cluster and the brake module.",["Trailer brake control switch electronics failed","Switch connector behind the dash trim loose or not seated","Damaged data or supply wire to the switch","Brake or cluster software not matched to a replaced switch"],["Service trailer brake message in the cluster","Gain buttons and manual slider have no effect","Electric trailer brakes not applied when braking"],2,0,["U0137","U0438"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מתג בקרת בלם גרור"],U064E:["Lost Communication With EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Bank 1","Many diesels steer recirculated exhaust around the EGR cooler while the engine is cold and through it once warm, using a bypass flap with its own position sensor. CARB 1968.2 (f)(6.2.5) requires the cooler system to be checked for poor cooling, and that check only makes sense if the controller knows the flap position. U064E is set when this sensor on bank 1 is a digital part and its data no longer arrives.",["Wiring to the cooler bypass actuator damaged by heat or vibration","Corroded or loose connector at the bypass actuator","Position sensor in the bypass actuator failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on","EGR cooler monitor not completed","Usually no change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2492","P2493","P2494","P2495","P2496","P24C4","U0651"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב מעקף מצנן EGR (בנק 1)"],U064F:["Lost Communication With Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor Bank 1","Diesel swirl flaps partly close one intake port per cylinder at low load so the charge spins and mixes better; a motor moves them and a sensor reports the angle. In GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B that sensor transmits by SENT, and U064F covers a missing or corrupt stream: an internal fault flag or message error, or position data not refreshed for over 6.25 ms with the line held steadily high or low.",["Oil or soot in the actuator connector, corroded pins","Position sensor in the swirl flap actuator failed","SENT signal wire chafed, open or shorted on the engine","Engine controller SENT input faulty"],["MIL after two trips with the fault","Swirl flaps left in default position, slightly rougher or smokier low-load running","Often no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P2008","P2009","P2010","P200A","P2014","P2015","P2016","P2017"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב מובילי סעפת יניקה (בנק 1)"],U0650:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Pressure Control Valve A Sensor/Switch","The exhaust pressure control valve is a throttle flap in the exhaust that diesels use to raise back pressure and exhaust temperature, for example during warm-up or filter regeneration. In GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B this flap is called ETV and reports its position by SENT.",["Wiring at the exhaust flap damaged by heat","Connector at the flap actuator corroded or loose","Position sensor in the flap actuator failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on from the first trip","Particulate filter regeneration delayed or blocked","Slower warm-up in cold weather"],2,1,["U067E","P0475","P0476","P048B","P048C","P048D","P048E","P048F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג שסתום בקרת לחץ פליטה‏ A"],U0651:["Lost Communication With EGR Sensor A","EGR sensors A to D are generic slots: a maker may assign them to valve position, pressure or another EGR measurement. In GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B, which has both a high-pressure and a low-pressure EGR loop, sensor A is the SENT position sensor of the high-pressure valve.",["SENT line to the EGR valve damaged by heat or chafing","EGR valve connector corroded or loose","Position sensor in the EGR valve failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on from the first trip","EGR switched off, possibly louder combustion","EGR monitor not ready"],2,1,["U0652","U0653","U0669","P0405","P0406","P0409","P046C","P046D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן EGR‏ A"],U0652:["Lost Communication With EGR Sensor B","U0652 covers a digital EGR sensor labelled B that has stopped delivering data. What B measures depends on the maker; it may be the position of a second valve or a pressure or temperature signal of the EGR path. No manufacturer documents U0652 publicly.",["Wiring to EGR sensor B open, shorted or heat-damaged","Connector at sensor B corroded or loose","Sensor B electronics failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on","EGR monitor incomplete","Possibly reduced EGR operation"],2,1,["U0651","U0653","U0669","P0486","P0407","P0408","P046E","P046F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן EGR‏ B"],U0653:["Lost Communication With EGR Sensor C","On GM's 2025 diesel with high- and low-pressure EGR (table 25OBDG04B), EGR sensor C is the SENT position sensor of the low-pressure valve, which as usual for such loops takes exhaust after the particulate filter and feeds it ahead of the compressor. Oddly, the table's text calls this valve the B position sensor while filing its codes under C.",["Wiring to the low-pressure EGR valve damaged near the exhaust","Connector corroded by road splash","Position sensor in the low-pressure EGR valve failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on from the first trip","Low-pressure EGR disabled, higher NOx","EGR monitor not ready"],2,1,["U0651","U0652","U0669","P044A","P044B","P044C","P044D","P044E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן EGR‏ C"],U0654:["Lost Communication With Diesel Intake Air Flow A Position Sensor","Diesel intake air flow valve A is the throttle ahead of the intake manifold: it creates the vacuum for high EGR rates, trims airflow for filter regeneration and shuts at switch-off. GM's 2025 diesel tables 25OBDG04A and 25OBDG04B read its angle by SENT and set U0654 when the data stop refreshing for more than 6.25 ms while the line is stuck low or high, a frame is faulty, or the counters freeze.",["Oil, soot or corrosion in the throttle body connector","SENT signal, supply or ground wire damaged","Position sensor in the throttle unit failed (usually replaced with the unit)","Engine controller SENT input fault"],["MIL in the first trip","EGR control restricted, particulate filter regeneration delayed","Engine may shake more at switch-off"],2,3,["U0655","P02E0","P02E1","P02E6","P02E7","P02E8","P02E9","P02EA"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ A"],U0655:["Lost Communication With Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor","Some diesels carry a second intake air flow valve, labelled B; which flap gets that letter depends on the engine layout and the maker. When its angle sensor is a digital SENT unit, U0655 reports that the engine controller no longer receives usable position frames from it. No manufacturer documents this code in public.",["Contaminated or loose connector at throttle unit B","Signal, supply or ground wire to sensor B damaged","Digital position sensor of valve B failed","Engine controller input fault"],["Check engine light","Particulate filter regeneration postponed or blocked","Little change in drivability in many cases"],2,3,["U0654","P2390","P2391","P2396","P2397","P2398","P2399","P239A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב זרימת אוויר יניקה דיזל‏ B"],U0656:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control A Position Sensor","On a variable geometry turbocharger the boost control position sensor reports where the guide vanes stand, and the controller needs that feedback to regulate boost and to check, as CARB 1968.2 (f)(7.2.3) asks, that the vanes reach their target in time.",["SENT, supply or ground line to the VGT actuator damaged","Connector at the actuator exposed to heat, oil or water","Position sensor or electronics in the VGT actuator failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["MIL on","Limp mode with clearly reduced power","Boost control codes stored at the same time"],3,3,["U02B0","P2562","P2563","P2564","P2565","P2566","P2598","P2599"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב בקרת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ A"],U0657:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Position Sensor","The bypass valve meant here sits on the intake side: on turbocharged petrol engines it lets compressed air recirculate when the throttle shuts, and on supercharged engines it routes air around the blower at light load. When the valve is electrically driven and reports its position digitally, U0657 marks that the position data from valve A has stopped arriving.",["Wiring to the bypass valve open, shorted or chafed","Loose or corroded valve connector","Position sensor in the valve failed","Engine controller input fault"],["MIL on","Less boost or hesitant throttle response","Unusual whoosh or flutter when lifting off"],2,1,["U066B","P2BBB","P2BBC","P2BBD","P2BBE","U0656"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A"],U0658:["Lost Communication With Windshield Temperature Sensor","To keep the glass clear before it mists, an automatic climate system can compare the temperature of the inner windshield surface with the cabin air's dew point right in front of it. Suppliers such as Sensirion (SAAF) and ScioSense (WSS2) build this into one small module at the mirror base that computes the dew point itself and reports over LIN at 19.2 kBd.",["Sensor not clipped back, unplugged or without glass contact after windshield replacement","Loose or damaged plug or LIN wire at the mirror base or headliner","Electronics of the humidity and glass temperature module failed","Code logged in a wake-up phase such as remote start without a real fault"],["Windshield fogs before the climate system responds","Automatic defog or anti-fog function inactive or less effective","Other sensors on the same mirror-base LIN line may also be missing"],1,0,["U0164","U065D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת שמשה קדמית"],U0659:["Lost Communication With Left Front Temperature Actuator","In a two-zone system the left front temperature actuator turns the blend door that sets how much of the air for the left side passes the heater core. As a smart LIN node it takes position requests from the climate master and replies with its state.",["Electronics of the left temperature actuator failed","LIN, supply or ground wire to the actuator open or chafed under the dash","Actuator plug not latched after dash or footwell work","Configuration or software fault in the module that polls the actuator"],["Left zone stuck hot or cold regardless of the setting","Check engine light on GM vehicles that list the code as Type B","Climate display may show a fault or ignore left temperature changes"],2,1,["U065A","U065B","U0164","B0168"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה קדמית שמאלית"],U065A:["Lost Communication With Right Front Temperature Actuator","The right front temperature actuator only exists where the right-hand front seat gets its own blend door, as in dual-zone systems; single-zone cars move one door for both sides and never run this check. GM lists U065A next to U0659 in its 2025 BCM tables, watching the frame AHDA05_Rsp with the same 11.5 s limit and Type B rating;",["Right temperature actuator electronics or motor failed","Wire to the actuator damaged behind the glovebox or console side panel","Climate module configured for the wrong number of zones after replacement"],["Passenger side blows hot or cold no matter what is selected","Right temperature setting has no effect while the left side works","MIL possible on GM models with the code rated Type B"],2,1,["U0659","U065C","U0164","B0168"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה קדמית ימנית"],U065B:["Lost Communication With Left Front Mode Actuator","The mode actuator decides where the air leaves the dash: face vents, footwell or windshield. A separate left front unit points to a layout where each front zone has its own distribution door; when the climate master gets no reply from it over LIN, U065B is stored. No maker documents this code publicly.",["Left mode actuator electronics failed","Break or short on the LIN branch to the left mode actuator","Shared actuator supply or ground missing"],["Left outlets keep blowing at face, floor or glass regardless of mode","Defrost selection does not move air to the left part of the windshield","Climate fault message or flashing mode indicator"],2,0,["U065C","U0659","U0164","B0150","B0170"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל מצב קדמי שמאלי"],U065C:["Lost Communication With Right Front Mode Actuator","A right front mode actuator lets the passenger side choose its own outlets, or in some designs close its share of the air altogether; Denso's US 2020/0189351 describes a passenger-side door driven by its own actuator so that only the driver is served. U065C means the climate master can no longer reach that right-hand unit over LIN. No maker publishes the code, so detection time and fallback depend on the vehicle.",["Right mode actuator internal fault","Connector on the passenger side of the HVAC case loose or wet","Damaged LIN branch toward the passenger side"],["Passenger outlets ignore mode changes","Little or no airflow on the passenger side","Uneven comfort between driver and passenger"],2,0,["U065B","U065A","U0164","B0150"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל מצב קדמי ימני"],U065D:["Lost Communication With Air Intake Actuator","The air intake actuator swings the inlet door between outside air and cabin air. Modern controllers move it on their own: Ford's SSM 51726 notes that the 2021-23 Bronco opens the inlet door to about half every 30 to 60 minutes in recirculation to refresh the cabin, and onsemi's TND416 describes stepper-driven recirculation flaps that find their end stop by stall detection and save compressor energy by reusing cooled…",["Inlet door actuator electronics failed","Water ingress at the blower housing reaching the actuator plug","LIN or supply wire to the inlet actuator damaged"],["Recirculation button has no effect","Windows fog quickly when the door is stuck on recirculation","Outside smells enter the cabin when it is stuck on fresh air"],2,0,["U065E","U0658","U0164","B0173","B0175"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל יניקת אוויר"],U065E:["Lost Communication With Ram Air Actuator","At speed, the wind pushes extra outside air through the cowl inlet into the climate housing. Some vehicles therefore fit the fresh-air path with a motorised ram air flap that narrows the opening as dynamic pressure rises, so airflow and noise stay steady; Behr's US 5,645,479 nests it with the recirculation flap, and Daimler's DE 10 2010 025 623 drives it through a non-linear linkage for fine throttling near closed.",["Ram air flap actuator electronics failed","Moisture or debris from the cowl reaching the actuator connector","LIN wire to the ram air actuator chafed or disconnected"],["Airflow rises noticeably with road speed","Air rush noise from the vents at high speed","Weak airflow at low speed if the flap stopped nearly closed"],2,0,["U065D","U0164","B0173"],""],U065F:["Lost Communication With Left Rear Temperature Actuator A","Vehicles with a separately controlled rear climate zone need their own temperature doors for the rear outlets, and in a split rear system the left side may use two of them, labelled A and B. Hanon's US 11,305,608 shows why two can be needed: one door ahead of the heater core and a second behind it mixing warm air into the rear cold-air duct. Which door counts as A is up to the maker.",["Software timing between modules logs a false history code (GM)","Left rear temperature actuator A failed","Rear HVAC harness or connector damaged in the floor or rear quarter"],["Often none when the code is only stored as history","Rear left air stays hot or cold","Rear temperature control has no effect on the left"],3,0,["U0660","U0661","U0663","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה אחורית שמאלית‏ A"],U0660:["Lost Communication With Left Rear Temperature Actuator B","Temperature actuator B is the second door for the same rear left zone that A serves. Where a rear zone uses two doors, one typically sets the split between cold and heated air and the other trims the mix further downstream, like the downstream rear door in Hanon's US 11,305,608; makers do not publish which letter goes to which. U0660 means the climate master gets no answer from actuator B over its LIN line.",["Actuator B electronics or motor failed","Fault in the wiring branch or plug that only actuator B uses","Replacement actuator not assigned or calibrated by the scan tool"],["Rear left temperature drifts or overshoots the set value","Rear left zone reacts slowly to temperature changes"],3,0,["U065F","U0662","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה אחורית שמאלית‏ B"],U0661:["Lost Communication With Right Rear Temperature Actuator A","A right rear temperature actuator is only fitted where the rear seats are split into left and right climate zones, as in four-zone systems of large sedans, SUVs and vans. Actuator A on the right is the counterpart of U065F on the left, so when this code is stored the passenger behind the front passenger seat loses temperature control while the left rear zone still works. No maker documents U0661 publicly;",["Right rear temperature actuator A failed","Actuator plug in the right rear duct area loose or corroded","Shared rear LIN segment faulty (then usually several rear codes)"],["Right rear zone stays at one temperature","Rear right temperature buttons have no effect","Left rear zone continues to work normally"],3,0,["U0662","U065F","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה אחורית ימנית‏ A"],U0662:["Lost Communication With Right Rear Temperature Actuator B","With four rear temperature actuators, A and B on each side, plus front units, a climate system may run many look-alike motors on LIN, where one master serves up to 15 slaves. Identical parts must be told apart, either by part variant or by position detection along a daisy chain, as the LIN article explains.",["Replacement or swapped actuator B without the correct LIN address","Actuator B electronics failed","Open supply, ground or LIN pin at actuator B"],["Right rear temperature imprecise or slow to settle","Code appears right after an actuator was replaced"],3,0,["U0661","U0660","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל טמפרטורה אחורית ימנית‏ B"],U0663:["Lost Communication With Rear Mode Actuator","The rear mode actuator steers rear-seat air between upper outlets, such as console or roof vents, and the rear footwell. Hanon's US 11,305,608 shows a dome-shaped rear mode door doing exactly this between console vent and rear floor vent.",["Software timing in the body or climate module storing a false history code (GM)","Rear mode actuator failed","Harness to the rear HVAC unit or console damaged"],["No symptom if the code is only stored as history","Rear air stuck at the console or roof vents or at the floor","Rear mode button has no effect"],3,0,["U0664","U065F","U065B","U0164"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל מצב אחורי"],U0664:["Lost Communication With Rear HVAC Air Cutoff Actuator","Some climate units carry a door that opens or shuts the whole air supply to the rear seats, so the system can send everything forward when nobody sits in the back or when the front needs full airflow. Hanon's US 11,305,608 places such an on-off door on the rear cold-air passage, and Denso's US 2020/0189351 moves its rear airflow door to feed or close the rear vent and heat outlets.",["Rear cutoff door actuator failed","Actuator plug at the rear outlet of the HVAC case not seated","LIN or supply wire to the cutoff actuator damaged"],["No air at the rear outlets","Rear outlets keep blowing although rear climate is off","Reduced airflow at the front during maximum cooling or defrost"],3,0,["U0663","U0164"],""],U0665:["Lost Communication With Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor Bank 2","Engines with one fuel rail per cylinder bank may give each rail its own pressure sensor, and newer ones send the reading digitally via SENT. U0665 says the controller has lost the bank 2 sensor's data. GM's 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 tables pair it with GM's own code U101C: path 1 trips when the signal line stays at high level, path 2 when it stays low, each after 0.5 s and within one trip.",["Bank 2 sensor signal wire open or shorted to ground or voltage","Fuel-soaked, corroded or loose sensor connector","Rail pressure sensor electronics on bank 2 failed","Engine controller SENT input faulty"],["Check engine light after one trip","Reduced power, hesitation or rough running","GM-specific code U101C stored alongside"],2,3,["U0625","P01BE","P01BF","P01C0","P01C1","P01C2"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסילת דלק (בנק 2)"],U0666:["Lost Communication With Reductant Pressure Sensor","The reductant pressure sensor watches the DEF line between the supply pump and the dosing valve. Bosch, for instance, offers its supply module with or without such a sensor; with it, the pump only runs when dosing is requested, the line stays pressurised through stop-start phases and is purged at key-off against freezing.",["DEF crystals or corrosion in the supply module connector","Harness to the tank or pump module damaged","Pressure sensor failed (often only with the pump module)","Fault in the dosing or engine control unit input"],["DEF system warning in the cluster","Dosing stopped, higher NOx output","Check engine light possible"],2,3,["P204A","P204B","P204C","P204D","P204E","P20E8","P20E9","U0619"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ אוריאה (AdBlue)"],U0667:["Lost Communication With Engine Oil Temperature Sensor A","Engine oil temperature feeds warm-up strategies, injection and protection functions, and on recent engines the sensor sends it digitally over SENT. U0667 says that link has failed. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary lists the code in its group of SENT sensor monitors, together with the oil pressure sensor (U0600), the mass air flow sensor and others: it sets when the SENT sensor reports a communication error, checked…",["Oil wicking into the sensor connector","Sensor signal, 5 V supply or ground wire damaged","Digital oil temperature sensor failed","Engine controller SENT input faulty"],["Check engine light","P0195 stored at the same time","Oil temperature reading missing in the cluster or scan tool"],1,1,["P0195","P0196","P0197","P0198","P0199","U0600","U0668"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת שמן מנוע‏ A"],U0668:["Lost Communication With Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit","Despite the word circuit in its name, U0668 concerns the data link to the oil level sensor, not a voltage fault. Sensors in the sump measure the oil height either thermally or by ultrasound; Hella's PULS type packs an ultrasonic transducer, a temperature sensor and an ASIC into one module that sends its result to the engine controller over a single signal line, and loss of supply or ground is one listed failure…",["Missing supply voltage or ground at the sensor","Sensor electronics failed or oil inside the housing","Corroded or damaged connector or harness at the oil pan","Receiving control unit input faulty"],["Oil level warning or service message in the display","Oil level reading unavailable"],1,0,["P250A","P250B","P250C","P250D","P250E","P250F","P252F","U0667"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מעגל חיישן מפלס שמן מנוע"],U0669:["Lost Communication With EGR Sensor D","Two makers document sensor D as an EGR pressure sensor with SENT output. Ford's 2024–2025 gasoline OBD summary lists U0669 as EGR sensor D communication for the SENT EGR pressure sensor it calls DPFE (range 0.1 to 408.8 kPa): it is checked continuously while the EGR monitor runs and flags a fault when the sensor stops talking or sends corrupt data, after about 5 seconds.",["SENT, supply or ground line to the EGR pressure sensor damaged","Connector at the pressure sensor corroded or loose","EGR pressure sensor electronics failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["MIL on","EGR flow monitor does not run","Sometimes rough idle or pinging when EGR is shut off"],2,1,["U066A","U0653","U0651","P2380","P2381","P2382","P2383","P2384"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן EGR‏ D"],U066A:["Lost Communication With EGR Sensor E","EGR sensors A to E are open slots in the code set: each maker decides whether a slot carries a valve position, a pressure or a differential pressure in the recirculation path. U066A means the engine controller no longer gets usable digital frames from the device it calls sensor E, typically a SENT part. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Signal, supply or ground wire to EGR sensor E damaged by heat or chafing","Connector at the sensor loose, corroded or contaminated with soot","Sensor electronics no longer transmitting","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","EGR switched off or limited, sometimes harsher combustion noise","EGR readiness monitor not complete"],2,1,["U0669","U0651","U0653","P2385","P2386","P2387","P2388","P2389"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן EGR‏ E"],U066B:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Position Sensor","When the throttle snaps shut, a compressor bypass valve lets boosted air recirculate to the inlet side instead of surging against the closed plate. Engines with two chargers or two compressor stages can carry a second such valve, and if its electric actuator reports the opening angle as a digital message, U066B means the engine controller no longer gets valid position frames from valve B.",["Signal, supply or ground wire to the bypass valve B actuator damaged","Connector at the valve loose, corroded or heat-damaged near the turbo","Position sensor electronics in the valve actuator failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Boost limited, reduced power","Compressor surge noise when lifting off the throttle"],2,3,["U0657","P2C2A","P2C2B","P2C2C","P00C0","P00C4","P2C29"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B"],U066C:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve Actuator B","Exhaust heat recovery sends hot gas through a coolant heat exchanger after a cold start and later steers it past; the steering is done by bypass flaps. Actuator B is the second such flap, present only where the layout has two paths or stages. U066C is logged once that actuator, linked over a serial bus such as LIN, stops answering the controller. No maker has published a definition for this code.",["Actuator B electronics damaged by exhaust heat","LIN, supply or ground wire under the vehicle damaged","Water or salt corrosion in the actuator connector","Low supply voltage during the check"],["Check engine light, on some systems only after two drive cycles","Engine and cabin heater warm up more slowly","Hybrid engine runs longer to reach temperature"],2,1,["U063E","P23A2","P23A3","P23A4","P23A5","P23A6","P23A7","P23A8"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מפעיל שסתום מעקף מחליף חום פליטה‏ B"],U066D:["Lost Communication With Charge Air Cooler Temperature Sensor Bank 1","The temperature of the charge air behind the intercooler tells the engine controller how dense the intake charge is and whether the cooler still removes enough heat; CARB lists charge air cooler temperature in the data diesel vehicles must report and requires an undercooling monitor in (f)(7.2.4).",["Signal or supply wire to the charge air sensor open or chafed","Oily or corroded connector at the charge air pipe","Digital sensor (often combined with boost pressure) failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Slightly reduced power at high load","Often no noticeable change in normal driving"],1,1,["U066E","P007A","P007B","P007C","P007D","P007E","P007F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) (בנק 1)"],U066E:["Lost Communication With Charge Air Cooler Temperature Sensor Bank 2","A bank 2 charge air temperature only exists on V or boxer engines that run one turbocharger and one intercooler per cylinder bank. There the controller can compare both sides, and a mismatch belongs to P007F, the bank 1/bank 2 correlation code. U066E is the digital-link failure for the bank 2 sensor: its frames are missing or unusable, so that comparison and any per-bank boost correction lose their input.",["Wiring to the bank 2 charge air sensor damaged, often routed near the hot side","Connector at the bank 2 charge air pipe loose or oily","Bank 2 sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Possible additional bank correlation code (P007F)","Mostly unchanged driving behaviour"],1,1,["U066D","P00A0","P00A1","P00A2","P00A3","P00A4","P007F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) (בנק 2)"],U066F:["Lost Communication With Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor","The low-pressure side of a direct-injection fuel system runs from the tank pump to the high-pressure pump, and a sensor there lets the controller regulate the lift pump. If that sensor transmits a digital value, for example over SENT, U066F records that its messages have stopped. None of the public manufacturer documents uses the code.",["Signal, supply or ground wire to the low-pressure sensor damaged","Connector at the sensor or fuel line corroded or not latched","Sensor electronics failed and no longer transmit","Receiving input or software of the engine or pump control module faulty"],["Check engine light","Longer cranking or hard starting","Hesitation or power loss under heavy load"],2,3,["U0604","U0625","P2539","P2540","P2541","P2542","P2543","P008A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מערכת דלק לחץ נמוך"],U0670:["Lost Communication With Fuel Temperature Sensor A","GM's 2025 direct-injection engines measure fuel temperature in the high-pressure rail with digital SENT sensors, and sensor 1 is the one GM files under U0670. The test counts pulses on the signal wire: if the line sits permanently high and four or fewer pulses arrive (25OBDG03A; 40 or fewer in 25OBDG03B), a sample fails, and 400 bad samples in a window of 500, one every 6.25 ms, set the code;",["SENT signal wire to sensor A shorted or open","Connector at the fuel rail loose or contaminated","Fuel temperature sensor A internally failed","SENT receiver in the engine controller faulty"],["Check engine light from the first trip","Usually no noticeable change in driving","Occasionally rougher hot restarts"],2,1,["U0671","U0625","P0180","P0181","P0182","P0183","P0184"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת דלק‏ A"],U0671:["Lost Communication With Fuel Temperature Sensor B","Sensor B is the second SENT temperature sensor in GM's high-pressure fuel rail (sensor 2 in 25OBDG03A and 25OBDG03B). Its link test mirrors that of sensor A, line stuck high with too few pulses, 400 of 500 samples at 6.25 ms, Type A.",["Signal wire of sensor B chafed, shorted or open","Shared 5 V supply or ground of both rail sensors faulty","Fuel temperature sensor B defective","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Sensor comparison and range checks of sensor B not completed","Often no drivability complaint"],2,1,["U0670","U0625","P0185","P0186","P0187","P0188","P0189"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת דלק‏ B"],U0672:["Lost Communication With Engine Coolant Pump","GM's 2.0 L LSY and 2.7 L L3B four-cylinders circulate coolant with an electric main pump that the engine controller commands over LIN. U0672 sets when the pump's response frame MWP_Rsp is missing for at least 250 ms (25OBDG03B; same logic in 19OBDG03D for the L3B) once the LIN channel is up, the relay is powered and battery voltage exceeds 11 V; as a Type A fault it turns the MIL on at once.",["Poor terminal tension, crimp or lock at the electric pump connector","LIN, supply or ground wire to the pump chafed or contaminated","Pump electronics or motor failed","Pump relay or fuse supplying the pump faulty"],["Check engine light immediately","Rising coolant temperature or overheating warning","Weak cabin heating","Reduced engine power to protect the engine"],2,3,["U019F","U04A0","U0623","P26CA","P26CB","P2B85","P2BA2"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע"],U0673:["Lost Communication With Ion Sense Module","After each spark, a small bias voltage across the plug gap lets the ignition system measure the current carried by ions in the burning mixture; Ford's patent US20170030322A1 shows such an ion sensing module passing this signal to the controller for combustion and knock assessment. U0673 means the engine controller no longer hears from that module.",["Powertrain controller software (Stellantis Hurricane engines)","Bus, supply or ground wiring of the ion sense module faulty","Ion sense module internally failed"],["Check engine light","Other stored codes from the same software issue","Usually no change in how the engine runs"],1,1,["U0901","U0353","P28C0","P28C1","P28C2","P034C","P0300"],""],U0674:["Lost Communication With Wastegate Position Sensor B","Electric wastegate actuators need position feedback so the controller can hold the turbine bypass at the commanded opening. On twin-turbo engines the second charger gets its own sensor, and U0674 says the digital frames from that sensor B have stopped or are corrupt. GM uses the sibling U0644 for wastegate A over SENT (25OBDG03B, Type A), yet none of the GM tables lists U0674.",["Wiring to the wastegate B actuator heat-damaged or chafed","Actuator connector loose or corroded","Position sensor inside the actuator failed","Weak supply voltage or poor ground"],["Check engine light","Reduced power, boost limited on one charger","Sluggish response under load"],2,3,["U0644","P2ABA","P2ABB","P2ABC","P2B82","P2B94"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ B"],U0675:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A","A speed sensor in the bearing or compressor housing lets the controller watch how fast the turbocharger rotor spins, mainly to keep it below its overspeed limit; a BorgWarner patent (US9353760B2) describes such a sensor and gives that reason, and CARB names turbocharger/turbine speed among the data diesel vehicles must output. Classic sensors send a pulse train whose faults are P2578 to P2582.",["Sensor wiring near the turbocharger heat-damaged or broken","Connector loose, oily or corroded","Speed sensor electronics failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Boost and power limited","Noticeably weaker acceleration at higher loads"],2,3,["P2578","P2579","P2580","P2581","P2582"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מהירות מגדש‏ A"],U0676:["Lost Communication With Fuel Level Sensor A","Fuel level sensor A is the main tank sender. Usually it is a float-driven resistor read as a voltage, and U0676 only applies where the sender itself reports digitally and its messages stop. Public documentation of this code from any manufacturer is lacking.",["Wiring at the tank or fuel pump flange damaged or corroded","Electronics of the level sender failed","Module that reads or forwards the level faulty","Connector under the vehicle not latched or water-damaged"],["Fuel gauge reads empty, full or freezes","Range display missing or wrong","Check engine light, EVAP readiness not set"],2,1,["U0677","U0678","P0460","P0461","P0462","P0463","P25B0"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס דלק‏ A"],U0677:["Lost Communication With Fuel Level Sensor B","A second level sender is needed when a tank has two chambers, as in saddle tanks that straddle the driveshaft, or when a vehicle carries a second tank. GM's 25OBDG03B calls it sensor 2 of the secondary tank, used on vehicles with two senders and a mechanical transfer pump; its circuit checks fail below 10 % or above 60 % of the 5 V range in 40 of 50 samples (P2067/P2068, Type B).",["Wiring to the secondary-chamber sender damaged","Sender B electronics failed","Connector at the secondary flange corroded","Receiving module or software faulty"],["Gauge drops suddenly or never shows full","Range estimate inaccurate","Check engine light"],2,1,["U0676","U0678","P2065","P2066","P2067","P2068","P25B1"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס דלק‏ B"],U0678:["Lost Communication With Fuel Level Sensor C","A third level sender only makes sense where the fuel volume is split further, for example a tank with three chambers or a main tank plus an auxiliary one. U0678 would be stored when such a sender C reports its value as a message and that message is lost.",["Wiring to sender C damaged or corroded","Sender C electronics failed","Module receiving the level data faulty"],["Gauge or range wrong when the third chamber is involved","Check engine light","EVAP readiness not completed"],2,1,["U0676","U0677","P25D7","P25D8","P25D9","P25DA","P25DC"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן מפלס דלק‏ C"],U0679:["Lost Communication With Transmission Fluid Pressure Sensor/Switch A","Automatic transmissions measure hydraulic pressure to confirm that a clutch or pulley really received the pressure the controller asked for. Which sensor is A varies: Ford's 2024 summary calls the sensors of its 10R60/10R80 and 8F units TFP A and B, analog with 0.5 to 4.5 V for 0 to 2,500 kPa, and sets P0841 when the reading sticks although the clutch still applies and releases.",["Transmission internal harness or lead frame to sensor A damaged","Transmission case connector leaking oil or corroded","Pressure sensor A electronics failed","Transmission control module input or software fault"],["Harsh or delayed shifts","Transmission stays in a fixed gear","Check engine or transmission warning light"],3,3,["U067A","P0840","P0841","P0842","P0843","P0844"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן תיבה‏ A"],U067A:["Lost Communication With Transmission Fluid Pressure Sensor/Switch B","Sensor B is the second pressure measuring point. In GM's CVT table 25OBDG03A it reads the secondary pulley, whose pressure sets the clamping force on the belt; its plausibility check runs only above 1,200 rpm with line pressure over 1,000 kPa and a secondary command above 500 kPa. In GM's 24OBDG07 B belongs to clutch 2, fed from its own reference VREF2, and Ford's 2024 summary checks TFP B with P0846 to P0848.",["Internal wiring to sensor B damaged","Pressure sensor B failed","Separate sensor supply for B faulty","Transmission controller fault"],["Firm shifts or engagement","Reduced engine torque, limp mode","Warning light on"],3,3,["U0679","P0845","P0846","P0847","P0848","P0849"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן תיבה‏ B"],U067B:["Lost Communication With Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor","Parallel hybrids put a clutch between engine and electric motor so the car can drive electrically with the engine stopped. Many close it hydraulically, and a pressure sensor confirms the clamping: in Ford's 10R80 MHT hybrid transmission, as Gears Magazine explains, the auxiliary pump closes the clutch and a pressure sensor watches that supply.",["Wiring or connector of the clutch pressure sensor damaged","Pressure sensor electronics failed","Transmission or hybrid controller input or software fault"],["Hybrid system warning, electric driving unavailable","Engine runs continuously or starts roughly","Check engine light"],3,3,["U02AA","U05AB","P28F1","P28F2","P28F3","P28F4","P28F5"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע"],U067C:["Lost Communication With Fan 3","Some engines need a third electric cooling fan, for instance for a charge-air or auxiliary radiator, and LIN lets each fan carry its own speed electronics. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B uses U067C for cooling fan 3: the response frame CFM3_Rsp must be missing for at least 2,437.5 ms, the LIN channel enabled and battery voltage above 11 V; the code is Type B, so the MIL lights after two trips.",["LIN wire to fan 3 chafed or open","High-current supply, fuse or ground of fan 3 faulty","Fan 3 controller electronics failed","Fan connector corroded by road spray"],["Check engine light after two trips","High coolant or charge-air temperature at low speed or when towing","Fan 3 silent or running constantly"],2,3,["U067D","U0632","U0633","P0482","P0695","P0696","P2CBB","P2CBC"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מאוורר‏ 3"],U067D:["Lost Communication With Fan 4","U067D is meant for a fourth cooling fan with its own network interface that has stopped answering. Four electrically commanded fans are rare. No manufacturer documents U067D publicly: GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B ends at fan 3, and the engines in GM's 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07, which do have a fourth LIN fan, report it with the GM-specific code U112B once its response frame ECM_LIN3_CFM4_RSP has been missed three…",["Bus wire to fan 4 damaged","Fan 4 power feed or ground interrupted","Fan 4 electronics or motor failed"],["Temperature climbs in traffic or under heavy load","Warning light depending on manufacturer","Fan 4 does not run"],2,3,["U067C","U0632","U0633","P2C3E","P2C3F","P2C40","P2C42"],"אבדה התקשורת עם מאוורר‏ 4"],U067E:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Pressure Control Valve B Sensor/Switch","An exhaust pressure control valve is a flap in the exhaust that diesels close partly to raise back pressure, which speeds warm-up and helps reach filter regeneration temperatures. Valve B is a second flap of this kind, and U067E concerns its position sensor or switch when that reports digitally: the controller has lost its messages. Public manufacturer documentation for U067E is lacking.",["Sensor wiring at valve B damaged by exhaust heat","Connector at valve B corroded or loose","Position sensor in the valve B unit failed","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Particulate filter regeneration delayed or not started","Longer warm-up in cold weather"],2,1,["U0650","P049F","P04A0","P04A6","P04A7","P04A8","P04A9","P04AA"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג שסתום בקרת לחץ פליטה‏ B"],U067F:["Lost Communication With Barometric Pressure Sensor A","Barometric pressure sensor A is normally the ambient sensor that corrects fueling, boost targets and many diagnostics for altitude; CARB requires barometric pressure, measured or estimated, in the OBD data stream. U067F covers a digital version of that sensor whose messages stop arriving.",["Data, supply or ground wire to the barometric sensor interrupted","Connector loose or corroded","Barometric sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Slightly off fueling or boost at altitude","Other diagnostics may be suspended"],1,1,["U0680","U068A","U0609","P2226","P2227","P2228","P2229","P2230"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ A"],U0680:["Lost Communication With Barometric Pressure Sensor B","The letter B need not mean a second ambient sensor; it can be any further pressure input that sees near-atmospheric air. GM's 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 tables, written for a program with two throttle bodies, use barometric sensor B for the pressure ahead of the bank 2 throttle and send it over SENT.",["SENT signal, supply or ground wire to the bank 2 pressure sensor faulty","Connector at the sensor ahead of the throttle loose or wet","Pressure sensor sends malformed frames","Engine controller software or SENT input fault"],["Check engine light after two trips","Uneven running between banks possible","Additional pressure plausibility codes"],2,1,["U067F","U068A","P222A","P222B","P222C","P222D","P222E","P222F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ B"],U0681:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D","In the generic code scheme the letters D, E and F normally mark the accelerator pedal tracks, while A to C and G belong to throttle bodies. U0681 is meant for a pedal module whose first track D reports digitally, for example over SENT or SPC as offered by Melexis' MLX90377 position IC, which lists pedal sensors as an application and comes as a fully redundant dual die. No manufacturer documents U0681 publicly.",["Wiring to the pedal module chafed in the footwell or at the bulkhead","Pedal module connector loose or corroded","Sensor electronics in the pedal module failed (replaced as a unit)","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light and possibly a powertrain warning","Sluggish, rate-limited throttle response","Reduced power"],1,3,["U0682","U0683","U0606","P2120","P2121","P2122","P2123","P2124"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ D"],U0682:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E","Track E is usually the redundant second signal of the accelerator pedal, which the controller compares with track D before trusting any torque request. U0682 marks the loss of digital frames from that track. No manufacturer documents it publicly; GM and Ford wire pedal E analog, with Ford setting P2127/P2128 on voltage limits and P2138 when D and E disagree by more than 0.9 degrees.",["Signal or reference wire of track E damaged","Water or corrosion in the pedal connector","Pedal module electronics failed"],["Check engine light and powertrain warning","Delayed throttle response","Fixed elevated idle with no pedal response if both tracks fail"],1,3,["U0681","U0683","U0607","P2125","P2126","P2127","P2128","P2129"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ E"],U0683:["Lost Communication With Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F","A third pedal track F is rare. It appears where a pedal module carries three signals, or where the F letter is used for an extra switch or a throttle input; the correlation codes P2139 (D/F), P2140 (E/F) and P212F (F/G) show that the scheme pairs F both with the pedal tracks and with throttle sensor G. U0683 means that digital frames for input F have stopped or fail their checks.",["Wiring for input F open, shorted or chafed","Connector at the pedal or sensor module loose or corroded","Sensor electronics for input F failed"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or limited throttle response","Additional correlation codes possible"],2,3,["U0681","U0682","U0688","P2130","P2131","P2132","P2133","P2134"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ F"],U0684:["Lost Communication With Catalyst Temperature Bank 1 Sensor 1","A catalyst temperature sensor tells the controller when the converter is hot enough to work and to be tested. Sensor 1 on bank 1 is the first such probe on the bank that holds cylinder 1. U0684 applies when the probe sends its reading as a digital message and that message has stopped.",["Sensor lead near the converter burnt or chafed","Evaluation electronics of the temperature sensor failed","Corroded connector under the vehicle","Engine controller input or software fault"],["Check engine light","Catalyst readiness monitor does not complete"],2,1,["U0685","U0686","P0425","P0426","P0427","P0428","P046A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם טמפרטורת ממיר קטליטי (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],U0685:["Lost Communication With Catalyst Temperature Bank 1 Sensor 2","Where a converter carries two temperature probes, one usually sits ahead of the brick and one behind it, so that the heat released by the reaction shows up as a rise between them. Sensor 2 on bank 1 is the second, downstream position. U0685 means this probe reports over a digital link and its messages no longer arrive. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, so thresholds and debounce times are unknown.",["Lead of the downstream probe damaged by heat, stones or road salt","Sensor electronics failed","Connector corroded or not fully latched"],["Check engine light","Catalyst monitor or sensor comparison stays incomplete"],2,1,["U0684","U0687","P042A","P042B","P042C","P042D","P046A"],"אבדה התקשורת עם טמפרטורת ממיר קטליטי (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],U0686:["Lost Communication With Catalyst Temperature Bank 2 Sensor 1","Bank 2 exists only on engines whose cylinder rows feed separate exhaust paths, so U0686 belongs to V or flat engines with one converter per side. It means the first catalyst temperature probe of that second bank has stopped delivering digital messages. Such probes are often a thermocouple paired with a small electronics unit;",["Sensor electronics on bank 2 damaged by heat","Harness on the bank 2 side chafed or melted","Connector corroded","Engine controller input fault"],["Check engine light","Catalyst monitor for bank 2 not completed"],2,1,["U0684","U0687","P0435","P0436","P0437","P0438","P046B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם טמפרטורת ממיר קטליטי (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],U0687:["Lost Communication With Catalyst Temperature Bank 2 Sensor 2","U0687 refers to the rear catalyst temperature probe of bank 2, the one behind the converter brick on the second cylinder row. Once its digital messages stop, the controller can no longer compare bank 2 inlet and outlet temperatures (P046B) and loses an over-temperature guard: such probes have long been used to warn when a converter runs hotter than it can tolerate, which on older two-way designs was around 750 °C.",["Lead of the rear bank 2 probe damaged","Sensor electronics failed after overheating","Connector corroded"],["Check engine light","Bank 2 temperature comparison not possible","No noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["U0686","U0685","P043A","P043B","P043C","P043D","P046B"],"אבדה התקשורת עם טמפרטורת ממיר קטליטי (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],U0688:["Lost Communication With Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G","Throttle sensor G is the second track of a second throttle body. GM's 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 tables, for a program with one throttle per bank, use it for throttle position sensor 2 on bank 2. Both tracks of that throttle travel in one SENT stream, so GM sets U0688 together with U0608 (sensor 1, bank 2) when the line carries no signal, pulse widths fall outside their window or the calibration pulse is off, within 0.13…",["SENT, supply or ground wire to the bank 2 throttle body faulty","Throttle body connector loose, wet or corroded","Sensor electronics in the throttle body failed (replaced as a unit)","Engine controller SENT input fault"],["Check engine light on the first trip","Reduced power, uneven running between banks","U0608 stored at the same time"],2,3,["U0608","U0606","U0607","P212A","P212B","P212C","P212D","P212E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת‏ G"],U0689:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger B Temperature Sensor","Twin-charger engines may monitor a temperature at the second charger, for instance to protect the compressor or turbine of charger B from overheating; CARB's diesel data list includes compressor inlet as well as turbine inlet and outlet temperatures. U0689 means the reading of the temperature sensor for charger B arrives over a digital link and that link has failed.",["Wiring near charger B damaged by heat","Connector loose or corroded","Temperature sensor or its interface electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Boost reduced as a precaution","Otherwise often unchanged driving"],2,3,["U0643","P2B8F","P2B90","P2B91","P2B92"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ B"],U068A:["Lost Communication With Barometric Pressure Sensor C","Barometric sensor C appears in two very different layouts. In GM's dual-throttle tables 23OBDG07/24OBDG07 it measures the air ahead of the bank 1 throttle; P227C and P227D judge its raw value (under 50 or over 115 kPa, 2 s), and U068A is set once the bank 1 SENT frames carry an incorrect length for 1.5 s, two trips to MIL.",["Signal, supply or ground wire to sensor C damaged","Connector at the intake pressure sensor loose or corroded","Sensor C electronics failed","Engine controller software fault"],["Check engine light after two trips","Bank 1 fueling less precise","Accompanying pressure codes P227B to P227D possible"],2,1,["U0680","U067F","U060F","P227A","P227B","P227C","P227D","P227E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ ברומטרי‏ C"],U068B:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor A","The inlet pressure sensor sits between air filter and compressor. Its reading shows filter restriction and, together with boost pressure, the pressure ratio the compressor works against. Ford's 2023 diesel summary connects sensor A via SENT and lists U068B in its SENT sensor group: U068B follows when the low-level SENT driver sees the signal line pinned to one voltage level, either up or down, monitored without…",["SENT signal wire shorted to ground or voltage, or open","Connector on the intake duct loose, oily or corroded","Inlet pressure sensor failed"],["Check engine light","Air filter restriction no longer monitored","Possibly somewhat reduced boost"],1,1,["U068C","P012A","P012B","P012C","P012D","P012E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ A"],U068C:["Lost Communication With Turbocharger/Supercharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B","A second inlet pressure sensor makes sense where each bank breathes through its own filter and charger, or where a two-stage system needs the pressure ahead of the second compressor. U068C means the digital frames from that sensor B no longer arrive in usable form. No manufacturer documents U068C publicly;",["Signal, supply or ground wire to inlet sensor B damaged","Connector loose or contaminated with oil","Sensor B electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Filter restriction on that side no longer detected","Slightly lower boost possible"],1,1,["U068B","P2374","P2375","P2376","P2377","P2378"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ כניסת מגדש‏ B"],U068D:["Lost Communication With EGR Temperature Sensor A","EGR temperature sensors show how hot the recirculated gas is, mostly behind the EGR cooler, so the controller can judge cooler efficiency and correct the gas density. U068D is the digital-link failure for sensor A. No public manufacturer source covers U068D.",["Wiring to EGR temperature sensor A damaged near the cooler","Connector oily, sooty or corroded","Sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","EGR cooler monitoring not possible"],2,1,["U068E","U068F","U0690","P040A","P040B","P040C","P040D","P040E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת EGR‏ A"],U068E:["Lost Communication With EGR Temperature Sensor B","GM documents this code in its 2025 diesel tables 25OBDG04A and 25OBDG04B, where sensor B is named EGR temperature sensor 1. Its circuit tests (P041C, P041D) are written for either a resistive probe or a digital thermocouple unit; the digital one counts as low below -72.8 °C.",["SENT signal, supply or ground wire to sensor B damaged","Internal fault in the sensor that shuts off its output","Connector corroded or contaminated by soot and oil","Fault at the controller input the sensor uses"],["Check engine light, on GM diesels in the first trip","Second code for the controller input stored alongside","EGR cooler efficiency not monitored"],2,1,["U068D","U068F","U0690","P041A","P041B","P041C","P041D","P041E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת EGR‏ B"],U068F:["Lost Communication With EGR Temperature Sensor C","Engines with both a high- and a low-pressure EGR loop need more temperature points, which is where slots C and D come in. U068F means the controller lost the digital messages of EGR temperature sensor C. There is no public manufacturer documentation for it.",["Wiring to sensor C near the exhaust aftertreatment damaged","Connector corroded by road splash","Sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Low-pressure EGR reduced or disabled"],2,1,["U068D","U068E","U0690","P04CE","P04CF","P04D0","P04D1","P04D2"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת EGR‏ C"],U0690:["Lost Communication With EGR Temperature Sensor D","Sensor D is the last of the four EGR temperature slots, used only on systems with many measuring points, for example on both sides of a cooler in each of two EGR loops. U0690 says its digital messages have stopped reaching the controller. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and none of the reviewed GM and Ford tables uses a D position at all.",["Wiring to sensor D damaged","Connector loose or corroded","Sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light","EGR cooler check incomplete"],2,1,["U068D","U068E","U068F","P04E5","P04E6","P04E7","P04E8","P04E9"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת EGR‏ D"],U0691:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Pressure Sensor A","On Ford's 6.7 L and 3.0 L diesels of 2023, exhaust pressure sensor A measures pressure ahead of the turbine and is a SENT device. Ford's diesel OBD summary sets U0691 when the low-level SENT driver sees a communication error or no data within the expected window, when the line is held at one voltage level, or when the sensor reports an internal fault; the check runs continuously and needs 5 s.",["SENT line shorted to ground or supply, or open, near the hot turbo","Sensor reports an internal error or stops sending","Connector heat-damaged or corroded","Sensor damaged by soot or condensate in the pressure line"],["Check engine light","Reduced boost or power on some engines","EGR and turbo running on substitute values"],2,3,["U0692","U069F","P0470","P0471","P0472","P0473","P0474"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ A"],U0692:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Pressure Sensor B","Exhaust pressure sensor B is a second pressure point in the exhaust, whose location the maker defines, for instance on the other bank or behind the turbine. U0692 means its digital output, usually SENT, has stopped delivering valid frames. Code-specific documentation from a manufacturer is not public.",["Wiring to pressure sensor B damaged by exhaust heat","Sensor B electronics failed","Connector corroded"],["Check engine light","Possibly reduced power"],2,1,["U0691","U069F","P047A","P047B","P047C","P047D","P047E"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ B"],U0693:["Lost Communication With Humidity Sensor","Intake air humidity influences combustion temperature and NOx, so some engines measure it, usually with a capacitive element built into the air-mass meter; Bosch offers such meters with optional humidity sensing over SENT, FAS or LIN.",["Humidity element in the air-mass meter contaminated or failed","Signal or supply wire to the sensor faulty","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Engine controller software fault"],["Check engine light after two trips","Usually no noticeable drivability change","Accompanying humidity or air-mass codes possible"],1,1,["P00F2","P00F3","P00F4","P00F5","P00F6","U060F"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחות"],U0694:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump A","Liquid-cooled traction batteries rely on an electric pump to move coolant through the pack, and pumps like Bosch's PCE accept their speed command by PWM or LIN and report faults themselves. U0694 records that battery pump A no longer communicates. Published manufacturer data do not mention it.",["Coolant entered the pump electronics housing","Bus, supply or ground wire to the pump damaged","Pump motor or controller failed","Battery or hybrid controller software fault"],["Hybrid/EV system warning","Reduced drive power","Slower DC fast charging"],3,3,["U0695","P0C47","P0C48","P0C49","P0C4A","P0CFF","P2CF3"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],U0695:["Lost Communication With Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump B","Pump B is a second pump in the battery thermal circuit; what it serves, for instance a parallel branch or a heater or chiller loop, is up to the manufacturer. U0695 is set when that pump stops answering on its data link. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Wiring or connector of pump B damaged or wet","Pump B electronics or motor failed","Controlling module or software faulty"],["Battery temperature warning or power limit","Charging power reduced","Hybrid/EV system warning"],3,3,["U0694","P0E1A","P0E1B","P0E1C","P0E1D","P2CF5","P2CF7"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U0696:["Lost Communication With Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C","In GM's 2025 diesel tables 25OBDG04A and 25OBDG04B, sensor C is the downstream relative pressure sensor, which reads the gauge pressure behind the particulate filter and carries its own temperature element (lost communication there is U06B6). U0696 is set when the sensor reports message faults above a fixed count or when its newest message is too old, judged as 158 failures in 200 samples at 12.5 ms intervals.",["Wiring to the downstream pressure sensor damaged by heat or chafing","Internal sensor fault that switches off the SENT output","Connector corroded by road splash"],["Check engine light, on GM diesels in the first trip","Particulate filter regeneration based on estimates or delayed"],2,1,["U0697","U0601","U0602","P2CE5","P2CE6","P2CE7","P2CE8","P2CE9"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C"],U0697:["Lost Communication With Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D","Sensor D is the fourth filter pressure slot and appears only in Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary, which watches particulate filters on both banks (P226D and P226E for a missing substrate). There U0697 sits with P2CEA in the circuit and lost-communication check for SENT-type pressure sensors A to D: it runs all the time and needs 5 s to log a fault.",["Wiring to filter pressure sensor D damaged","Sensor D stopped transmitting","Connector corroded or unlatched"],["Check engine light","Particulate filter monitor for one bank incomplete"],2,1,["U0696","U0601","U0602","P2CEA","P2CEB","P2CEC","P2CED","P2CEE"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D"],U0698:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump E","Coolant pump E continues the generic letter series of auxiliary electric pumps after A to D. Mercedes-Benz uses it for the second coolant pump in its low-temperature circuit: bulletin LI20.00-P-076708 lists U0698E4 and U0698E5 in the powertrain control unit N127 together with other LIN devices such as fan, charge-air cooler pump and high-temperature control valve.",["Powertrain control unit software (Mercedes N127 version 22A)","LIN wiring or intermediate connector chafed or corroded","Pump E electronics failed"],["Check engine light","Coolant warning message","Radiator fan running at full speed"],2,3,["U0699","U0623","U0624","U062F","U0649","P2DF4","P2DF8","P2D26"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E"],U0699:["Lost Communication With Coolant Pump F","Pump F is the sixth auxiliary electric coolant pump in the generic lettering, and the code flags that this pump has stopped responding on its data line. No manufacturer documents U0699 publicly; even the Mercedes bulletin that uses the E code for a low-temperature pump lists no F.",["Data, supply or ground wire to pump F damaged","Pump F electronics or motor failed","Controlling module or software fault"],["Warning light depending on manufacturer","Loop served by pump F runs too warm","Radiator fan running more often or at full speed"],2,3,["U0698","U0623","U0624","U062F","U0649","P2D27"],"אבדה התקשורת עם משאבת נוזל קירור‏ F"],U069A:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 1 Sensor 3","The third exhaust temperature sensor on bank 1 usually sits in the aftertreatment, ahead of the filter or SCR stage. GM covers U069A in both 2025 diesel tables, 25OBDG04A and 25OBDG04B: a SENT sensor whose output was switched off by an internal fault, or that sends faulty or outdated messages, fails the check once 19 readings out of 25, taken every 100 ms, are bad.",["Sensor harness along the aftertreatment burnt or chafed","Electronics module of the thermocouple sensor failed","Connector corroded","Controller input fault"],["Check engine light, on GM diesels in the first trip","Particulate filter regeneration blocked or postponed","Further code for the controller input"],2,1,["U069B","U069C","U061F","U0620","P242A","P242B","P242C","P242D"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],U069B:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 1 Sensor 4","Sensor 4 is the fourth temperature point along the bank 1 exhaust. Of GM's 2025 diesel tables only 25OBDG04A contains U069A's partner U069B; 25OBDG04B ends at sensor 3. The logic is the same SENT check as for sensor 3, 19 bad samples of 25 at 100 ms after the sensor's start-up delay, Type A.",["Harness to sensor 4 damaged by heat during regeneration","Sensor electronics failed","Connector corroded"],["Check engine light","Regeneration interrupted or not started"],2,1,["U069A","U069D","U0620","P246E","P246F","P2470","P2471","P2472"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 1, חיישן 4)"],U069C:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 2 Sensor 3","U069C refers to the third temperature probe in the bank 2 exhaust path, so it can only occur where each cylinder bank feeds its own aftertreatment line, as on some V engines. Such a probe is a digital unit that reports its reading as SENT or CAN frames; the code is stored when those frames stop or keep failing their checks. No manufacturer documents U069C publicly.",["Sensor harness on the bank 2 exhaust side chafed or heat-damaged","Electronics box of the probe failed","Probe has lost its supply or ground","Connector corroded or not latched"],["Check engine light","Filter regeneration on bank 2 postponed or blocked","Probe shows no value in live data"],2,1,["U069D","U069A","U0621","U0622","P2466","P2467","P2468","P2469"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],U069D:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Bank 2 Sensor 4","Sensor 4 is normally the final measuring position in the bank 2 exhaust, often placed further down the aftertreatment where the controller judges how hot the gas leaves the filter or catalyst stages. U069D reports that this digital probe has gone silent on its data link. Code-level documentation from a maker is not public; CARB only demands that a coded digital input which stops talking gets a code of its own.",["Probe lead melted or torn near the rear aftertreatment","Electronics unit of the probe dead","Supply fuse or feed wire of the probe faulty"],["Check engine light","Regeneration delayed or cancelled"],2,1,["U069C","U069B","U0622","P2473","P2474","P2475","P2476","P2477"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה (בנק 2, חיישן 4)"],U069E:["Lost Communication With Coolant Heater A","Coolant heater A is an electric heater with its own control electronics that warms coolant for the cabin and, in some designs, for the traction battery – usually a high-voltage PTC unit in hybrids and EVs. The vehicle commands it over a data link, mostly LIN: DBK's 400 V heater is driven via LIN 2.0 plus a PWM input, and Webasto's 800 V range adds CAN on its larger models.",["LIN or CAN line to the heater broken, shorted or connector loose","12 V supply or ground of the heater electronics missing","Control electronics inside the heater failed","Heater or master module software fault"],["Little or no cabin heat in electric mode","Engine starts more often in cold weather to supply heat (hybrids)","Slow battery warm-up or reduced charging power in frost, where the heater serves the battery"],2,0,["P2B72","P2B73","P2B74","P2B75","P2DA4","P2DA5","P2DA6","P2DA7"],"אבדה התקשורת עם גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A"],U069F:["Lost Communication With Exhaust Pressure Sensor C","Exhaust pressure sensor C is a third pressure measuring point in the exhaust; where it sits is up to the manufacturer, for example behind the turbine or on a second exhaust branch. U069F: this digital sensor, typically a SENT device, no longer supplies usable frames. No manufacturer documents U069F publicly.",["Signal, supply or ground wire of sensor C damaged by exhaust heat","Sensor C reports an internal fault or stops sending","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector"],["Check engine light","Possibly less boost or power","Pressure value missing or frozen in live data"],2,3,["U0691","U0692","P2E54","P2E55","P2E56","P2E57"],"אבדה התקשורת עם חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ C"],U0901:["Invalid Data from Ion Sense Module","An ion sense module evaluates the tiny current that the burning mixture conducts between the plug electrodes after ignition for the engine controller, which uses it to spot misfire, knock and poor combustion; Ford's patent US20170030322A1 places such a module in the ignition system.",["Software of the engine controller or ion sense module (update available)","Disturbed data line, for example from ignition interference or a poor ground","Ion sense module internally faulty"],["Check engine light","Possibly reduced power from knock protection","Misfire or ion sense codes stored alongside"],2,3,["U0673","U0353","P034C","P28C0","P0300"],""]};export{e as default};
